window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5601,"title":"Chapter 5601: Chapter 5600: You Must Remember! I","paragraphs":["In THE Provenance Realm of the First Lifeform, evening light lay warm over everything.","The blue gold hills rolled out soft and endless from the long hall, and the river of light murmured through its star-pools, and the standing stones kept their patient watch over orchards heavy with fruit, and above it all, ten stars turned slowly through a sky that belonged to no one else in existence. Peace lived here in abundance!","And on the threshold of the long hall, Noah stood grasping the vibrating Aurate Collar of the First Purity.","It buzzed against his palms, pale ancient bone shaped into a seamless band, worn smooth by an age no record reached, faint golden light moving through its depths in slow pulses. The chest bones of a First Lifeform, mistaken by many for a Remnant Existential Treasure, and it had waited on his threshold in silence for days.","It was not silent now.","Noah raised it, and put it on.","The moment it settled against his chest, the buzzing deepened! Pulse after pulse rolled out of the bone and into his frame, stronger and stronger, and he felt his Provenance within him begin to answer, ten singularities cycling and pulsing in rhythm with the collar as though two old clocks had finally agreed on the hour!","And everything nearby began humming.","The grass hummed. The stones hummed. The air itself took on a weight of enormous age, ancient in a way even his Realm had never felt, and Noah found that he could see through more of the collar than ever before, layer after layer of its weavings parting before his senses! And from somewhere deep inside it, a heavy hum rose, and within the hum...","Words.","A voice! A heavy, somber voice, filled with dignity and immensity, speaking from a distance no measurement could cross, and he could barely make out the shape of it!","Noah closed his eyes, and focused everything he was on listening.","And distinctly, at last, he heard.","|Before the first light, before the first law, we were, and we were our own. Nothing granted, nothing borrowed, nothing owed. What I am, I made. Let existence witness the First, come again!|","HUUUM!","The first time he heard them in full, his entire existence VIBRATED! His ten singularities buzzed in their orbits as though called by name, his blood sang in his veins, and the words did not stop, they continued, repeating in that deep somber voice, a declaration circling through ancient bone!","Noah’s gaze was heavy as he listened, and as he listened, something gave way.","He finally felt like he grasped a portion of the Aurate Collar, and information flowed into his existence!","|You have refined THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity to a sufficient level. You have grasped some of its uses, and understood its nature somewhat.|","|THE First Purity is a piece of a First Lifeform, and it carries their oldest idea: that Purity was not a virtue. It was the only possible way to exist. Everything that came after it, every framework, every granted power, every borrowed authority, is, from the collar’s perspective... sediment.|","|The collar was shed by one of THE First Lifeforms as a covenant object: an instrument that preserves and enforces the original condition of purity. Its full purpose is not entirely clear.|","| Its first grasped usage: the induction of THE Provenance Kismet of First Purity, one time. This is an ability that decently powerful lifeforms holding an abundance of Provenance Essence have the capability of utilizing.|","|THE Provenance Kismet of First Purity: the wearer pushes their Provenance Essence to cause the emergence of something purest to the wellbeing of their existence. This may be the generation of further Provenance Essence. It may be a Unique State of Existence exceeding Inner Peace, in which epiphanies arrive that make existence itself part of one’s limbs. It may be more. The effect answers only the one who calls it: it is, and remains, unique to the lifeform utilizing it.|","...!","Noah stood very still on his threshold, and his thoughts moved rapidly.","This was an outer ability! A first grasped usage, the shallowest thing the collar was willing to show him, and it was already terrifying! An induced event of pure benefit, shaped by nothing but the truth of the one who called it... and when it came to the emergence of something purest to the wellbeing of HIS existence, what else would his existence pave the way for, if not the emergence of more Provenance Essence?","Because if he could break past the count of ten... he knew, the way he knew his own heartbeat, that something significant would happen to his existence!","So without any delay, he sought to activate THE Provenance Kismet of First Purity, and of course, the trigger to utilize it seemed to be the first part of the words resonating through the bone.","He spoke them out somberly, into the evening quiet of his Realm.","\" Before the first light, before the first law, we were, and we were our own...\"","There was a heavy silence.","Then...","HUUM!","The collar on his chest shone with a resplendent invisible light that tapped onto his body, and he felt his ten Provenance Essences SEETHE!","And above him, out of him, phantoms bloomed, ten spectral singularities of incandescent blue rising into the evening air and beginning to spin!","Noah looked at them with shining eyes, and waited to see what effect would emerge.","However random existence chose to be, his trueness was unquestionable. Whatever came out of this would be something of utmost benefit to him, if it truly did regard something purest to his wellbeing!","And he watched as the phantom singularities spun faster, and faster, and then descended, landing on the grass before him in a wide ring, ten points of turning blue light, spinning, spinning...","And his Provenance Realm began to shake.","Noah frowned. The hills trembled. The river of light shivered in its bed, and the ten stars flickered above the hall, and then his frown deepened into something somber, because the shaking did not stop at his Realm’s borders!","He felt it extend OUTWARD, out through the doorway, out into the endless seas beyond, until THE Infiniverse herself was trembling around the small homestead she carried!","What was this?","With a heavy gaze, he looked down, and saw that the spinning singularities had formed the circular outline... of a pool!","A white pool!"]},{"number":5602,"title":"Chapter 5602: Chapter 5601: You Must Remember! II","paragraphs":["His eyes opened wide as something cold moved through his memory, because he felt like he was having deja vu! A white pool!","Was this... the actual pool that Ulf had painted and not the one he saw prior?!","He wondered, and the pool answered by filling!","Within the ring of spinning singularities, liquid white rose and began to swirl, and Noah’s senses read its substance and went sharp, because it swirled with immense concentrations of THE Argent Loom, braided through with Infinity and THE Primordial Source, and threading through all three, faint and unmistakable... a glimmer of his own Provenance Essence!","Noah’s gaze was heavy on it.","Would the pool be empty? Would it lead to some place? Just what...","HUUM!","As he was thinking, his entire existence buzzed, and the pool before him went CHAOTIC!","The white surface erupted into thrashing, churning violence, a heavy storm raging inside a circle ten steps across, waves of loomlight and Infinity crashing against the ring of spinning phantoms, and then, out of the chaos, in a moment that stretched itself slow before his eyes...","A hand erupted from the pool.","A fair, slender hand, fingers spread, reaching up out of the thrashing white, and it was not rising! It thrashed with the storm, clawing at the air, and the body beneath it was not coming up, could not come up, would not come up... unless Noah reached in to help them up!","What the hell was this?","Noah stood somber and astonished at the pool’s edge, watching the slender hand grasp at nothing, and he could feel it, distinctly, through no sense he could name: the hand was panicked. It was scared. Whoever was underneath was drowning in that white storm, and the hand was the only thing they had managed to send up to ask for help!","He thought of the capability of the Aurate Collar. The emergence of something purest to the wellbeing of his existence. He thought it in the span of one breath, with the hand already beginning to sink.","And after that brief hesitation... Noah kneeled down...and reached in.","His hand plunged into the thrashing white and grasped the slender fingers in the last second before they drowned and disappeared under the depths, and he pulled!","HUUUM!","And... it was so HEAVY!","Heavier than an Observable Existence! Heavier than a few of them together! Heavier than even the stone he had carried on his shoulders in the obsidian domain, before he had ever worn the Aurate Collar, and his arm screamed and his feet drove into the grass and the whole Realm groaned around the effort!","Noah bellowed grandly into the storm!","All ten singularities of Provenance Essence blazed alight upon his chest as blue brilliance covered everything, the hills, the pool, the sky, the whole evening drowned in incandescent light, and with everything he was, he YANKED the hand up out of the white pool as...","BOOM!","The white pool fissured! Cracks tore across its surface and out through the surrounding existence, the grass splitting, the air itself webbing with thin bright fractures, and Noah staggered back with his prize, still feeling like he had pulled something far, far too heavy for any measure he owned, and he set it down upon the grass to see...","...!","Something that caused his eyes to open wide as all of existence seemed to pause.","Now, Noah was experienced . He had seen many things. He had stood before queens and Primevals and the manifest wrath of ancient authorities. But what he saw now was utterly incomprehensible to him, because before him, on the grass of his Realm, was... a woman.","Okay, a woman, so it wasn’t that incomprehensible but...","If somewhere in the depths of his psyche there lived a fantasy of a woman, held quietly since puberty and never once spoken of, then what he saw before him exceeded even that.","And she was shaking. And she was injured. And she was utterly breathtaking.","She had red hair, loose and soaked and clinging to her face and shoulders. Freckles were scattered light across her nose and cheeks, small and human and utterly at odds with the immensity coming off her frame.","Her features were beautiful as existence itself glowed aroujd her, a soft jaw, a small nose, pale red lips pressed thin against pain, and she wore a robe of white and blue, simple and flowing.","And the robe was filled with blood.","Crimson gold blood.","It soaked through the white cloth across her chest and side, and her hand clasped over her chest as she heaved on the grass, and her face was full of fear and alarm, the face of someone still drowning even on dry land!","Then she raised her head, and looked at him.","And Noah watched the fear fade out of her face! Even through the tremendous pain, her eyes flooded with immense relief, relief so total it looked close to breaking her, and she began to speak even as blood spattered out of her mouth with the words!","\" You’re alive... you’re still alive! We have to...!\"","BOOM!","What?","She had begun to walk toward him, pushing up off the grass, and Noah took a step back!","Because this injured lifeform, this bleeding, shaking woman... every single step she took caused the ground of his Realm to CAVE and shudder! The grass split under her bare feet, the hills groaned, and he could feel his Provenance Realm barely holding itself together around her presense, a homestead straining to carry something it was never sized for!","She saw him take the step back.","And the relief on her face died. Horror and fear covered it again, and her voice came out absentminded and cracking, half to him and half to no one at all.","\" You... don’t remember me? You don’t remember...!\" Her eyes went wide and distant.","\" He must have already begun. Listen closely! THE Sealed One he has grasped IT! In the future...he got IT! Nobody thought... nobody expected... ah!\"","Blood ran freely from her lips as her words tumbled over each other.","\" He has begun to target us. To target YOU. He will target all those who stood against him, across Dimensions and Time, as even your past Origins are not safe! Those around you are not safe! THE Infiniverse is not safe! Mother is not safe! I...\"","Her hand reached toward him, shaking. \" You must remember! You promised to always remember! You-...!\"","She spat out waves of crimson gold blood, and her hand flew to her chest and clutched it tightly...","And she collapsed in front of Noah, and actually passed out, sprawled across the trembling grass of his Realm!","...!","Her words rang through him, every one of them filled with terrifying meanings- the future, the past, the targeting, IT, Origins, Mother, a promise he had never made or could not remember making!","But worst of all was the little he could identify of the woman herself, lying bleeding before him, as his senses reached for her and returned almost nothing at all!","|??????|:: A Provenance Lifeform... ???????","...!"]},{"number":5603,"title":"Chapter 5603: Chapter 5602: Thalia! I","paragraphs":["A Provenance Lifeform had sprouted out of a pool that was induced by the capability of a treasure that stemmed from the bones of a Provenance Lifeform.","It was a ridiculous reality! And yet it lay bleeding on his grass, and Noah’s entire existence was forced to be very serious at this moment, because he had already sent a message ringing through his connection to THE Infiniverse to be on high alert!","And while his hands moved, his mind broke her words down piece by piece.","If what she said was true, then THE Sealed One attains IT. And she had said it in a tense that dragged an entire abyss open behind it: in the future.","Then the targets. All who stood against him. Your Origins are not safe. Origins! His beginnings? His very path at this moment could be considered a beginning if someone wanted to close things off.","But apart from all that was the message that...Those around you are not safe. THE Infiniverse is not safe. And then the word that had tightened everything in him.","Mother.","Naturally, he was inclined to think she was talking about HIS mother! About Amelia, the Originator of THE Infinite Cause that was now Telos!","And if a stranger from a drowning future knew his mother well enough to count her among the unsafe... then the avenues of possibility that opened up were many, and not one of them could be walked until the woman on his grass opened her eyes!","So the biggest thing now was simple. Stabilize her. Wake her.","\" Ruination .\" He affirmed his companion as his crown’s weavings spread. \" Take care of everything else. All weavings of existence should be ready to anticipate and react to any potential attack.\"","|Understood, Master.|","Across the connection, THE Infiniverse was already moving, her weavings pulsing on high alert through thousands of realms.","Meanwhile, Noah crossed the trembling grass and knelt beside the woman with no more hesitation.","And up close, the state of her was grievous!","On the left side of her chest, a huge tear ran through robe and flesh alike, and within it, stellar blood welled continuously around the faint shapes of organs, and Noah’s expression hardened as his senses reached deeper, because through the injury, faintly, he could see further inside her existence.","Clusters.","Clusters of many, many singularities, turning slowly in her depths, and they should have shocked him by count alone, because there were far more than his ten! Provenance Essence, in constellations!","And yet they were... dim.","Every one of them! Singularities that should have blazed the way his own blazed were guttering low, their light thin, their turning slow, an entire sky of essence burning at embers!","Noah went to work.","He tried everything he had. The Realm’s healing boon pressed into her, warmth for anything whose Lifeline was not entirely shattered. He set the Yoke against the weight of her injury itself, bearing what pressed on her frame so her body could spend itself on mending. And still the stellar blood welled, and still she paled, and so, in the end, Noah opened his own palm with a blade of his blood, and began to give her his!","His crimson gold flowed into her, glowing from within, the light of his ten Provenance Essences carried through every drop, and he watched it sink into the tear and vanish, and he kept it flowing, steady and unhurried, while she lay unconscious and breathing shallowly on his grass and his mind turned her every word over and over!","Like this, time began to pass.","Minutes turned into hours. The three stars wheeled slowly over the long hall. His blood flowed, and her blood slowed, and she did not wake.","Noah stayed kneeling beside her, and at some point in the second hour, he spoke quietly to no one at all.","\" To heal is also human. \" His palm stayed open above her wound. \" The first thing a human ever did with knowledge was probably pull a thorn out of someone else. To take care of another who cannot ask for it... that is as human as anything else...\"","In the third hour, her wounds stopped bleeding.","The tear across her chest began to close, flesh knitting slowly under stellar light, and Noah leaned in to press more of his blood into the healing... and her body rejected it!","His crimson gold stopped at her skin and simply would not enter! The Realm’s warmth slid off her! Every gift he offered was turned back at her boundary, gently, absolutely.","It was the distinct rejection his own existence gave to everything external, as if her whole unconscious frame was saying one thing at this time.","I am a Provenance Lifeform. I do not need anything external!","No matter what he tried after that, her body inherently denied it. She would finish her own mending, with her own dim constellations, at her own pace. He could only wait for her to wake.","Noah sat back on the grass beside her, and sighed, and spoke out loud to the evening.","\" How the hell did that fucker attain IT? What even IS ’it’?\"","The Realm did not answer. The woman did not answer. The collar on his chest hummed its old covenant to itself and offered nothing, and there were so many questions stacked up in him that they had begun forming an orderly line!","So, since he could do nothing for now... he made himself busy.","And he began to cook.","A Wok formed itself out of his weavings easily enough, wide and black and heavy, and a fire bloomed beneath it on the grass, and from his stores he drew out the meats he had scooped up long ago in THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension, flesh marbled in rings, pale sirloin that deepened Trueness, and THE True Human Emperor rolled up nothing at all because he wore no sleeves, and began to cook and grill beside an unconscious Provenance Lifeform!","Smoke rose sweet and heavy over the blue gold hills. His blades of blood, so recently instruments of lineage surgery, sliced meat in paper-thin sheets, and his main body worked the fire born of his Infinite Sanguine Mana in unhurried peace while far away, his clones oversaw THE Ymnaros, where the long Dimensionlapse was finally finishing, another Dimension folding its last edges into his own, THE Vaelos, the sky from which the armies of Infinite Lifeforms had once poured, settling into place as new territory.","And Noah ate as he cooked.","Because to enjoy the harvests all around existence... was also human! He ate standing over the fire, and he planned as he ate, contingency stacking on contingency! If her warning was true, there would be much to do as he needed more information first.","And as he did all this, on the tenth hour since her arrival...","The nose of the unique lifeform on his grass twitched.","Once. Twice.","An instant later, her eyes flung open as existence began to buzz around her, and her figure rose up off the grass in a single motion, and her eyes, wide awake and shining...","Were locked onto the array of food Noah had arranged before him!"]},{"number":5604,"title":"Chapter 5604: Chapter 5603: Thalia! II","paragraphs":["Noah gazed at the woman before him as she blinked and looked toward the food, almost in a daze, then down at her own mended body, and then back at him.","And he locked his gaze with hers, and read the many things moving through it!","There was pain there, and relief, and exhaustion, but the biggest of them, the one that pulled at something in his existence, was a longing for a thing that did not seem to exist.","She was looking at him the way a person looks for someone in a familiar face and cannot find them. Searching him and not finding whoever it was she searched for.","She spoke, and her voice came out soft, and low, and carried a strange composure even soaked in her own dried blood.","\" You haven’t cooked for me in this place for a long time. I missed it.\"","...!","Once more, she talked as though she knew him unfathomably well!","Was this truly someone he was with in the future? He could believe it of himself, oddly. He did not doubt that the man he was becoming might stand at a fire cooking for a woman like this. But belief was not knowledge, and there were far too many empty spaces in this, so he asked.","\" Before anything else. \" His voice stayed level. \" Is there immediate danger. Right now?\"","She closed her eyes, as though searching somewhere deeper than the Realm around them, and when she answered, the softness had a certainty threaded through it.","\" There should be some time. And leeway.\" Her eyes opened. \" No matter how powerful a thing is, Existence does not like things moving backward. Me included. THE Sealed One included. Existence is forward looking. I panicked, a little, when I arrived here. That was... unbecoming of me. But there should be some time.\"","Noah nodded slowly.","And he waved his hand, and offered her the food.","Vibrant grilled and cooked meats arranged themselves on shimmering plates of blue light, drifting toward her across the trembling grass, sweet smoke curling off them, and as they settled before her, he spoke.","\" Then tell me if I get anything wrong .\" He watched her face.","\" You and I...are close, in the future. You are a Provenance Lifeform. Something catastrophic has happened in that future, where THE Sealed One somehow obtains IT, and his actions afterward forced you to traverse across time itself. I-\"","\" You and I are not close in the future.\"","BOOM!","She interrupted him with those heavy words, and Noah looked at her, and she was smiling. A smile full of pain!","\" You were. You are...my Provenance. It is, as you would put it, far more quintessential than any closeness.\"","The smile turned faintly wry.","\"I did not traverse across time on purpose as my Provenance saught to warn you. And THE Sealed One does not obtain IT by mistake. The hands of Those Who Remain are steeped in it. But...\"","Her face went pale as she spoke.","Noah frowned, watching the color drain out of her cheeks mid-sentence, watching a fresh thread of stellar blood well faintly at the edge of her half-closed wound!","\" Moving across Time of such pivotal weavings is not without cost,\" she said, quieter now, pressing her hand lightly to her chest.","\" Especially for lifeforms of our kind, and our level. Anything I say, anything I reveal, it hurts my Provenance. It hurts what I am. So I must be very selective in what I tell you, because if I reveal something too heavy...I pay dearly. I fainted for hours, just now, on what little I said when I panicked.\"","She drew a slow breath, and steadied.","\" What you began to do is good, actually. Asking me to correct you when you are wrong. The less I speak of the future, the more I am able to do within it.\"","...!","And with that, in the next moment, she began to eat.","She ate with a quiet, absolute focus, as if the food before her were one of the most important things in all of existence, lifting a sheet of grilled meat with an unhurried grace that made the simple act look almost ceremonial!","Noah was silent for a moment, and watched her.","He watched her delicate features, the freckles scattered light across a face built with no waste in it, watched her lips part to eat and chew, watched the paleness recede as rosiness slowly returned to her cheeks with every bite, the wound at her chest knitting a fraction further as she took in the harvests of his fire.","And every single thing she did, the tilt of her head, the composure, the way she held stillness even while moving, screamed of a unique charm he could not quite put a finger on!","If revealing too much harmed her, then he would not make her reveal.","He would play the guessing game.","So he thought. He set the recent shape of things beside the little she had let slip, and an instant later his eyes lit up, and he spoke.","\" Was THE Sleepless Fiend one of Those Who Remain who helped THE Sealed One obtain IT?\" His gaze sharpened on her.","\" Do I offend them enough, by the time this future comes, that to be rid of me... they allow it? Aid it? They let THE Sealed One reach IT?\"","...!","He looked at the face of the Provenance Lifeform, and she locked onto his eyes, and she smiled at him, sadly, and said nothing at all as she continued to eat!","Noah breathed out, and his eyes flashed coldly.","Every choice had a consequence. He had always known that. But he had not thought the butterfly of some future choice of his could grow wings THIS heavy, heavy enough that ancient things would part their hands and let a monster reach for It!","But whatever the future held... the present still mattered most! It always had! The future was a storm on a horizon, and the present was the ground under his feet, and he would keep doing everything he could on the ground he actually stood on!","HUUM!","He rose to his feet.","\" Existence is.\" His voice rolled out quiet and certain over the fire. \" The past is set, regardless of what anyone tries to do to it. And it seems even THE Sealed One has trouble collapsing me in that future, because if his reach tries to stretch back into the past to unmake me here... it should face the same difficulty you faced coming back. If not more. Existence does not like things moving backward.\"","His eyes settled on her.","\" Even you, appearing here, in this time. That can be considered a loop being closed, not broken. You were always supposed to be here. At this exact moment. Which means the past is set.\" He said it again, to himself as much as to her, tasting the certainty of it. \" The past is set. So...\"","He walked toward her.","And he put out his hand.","\" Let us have an official introduction, then. I am Osmont. Noah Osmont .\" His hand hung in the warm firelit air between them. \" And you are...\"","And the Provenance Lifeform raised her right hand to his, while she continued to eat with her left, and there was grace in the gesture, and an immensity under the grace, an old regality that no exhaustion and no blood could dim, and she took his hand and answered with quiet, total confidence.","\" Thalia Vasiliou. \" Her eyes held his. \" Your future destiny. And your present... Provenance.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5605,"title":"Chapter 5605: Chapter 5604: The Weight of All Things!","paragraphs":["His Destiny! His Provenance!","She said the words with such total confidence that even Noah paused, because when he held her hand, he felt something he had not expected!","It was as though he were holding onto a boundless sun. A pull came off her frame through their joined hands, an unfathomable sense of attraction that reached into him and did not ask permission, drawing at his existence.","Thalia smiled, and let go!","\" While I did say we have some leeway ,\" she said, folding her hand back into her lap, \"the dangers are very much real. You have to prepare. Nobody knows what THE Sealed One is truly capable of, with IT. \"","Her eyes stayed steady on his. \"I need to make sure that you and THE Infiniverse are ready. So that Mother, and the others, are safe.\"","Her poise was grand even seated in her own dried blood, and Noah looked at this unfathomable woman and repeated her name silently, cementing it into his existence.","Thalia Vasiliou. Thalia!","\" And what could be done to prepare that I have not already set in motion ?\" he asked .","\"Nobody progresses across existence as fast as I do.\"","Thalia looked up, and raised her brows.","\" Do not be so sure.\"","Noah’s eyes sharpened.","\" Existence is vast. And Provenance Lifeforms are grand .\" She set down her plate of light. \" Even you have not fully grasped your own Provenance. By the measure of what you could be... you are weak .\"","\" Us First Lifeforms. Our power comes from within. That is what makes us the strongest things in existence. It is also what makes us the slowest. Everything we are, we must generate. And so where our peers consume treasures, devour one another, drink external authorities to swell their power in leaps, we cannot. We can only spur our own existence to produce more, and more, and more Provenance. From nothing but ourselves.\"","\"...Which is slow, \" Noah said.","\" Which is agonizingly slow.\" A small nod. \" So agonizing that among the very first of us, a technique was developed. A way to spur the existence to grow faster than it ever would on its own.\"","...!","She wiped her lips with a slow grace and rose to her feet, and Noah caught himself watching the red of her lips as she moved.","\" You always become distracted when you look at me.\" She said it as a simple, established fact. \" But I need you to focus. This will be critical. We fortify you first, and then we fortify Mother and the others, so that even across time, their existences cannot be targeted, because THE Sealed One WILL reach for them, exactly as he reached for me. And for that, you need to be far more than you currently are. \"","Her expression steadied into something almost solemn. \" This will injure me. So I will show it to you while I explain, and spend the cost only once. In the ages past, this was designed by lifeforms you and I would both revere.\"","She lifted her chin, and the exhaustion fell away from her bearing, and immensity gathered around her slender frame.","\" This...is THE Sovereign Genesis of the Weighted Origin.\"","HUUM!","\"It is not a technique of movement, or of striking, or of casting,\" Thalia said, and as she spoke, the air of the Realm began to change around her. \" It is a technique of bearing. You have already met its shallowest cousin in your own bones, I think. The bearing of weight. This reaches out... and calls the weight down.\"","The blue gold hills groaned!","Above Thalia, the evening sky of the Realm darkened, and something began to descend, invisible and immense, pressing down toward her standing figure, and Noah’s senses flared as he read what it was, and his eyes widened!","It was the weight of Existence itself!","\" You open your existence ,\" she said, her voice tightening with the growing pressure, \" and you invite the weight of all that surrounds you to settle upon it like a challenge through your Provenance. The weight of THE Primordial Source. The weight of Infinity. The weight of THE Argent Loom.\"","The white rivers of the Realm bent toward her, pouring their pressure onto her shoulders. \" The weight of Dimensions. Of Observable Existences. Of the frameworks, the Scales, the whole architecture of everything near you .\"","Her knees bent under a load Noah could feel from where he stood, the grass caving in a wide ring beneath her. \" And the weight of things you cannot yet perceive. All of it. Called down. Set upon a single existence, on purpose.\"","\"It will try to crush you. That is the entire point. The weight becomes a catalyst. A pressure so total that your existence, refusing to be flattened, is forced to answer it, and the only answer a Provenance Lifeform has... is to generate! Pressed hard enough, from every direction at once, the existence spurs itself to produce more Provenance simply to have something to push back with. The weight is the enzyme. The Provenance is what it forces out of you!\"","The pressure peaked, and Noah watched it happen!","Within Thalia’s dimmed depths, among her guttering constellations, a change moved, her existence straining against the descended weight of all things, and slowly, painfully, one of her dim singularities flickered, and brightened a fraction, spurred to answer a pressure that would not relent!","\" And it does more than generate ,\" she forced out, her frame trembling under the invisible mountain of existence. \" The adversity refines you. The same weight that squeezes out your Provenance also grinds your existence finer, layer by layer, tempering what you are against the pressure of everything you are not. You come out the other side both greater... and truer\"","Then she exhaled, and released it.","The weight lifted off her in a slow tide, the sky lightening, the grass beneath her sighing back up, and she stood breathing hard, one hand at her wounded chest!","\" But understand the danger, because this is why it is a technique of the first among us and almost no one else. \" Her eyes were hard and clear. \" You are calling down the weight of Existence itself. If you call too much, or hold it wrong, or your own generation cannot rise to meet the load in time... the weight does not simply hurt you. It flattens you out of existence entirely. One wrong movement, and the mountain you invited becomes the mountain that buries you. There is no injury to recover from. There is only perishing.\"","Noah’s gaze burned as he studied everything she had shown!","\"It is simple to speak ,\" Thalia continued, quieter, \" and it is monstrous to begin. To even attempt the first cycle, an existence must meet heavy conditions. It must generate Provenance already, truly, from within, or it has nothing to answer the weight with and dies in the first breath. It must be able to bear great weight without shattering, or the load caves it instantly. And it must be true enough to itself that the pressure of all that is NOT itself cannot rewrite it into sediment. \" She looked at him.","And Noah’s eyes shone.","Generate Provenance from within. He had ten singularities! Bear great weight without shattering. He had...well, THE Yoke of the Standing Sky and a spine seated with the Telos of Paradox! Be true enough that the weight of everything else could not overwrite him. He was...Quintessentially true.","He looked towards Thalia because the cost had come due!","Her face had gone pale again as she spoke and demonstrated, the color she had eaten back into her cheeks draining away, a fresh line of stellar blood welling at her healing wound, the price of passing down even this knowledge landing on her Provenance exactly as she had warned!","And yet she remained unfettered, standing straight through it, and she wiped a thread of crimson gold from the corner of her lips, and looked at him, and said one word.","\" Try.\"","...!"]},{"number":5606,"title":"Chapter 5606: Chapter 5605: Try!","paragraphs":["Thalia waved her hand.","A single small singularity of light drifted off her fingertips and crossed the space between them, unhurried, turning slowly, and Noah lifted his own hand and let it settle against his palm, where it sank into him and unfolded, and the whole methodology of THE Sovereign Genesis of the Weighted Origin flowed into his existence at once!","\" Before you try, understand the shape of it,\" Thalia said, lowering herself back to a seat on the grass, one hand resting light at her wounded chest. \" Because failure here is not a bruise. It is a beginning erased.\"","Noah held still, receiving.","\" You cannot simply call down the weight of Existence and stand under it as one man. The art works because the weight must course through the anatomy of your Provenance itself. It moves the way a resource moves. Directed. Channeled. Placed. And you begin at the smallest possible place.\"","\"A cell ?\" Noah said, reading it even as she spoke.","\" A single cell .\" She nodded. \" You take the entire descending force of all incoming existence, every ounce of the weight you call down, and you land it on ONE cell of your body. And that one cell must bear the weight of THE Primordial Source, of Infinity, of THE Argent Loom, of Time, of Dimensions and Observable Existences and the imperceptible, alone, and survive it. And when it survives, when that single cell has borne all of existence and held... you move the weight. Off that cell. Onto the next one.\"","Noah’s eyes sharpened.","\" There are fifty trillion cells in a Provenance Lifeform,\" Thalia said quietly. \" When each one of them, individually, one after another, has borne the full weight of Existence and survived it... the first cycle is complete.\"","...!","Fifty trillion!","Fifty trillion times, the weight of all things called down onto a single point of him, borne, survived, and moved along! And she was not finished!","\" This is why so few of even our kind walk this path ,\" she continued. \" Because if you fail with even a single cell, if one bursts under the weight instead of bearing it, the cycle collapses, and you begin again. From the first cell. Every time.\" Her eyes held his, steady and unsoftened.","\" There is no partial progress. There is only a completed cycle, or a body that has to start over. And you will fail. Everyone fails, at the start. The question the art asks is not whether you can bear the weight once. It is whether you can begin again fifty trillion times without your will breaking before your body does.\"","\" Each cycle, you call down more. More weight, more of existence, pressed through more of you at once, and each cycle your existence is forged grander against it. It is not only your Provenance that swells. It is the whole of what you are, tempered by adversity.\" Her hand rose, and touched her own forearm.","\" Early on, your skin alone begins to change. Cultivate far enough, and that skin, with no Provenance spent at all, no art, no essence, nothing but what the weight has made of it... will reject the power of any Primeval One. It will turn aside the strike of a Descendant the way a wall turns rain.\"","Noah went very still at that.","\" And beyond that? \" Thalia’s voice dropped, quiet and vast. \" Cycle upon cycle upon cycle, the body climbs through tiers most never live to see. A stage where your flesh alone shrugs off authorities that flatten Provenance Lifeforms. A stage where, cultivated high enough...\" She looked at him.","\" You could stand before one of Those Who Remain, in the flesh, and feel no pressure at all. Not because you shielded yourself. Because your existence had simply been made heavy enough, and true enough, to stand in the same room as theirs and remain unbent.\"","Stand before one of Those Who Remain, and feel nothing!","The words settled into Noah with enormous weight of their own, and his eyes burned, because a path that ended there was a path worth fifty trillion failures!","| You have received the initial methodology of THE Sovereign Genesis of the Weighted Origin.|","|A cultivation art of THE First Lifeforms. You call down the weight of surrounding Existence and channel it, through the anatomy of your Provenance, onto a single cell of your body, which must bear it alone and survive. The weight is then moved to the next cell. When all cells have individually borne the full weight, one cycle completes. Cycles repeat without limit, each calling down more, each refining your existence grander and truer.|","|Per-cell reinforcement: a cell that bears the full weight and survives does not merely endure. In the moment of surviving, your existence floods that cell with Provenance, and the pressure that would have shattered it instead tempers it, the way a blade is quenched. That single cell is remade, reinforced with your own generation, refined until it can withstand the weight of Existence itself and hold. It is no longer ordinary anatomy. It has become one grain of a true Provenance Body.|","|Failure of a single cell collapses the cycle. You begin again from the first cell. There is no partial progress.|","| THE FIVE TIERS OF THE PROVENANCE BODY:|","|FIRST TIER- THE SEDIMENT-SHED SKIN: the outer body is remade. Your skin alone, with no Provenance spent, rejects the authority of Primeval Ones and Descendants, turning aside their strikes as a wall turns rain.|","|SECOND TIER- THE UNBREAKING PROVENANCE FRAME: flesh and sinew are remade. ????|","|THIRD TIER- THE WEIGHT-BEARING SOVEREIGN BONES: ??????.|","|FOURTH TIER- ???????.|","|FIFTH TIER- ?????????. You may stand in the flesh before one of Those Who Remain and feel no pressure at all...|","|Conditions to attempt met: you generate Provenance from within. You bear great weight without shattering. You are true enough that what is not you cannot overwrite you.|","|Warning: the weight you invite can flatten you out of existence.|","Noah breathed out slowly, and set his stance on the grass, and closed his eyes.","He reached out with his existence and pulsed his Provenance Essence out into the surroundings almost like a challenge.","As if he was telling existence...come at me!","The sky of the Realm darkened. The hills groaned. And the weight of Existence began to descend toward him, invisible and total!","Noah gathered all of it, and channeled it through the anatomy of his ten singularities, and aimed the entire crushing mountain of it at a single cell within his body!","A cell inside his palm.","He raised his hand and looked at his palm thst pulsed, observing that single cell as...","BOOM!","The cell burst instantly!","It did not bear the weight for even a fraction of a moment! The full force of existence landed on one point of him and that point simply ceased, and worse, it did not end there, because the sudden collapse tore into the cells around it, and a chain reaction ripped outward, a million cells bursting in a cascade before Noah could wrench the weight back up off his own body!","He staggered, and stellar crimson gold blood sprayed from his palm as a ragged wound of ruptured existence bloomed, the mountain of weight scattering back into the Realm’s air as his control shattered!","He had failed. Instantly. Completely. On the very first cell!","Noah wiped the blood and looked up.","And Thalia was watching him calmly, seated in the grass, entirely unsurprised.","\" Failure is the sudden, illuminating friction between what we imagined and what simply is.\"","She gestured at the grass before him, and settled her hand back over her wound, and there was no pity anywhere in her, only a boundless, patient certainty that reached into him like the pull of a sun.","\" Try again.\"","WAA!","But Noah did not try again. Not yet.","Istead of reaching for the weight a second time, he turned his attention inward, and examined the art itself. Piece by piece.","And as he examined it, his existence pulsed!","It rose out of his depths without his willing it, the plain Quintessential tyranny that had crowned him, the same voice that had refused a borrowed system and cast out an entire ocean of power to build his own, and it looked at THE Sovereign Genesis of the Weighted Origin, this grand and ancient technique of the First Lifeforms, and it rejected it!","Not because the art was weak. Because the art was not HIS.","\" This is a magnificent technique. Truly. But I...am not going to use it.\"","HUUM!","Thalia said nothing. She only watched him!","\"I watched why it failed. My cell burst the instant the weight touched it, and it burst because a cell is too large. \" He held up one hand, turning it slowly in the firelight.","\"A single cell is a crowded thing. It contains so much. Structures, and processes, and pieces beyond count, all bound together, all interfering, all of them a hundred different points where the weight of Existence can find a seam and tear. You asked one cell to bear everything, and the cell had too many parts to hold anything cleanly. It did not fail because I was weak. It failed because the vessel was impure.\"","His eyes lit with a cold, climbing brilliance.","\" So I will not start at the cell. I will go smaller. Far smaller. Smaller than the cell, smaller than the molecule, smaller than the atom itself!\" His voice rose, tyranny gathering under every word.","\" Because the smaller I begin, the purer the vessel is, and the purer the vessel, the more perfectly it can bear a pure and total weight! I will not ask a crowded cell to hold all of existence. I will ask a single, simple, indivisible thing to hold it!\"","He closed his hand into a fist.","\"I will start with my quarks!\"","HUUM!","\" There are two hundred Decillion quarks in my existence,\" Noah declared, and the number rolled out of him without strain, \" and every single one of them will individually bear the weight of Existence! One quark. The weight of Existence imposed on the purest and simplest vessel my body owns, borne, survived, reinforced, and moved to the next!\"","The grass caved around him. The sky darkened. And Thalia’s eyes were shining now, wide and fixed on him!","His ten singularities blazed to life on his chest, incandescent blue drowning the fire. \"This will be my technique. Not borrowed. Not inherited. Generated, from the truth of my own existence, the way everything I own must be. This will be MY first Provenance Art!\"","He threw his head back, and named it into the darkening sky of his own Realm.","\" THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis!\"","HUUM!","His Provenance Essences pulsed brilliantly, ten suns turning on his chest, and the whole Realm rang like a struck bell around the naming!","And as the art settled into his existence, it took on one more dimension that even he had not spoken aloud, because his nine Teloi answered the design on their own!","| You have designed a Provenance Art of your own: THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis.|","|It shares its root with THE Sovereign Genesis of the Weighted Origin, and diverges completely in execution. Where the Genesis conditions a Provenance Body cell by cell, your art conditions your existence from its subatomic foundation, quark by quark, across the 200 Decillion quarks that compose you. A vessel this small holds no seam for the weight to tear, and so bears a purer and more total load.|","|A further divergence, arising from your Nine Osmontian Provenance Teloi: a quark that merely survives the weight is not enough for you. In the moment a quark bears the full weight of Existence, you seat one of your Teloi within it, and the weight, the Provenance, and the aim fuse. The quark is not simply reinforced. It is REMADE into a PROVENANCE TELOS QUARK: a subatomic vessel that is stable, self-generating, and aimed, carrying a grain of Quintessence, or Existence, or Paradox, or Chaos, or Adversity, or Apocalypse, or Mana, or Harvest, or Tyranny within it.|","|A quark is only counted as borne once it has become a stable Provenance Telos Quark. Only then may the weight move to the next. An unstable quark that has taken the weight but not yet seated an aim will collapse, and its collapse fails the cycle.|","|Consequence of completion: an existence rebuilt in this way is not a body threaded with Teloi. It is a body in which every one of 200 Decillion foundational particles is itself a seated aim. Your Nine Teloi would no longer sit in nine organs. They would compose the whole of your matter, from the ground up, indivisible from what you physically are.|","| The five tiers of the Provenance Body will be reformed under your vision as you see fit.|","Noah read the technical shape of what he had made, and a slow, cold smile touched his mouth, because this was right!","Without any further word, without pause, without a breath of hesitation, he got started!","He reached out with his existence, and called the weight of all things down once more, THE Primordial Source and Infinity and THE Argent Loom and Dimensions and the imperceivable descending toward him in an invisible mountain, and this time he did not aim it at a cell!","He channeled it through the anatomy of his ten singularities, refined it, narrowed it, focused the entire crushing weight of Existence down to a single point finer than any his body had ever isolated, and he set it upon one quark!","One indivisible thing. One pure vessel. The whole weight of everything, landing on the smallest true piece of him!","And the quark trembled, and strained, and did not burst!","It did not burst!","Across the glory, Thalia Vasiliou watched him work, watched the man call down the weight of Existence and shatter a grand old art to build his own in the span of a single failure, and she raised one hand, slowly, and wiped away a tear that had gathered at the corner of her eye.","A sad tear. A relieved one. Both at once.","He truly was her Provenance. He...made the same choice even now!"]},{"number":5607,"title":"Chapter 5607: Chapter 5606: Two Halves!","paragraphs":["The first quark held, and Noah seated a Telos within it instead!","His Telos of Adversity answered first, a grain of the aim that lived in his lungs threading down into the borne quark, and the weight and the Provenance and the aim fused in one instant, and the quark stabilized and turned bright and stayed! One Provenance Telos Quark, the first grain of a body that would eventually be nothing but grains like it!","He moved the weight to the next one.","And the grandness of what followed filled the Realm from its first hill to its last!","The weight of Existence hung over him unending, an invisible mountain of THE Primordial Source and Infinity and THE Argent Loom and Time and Dimensions and Observable Existences and everything imperceivable, and Noah stood beneath it and did not sway, and quark after quark took the whole of it and held!","Bear, seat, stabilize, move! Bear, seat, stabilize, move!","The rhythm found itself and then quickened, ten quarks, a hundred, a thousand, the weight sliding through the anatomy of his ten singularities with less and less friction as his existence learned the shape of its own art!","And Thalia Vasiliou did not take her eyes off him.","She sat in the grass with her hand at her wound and she watched, and she did not blink more than she had to, because what she was watching should not have been happening!","There was supposed to be failure here! There was supposed to be a body bursting and starting over, and starting over, and starting over, and instead there was a man beneath the weight of all things transforming himself particle by particle without a single collapse!","Because Noah’s body was changing in real time.","His muscles rolled beneath his skin, sliding and pulsing as though they were being rewritten while they moved, fibers unmaking and remaking themselves denser with every thousand quarks converted! His frame drew tighter and grander, shoulders broadening under a weight that would have flattened Dimensions, his bare chest hardening as stellar blue threaded through the crimson gold of his blood beneath the surface!","His hair lifted in the pressureless air. His obsidian singularity pupils burned brighter. And all of him took on the bearing of some ancient lifeform overcoming its own limits again and again, tearing past the ceiling of what it was, then finding a new ceiling and tearing past that too, an existence in the middle of arguing with the size of itself and winning!","Ten thousand quarks!","Fifty thousand! The grass beneath him had caved into a crater and the hills groaned around the crater’s rim! Eighty thousand! His breathing had gone deep and slow and enormous, each inhale pulling the weight further into him instead of pushing it away!","One hundred thousand Provenance Telos Quarks!","And on the one hundred and first thousand... his existence ERUPTED!","BOOM!","Provenance detonated out of his depths in a flood, all ten singularities blazing at once as the accumulated generation of a hundred thousand aimed and remade particles finally crossed some threshold his existence had been climbing toward without telling him, and in the incandescent blue storm at his core...","An eleventh singularity bloomed!","...!","Eleven! He had broken past the count of ten, and the moment he did, the moment that new sun turned its first turn, something else happened, and Noah felt it arrive at the sides of his own head.","Radiant...blue wings bloomed!","They unfurled on either side of his head in brilliant light, wide and layered and beautiful, feathers of pure incandescent Provenance stretching out from his temples, and for one breath the Realm was lit by them alone!","Then the wings tranaformed!","They folded inward, drew together, condensed, and out of each of them rose a figure! Two miniature humanoids of stellar blue gold light, each hovering at either side of his head, each no larger than a forearm, and each one wearing his own face!","Two versions of Noah Osmont, floating at his temples with their eyes closed.","The one at his right sat cross-legged in the air, hands resting open on its knees, its light soft and even and warm, a stillness coming off it that felt like the doorway of his long hall and the murmur of his river and the calm of a man entirely aimed. Peace, personified. His Provenance as the thing that heals, protects, and gathers.","The one at his left stood upright with its arms folded, and its light burned dark gold at the edges, and its miniature frame carried a fiendish ancient weight that made the air around it feel narrower, a crown of shadowed brilliance turning above its head. Tyranny, personified. His Provenance as the thing that takes, breaks, and rules.","Both of them kept their eyes closed. Both of them waited.","HUUM!","|Your Provenance Essence has broken past the count of 10. PROVENANCE: 11.|","|A threshold has been crossed. The generation of 100,000 Provenance Telos Quarks and 11th Provenance Essence has produced what your art was designed to produce: an existence that no longer merely holds Provenance, but personifies it.|","|A UNIQUE PRECEPT has been written: THE PRECEPT OF THE SUNDERED PROVENANCE.|","|Your Provenance now expresses itself as two manifestations of yourself, seated at either side of your head: THE PROVENANCE OF THE OPEN HAND and THE PROVENANCE OF THE CLOSED CROWN.|","|THE PROVENANCE OF THE OPEN HAND: the peaceful half of your generation, personified. It heals, shelters, gathers, and mends, and it will pursue your Provenance through kindness by whatever means it judges best.|","|THE PROVENANCE OF THE CLOSED CROWN: the tyrannical half of your generation, personified. It breaks, claims, rules, and ends, and it will pursue your Provenance through dominion by whatever means it judges best.|","|You may select one to act. The selected manifestation carries out your Provenance however IT chooses, requiring nothing further from you: you may sit back entirely. Whichever one acts expresses power at twice your own current strength.|","|Only one may be awake at a time. What one begins, the other cannot undo.|","|Your cultivation has borne further fruit. VERITAS: 14. PONDUS: 16. Your existence has been refined by the imposed adversity of all things.|","|100,000 of 200 Decillion quarks converted. Cycle 1 continues.|","...!","Noah opened his eyes and looked at his own immensity.","At the eleven suns turning in his depths. At the two small versions of himself floating at his temples with their eyes shut, one open-handed and still, one crowned and folded, both of them him, both of them waiting to be chosen. At his own hands, which had been rebuilt one hundred thousand particles’ worth while he stood in one place, and which now held a weight of presence that made the very grass lean away from them.","Twice his current strength. From a thing that acted on its own judgment while he sat back and watched.","He had wondered, once, what an Art built on Provenance Essence itself rather than through his blood would give him. Now he knew!","And ahead of him, Thalia Vasiliou nodded slowly.","She had watched every moment of it without once looking away.","\" You should be good, for now.\" Her hand pressed lightly at her healing chest as she rose to her feet. \" But the others are not.\"","Noah’s gaze sharpened.","\" Can we... \" And for the first time since she had come out of the white pool, her composure thinned, and what came through the gap was not a Provenance Lifeform of constellations and immensity, but something much smaller and much older in its want.","\" Can we go see Mother?\"","...!"]},{"number":5608,"title":"Chapter 5608: Chapter 5607: Your Most Favorite!","paragraphs":["Mother!","Noah looked at this unique lifeform before him, and wondered just what her future with him had actually been. Mother. Not \"your mother.\" Mother, the way a person says it about their own.","He felt the Provenance and the power rolling through his existence, eleven suns turning in his depths, and he nodded and turned to lead the way...","And Thalia hummed, and started walking.","She crossed the grass of his Realm without waiting for him, unhurried, her bare feet finding the path between the standing stones as though she had walked it ten thousand times, and she angled toward the distant doorway with the ease of a woman going home!","Noah followed.","\" Causes ,\" she said as she walked. \" That is where we start. Causes are one of the surest protections in all of existence, because they do not require the protected to do anything at all. A being backed by Causes is simply harder to touch. The Causes stand under their existence, and anything reaching for them has to reach through those first.\"","\" Yours are not Causes anymore. What you have covers you well enough, and they extend to Mother to a degree, because she is the Originator.\" She stepped over the river of light without looking down.","\" But the others? Barely at all. Your daughter, your son, your people, the ones who eat at your table and sleep inside your home. If something reached for them tomorrow, most of them would have nothing beneath their existence but your reputation.\"","Noah’s eyes pulsed as he asked grandly...","\"Is there anything more you can reveal so I have a better picture?\"","\"Its all because of him.\" Her voice cooled. \" What I can say without paying too dearly is that something happened to the mind of THE Sealed One. Before he attained IT, his mind had seemingly... shattered. \"","\" He now moves with different motivations depending on the vessel he is wearing. One will be reasonable. One will collect. One will burn a Dimension for the pleasure. Too many things about him are unknown, even to me, but two are certain. His main vessel is vindictive. And he is tying up loose ends.\" She glanced back over her shoulder. \" You are an unfathomably big loose end.\"","Noah walked behind her figure as she moved through his own home like she owned a key to it, and he watched her dazzling red hair catch the last of the evening light, and the grace of how she moved and talked, that composure that never once slipped even while she bled...","And at this time, a voice spoke up in a heavy, cool tone.","\" We got a baddie right beside us who obviously has history, and why ain’t we made a move yet? Just tap me in and let me do what needs to be done.\"","...!","Noah blinked!","The voice had come from the left side of his head, and it was HIS OWN voice, deeper and colder and entirely unbothered, and THE Provenance of the Closed Crown had actually spoken, arms still folded, crown of shadowed brilliance still turning, its grand eyes still closed!","And not a moment later, another voice echoed out from his right.","\" All things happen in due time. She is obviously traumatized by whatever happened, and we are different from the man she later knows. Give her time. Let her acclimate.\"","THE Provenance of the Open Hand, cross-legged and calm, hands open on its knees, eyes closed as well.","Noah felt like he was going insane, and yet not, because this was not madness. This was simply listening to his own thoughts the way he always had, except now they were sorted, separated, defined out to their absolute extremes, and spoken aloud, loud and clear, by two halves of himself that no longer bothered to compromise before reaching him!","\" Every time she looks at us,\" THE Closed Crown said, \" her entire existence exudes how much she wants to come close to us. Our future self already did all the work. All that is left is for us not to drop the ball, and you want to kick the ball away?\" A pause. \" We can also use this as a chance to understand the anatomy of a genuine Provenance Lifeform.\"","\" Our anatomy is what matters most, \" THE Open Hand answered calmly. \" Do not rush a process. And think about her.\"","...!","His thoughts buzzed in his mind, and he was so focused on the argument happening at both sides of his own head that he did not notice they had left his Provenance Realm entirely!","The doorway had passed behind them, and the endless blue of THE Infiniverse had opened and closed, and now he was floating in the skies above a realm of harvests and abundance, golden fields rolling out beneath him under a warm sun, orchards heavy, rivers bright.","His mother’s realm.","Thalia turned back in the air to look at him, and her eyes went to the two small figures floating at either side of his head, and a mischievous, knowing smile spread across her face.","\" Are you hearing voices in your head, my Provenance?\" Her smile deepened. \" You should listen to your tyrannical side more.\"","BOOM!","And she took one step and vanished toward the lands below, leaving Noah floating there astonished, as the voice of THE Closed Crown boomed out angrily beside his ear.","\"I fucking told you.\"","\"...\"","With no words at all, Noah went down as well!","Below, on a vibrant cliff overlooking a radiant river, Amelia Osmont sat fishing with Seo-yeon.","Two rods leaned out over the water, catching light. A small basket sat between them. Seo-yeon’s legs swung off the cliff edge as she watched her line with fierce concentration, and Amelia sat beside her with the deep unhurried ease of a woman who had earned every quiet hour she would ever get.","Thalia appeared behind them. Noah touched down a second later.","Both heads turned, and Seo-yeon brightened up, dropped her rod entirely, and smashed into Noah’s chest with a hug!","\" Aba, you have changed again!\"","\"I have ,\" Noah said, smiling as he patted her head.","Amelia turned with a smile of her own, and then her gaze moved past him, and found the red-haired woman standing on the grass in a white-blue robe stained with dried crimson gold.","\"... Who is this?\"","And Thalia walked forward with her eyes full of respect and adoration, and bowed to Amelia Osmont.","\" Hello again, Ama .\" She straightened, composed as ever. \" I am Thalia Vasiliou. Your most favorite daughter in law.\"","...!"]},{"number":5609,"title":"Chapter 5609: Chapter 5608: Tesseracts! I","paragraphs":["Silence fell over the cliff!","Seo-yeon’s mouth opened. And Amelia turned her head slowly toward her son, looked at him for a long moment, then shook her head with the exasperation of a mother who had given up on receiving news in a timely fashion, walked forward, and raised Thalia’s bowed head with both hands and a smile.","\" How did he hide you for so long without me knowing?\" She kept hold of her. \" Come on. Let us get to know each other.\"","\"Mm!\"","Thalia smiled brightly and nodded.","\"I know you like fishing ,\" she said as they walked. \"I have a technique that lets you fish across Dimensions, from your own home. The things you can catch...\"","And she began talking to his mother so naturally, so easily, that both Noah and Seo-yeon stood there astonished, watching the two of them stroll off along the cliff together like they had been doing it for years.","And as they walked, Thalia’s voice arrived quietly in his mind.","’I will relax by Mother’s side for now. See if you can get started on expanding the backing of Causes on those closest to you. Existence is vast and full of terrors, and dangers are going to come at you and yours from all sides. You may be invulnerable... but your enemies will look for the easiest way to hurt you, and that way runs through the Provenance of those around you. And THE Sealed One is not your only enemy. To get me, you offended a great many Provenance Lifeforms. And another one of Those Who Remain.’","...!","Such crazy words dropped on him, and Noah shook his head slowly while Seo-yeon leaned up and whispered against his chest.","\"Aba. She is very pretty. I approve!\"","Noah sighed.","\"I approve as well.\"","He definitely approved. Everything this woman did and said was magnetizing to his very existence! But there were much more important matters right now, and his mind had already gone to them.","He knew the threads of existence connected to him. A few dozen beings within THE Infiniverse whose threads ran thick and bright, and many more whose connections were thinner but present all the same. To protect them all through Causes was hard, and it was also simple. Even Those Who Remain worked this way. Even THE Sleepless Fiend played with Causes inside the bodies of Steeds!","And for him to back somewhat weak lifeforms with Causes, the easiest way was something he had already done three times, for Seo-yeon, for Henry, and for his mother.","When he had made them backers of their own emerging Observable Existences.","THE Genesis Tesseract!","The thing he had gained from THE Tide That Owes Nothing, in return for reaching into a drowned existence and giving it another chance.","And THE Tide had been preserving the generation of boons for everything he had done and never claimed, for a while now, growing past all precedent while he told it to continue and walked away!","It seemed that now was the time to take all of it. Every generated boon, in the form he needed most.","Genesis Tesseracts.","It would mean the birth of many, many Observable Existences with many different founders, nested inside THE Infiniverse, and that would elevate HER as well, her Dimensionality, her Causes, the whole architecture of what she was, guaranteeing a web of Causes standing beneath everyone he loved!","Noah stretched his neck, and looked up at the warm golden sky of his mother’s realm.","\" Infiniverse. It’s time to unleash all that has been generated within THE Tide That Owes Nothing.\"","...!","From the surroundings, a grand affirmation came!","| Understood.|","The sky above his mother’s realm changed.","It began with a single point of light kindling high in the warm gold, and then another beside it, and then a hundred, and then the whole vault of the heavens was catching fire in quiet increments as the preserved generation of THE Tide That Owes Nothing came due all at once!","They bloomed into being like stars arriving early.","Every one of them a hypercube of deep blue-white, a cube nested inside a cube and joined across an axis the eye kept sliding off, edges burning with a light that had no business being that clean, and each one turned slowly in place, unfolding and refolding through a dimension that the sky of an Observable Existence simply had to make room for!","They littered the heavens from horizon to horizon, uncountable at a glance, a canopy of geometry hanging over golden fields and a radiant river, and the fields below lit up blue as their light came down through the orchards!","Seo-yeon’s eyes opened wide.","Far along the cliff, Amelia had stopped walking and beside her, Thalia Vasiliou looked up at a sky full of folded beginnings with an expression Noah could not read from where he stood.","HUUM!","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has released everything it preserved for the first experiment of a Generation of a select prior reward. It bodes well for targeting the Laestrygonians as further rewards.|","|Ledger settled. Boons generated and held in trust for: leadership given to a domain. Protection given to millions. Marks given to the marked. Affirmation given to the grieving. Salvation given to the dying. A lineage given back to its bearer. A Sovereign given to existence. Death granted to a unique lifeform. Every act of giving you performed and never claimed a return for.|","|The Tide has answered in the form its ledger judged most fitting to what you gave.|","| Yield: 1,800 GENESIS TESSERACTS.|","|Each holds the Infinite Source Potential of a First Cause, and the latent template of all nine Prime Causes folded within. Each is the graspable seed of an entire Observable Existence, awaiting a founder honest enough to tell it what is true.|","|This is the largest single return in your records.|","...!","Eighteen hundred!","Noah looked up at a sky he had accidentally filled. Eighteen hundred foundations, eighteen hundred nine-Cause structures, eighteen hundred sets of roots that could be planted beneath the existences of everyone who mattered to him!","It was a ridiculous number.","He raised his hands.","And he called them down.","WAA!"]},{"number":5610,"title":"Chapter 5610: Chapter 5609: Tesseracts! II","paragraphs":["The heavens answered as eighteen hundred Tesseracts fell out of the gold at once, streaming down in long blue-white lines toward the cliff, and they did not scatter or crash, they came to him, gathering into a vast slow orbit around his body, hundreds upon hundreds of folded hypercubes turning through the air in nested rings, their light washing the cliff and the river and the orchards in deep cerulean, and the whole realm hummed with the pressure of that much beginning held in one place!","Noah stood in the middle of his own storm of seeds, and turned to his daughter.","\" Seo-yeon.\"","She looked up at him with wide shining eyes, and he reached into the orbit and drew out nine.","They drifted across to her, one after another, settling into a small ring around her, and their light lit her face blue as she stared at them.","\" Nine ,\" Noah said. \" THE Mirrored Hearth was your first, now design nine more.\" He crouched to her level, the way he always did. \" Whatever you want them to be. Reach for what you are, and let them take their shape from that. And when they are grown, ten Observable Existences will stand under your existence, and anything that ever reaches for you will have to reach through all ten first.\"","Seo-yeon’s small hands closed around the nearest hypercube with trembling hands!","And she nodded so hard her hair bounced!","Then Noah rose, and looked out over the turning orbit of everything else he held, and began sorting it in his mind.","Henry would receive multiple. Adelaide. Barbatos. Kazuhiko. Khor. Sigrid. Titano and the Emperor Penguin and Erikson and Lich Ra’Zan, Amser Modred, Malphas the butler who had been bowed to by a being that once mistreated him, Emotive, the nine Daughters of THE Dora Shath’yar, Naldine, even the arrogant goat Heidrun who would probably found something insufferable and beautiful!","Every single one of them, given not one seed but several, so that each existence at his table would stand on the backing of the Causes of MULTIPLE Observable Existences!","And after them, the ones whose threads ran thinner but ran all the same would receive something.","Not everyone could be what he was. That was simply true. Provenance was not transferable, and no gift he could make would let another being generate the way he generated!","But that had never been the only road to grandness!","Existence had frameworks, ancient and established and full of ladders, and he had spent his whole climb learning exactly how those ladders worked. Causes. Foundations. Observable Existences. Intents and Scales and Sources. The whole architecture that beings like THE Sleepless Fiend used to make Steeds carry Causes and Descendants carry sentences, the architecture that Vakochev had built a ladder out of and named after himself!","Noah could not make his people First Lifeforms.","But with eighteen hundred Genesis Tesseracts turning around him, he could make them unfathomably grand inside every framework that existence had ever offered, until each one of them stood on so many foundations that reaching them meant unmaking a dozen Observable Existences first!","And every single one of those Observable Existences would be born nested inside THE Infiniverse.","Which meant she would grow too.","His eyes lifted, and he got to work!","---","<THE Sealed One>","Far too many days had passed since a new Sword had stood in THE Hall of Swords.","The Hall did not stand anymore.","Its vaulted ceiling was gone, torn open to the raw dark of a separate Dimension of Existence that no longer had walls to separate it from anything. The ancient stone lay in continents of rubble. Out beyond where the Hall had ended, the fold of reality itself had been decimated for a distance no measure in the Source Lands bothered to keep, whole stretches of the Dimension hanging in unlit ruin, the light that had come from no visible source snuffed out entirely.","And THE Throne of Swords was broken.","The great obsidian structure of countless blades lay split down its center, and hundreds of the swords woven into it were shattered, each broken blade meaning a Source Armament somewhere across existence had just stopped being whole.","Before the ruin of that throne, THE Queen Regnant knelt.","Her hundreds of glistening tentacles were spread flat against the shattered stone, her gaunt elongated arms braced, her writhing head bowed so low that the pale suctioned tendrils around her clattering aperture brushed the ground.","Grey and obsidian flesh wept slime and something darker. The Primordial Source and Infinity running side by side through her existence still ran, still nearly touching union, and both of them guttered.","And she was not willing.","Every wet twitch of her said it. The tendrils along her torso strained upward against the posture, over and over, and were pressed back down. Her claws had gouged trenches into the stone beneath them from the effort of holding still. The kneel had been imposed on her body, and her existence had not agreed to it, and it went on refusing in small useless increments with every breath she did not have!","Behind her, in rows that stretched back through the rubble, the Swords of Existence knelt too. Mesozoic Scale beings and more... all of them down, all of them shroudless, most of them bleeding.","And walking through the ruin of it, unhurried, was a tall pale man in layered dark robes.","THE Sealed One looked around the wreckage with mild interest, and when he spoke, his voice carried easily through a Dimension too broken to echo.","\" You know, I do not truly wish to destroy.\"","He stopped beside a fallen column and rested a hand on it.","\" Destruction is expensive. It is loud, it is imprecise, and it leaves nothing behind that can be used.\" He looked up at the missing ceiling. \"I did not want this. This was the cost of a hall that would not open its doors.\"","\"... Then unbend my spine ,\" THE Queen Regnant said, \" and we will discuss doors, O Infinite Liar.\"","Her voice came out of the bowed writhing mass, and even flattened, even wrecked, it was sweet. Calm and sweet, almost gentle!","\" There she is.\" THE Sealed One smiled slightly. \"I was hoping the pressure had not taken the voice. Your voice is the finest thing in this hall. Was, I suppose.\"","\"I am making an offer right now .\" He resumed walking, threading between kneeling rows. \"I seek to rule. That is all. Not to end. You, the Swords, the True Lifeforms, the Primeval Ones who graze across THE Source Lands and think their earliness makes them permanent, all of it will soon fall to me. And the falling is not the point. What comes after is the point.\"","\" After?\" Her teeth clattered. \" You ground an Age of your own children into three pills and ate one where everyone could watch. What exactly do you imagine comes after, for the rest of us?\"","He crouched, comfortable amid the rubble and smiled.","\" Do you know how many exceptional lifeforms existence produces in an Age? Thousands. Do you know how many of them ever amount to anything, left to their own devices? A handful. The rest bloat, and squabble, and are eventually eaten by something with a better appetite, and every ounce of what they were goes into a mouth that does nothing with it.\"","His voice stayed perfectly reasonable.","\"I took an Age of waste and I concentrated it. Their potential exists TODAY, doing something, instead of having been spent on nothing across ten thousand pointless little conflicts. Nothing was destroyed. Things were merely... reassigned.\"","\" My disciples...my Followers...Do you imagine I felt nothing? I remember all of their names. Every one. I keep them, which is more than existence ever offered them. Existence would have forgotten them entirely. I am the only reason a single one of those disciples still exists in any form at all.\" He tilted his head. \" A farmer does not hate his pigs when the winter comes. But he does remember which ones fed him.\"","Her tendrils strained upward again, and were pressed down again.","\" That is the part none of you ever understand, \" THE Sealed One continued, rising, brushing dust from his robes. \" You think I am hungry. Hunger is what I use, it is not what I am for. Look at what existence IS. Chaos. Dimensions folding into other Dimensions and drowning everything inside them while nobody is even accountable for the folding. Millions of petty sovereignties, each one certain it is the center, all of them grinding against each other forever, and the total sum of all that motion across all those Ages is... nothing. No direction. No decision. No one accountable.\"","HUUM!","His voice sharpened, and for one moment something almost passionate showed through the collector’s calm. \"I do not want to eat existence, Your Little Majesty. I want to FINISH it. I want one hand on it, and one accounting, and an end to the endless committee of the useless mighty. And I am the only being who has been at this long enough to do it. Fuck Those Who Remain as they won’t do it, so I will do it on their behalf.\"","THE Queen Regnant was silent for a long moment.","\" And your followers? \" she said at last. \"In this finished existence of yours. Do they get names, or do they get shells?\"","\" They get to be part of something that arrived somewhere.\" He said it gently.","He walked past her, toward the split obsidian throne, and stopped in front of the broken blades of every Sword in existence.","\"I will not rush this. I never rush .\" His pale hand traced the shattered edge. \" There is a being out there, a new thing that you have met before, a genuine anomaly, and he cannot be handled the way anything else is handled. Strike him unprepared and you do not wound him, you feed him. Every adversity he survives makes him grander. So I do not offer him adversity. I offer him nothing at all, and I gather, and I map, and I wait, and when I finally move it will not be a contest he can survive and grow from. It will be a collection.\" He glanced back over his shoulder.","\" Do you see the discipline in that? I have watched a thousand mighty things die of impatience. I intend to die of nothing.\"","\" You may consider yourself a preparation. It is not an insult. Everything is a preparation.\"","He turned fully then, and looked out over the rows of the kneeling, and the mildness in him thinned into something very old.","\" One last thing, and then I will leave you to your rubble and your thinking.\"","The ruined Dimension held still.","\" Lately, I have begun hearing whispers .\" His borrowed eyes lifted, past the missing ceiling, into the unlit dark. \" From myself. From a version of me that is not here, and has not happened yet, speaking backward into the ear of the one who is.\"","He listened for a moment, and the smile that came over his face was almost reverent. \"I do not yet know all of what he says. But I know the shape of it. And whatever is coming...\"","HUUM!","\"...it seems to be GRAND.\""]},{"number":5611,"title":"Chapter 5611: Chapter 5610: Which One Am I?","paragraphs":["<THE Sealed One>","Far from THE Source Lands.","Deep in THE Infinite Carcosa, in the drifting Dimension called THE Hollow Argosy, an army stood waiting.","Millions of them!","Rank upon rank of Infinite True Lifeforms filled the middle distance, their silent seas running silver through their frames, escalation stacked upon escalation until the air of the Dimension rang with compounding weight.","Beside them and above them stood the Gilded Ones in their brilliance, amplified Egos burning gold and white across the ranks, an ocean of exposed glory that lit the underside of the Dimension’s broken sky.","Millions of the mighty, holding formation in silence, waiting on one man at the forefront.","And at the forefront stood a vessel of THE Sealed One.","This one wore a tall frame in dark imperial layers, hands clasped behind its back, and it looked out over the assembled millions with the easy pleasure of an owner walking his own fields.","Beside him stood a Primeval Lifeform.","The old thing was pale as cooled glass, tall and thin and hairless, its flesh carrying the faint grain of stone that had been polished across ages by nothing but time. Its eyes did not blink and did not warm. It had watched the gathering of this army the way it watched everything, from a great distance that had nothing to do with the space between them, and every line of it made plain that it found the being beside it distasteful.","And it obeyed anyway.","\" What are your plans ?\" the Primeval said.","The vessel smiled. \" The plan is rulership. All of these forces, spread across the Carcosa, taking region after region under one accounting. Not slaughter. Subjugation. A thing that has been subjugated still works.\"","\"Rulership for its own sake.\"","\" No. Never for its own sake. \" The vessel turned his head. \" What I am seeking cannot be grasped by any being that only wields power. It can only be grasped by one who holds rulership over a large portion of Existence, and who carries a tremendously high Dimensionality. And those two things go hand in hand most of the time. Rule enough of existence and your Dimensionality rises to meet what you rule. Raise your Dimensionality and you begin to perceive what is worth ruling.\"","He gestured out over the silver and gold ranks. \" So I gather. And with every region that answers to me, I climb, and the thing I am reaching for comes a little further into view.\"","He clasped his hands. \" Now. Your assignments...\"","The Primeval waited.","\" THE Pale Meridian first. The old spine of roads through the Carcosa, where every crossing eventually touches. Take it under my name.\"","\"Then THE Nine Silent Markets. True Lifeforms have bartered there since before many had names.. .\"","The vessel continued smoothly to list names of various places within THE Infinite Carcosa!","\" After the Markets, THE Ossuary Terraces. Stacked bones of dead Observable Existences, gigaparsecs of them, and every scavenger in the Carcosa keeps a house on those terraces. Clear them, and hold them, subjugate all of them .\"","\"...\"","The Primeval regarded him with its unblinking, unwarming stare as if he wanted to ask...was that fucking all? Because that was a lot!","But in the end...","\" As you command\"","\"Mm. As I command.\" The vessel’s smile widened, and he changed subjects entirely with the ease of a man turning a page. \" Do you know what I like about this particular body I am wearing?\"","The Primeval said nothing.","\" This one is unique among all my vessels. It is the only one I did not take.\" The vessel raised his own hand and studied it, turning it in the light of a million Gilded auras.","\" This one came for ME. It was ambitious enough, and frankly stupid enough, to attempt to assimilate something as True as I am, carrying a Dimensionality it could not have measured on its best day. That should have ended the way such things always end. Something small opens its mouth around something enormous and discovers what enormous means.\"","He flexed the borrowed fingers.","\" And yet, somehow... he actually succeeded.\"","...!","\" Not completely and definitely not cleanly. But he got his teeth into the thing he bit, and it held, and what stood up afterward was not him and was not entirely me either.\" The vessel sounded genuinely delighted.","\" This portion of myself is half me, and half this vessel. Neither party filed a complaint, because by the time either of us could have, there was no longer a clean seam to complain across.\" He looked out over the waiting army with something almost like affection.","\" Existence is so unique. All the Mutants. All the Anomalies. You spend eons believing you have catalogued every way a thing can go wrong, and then some ambitious creature swallows a piece of you and comes out the other side as a co-author.\"","\"Ah, I just find it interesting, and I do not find much interesting anymore.\" The vessel waved a hand at the ranks. \" Go. THE Pale Meridian in a few days.\"","The Primeval turned without a word, and the silver and gold sea parted around it as it walked into the army, and the ranks began to move behind it, millions of the mighty flowing out of THE Hollow Argosy toward the roads of the Carcosa.","And the vessel of THE Sealed One stood alone at the forefront, and hummed.","It was a small hum, and an old one, and it did not belong to THE Sealed One at all. It belonged to whoever this body had been, and the vessel let it come out anyway, and then it stopped humming and smiled at nothing.","\" Adrastia ,\" he said. \" Emperor King. Sealed One.\"","He tilted his head.","\" Which one am I, in this vessel?\"","The ranks flowed past. The broken sky held its light.","\" Due to the fact that I cannot even imagine harming little Rose, or a single one of those inside your Inner Dimension...\" He laughed softly, and the laugh had two textures in it, one patient and ancient, and one that was simply a young man’s. \" Am I you? Or are you me?\"","\"Hmm!\""]},{"number":5612,"title":"Chapter 5612: Chapter 5611: Chain Them! I","paragraphs":["<Axon>","Gigaparsecs from THE Ymnaros, inside a pocket of dimension that had been folded out of the dark and would be folded back into it within the hour, two collared servants of an unnamed order made their report.","The pocket held nothing! No stone, no floor, no light of its own. Only white rivers of THE Argent Loom threading slowly through the fold, and standing among them, an illusory figure of Warden Yrsa, plain garments, dark hair bound back, pale eyes, and no authority radiating off her even in projection.","Axon stood before her as his halos of white light turned slowly, shoulder to heel. Ohmran stood behind him, vast and clay-skinned and silent, the pale gray band catching the loomlight at his throat.","\" Report.\"","\"THE Ymnaros has completed its Dimensionlapse,\" Axon said. \" Another Dimension folded into it fully. We observed for a few hours after the fold settled.\"","\"And?\"","\"Well, it has been taken over, Warden.\" Axon’s gaze stayed level. \" The whole fused Dimension answers to a single figure. They call him the Blood-Crowned One.\"","\" The dominant lifeforms of the largest domain are unique ones. The Superpowered Lifeforms...\" Axon’s halos brightened faintly as he came to it. \" They hold no traditional authority. No Intent. No Source. No Infinity. Nothing our instruments read as authority at all. Their power appears to derive from their own physical existences as they exert weight and they endure weight and they do it with nothing under them but themselves.\"","\"Really now? Okay.\" Yrsa turned back. \" What about the figures around this Blood-Crowned One?\"","\" We listened to the most powerful of them speak among themselves, which is where the useful informstion was. \" Axon inclined his head.","\" There is a dragon. White beneath, crimson within, red gold wings. They call her Hvitrmarr. There is a being with a blindfold of crimson gold hands over a single great eye, Damodred. There is a scholar who emanates absolutely nothing and around whom Intent visibly splits. There are others below them.\"","Axon’s voice sharpened with the pleasure of a clean finding.","\" Every one of the key figures is surrounded by a unique authority. The same authority. It is not their own. It is The Blood-Crowned One’s, wrapped around them, seated in them, and it is unlike anything we have catalogued.\"","\"Hmm.\" Yrsa’s projection folded its hands. \" What else?\"","\"There is a being standing guard outside the Dimension entirely, in the crossing-dark, and he is not one of theirs by lineage.\" Axon’s halos slowed. \" He should be... a Descendant.\"","BOOM!","Silence filled the pocket!","\"... You are certain?\"","\"His existence is written as it gives off that same sensation. One unbroken line running backward out of him past the horizon of what I can read. There is no mistaking it, and there is more.\" Axon lifted his chin. \" He has what looks to be... a Mount with him. A Steed.\"","Ohmran’s slow eyes shifted at that.","\"I know many variations of Descendants, \" Axon continued. \" Across the Dimensions we have visited. Lineages that hold thrones. Lineages that hold silence. But those known to travel with Mounts, with Steeds...Are they not the Cursed Descendants of THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension?\"","\" They... should be...\"","Even Yrsa seemed surprised to confirm this!","\" Then a Cursed Descendant of THE Krazhor-Nul is standing guard outside THE Ymnaros. And Warden, he is very much not looking cursed! There is no rot on him. Nothing failing anywhere in that existence. His Steed either! Both of them are whole!\"","\"...\"","\" And both of them emanate the aura of the Blood-Crowned One.\"","HUUM!","\" We watched manifestations of that same figure hold the sky over the largest domain for a little while observing the Dimensionlapse ,\" Axon said, \" and then vanish some hours ago. Whatever moved them, moved them together. And this Descendant and his Steed carry that same crimson gold signature threaded through their existences.\" His halos turned.","\" This should be the being THE Sealed One had trouble with. The Remnant Existential Treasure should be on him or near him, and everything the vessel told you about a young lifeform growing into power was true and also badly incomplete.\"","\" Because a young lifeform growing into power does not have a Cursed Descendant standing in his doorway!\"","Axon’s composure finally showed a crack, and what came through it was... appetite!","\" What cured that Descendant? How? Under what authority? By whose permission? And if it was done without permission...\"","He stopped there, because there was nowhere polite to take it.","Yrsa’s projection said nothing for a long moment.","Then she spoke, and her voice was exactly as calm as it had been when she broke a hand.","\" This Dimension is now of the highest importance.\"","Axon straightened as her pale eyes moved between them.","\" Descendants have been off limits. We had been waiting on instructions, and the instructions have not come.\"","\"But Warden...\"","\"I am clearing it as of now.\"","...!","\" We move on THE Ymnaros. I will seek clearance, but I now have enough basis.\" Yrsa did not pause. \" We will use the Inhibitors in one sweeping action: the Descendant first, and every important and most powerful figure in that Dimension simultaneously. The dragon, the blindfolded one, the scholar who emanates nothing, all of them, in the same breath. Nothing sequential. Sequential gives the mighty time.\"","\"And the Superpowered Lifeforms?\"","\"A lifeform to study.\" Something almost like interest touched her voice. \" We do not know whether our Inhibitors work on them. That question needs answering. Collar what you can reach among them and record everything.\"","\" Understood.\"","\"I will arrive myself. I will lead this incursion, and I will bring others.\" Her projection’s hands unfolded. \"I will handle the shackling of the Descendant personally. The rest of you move in one sweep on the others. And to ensure success...\"","She said it grandly!","\"I will requisition a Dimensional Inhibitor.\"","...!","A Dimensional Inhibitor!","Axon’s halos flared bright before he could govern them, and even Ohmran’s slow head turned!","Because that was one of their foremost weapons! A device that made authority obsolete across a region of an entire Dimension, everything within it stripped and inert at once, no exceptions, no negotiation, no ladder that held! Barely less than a second of effect, and then nothing for a long while after!","But in that second, everything mighty inside the region was simply a body!","They had taken down Primeval Ones this way. They had taken down True Lifeforms, in a single second, in one sweep, before any of them understood the shape of what had happened to them!","The last of her flickered in the loomlight.","\" Hold your positions and observe. Touch nothing.\"","\"...\"","\"I will arrive soon,\" Warden Yrsa said. \" Then we will actually get started.\""]},{"number":5613,"title":"Chapter 5613: Chapter 5612: Chain Them! II","paragraphs":["<Warden Yrsa>","Warden Yrsa came into the crossing-dark outside THE Ymnaros.","The white rivers opened behind her, and her forces came through.","They came in silence as dozens of them poured out of the loomlight, and every one of them was shrouded head to toe in white cloth that left nothing of a face or a frame to read, their wrappings drawn tight and bound at the wrists and the throat, and around each shrouded figure, rivers of THE Argent Loom turned slowly in orbit!","Not one of them emanated a thread of authority as they fanned out toward the fused Dimension! Not an Intent among them. Not an ounce of Source, not a breath of Infinity, and their presense registered nowhere at all as they went!","Yrsa watched them deploy.","A single one of them was equivalent to a weak Primeval Lifeform.","One shrouded servant, wrapped and bound and silent, carried enough refined force to end the kind of ancient thing that entire Dimensions built religions around, and she had brought dozens of them, and they moved in units and obeyed without a sound! Existence outside these folds had no records of them, and existence would learn of them one incursion at a time!","And her own power exceeded any common Primeval One.","She did not dwell on it. She had stood before Primeval Lifeforms fat with Ages, things that had grazed on Dimensions since before the frameworks were named, and she had walked out of those meetings and they had not.","Below and ahead, THE Ymnaros went about its afternoon! Countless lifeforms moving through Observable Existences and a fused Dimension, and above them, the guardians of this Dimension stood at their posts and felt nothing coming!","Yrsa looked at all of it, and she thought about the weavings of the unworthy.","Authority was not evil. Authority was a hammer that existence handed out at random to whoever climbed the right ladder fast enough, and the trouble was never the hammer!","The trouble was that existence handed it to ANYONE, and then walked away, and never once came back to check what was being built with it! THE Sealed One had been handed a hammer and had ground an entire Age of his own children, and he was not the exception, he was simply the example everyone remembered. There were many like him.","Not one of them had been worthy of what they held.","\" Positions ,\" Yrsa said.","The shrouded ones reported across the loomlight in a flat overlapping chorus.","|The dragon.|","|The blindfolded one.|","|The scholar.|","|The strongest of the ones with no authority.|","|The pledged beneath them.|","\" The Descendant outside is mine ,\" she said. \" Nobody touches him but me. Chains ready. Cages ready. Nothing sequential.\"","|Understood.|","She raised her hand, and the thing in it was a plain gray cylinder without a single mark on it, and thread-fine lines of white ran through its surface the way they ran through every collar her order had ever closed.","A Dimensional Inhibitor.","One second. Barely less. And then nothing from it for a long while after, because there were not many of these in all of existence and each one was worth more than a thousand Primeval Ones!","\" Sweep ,\" said Warden Yrsa.","And she broke the cylinder.","HUUM!","A silent light wept across everything like the cry of existence itself being disallowed to express itself!","And...","Authority died across THE Ymnaros!","It went out everywhere at once, a single silent second in which every ladder in the Dimension simply stopped existing, and nothing struck anyone, and nothing burned, and nothing was even touched! Things were simply subtracted! Intents guttered as Pantheons of Infinite Lifeforms folded, and the crimson gold weavings threaded through the key figures of this domain went dark from the sky down to the soil!","And her forces MOVED!","—","Hvitrmarr was flying the northern side of the fused Dimension filled with Infinite Lifeforms, enjoying her freedom, when the sky went quiet.","The White Steed, THE Blood Duke, vampiric crimson beneath white with her red gold wings spread across gigaparsecs of new territory, felt her nine transforming organs stop answering her instsntly!","Every single one of them went silent inside her body as her wings kept beating out of nothing but muscle and habit!","She fell.","A being who had carried burdens across three thousand years of chains dropped out of the northern sky and struck the ground hard enough to crack it for miles, and she smashed into shocked clusters of Infinite Lifeforms that were turned to pulp by her weight alone as none had any authority at this point!","Four shrouded figures came down on top of her.","They climbed her. White wrappings moved up her flanks and across her spine as the Loom-rivers around them bent down and pinned her wings flat to the stone, and when her wings strained against the pinning, the shrouded ones simply pressed harder, folding the great red gold spans backward at angles wings were never made to hold, and Hvitrmarr screamed in pain!","One of them walked the length of her neck with a gray band held open in both hands. She thrashed. She tore gorges through the ground with claws that were only claws now, and another shrouded one stepped onto the side of her head and stood there, its full Primeval-grade weight pressing her jaw into the broken stone, holding her skull utterly still no matter how she heaved beneath it, and the band closed anyway!","CLICK!","And then the chains came.","Loomlight poured off the shrouded ones in ropes as they wound them around her legs and her wings and her jaws, hardening as they wrapped, and they wound her jaws shut, muzzling an ancient queen mid-scream, and her voice broke off into a strangled sound through bound teeth, and her ancient existence read to every sense in existence as... a very large animal being tied down by farmhands!","\"... Mmh! MMMH!\"","She was still trying to say something through the muzzle.","Not again. Not again!","She did not want to be chained again!","They dragged her- two shrouded ones took the chains at her legs and hauled her across the ground on her side, her white flank grinding through the gorges her own claws had torn, and above the northern sky, something began to appear!","It came out of nothing in a grinding of dull gray metal, a cubical cage of that same seamless metal, wide enough to hold a dragon, and then another beside it, and another above that, stacking themselves into the air of a Dimension that had been free for hours!","They hauled her up to the first one, and they THREW her in!","Three thousand years of chains, hours of sky, and a being who had broken her own bindings through pure conserved will was thrown in without a shred of care, cargo and nothing more, striking the far wall hard enough to ring the whole cage, and the door ground shut on her before she had stopped sliding!","Inside it, bound and muzzled, THE Blood Duke shook in pain as she tried to scream...and was unable to.","—","Damodred was in the citadel when it happened.","The last Laestrygonian had been standing among Humans, as he often did now, letting the children stare at the blindfold of crimson gold hands across his face, and the moment the sweep landed, the hands went dark and dead and the great eye behind them shut for the first time.","He stood there in the street with his blindfold gone lifeless, and he understood immediately what had been done to him as he sought to move!","Three shrouded figures walked out of the crowd toward him at speeds his current existence could not follow, because all authority became inhibited and nullified... he was not able to do a thing!","But he could still move his body, and so the last Laestrygonian did the only thing left to him.","He stepped in front of the children.","He spread his arms across a street full of small staring faces, a being with a dead blindfold shielding Humans with nothing but his own frame, and the shrouded ones did not slow down for any of it!","They came through the crowd in straight lines, and the crowd was simply IN the lines! Their movements and authority trampled hundreds of nearby Humans to bloody pulp, bodies that had been laughing in a market street one breath ago crushed beneath wrappings that never once looked down, and Damodred ROARED, a sound no one in this citadel had ever heard from him, and threw himself at the nearest shrouded figure with his bare hands!","His fists struck a thing equivalent to a weak Primeval Lifeform, and his authority was gone, and the shrouded figure did not even sway.","They put the band on him in the middle of the screaming street, and they were not gentle about a single motion of it! One shrouded hand gripped the back of his neck and bent him, forcing the last Laestrygonian a murdered race down over the bodies of the Humans he had failed to shield, holding him folded there while the band clicked shut, and then the loomlight ropes went around his wrists and his elbows and his knees, cinched tight enough to cut, and they dragged him upward off the ground by the rope at his wrists, hanging, and a second cage ground into existence above the citadel and took him in the same way the first had taken the dragon!","Thrown. Rung against the far wall. Sealed.","And below, many Humans and some Superpowered Lifeforms stood in a street painted with their own people, and watched their new protector hang and vanish into a metal box in the sky.","In another direction.","Anaximander did not resist as he seemed to have sensed something in the last possible moment.","He watched Axon approach with the band, and he made no attempt to leave.","The band closed around the neck of a being no framework had ever managed to file.","And nothing happened.","...!","Axon’s halos stopped turning.","Because the collar sat there at the scholar’s throat, seamless and sealed and doing absolutely nothing at all, and Anaximander looked down at it, and then he looked up, and there was nothing scholarly left in his face! Cold anger sat there instead.","And around him, the skies filled with weight!","They came from every direction at once. Ianthe Kallias landed on the stone beside him, and old Peleus came, and dozens more, many Superpowered Lifeforms of THE Ymnaros arriving as some of them were collared. And every one of them exactly as strong as they had been an hour ago!","\" Were these collars... supposed to do something? \" Anaximander said coldly.","And he reached up, took hold of the band at his throat with both hands, and tore it apart!","CRACK!","The pieces fell.","Anaximander stepped forward and cracked his knuckles as surrounding existence began to shake!","—","And gigaparsecs out, in the crossing-dark beyond the fused Dimension, Warden Yrsa went to collect the Descendant.","She found Jarl Skallagrim on his feet with his last Steed beside him, both of them stripped by the sweep, his crimson gold seas guttered and his fissures gone dim, and she walked toward them across the black with two gray bands in her hands and no hurry in her at all.","The Steed she took first.","It shrieked and tried to bolt, and one loomlight rope caught its neck and folded its legs beneath it mid-stride so that it crashed chin-first into the dark, and Warden Yrsa walked over to it, and set her boot on its neck, and closed the band around its throat with the ease of a keeper closing a gate!","CLICK!","Chains wound over it, cinched down until the little Steed could not raise its head, and it lay pinned in the dark and shook, uncursed and uncollared for barely a few hours of its existence, and collared again now, and its eyes rolled toward Skallagrim the whole time, asking him for something he could not give!","Then she turned to the Descendant, and she pressed the second band to his throat, and it began to close.","And it stopped halfway!","Because the shroud had come out!","THE Thousand Deaths I Do Not Owe billowed out of Skallagrim’s fissures in ragged dark crimson gold, every death that had ever been written into his clause and was now unpaid, and it drove itself into the closing band and jammed there, wedging the gray metal open a finger’s width from sealing!","The collar was still winning, closing by slow increments as the shroud thinned, and the Blood Sovereign’s arms shook as he held the thing off his own throat with a power that should have been switched off entirely!","Half bound. Half free!","Yrsa stopped, and she watched it for a long moment.","\" Hm .\"","She tilted her head as she studied the wedged band.","\" This is definitely a first. But I knew a Descendant would be troublesome...\"","...!","Skallagrim’s shroud thinned another fraction, and he dragged it back up with a roar!","\" So. \" Yrsa clasped her hands.","And she looked past him at the Dimension behind his shoulder, where cages were still grinding into existence in the sky above a citadel, and a dragon lay muzzled and chained in the first of them, and a Laestrygonian hung bound in the second above a street of pulped Humans, and the only things still standing in that whole domain were beings who could not be collared and a scholar who had torn her work apart with his hands!","\" What now?\"","Skallagrim said nothing. His arms shook, and his crimson gold eyes moved once, past her, to the little Steed pinned under chains in the dark, and then back to her.","\" Every powerful being in THE Ymnaros with authority to take has been taken. Your Steed is on the ground at my feet. And you are holding my band open with your own sheer will, which is magnificent, and which changes nothing at all.\"","Her hand rose, and settled on the wedged gray metal at his throat.","\" So call forth your Master, you unruly motherfucker.\"","...!","As she said such words, she used her power to forcefully close the Inhibitor around Skallagrim’s neck!"]},{"number":5614,"title":"Chapter 5614: Chapter 5613: Accountable!","paragraphs":["<Warden Yrsa>","An existence that gave THE Sealed One problems was not to be underestimated.","Yrsa held that thought at the center of everything as her hand pressed the wedged band.","Whatever this Blood-Crowned One was, a vessel of the oldest deceiver in existence had walked away from him, and things that made THE Sealed One walk away were things you learned about before you stood in front of them!","She needed knowledge. She had every advantage at this exact moment, and advantages were not things you saved for later!","So she moved, within spans of nanoseconds, while the capability of the Dimensional Inhibitor still held its subtraction over everything it had swept!","She could not do it to the Descendant as he was special. But she did not have the time to obtain information properly, and she did not need to, because information was lying right there in the dark, pinned under chains.","The steed.","It was now just a beast of flesh and bones! No authority. No curse. No frameworks, no ladders, nothing left in it that existence would even bother to name, and its brain held its memories and informstion all the same, so...","Warden Yrsa put her hand on the head of the fearful steed, ruthlessly, without a single word!","And she extracted.","Her power poured down through her palm into a skull that had nothing left to answer with, and the little steed’s whole body seized against its chains as its eyes flew wide, and it screamed, and no sound came out! Its jaws strained against the loomlight bindings in total silence as its memories were dragged up and out through the tearing, hours and years and a thousand cursed years hauled backward through flesh that was only flesh, and blood began to leak from its eyes, running down its face in thin dark lines as its silent scream went on and on!","Skallagrim’s roar shook the crossing-dark!","He heaved against the half-closed band with everything in him, his shroud flaring ragged, and the steed’s rolling eyes found him one last time through the blood!","And then...","BOOM!","Its head could not withstand the authority tearing across its existence!","The skull of that glorious steed burst apart in the dark, and the silent scream ended, and its entire existence simply ceased, every thread of it going out at once, and what lay pinned beneath the chains was a lifeless corpse that had been uncursed, and free, for less than a single day of its long and obedient life!","\"...!\"","And Warden Yrsa breathed in.","Her eyes, pale and unmoved through many collarings, showed tremendous surprise!","Because the memories were in her now, hours of them, and what they held was... more than she had reckoned for! Far more! Her mind ran through them within nanoseconds, and her conclusions rearranged themselves, and she did not waste a single one of those nanoseconds standing still!","She moved.","Warden Yrsa appeared instantly behind Skallagrim, and her hands waved once!","HUUM!","Hundreds of radiant white swords manifested out of the loomlight, blades woven purely from THE Argent Loom, and they poured into orbit around the rageful figure of the Descendant, circling him in layered rings, and every single one of them came to rest a single millimeter from his skin! Points at his throat, his spine, his eyes, his fissures, hundreds of terrifying weapons of terrifying authority holding at a millimeter, so that any motion from anything, anywhere, would see them pierce him in but an instant!","Because existence outside the Dimension behind them had begun to tremble and shake!","Even without turning, Yrsa sensed the immense pressure that had arrived, pressure that had no business existing inside a region her Inhibitor had swept, and she turned her head calmly and gazed at what stood in the crossing-dark!","A manifestation of the Blood-Crowned One!","Crimson gold, crowned in blood, floating in the black with stellar light rolling off his frame in slow waves, and he had not just appeared here! Across her senses, similar manifestations were appearing in various areas of THE Ymnaros Dimension, above the citadel, over the northern skies, before the cages themselves!","But it did not matter.","She had already sent her commands within those same nanoseconds, to Axon, to the shrouded units, to every position her order held: utilize the prisoners. The chained and the collared and the caged were no longer captives now, they were leverage, placed exactly where they needed to be to control the flow of whatever battle would be commencing!","Warden Yrsa breathed out, and she looked ahead.","The manifestation before her was one of his clones, she knew that much from the dead steed’s memories, and his entire expression was unfathomably cold and rageful! Crimson gold eyes with singularities turning in their depths bore down on her with a weight that surprised her, his gaze moving once across the corpse of the steed, once across the hundreds of blades holding a millimeter from Skallagrim’s skin, and back to her!","And Yrsa was unfazed even as her existence pulsed as she felt like she was being looked at by something ancient! Haha, just who was this fucker to make her feel like this?","She shook her head slowly, and when she spoke, her voice was as calm and plain as it had been all afternoon.","\" What an arrogant and unique piece of work you are.\" She glanced at the wedged band on Skallagrim’s throat. \" Healing the curse of Steeds and cursed Descendants? Sheesh.\"","The dark trembled around his silence.","\"I see you are angry. But it is nice to meet you.\" She tilted her head. \" From the memories of that sad steed that unfortunately died after the memory extraction... I see you have been busy since curing Hvitrmarr and coming here. You even went as far as to cure a cursed Descendant. To give something salvation... when it was not your place to do so.. .\"","\" Who knows what more you would have done if I had not come along?\"","The manifestation’s rage pressed against the crossing-dark, and still he did not move!","\" But seeing you pause in rage there, you seem to already grasp the situation at hand.\" Yrsa raised one finger, and every blade in orbit brightened.","\" Any move from you means this cursed Descendant, well... not cursed anymore... it means that this Descendant, and that dragon inside the Dimension, and all the others that my people have shackled and bound and inhibited... will die.\"","\"So I advise you not to make a move.\"","The blades turned slowly at their millimeter, and Skallagrim’s shroud flickered between them, and his crimson gold eyes burned at her back with something that had no words in any tongue!","\"I will even go as far as to say I don’t give a damn about this Descendant. Or the steed inside. Or that ugly looking thing with severed hands on its head .\" She said it all evenly, without a shred of heat. \" If you just bring your body here... I can swap their freedom for yours. After all, they are merely followers. You are the leader.\"","Warden Yrsa clasped her hands behind her back, and looked into the cold rage of the Blood-Crowned One, and finished plainly.","\"It is always those who lead that need to be held accountable. And I wanna hold you accountable, O Cure-Giver. O Blood-Crowned One.\"","Her pale eyes were very steady.","\"I want... to hold you accountable.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5615,"title":"Chapter 5615: Chapter 5614: Mistakes!","paragraphs":["<Existential Interlude- Mistakes>","Nobody knows how long ago it was.","The record itself does not claim a time. It only claims that it happened, in the age when Those Who Remain still spoke often, and existence was still young enough to listen closely.","One of Those Who Remain had many Descendants.","His name is not written as the record calls him only the Father, and it calls his youngest Descendant Alvarr, and it says that Alvarr was born restless.","One day, Alvarr came before the Father and said, \" Father, I wish to prove myself to you. Give me a quest.\"","The Father considered him for a long time. Then he said:","\" Go out into existence, and bring me back a thing I do not have.\"","Alvarr bowed, and left that same instant!","This was the first mistake, and it was the mistake of haste.","Alvarr crossed a hundred Dimensions before it occured to him that he had never asked what the thing was. What did his Father lack? What could a being lack, when existence agreed with almost every one of his words? He did not know! He had been so eager to begin that he had run past the beginning entirely, and now an Age had been spent, and all of it was wandering!","He returned to his Father empty handed and ashamed, and he waited to be punished, and he waited a long time as his father was entertaining himself with one of THE First Lifeforms at that time for a whole millennium.","After waiting for his punishment in that millennium...","The Father did not punish him.","\" Why would I punish a teacher?\" the Father said. \" Your mistake has just taught you what nothing else could have. You mistook motion for progress. All the living do this once. Most of them do it forever. Now you will not. Go again.\"","The second mistake was the mistake of the mirror.","Alvarr went out and gathered treasure. He took the hearts of dead Dimensions and the crowns of drowned kings, rivers of authority and seeds of unborn Observable Existences, everything that made his own chest burn with wanting, and he piled it before his Father in a heap that bent the light.","The Father looked at the heap, and then at his son.","\" You have brought me everything YOU desire,\" he said. \" You looked into Existence and saw only your own face in it. This is the mistake of the mirror, and every living thing commits it: to give others what we ourselves want, and call it generosity. Do not be ashamed. Be corrected. To find what another lacks, you must first put down the mirror and listen. Go again.\"","And so the Descendant went on and commited another mistake!","The third mistake was the mistake of pride.","Alvarr resolved to listen, and so he sought out the oldest and grandest beings in existence, Primeval things and sovereign things and Provenance Lifeforms, and he asked them what a being such as his Father could lack. They gave him grand answers, and every answer was wrong.","At the edge of a small Observable Existence, a farmer who was nothing at all offered him directions, and Alvarr did not stop, because what could nothing at all know?","He wandered another Age. When he finally passed that way again, humbled and worn, he stopped at the same field, and the farmer gave him the same directions, and they were true ones.","When he told his Father, the Father nodded slowly.","\" Pride is the worst of the mistakes ,\" he said, \" not because it is the largest, but because it is the jailer of all the others. Every mistake can be cured by asking. Pride is the mistake that forbids asking. A being who cannot ask can only repeat. Remember the farmer. Go again.\"","And he went on!","The fourth mistake was the mistake of the closed hand.","Following the farmer’s directions, Alvarr came upon a wonder: a dying beast of the old dark, and cradled in its fading coils, a thing that existed nowhere else, offered freely to whoever would take it before the beast’s last breath.","And Alvarr hesitated.","Was it a trick? Was it worthy? Was he? He weighed, and he doubted, and he waited to be certain, and while he waited, the beast breathed its last, and the wonder went out with it, and no power in all existence could light it again.","\"I made no move at all,\" he told his Father, bitter. \" How can doing nothing be a mistake?\"","\"Because hesitation is not the absence of a choice, \" the Father said. \" It is a choice wearing the mask of caution. The closed hand believes it is keeping itself safe. It is only keeping itself empty. Some doors open once, my son. You will grieve this one for a long time, and the grieving is also the learning. Go again.\"","And this fucker went on to commit yet another mistake.","The fifth mistake...was the mistake of the buried wound.","For in his wanderings Alvarr had erred against a companion, a small betrayal, committed in a weak hour, and rather than confess it, he had hidden it, and told himself it was too small to matter.","But a hidden mistake is a planted one!","It grew in the dark. The small betrayal became a distance, and the distance became a silence, and the silence became a parting, and by the time Alvarr understood what he had buried, the companion was gone beyond finding, carrying a wound with no name on it.","He confessed it to his Father last of all, and his voice failed him twice in the telling.","\" Now you know the accounting every liar learns too late,\" the Father said. \" A mistake confessed is half repaired. A mistake hidden compounds. Shame promises to protect you from the cost of your errors, and instead it collects interest on them. Bury nothing, my son. The buried does not rot. It grows. Go again.\"","Finally, lastly, he commited his last mistake.","The sixth mistake was the mistake of the ended story.","Alvarr did not go again.","He sat down at the rim of a dead Dimension, and he counted his failures, one Age of haste, one Age of mirrors, pride, an empty hand, a buried wound and its silense, and he concluded that he was a being MADE of mistakes, and that a being made of mistakes could bring his Father nothing, and that the quest was over because he was over.","He sat there for a long time. Long enough that the dust of the dead Dimension began to know him.","And at last, because there was nothing else left to do, he stood up anyway, and walked home to say the failure aloud rather than let it also become a buried thing.","He came before his Father with his hands open and empty.","\"I have failed the quest ,\" Alvarr said . \"I searched every reach of existence, and I found nothing you lack. I bring you nothing. Only my mistakes.\"","There was a long silence!","And then the Father did something the record insists upon, though it strains believing. He leaned forward, and his ancient existence trembled, and he said:","\" Say that last part again.\"","\"...I bring you only my mistakes.\"","\" Then the quest is complete, \" the Father said. \" You have brought me the one thing I do not have.\"","BOOM!","Alvarr stared at him, uncomprehending, and the Father spoke on, and the record keeps his words whole:","\"I am one of Those Who Remain. When I speak, existence is supposed to agree. I have never reached for a thing and missed it. And so I have never once, in all the reaches of my existence... learned anything. A mistake is a teacher that existence sends for free, and no teacher has ever been permitted to reach me!\"","And so it was, the record says, that every evening for an Age, a being whom existence obeyed sat quietly in the dark and was taught by his own child, hungering after the one wealth he could never mint!","The record ends with three sayings.","To err is to be alive. Stones are flawless, and they are stones.","A mistake is only a failure if it is the last one you consult.","And the young make mistakes and become old. The old make mistakes and become wise. The wise make mistakes and become stories, and the stories go on erring in the mouths of everyone who retells them, and this too is how the living remain alive.","But not all of Those Who Remain listened the way this Father listened. Some paint an entirely different picture that would make one question whether Those Who Remain were so grand and wise.","Because some believe Those Who Remain are filled with faults, and no more grander than any other lifeform out there.","That is another story.","---","<THE True Human Emperor>","It was human to make mistakes.","Noah Osmont was human.","So he made a mistake!","It did not look grand when he made it. Mistakes rarely do. His mistake was only this: he pulled all nine of his clones out of THE Ymnaros and into THE Infiniverse, to stand among his people, to place eighteen hundred beginnings into the right hands, to watch his daughter’s face as she held nine seeds of her own. A father’s errand. A ruler’s errand. A few hours of work inside his own home!","And it did not seem like anything at all!","Damodred was out there. Hvitrmarr was out there, a queen who had broken her own chains. Anaximander was out there, and nothing in existence had ever managed to file him. Skallagrim stood guard at the very door with a Steed at his side and all twenty of Attributes in his frame. Four of the mightiest beings Noah had ever gathered, watching a Dimension at peace, and if anything happened, anything at all, he could be there in a short period of time.","Or so he thought!","It arrived in the span of a nanosecond.","Noah was standing in the golden light of his mother’s realm with Tesseracts turning around him in their slow orbit, and between one beat of his Heart and the next, the threads went dark!","Hvitrmarr’s thread, the Blood Duke’s bond of crimson gold running from his existence to hers, snuffed out between one instant and the next! Damodred’s presence, wrapped in his authority, gone! The weavings he had seated across the key figures of an entire Dimension, dozens of them, extinguished instsntly in a single silent moment, and through the one thread that remained, through Skallagrim’s Sovereign bond, strained taut and screaming, sensations poured into him that made his blood turn cold and then ignite!","Shackled!","Inhibited!","IMPRISONED!","His people! His guardians! Beings he had healed and freed and seated with his own hands, silenced across gigaparsecs in less time than a thought takes to finish, and something in him went very still and very quiet, and then everything in him that was not still and not quiet stood up at once!","Fury rolled off his body as the golden fields bent flat around him!","Sanguine light erupted around his body as from different direction, nine crowns of blood tore themselves away, and his hands were already moving, and in the distance, along the cliff above the radiant river...","Thalia Vasiliou frowned.","She was standing beside his mother with a fishing line still in her hand, and her head had turned upward, toward the skies of THE Infiniverse, toward the outside, exactly toward the place where his threads had died, and her narrowed eyes seemed to reach through his home’s endless blue to the wound beyond it!","And her thought arrived in his mind, low and level and grim.","’This force? This early?’","His racing paused on those words!","’ Those are particularly troublesome ones, and their backing is unfathomably deep . It would hurt me a great deal to give you any information about them. So you may have to put in a bit of work with these ones yourself. Try any way you can to obtain information about them, and...’","The pause stretched!","’...I am sorry for any pain of your people they and you are about to have.’","...!","She said such heavy words, and Noah did not answer her, because there was nothing to answer with, and because he was already gone!","He set off!","His clone came to a stop in the crossing-dark outside THE Ymnaros, and stood opposite the leader of those who had attacked his Dimension and his people!","She stood with her back to a half-collared Sovereign wrapped in hundreds of white blades. A plain woman in plain garments, dark hair bound back, pale eyes, no authority anywhere on her at all, and at her feet, chained and pinned and headless, lay the corpse of a small Steed that had been free for less than a single day!","And she looked into the cold rage of his manifestation without a flicker, and told him what she wanted.","Him!","His body, delivered to her hands, in exchange for every chained and caged and inhibited existence his mistake had left behind!","It was human to make mistakes.","Noah was human.","And outside THE Ymnaros, in the crossing-dark, the price of his was standing in front of him with pale, patient eyes, waiting to be paid!"]},{"number":5616,"title":"Chapter 5616: Chapter 5615: The Golden Leash!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","He looked at Yrsa coldly, and his eyes flashed!","THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard swept across the leader of the incursion as it reached for her truths, and her details unfolded before him as the crossing-dark itself seemed to lean in!","|Warden Yrsa|:: VERITAS: 23. PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 25. PONDUS: 28. A Warden of ?????. Her origin is ?????. She has never once broken a rule she set for herself. ?????","...!","Every attribute, apart from Provenance, above twenty!","Every single one! Above the wall of ten that had once capped his own sight, sitting in the range where Skallagrim’s completed panel sat and climbing past it, all of it seated inside a being who radiated absolutely nothing at all! Her PONDUS alone stood at twenty-eight, a bearing grander than a Blood Sovereign’s, wrapped in plain garments and a clerk’s calm!","Questions stacked themselves in his depths, and Noah set every one of them aside, because his rage had not moved an inch and neither had he!","He was undaunted.","He looked at the panel, and then at her, and when he spoke, his voice rolled out grand and cold across the crossing-dark.","\" You have made yourself my enemy just now.\" His crimson gold eyes held her pale ones. \" And because I am so fucking magnanimous, I give you this one chance to change course. In existence, when the many are dying and getting collapsed, they always wish they had done something different in the past. Some moment where the road forked, and they took the wrong side of it.\"","He let the dark hold the words. \" That moment, for you, is this one. Change your course. Release my people... and you may yet have salvation in your future.\"","Yrsa listened to all of it without a flicker.","And then she smiled, calmly.","\"I do not fear death .\" She said it plainly. \" For my cause, I can gladly die. If what I am doing now becomes the reason I die in some future? I have no qualms about it at all .\"","Her head tilted. \" But that is me. You... have these people I have chained.\"","Her pale eyes did not leave his.","\" So, to show you how serious I am. In the next nanosecond, I will start by breaking the bones of the steed you cured and took from THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension . Or you can bring your main body here, alongside a certain Remnant Existential Treasure, and make the exchange. I will even honor you properly.\"","She waved her hand!","HUUM!","Light bloomed above her palm as a collar band manifested there, and it was not gray!","It was GOLDEN! A dazzling band of deep gold, seamless and unmarked, turning slowly above her hand as off its surface rolled a silent air of suffocation that pressed against the crossing-dark itself, a pressure that did not attack and did not threaten and simply sat there promising an ending to expression itself!","\"A special Inhibitor ,\" Yrsa said. \" Meant to stifle the terrifying Descendants of Those Who Remain. I have never yet had cause to use one. For you, I will.\"","Noah looked at this lifeform coldly as, at the sides of his head, his own voice began to speak!","\" We need to collapse every fucking shred of existence that she and her forces have .\" THE Provenance of the Closed Crown spoke low and flat from his left, arms folded, eyes shut. \" Just go utterly apeshit, and figure everything else out later.\"","\" That is feasible,\" THE Provenance of the Open Hand answered calmly from his right. \" And Hvitrmarr and the others may die in the doing of it. For what? A momentary release of anger?\"","The cross-legged figure’s light held even and warm. \" Thalia said we need to obtain information about these ones. Brute force is not ideal here, and it is not even efficient. But we have other means. Consider what she is actually asking. She wants to chain us... and we cannot be chained. She does not KNOW we cannot be chained. So we play along. We let her close her collar, and she will take us to wherever this force of hers belongs, into the heart of everything she serves... and we can obtain information in abundance while every one of them believes they are guarding a prisoner. We would gain more there than we could ever gain by overcoming her here. And overcoming her here guarantees casualties.\"","\"At what cost?\" the Crown said coldly. \" Think of what we are. Think of the stature of what we have built and become. How could someone of our standing be WILLINGLY imprisoned? Leashed? Paraded into their cages by our own consent?\"","\"Are we truly so prideful? \" the Hand asked. \" So overly arrogant that we cannot play a part? A prisoner’s part, worn for a while, in exchange for the best results our people can be given?\"","...!","Noah listened to all the parts of himself, coldly, completely.","And before a nanosecond had passed...","HUUM!","Beside the clone that had first appeared in the crossing-dark, his main body arrived!","Crimson gold and stellar blue, the collar of First Purity at his chest as eleven singularities turned in his depths, THE True Human Emperor himself stepped out of nothing at all, and he looked at Warden Yrsa as he spoke with total calm.","\" My freedom... for my people.\"","...!","It was something surreal!","Even Yrsa seemed surprised! Her pale eyes moved over him up and down, and then she nodded once and came over unhurried as the golden collar in her grasp opened itself and floated across the dark toward his throat, a leash of dazzling gold hanging still in the silence between them.","\" Put it on.\"","...!","Noah gazed at the thing hanging before him, and prompts unfolded across his sight!","|You are observing a Lineage Inhibitor: THE GILDED CLAUSE.|","|The highest grade of Existential Inhibitor in its order’s records. Where common Inhibitors subtract granted authority, THE GILDED CLAUSE suppresses the genetic and existential expression of any and all authority at its root: granted, devoured, inherited, or written. Intents, Sources, Infinities, Pantheons, and frameworks are stifled at the level of expression itself. Even the sentence-lineage of a Descendant of Those Who Remain, the unbroken written line running back to the speaking hand, is silenced clause by clause while the band remains closed.|","|It adapts. Expressions that attempt to rise are read, and counter-written, faster than they form.|","|Its make is ?????. Its count in existence is ?????.|","Noah read every line of it coldly.","And he knew, with plain certainty, that it would do nothing to him! It was a masterwork raised against every power existence had ever handed anyone, and nothing he carried had been handed to him! Nothing granted. Nothing borrowed. Nothing owed!","So, calmly and efficiently... Noah put the leash on his own neck!","CLICK!","And in the same instant, he made the oppression around himself disappear!","His pressure folded inward and vanished as his presense dimmed, the weight that bent grass and caved stone withdrawing entirely, until THE True Human Emperor stood in the crossing-dark, collared in gold, and gave off the air of... nothing! Nothing at all! A man, in a band, powerless to every sense that would ever check!","\"I detest this ,\" THE Closed Crown said flatly at his ear.","\" Going through things one does not like,\" THE Open Hand replied, serene, \" is part of being human. We do it constantly. We wait, we swallow, we wear what the hour demands, and we do it because the results on the far side may be something unfathomably grand.\"","Its closed eyes did not open, and its voice settled soft over the golden collar. \" To be human... is to do a lot of things one does not like.\""]},{"number":5617,"title":"Chapter 5617: Chapter 5616: Promises!","paragraphs":["The golden leash sat closed around the neck of THE True Human Emperor.","And beside him, his clone trembled.","The crowned manifestation of blood shuddered once in the crossing-dark as its crimson gold light guttered and dimmed, and then it came apart, seemingly starved of everything that had sustained it, scattering into fading motes that dimmed and went out between one breath and the next!","Gone. As though the band at his throat had reached through him and unmade even the works of his blood!","Yrsa watched the motes fade.","Then she floated over to him, unhurried, and took his hand in hers, and with the casual efficiency of a clerk testing a seal... she broke his finger.","CRACK!","The bone snapped sideways under her grip, and blood welled dark at the joint, and the finger stayed broken! No stellar light rushed to it. No mending crawled beneath the skin. Nothing in him rose to answer the injury at all, and Noah allowed every bit of it to happen as he gazed at her coldly, his expression unmoving over a seemingly leashed and powerless body!","Yrsa looked at the broken finger for a moment longer. Then she released his hand, and nodded slowly.","\"I am entirely surprised.\" She drifted back half a step as her pale eyes stayed on his face. \" Do you know how many times I have stood before a leader and offered this exact exchange? Their freedom for their people’s. I have offered it to sovereigns of clusters of Observable Existences. To Primeval things with congregations beyond count. To kings whose subjects sang their names in numbers that bent the air.\"","She shook her head once. \" Leaders rarely put themselves on the line for their people. Almost never. They would rather their people die, every last one of them, than give up their rulership. They tell themselves they will avenge the dead after, as if vengeance were a kind of protection they could pay in arrears. I have heard that reasoning so many times I could recite it in my sleep.\"","Her gaze moved over the golden band at his throat.","\" You actuslly stood for your people! For that... I will stick to my word, and release your people.\"","She raised her fingers and gestured once!","The shrouded beings appeared around them in silence, white-wrapped figures with Loom-rivers turning in orbit, circling Noah in a loose ring with their presense registering nowhere, and one of them drifted forward bearing a set of golden chains that uncoiled in the dark and wound themselves around Noah’s hands, coiling wrist to wrist in dazzling links that clicked softly as they settled!","And Noah did not watch the chains.","He gazed past them, at Skallagrim.","The Blood Sovereign still stood half-bound where she had left him, the wedged band at his throat, and the eyes of this Descendant were RAGING! Crimson gold seas churned in them with a violence that had no outlet, fixed on the leashed figure of the man who had rewritten his lineage, and his shroud of unpaid deaths strained against the band in useless ragged pulses!","Yrsa waved her hand.","The hundreds of Argent Loom swords orbiting him dissolved, blades unraveling back into loomlight and draining away into the dark, and in the next instant she waved her hand again, and the half-closed Inhibitor around Skallagrim’s neck opened instsntly, releasing its grip clause by clause as it floated back across the crossing-dark toward her waiting palm!","HUUM!","Skallagrim erupted!","Power detonated out of the Descendant as his crimson gold seas came roaring back to full flood, all twenty of Attributes in his frame igniting at once, and the surrounding existence MELTED, the crossing-dark itself running and warping around his fury for light years as his fissures blazed and his shroud whipped wide!","And Yrsa smiled at it.","\"I could have unshackled you after we left,\" she said, mild and even inside the melting dark. \" But I did this here, in front of him, to show your master that I keep my promises.\"","Her head tilted slightly. \" Be a good boy. I am still stronger than you, even while you are not inhibited. Your Master will be gone, and you... should take care of his Dimension, and his people. They will need it.\"","Her pale eyes did not so much as narrow against the heat of him. \" And if we notice anything here that draws our attention again... I cannot promise we will not be back, to put this whole Dimension through processing under full inhibition. So. \"","A small nod, the nod of a keeper closing up for the day. \" Do not let your master’s actions be in vain. Okay?\"","...!","With such words, Warden Yrsa drifted back to float beside Noah!","And around them, the rest of her order arrived. Axon descended with his halos turning shoulder to heel, and Ohmran’s vast clay-skinned bulk settled into the dark, and the many shrouded lifeforms they had come with gathered in from every direction, dozens of white-wrapped figures with rivers of the Loom in orbit, all of them closing into formation around a single leashed and chained Human Emperor!","Noah stood at the center of all of it, golden at the throat and golden at the wrists, and his cold gaze swept across Skallagrim one last time!","And in the next instant, all of them disappeared!","The crossing-dark emptied. The white rivers closed.","And left behind in all that silence stood Jarl Skallagrim, wreathed in his own useless erupting power... and the chained, headless corpse of a small Steed that had been free for less than a single day.","Moments later, existence split!","Anaximander appeared in the region with his robes still and his eyes cold, and the anger on the scholar’s face was a thing that had never once been seen there in all his wandering, and he looked around the empty crossing-dark, at the melted scars of Skallagrim’s eruption, at the corpse, at the nothing where an entire incursion force had stood!","\" Where did they go?\" His voice came out low, and then it cracked upward! \" WHERE?!\"","He asked as...even he could not sense it!","Skallagrim did not answer.","The Blood Sovereign stood with his fists shaking at his sides, filled with a boundless fury that had nowhere at all to go, and he could not even bring himself to speak!","And in THE Ymnaros Dimension, the promises were being kept.","On the northern shelf, high in its stacked cage, a shackle came loose from Hvitrmarr!","The gray band at her throat released, and the chains unwound from her legs and wings and jaws, and her nine transforming organs came roaring back awake inside her as her power flooded home, and THE Blood Duke rose inside the metal box and broke it, tearing the cage apart from within as dull gray plates rained down the sky, and she burst out into the open air with her red gold wings flung wide and ROARED!","HUUM!","The roar rolled across gigaparsecs! It shook the shelf and the fields and the far terraces, a sound of rage and grief and three thousand years of chains pressed into a single note, and it did not sound anything at all in it of freedom!","And above the citadel, Damodred appeared.","The last Laestrygonian stood unshackled in the air over the streets where they had taken him, his blindfold of crimson gold hands alive once more and opened wide around the single great eye beneath!","Below him lay what the taking had cost.","The casualties were still there. Hundreds of Humans lay broken across the stone in blood and death, the trampled and the crushed, small figures being lifted and wept over and carried, a street that had been a market this morning, and the survivors moved through it slowly under the floating cages’ empty shadows!","Damodred looked down at all of it.","And his single eye pulsed with a terrifying rage!","...!"]},{"number":5618,"title":"Chapter 5618: Chapter 5617: THE ETERNAL PAX! I","paragraphs":["Purple gold strings surrounded everything.","Noah stood leashed and chained in an area walled by them on every side, countless strings pulsing and thrumming as they moved at tremendous speeds through the dark, each one racing along its own path as though it had a set destination it had crossed a billion times before, and his senses read them quietly from behind an expression of nothing at all!","The Argent Loom. Expressed differently here, dyed purple gold and woven into roads!","Around him, the incursion force stood in loose formation as Warden Yrsa gave her orders, clipped and efficient, and group after group of shrouded ones bowed and stepped onto the racing strings and vanished along them, dozens of departures in moments, until the transit dark held only four figures: Noah, Yrsa, the vast clay-skinned Primeval with a pale band at its own throat... and the being wrapped in turning halos.","And at this time, prompts rose before Noah’s eyes alone!","|You have remained quintessentially true to your Provenance.|","|You were threatened, and you did not bend. You were collared, and you were not contained. You walked into the hands of your enemies as an act of your own design, wearing their chains as instruments of your own aim, and at no point did your existence argue with itself. To be true under freedom is common. To be true under a leash is generation.|","|Your attributes have increased.|","| VERITAS: 15. PROVENANCE: 11. POTENTIA: INFINITE. PONDUS: 17.|","...!","Growth! Here, of all places! Chained at the wrists and collared in gold at the center of an enemy formation, and his existence had weighed all of it and called it truth, and grown!","As he read the panel, Yrsa moved!","Her leg swiped at his feet without warning, and Noah played along perfectly, his stance breaking as he fell back and sat down hard against the dark, chains rattling, and Yrsa lowered herself to sit beside him, entirely at ease, and when he looked at her, her pale eyes were shining with open interest and wonder!","\" What an interesting thing you are .\" She studied his face. \" Capable of curing the Cursed Steeds and the Cursed Descendants made so by THE Sleepless Fiend himself. And you ran circles around THE Sealed One to obtain the Remnant Existential Treasure he wanted so badly .\" Her gaze dropped to his chest. \"Is that it, by the way?\"","She reached out to the Aurate Collar!","And the moment her finger touched the ancient bone...","SSSS!","Her finger singed!","It was a reaction of touching the sun itself! Pale skin scorched black at the tip in an instant as a thread of smoke curled up between them, and Yrsa pulled her hand back with genuine surprise crossing her face for the first time since the crossing-dark, shaking her finger once as the burn slowly closed!","Noah looked at her coldly.","\" A treasure such as this is bound to me by my blood .\" His voice stayed level. \" As long as I live, even grasping it will be an issue for you.\"","...!","Yrsa smiled at that.","\" Is that right?\" She flexed her singed finger, unbothered, almost pleased. \" You are definitely interesting. Your power may even be close to Axon, or even me, if that Descendant was made what he is under you.\"","Her smile cooled a fraction. \" But all that power means nothing if it is inhibited now, hm?\"","Noah felt the golden leash sit against his neck, and he kept his voice calm.","\"I saw the prisons and the leashes you almost brought out for THE Ymnaros Dimension .\" His cold eyes held hers. \" Are you doing this to others too? What exactly do you want?\"","...!","Yrsa smiled coldly, and then she sighed, and for the first time, she truly began to talk.","\" Authority .\" She said the word with an old, cold weight. \" In the hands of the unworthy, existence suffers. It has always suffered. It suffers right now, in a hundred thousand places at once, because some random thing climbed a random ladder and was handed a hammer at the top of it, and existence never once checked what would be built.\"","Her pale eyes did not blink. \"I am an Enforcer. One among many. Our task is stability, and our method is subtraction: we take away the capability to utilize authority, from the many who should never have held it. Existence’s randomness hands authority to too many, too easily, with no test and no ledger.\" She turned her head to him.","\" We are the answer to that randomness.\"","Noah listened to all of it, and then he spoke, grand and quiet.","\" And who are you to pick and choose who is unworthy of authority?\" His chained hands rested still in his lap. \" Line up every being you have ever collared, and every judgment you made over them. Who weighed YOU? What gives you the right?\"","\" Why ...\" Yrsa’s answer came without a heartbeat of delay, serene and total. \" Existence gave us the right, of course. We would not have the right otherwise.\"","Noah gazed coldly at her.","\" Then I can assume one of Those Who Remain paved the way for all this. Or several of them.\" He let it land. \" You should be just the hounds of someone with a true vision.\"","Yrsa laughed at that, one short breath of it, and she waved her hand as she pointed lazily across the transit dark, at the haloed being, at the collared Primeval!","\" Others may be hounds .\" Her smile spread. \" But some of us have that glorious vision ourselves. Haha! And you will see a glimpse of it, as we... are here.\"","HUUM!","The purple gold strings around them pulsed once, brilliantly, and faded!","|You have crossed an unfathomable distance. You have arrived in an unknown Dimension.|","And existence opened up around Noah.","He stood upon a purple gold floating mountain! Its slopes fell away beneath him in terraces of radiant stone, and it was one among MANY, dozens of serene floating mountains drifting upon endless seas of white clouds, each one glowing softly in gold and violet, arranged in a vast outer ring around deeper reaches where more mountains rose, grander and brighter, ascending toward some far center that burned too radiant to look at directly!","It was beautiful. It was serene past anything an incursion force had any right to come home to!","And then Noah looked outward, past the ring, at what surrounded the mountains.","Cages.","Countless stacked cages extending for light years!","They filled the skies beyond the outer ring in every direction, gray cubical prisons of that same seamless metal stacked upon each other in columns and walls and gigaparsec reaches, tier upon tier upon tier, an architecture of captivity vast enough that his eyes could follow a single column of cages upward until it thinned into the distance and never find its end!","And they were full!","Some cages held clusters, dozens of Source Lifeforms crowded together in one box, their dense patient light guttered to almost nothing, or huddles of Infinite Lifeforms whose silver seas lay still, or crowds of Gilded Ones whose brilliance had gone out entirely, dim golden figures sitting shoulder to shoulder in the dark of their boxes!","Other cages held lone figures, single True Lifeforms in single boxes, beings who had crossed the threshold of Trueness itself sitting alone with their heads down! And other cages, set apart and wound with extra bands of loomlight, held lone PRIMEVAL Lifeforms, ancient things older than frameworks, lying motionless along the floors of metal boxes!","And as Noah gazed across them, what struck him hardest was not the count.","It was the stillness!","So many of the jailed looked despondent past all reaching, without any will left to live at all! Beings sat unmoving with their eyes open and empty. A Source Lifeform leaned against its bars with one hand stretched out through them, reaching toward a cage across the golden road where smaller lights huddled, and the hand simply hung there, unmoving. It had been reaching for a long, long time!","His eyes flashed, and panels unfolded across the nearest of them!","|A True Gilded Lifeform|:: VERITAS: 0.8 (0, Inhibited). PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 0.6 (0, Inhibited). PONDUS: 0.7 (0, Inhibited). She has stopped counting the days.","|A True Infinite Lifeform|:: VERITAS: .4 (0, Inhibited). PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 1.9 (0, Inhibited). PONDUS: 1.1 (0, Inhibited). He no longer remembers the sound of his own Pantheon.","|A Primeval Lifeform|:: VERITAS: 11.6 (0, Inhibited). PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 5.8 (0, Inhibited). PONDUS: 8.2 (0, Inhibited). It has been lying in the same position for ?????.","...!","Decimals! His sight resolved them now, fine measures it had never needed before, and the numbers rearranged many things about the mighty of existence!","Beside every true value, in the parenthesis, flat and total: (0, Inhibited). What they were, and what they were now permitted to express!","And then he saw the roads.","Down the wide golden roads that ran between the cage-walls, shrouded beings were leading rows of inhibited lifeforms!","Lines of them, hundreds long, collared and chained wrist to wrist, shuffling between the stacked prisons toward open cages waiting with their doors ground wide, and the lines moved in silence, and the silence was the silence of beings who had already learned!","Because as Noah watched, one did not move in silence!","A Gilded Lifeform midway down a row stopped walking! It turned at an open cage door and refused, planting itself, shaking its dimmed head, and its mouth opened.","\"I am SUPERBIUS! Do you understand this? My pride burns even now-...!\"","Two shrouded ones descended on it instsntly, and they beat it! They beat it down onto the golden road with blows that cracked across the distance, methodical and unhurried, and the row around it stood still and stared at their own feet, and when the Gilded Lifeform still dragged itself up one more time and reached for the shroud of the nearest one...","It was killed.","One blow, dispensed with the same clerical efficiency as all the rest, and a being that had once been brilliance itself splattered across the golden road, its dimmed light bursting apart and raining down over the stone and over the feet of its own row, and the shrouded ones stepped over what remained and gestured the line forward, and the line moved!","The golden road drank the light, and did not change color!","Noah looked at all of it. The mountains. The cages. The reaching hand. The road.","And he turned to Yrsa, and his voice came out heavy.","\" Is this... your vision?\" His chained hands did not move. \" Lifeforms in cages? This brutality, occurring all around?\"","...!","Yrsa harrumphed!","She looked around at the whole of it, the columns and the roads and the stillness.","\"I do not like this any more than you.\" She said it plainly. \" But things must be done for prosperity. All are chained for NOW, because we are in the process of collecting. Do you understand? This is the middle of the work, not the end of it. Domains and Observable Existences are being prepared and cleared out at this very moment, and we have already begun transporting the collected to them, where, with no authority at all, they will learn to build their own Civilizations again. As normal lifeforms.\"","Her voice steadied into the cadence of a thing recited and believed. \" Farmers. Workers. Soldiers. Protectors. All of it without a shred of authority anywhere among them, and no hammer for existence to hand to anyone ever again. We usher in an era of peace.\"","Her pale eyes moved to the stain on the golden road below. \" Those who rebel against this vision, even after they are told not to be unruly... those are the only ones that can make things here seem brutal. But we...\"","She looked back at him.","\" We are good. We are good.\"","HUUM!","She rose, and moved behind Noah, and kicked him forward!","He stumbled ahead as a white cloud of Argent Loom formed beneath their feet, catching them both, and it began to float across the mountain’s radiant terraces as the wind of the heights moved over them, and Noah focused his senses outward as they flew!","And he felt them!","Terrifying auras, many of them, seated across the deeper mountains! A presense of weight after weight that he had rarely felt anywhere in existence, each one settled on its own peak within the inner rings, patient and immense!","\" Now that you are chained, \" Yrsa said behind him, conversational, \" you will be brought before an Enforcer a level above me. It is for one of them to decide what is to be done with someone who can go against the words of one of Those Who Remain. Enforcer Mahishasura. Or really... Descendant Mahishasura. He would love to understand someone like you.\"","...!","A Descendant! An Enforcer above her, and it was a Descendant, inside the same order that collared Primevals and preached against every hammer existence had ever handed out! Noah set the contradiction atop the growing pile of them, and gazed around at the mountains as the cloud carried them higher.","\" You could at least tell me where we are,\" he said, \" and what you belong to.\"","Yrsa smiled.","And she rose to her full height upon the flying cloud as she raised her hands wide to the mountains and the clouds and the countless cages stacked against the sky, and her plain voice rang out across the radiant heights with the pride of a believer come home!","\" Welcome... to THE Serenaros!\" Her arms spread wider. \" One of the seats of stability across existence! The answer to every unworthy hand! Welcome, O Blood-Crowned One...\"","Her pale eyes shone down at him.","\"...to THE ETERNAL PAX!\"","...!","\"The Pax provides, The Pax protects, The Pax subtracts! The Pax is here for the glory and stability of Existence!\""]},{"number":5619,"title":"Chapter 5619: Chapter 5618: THE ETERNAL PAX! II","paragraphs":["THE ETERNAL PAX.","Of course, a name told you what a thing wished to be, not what it was . Noah turned the ridiculous title over as the cloud carried them on, and behind him Yrsa yawned and stretched, in the manner of a woman who felt she had done quite enough for one cycle.","The distant figures she had been commanding fell away behind them, and then it was only the two of them, crossing the vibrant mountains alone.","Since the crossing was long, Noah was able to see many things.","The first was the strangeness of the shrouded figures. In the areas they passed, many of them moved about continuously, leading rows and hauling chains along the golden roads, and that much was ordinary enough.","But others were not moving at all.","They stood straight and stationary in ordered clusters across the terraces, dozens together, unbreathing and unswaying, and the longer he looked at them, the more a question settled in him. Were these truly lifeforms at all? Or was he looking at an army of things that only wore the shape of one?","His eyes flashed quietly, and details bloomed.","| You are observing THE LOOMWROUGHT SHROUDS.|","|Artificial lifeforms of THE ETERNAL PAX, born from woven authority and unknown technology. Each is grown around a core of refined Argent Loom and wrapped in a body manufactured to a single exacting standard. They do not eat, do not rest, do not age, and do not question any orders. They activate upon assignment and stand down upon completion.|","|A Loomwrought Shroud|:: VERITAS: 11. PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 11. PONDUS: 11. It has never asked a question.","He swept his gaze across the stationary clusters, panel after panel unfolding, and every one of them read exactly the same. Eleven, eleven, eleven, across every attribute, on every figure, without a single decimal of deviation. Compared to the wild variance he had seen in the caged, where a Primeval measured differently in every limb of its panel, this uniformity said something all its own.","A grown thing varied. A made thing matched. And someone, somewhere, had made a very great number of soldiers who each carried the weight of a weak Primeval Lifeform!","How many of them existed? How long had they been standing?","Ahead of him, Yrsa laughed.","\" Why look around so much? \" She did not even turn. \" It is not like anything you see here will help you. Once jailed, there is not really any going back. Many powerful beings realized this in time. You are in it for the long haul, as your fate will be decided soon enough.\"","Noah said nothing to that, and continued observing coldly. After all, she believed the leash at his neck was working.","At the sides of his head, his own voices spoke instead.","\" We could begin by nuking this entire place,\" THE Closed Crown said. \" The mountains, the roads, the towers. Make sure nothing here leaves alive, and let existence sort out what it lost.\"","\" Destruction can come in time, \" THE Open Hand answered. \" Right now, we understand. We already paid the price of being chained, and the price is spent. So we collect as much as possible against it.\"","In truth, there was a great deal to collect.","He saw processing terraces cut into the mountainsides, where inhibited lifeforms stood sorted into queues by their varieties, Source with Source and Gilded with Gilded, each line advancing toward seated figures in layered robes. Every collar was touched in turn, and floating ledgers of purple gold script recorded each one’s informstion into some greater count.","Farther out, cage-caravans slid along the string-roads between mountains, boxes in trains a thousand long, bound for reaches he could not see the end of. In the middle distance, silent crews of Shrouds were hollowing out an entire mountain, carving its radiant stone into tier upon tier of empty archive.","Compared to what he had first assumed, an incursion force with a fortress behind it, this was something else entirely. This was a complex organization!","Ultimately, they came to one of the larger mountains, and Yrsa guided the cloud down toward a single purple tower on its upper slopes. The tower was tall, windowless, and smooth, and they passed through its gates on foot, his chains ringing softly in the quiet.","The halls inside were filled with Loomwrought Shrouds. They lined the corridors in stationary rows, filling alcoves and junctions, and some of them had clearly stood in their places for centuries. Not one turned its head as a leashed emperor walked past.","At a wide junction, another figure came out of a side hall. An Enforcer, judging by the layered robes and the purple gold sash, broad and scarred, with a ledger of light folded under one arm. He stopped when he caught sight of them, and looked Noah up and down with open appraisal.","\" Warden Yrsa .\" A nod. \"I heard you bagged a unique one?\"","\" Mind your own business, Enforcer Halvard.\" said Warden Yrsa, and kept walking.","The Enforcer laughed once behind them before his expression became cold as he moved on. Noah noted the exchange without comment.","The corridor ended at massive purple gold doors, and they ground open before Yrsa’s raised hand.","What lay past them was, of all things, a mess.","The great hall beyond was cluttered from wall to wall. Loomwrought Shrouds filled it, though not in ordered ranks. Some stood active, drifting between tables on silent errands, while others slumped against the walls and across benches as if they simply were not operational, white-wrapped bodies folded over in the manner of set-down tools.","Hundreds of collars and leashes lay strewn about in heaps and coils, gray bands and golden bands, whole and half-made and taken apart, spread across tables and hanging from racks and pooling on the floor between instruments Noah had no names for.","Yrsa entered with shining eyes, looking straight ahead, and Noah understood why quickly enough. At the center of the clutter sat an area where even he was forced to focus, because a boundless immensity rested there without bothering to announce itself!","A figure stood at a long table with his back to them.","He was tall and lean. Pale gold hair fell straight and unbound down his back, and every thread on him was royal: a long coat of deep black, high-collared, worked with fine gold embroidery down its seams, over a white shirt whose laced collar rose elegant at his throat, a dark half-cloak hanging from one shoulder.","Upon his brow, half-veiled by the pale hair, sat a small mark of pure obsidian. Amid all the mess of his own making, he alone was immaculate!","This was Descendant Mahishasura!"]},{"number":5620,"title":"Chapter 5620: Chapter 5619: THE ETERNAL PAX! III","paragraphs":["And at this moment, curiously enough, he was tweaking with an opened Loomwrought Shroud. The artificial lifeform lay spread on his table with its white wrappings parted and its inner weavings exposed, threads of refined Loom glowing softly around a dim core, and his long fingers worked inside it with total delicacy. When Yrsa and Noah arrived, he set his instruments down, turned around, and wiped his hands on a cloth.","Then he looked at Noah with shining eyes!","Noah looked back, and his own eyes flashed.","|Descendant Mahishasura|:: VERITAS: ????? PROVENANCE: ????? POTENTIA: ????? PONDUS: ????? A Descendant of ?????. His purpose here is ?????. ?????","Rows of veiled unknowns, where nearly every other being had opened to him. Apart from the name, and the fact of what he was, very little was visible at all. Compared even to Yrsa, whose panel had at least given him her numbers, this being was a closed book with a title on its spine!","His existence began to silently work to unmask more details of this being as just because they were question marks now did not mean they would be question marks in a few minutes as his Foundations and Appendages went to work!","\"A Lifeform that cured one of my Cursed Brethren.\" The voice came out soft, each word set down with care. \" You have outdone yourself, to bring such a creature to my door, Yrsa. \"","The amber gold eyes did not leave Noah.","\" In the weavings of the Descendants, a little rumor had risen, here and there. Something unique occurring among our Brethren on the far side of existence. I confess I dismissed it as the weavings of our people embellish themselves, as they do.\" A faint smile arose.","\"I never expected to have the one responsible standing in my workshop.\"","He looked Noah up and down slowly, and Yrsa nodded.","\"I wanted affirmation on what to do with him, since he is so unique. He was even involved with THE Sealed One. There are multiple unique threads of existence around him, and I...\"","As she spoke, she smacked Noah forward a step.","Descendant Mahishasura frowned.","\" None of that.\" The soft voice went stern, and the sternness filled the cluttered hall. \" Treat him with a level of respect, my dear Yrsa.\"","The admonishment visibly surprised her. Warden Yrsa, who had broken a finger and burst a steed’s skull with the same expression, blinked once, nodded, and stepped back. Noah looked at her coldly from behind his chains, and in his mind, nothing about her standing had improved. Her death had been decided long ago. The only open question was the order of it!","He turned the same cold gaze on the Descendant, tyranny sitting open in his crimson gold eyes, and when this fucker saw that gaze, he actually smiled, and walked closer through his own clutter.","\"I know, I know .\" He spread his elegant hands. \"It looks like we are the bad guys here, putting lifeforms in cages. I see how all of this looks. Truly, I do.\"","He stopped a few paces away, entirely at ease before a leashed emperor.","\" But nothing good comes easy. Many kings only ever achieved peace by killing millions first. You yourself, across your own life, have likely killed a great many to arrive at your peace... before we interrupted it. Yes?\"","He did not wait for an answer.","\" We are only containing lifeforms, at present. We had the option of genocide on the table, and we looked at it, and we said no. We are better than all the others. Let us simply collect them all.\"","He turned, pacing slowly along his tables, one hand trailing across a heap of half-made collars.","\" Two Ages ago, there was a Primeval One that grazed the borderlands of THE Infinite Carcosa. Old past records, and patient past measure. Every third of an Age, it would drink a Dimension. Every civilization inside, every Observable Existence, every small bright thing that had spent years becoming itself, swallowed in an afternoon, because a being with an appetite past all measure and the accountability of nothing happened to be hungry.\"","He glanced back at Noah.","\"It sits in a cage now, four columns east of this mountain. It has drunk nothing for a long while. Run the count yourself, Cure-Giver. How many countless decillions are alive at this moment, in Dimensions that still exist, because one appetite was subtracted? Weigh every despondent face you saw on the way here against that number, and tell me honestly which way the scale falls.\"","Noah said nothing, and the Descendant seemed to enjoy the nothing, and continued.","\" Or take a fresher example. THE Sealed One.\" The amber eyes glinted. \" We know him well. We hold multiple of his vessels in inhibition at this very moment. Bodies he spent Ages hollowing and seeding across existence, each one a plot with a pulse, each one meant to burn something down on a schedule only he can read. Every vessel we chained is a Dimension that does not burn. A court that is not hollowed. A war that never finds its excuse. He has noticed the silences, I am sure, and it unsettles him, and I consider that unsettlement a public service.\"","A soft laugh echoed, and then the warmth deepened!","\" The mighty of existence produce catastrophe the way harvests produce grain. Reliably. Seasonally. At scale. And existence has never once had a structure whose task it was to stop them. Not the Scales, which only rank them. Not the frameworks, which only feed them. Us. We are the first accountable thing existence has ever built, and our early reports from the resettlement Observable Existences say the first generations born there, with no authority anywhere among them, are the most peaceful populations in any record we hold .\"","He set a golden band down on the table. \" Cages are ugly. I know. But they are the ugliness of a hospital, not the ugliness of a slaughterhouse, and everyone in existence has been living in the slaughterhouse so long they have forgotten there was ever another building.\"","HUUM!","Mahishasura came to a stop before him again, and folded his hands behind his back, and his composed face held something genuinely curious.","\" Well. That is one thing. The other is how to put you to use.\" A slight pause. \" You see, I keep watch over some Cursed Descendants here. Brethren who earned the ire of Those Who Remain, and well... became Cursed for it. I have made promises to each of them, and now the being who can keep those promises has walked leashed into my workshop. \"","The soft voice did not change at all as he said it. \" Each of them will have their chance with you. And if you play ball... if you play along... even your freedom is not out of the question.\"","The amber gold eyes shone.","\"I am not trying to be some ridiculously evil guy here. I am very reasonable. Existence is give and take, and you currently find yourself in a predicament, and depending on how much you give...\"","A slight, elegant bow of his head.","\"...there may be a lot to take, Cure-Giver.\""]},{"number":5621,"title":"Chapter 5621: Chapter 5620: A Dance Beneath Budding Skies!","paragraphs":["Inside THE Infiniverse, a body of Noah floated quietly beneath the endless blue, looking up at the skies with a heavy gaze.","Of course, the heaviness had little to do with anything above him. It had to do with what was unfolding countless gigaparsecs away, before a main body that the members of THE ETERNAL PAX believed to be leashed, chained, and safely inhibited. An organization with grand workings and origins!","THE ETERNAL PAX.","As he turned the name over yet again, a figure came over the grass toward him.","One moment the stellar fields held only wind, and the next she was beside him, red hair loose over the white and blue of her robe, composed and unhurried, carrying her immensity so lightly that the grass barely bent beneath her feet. Since her wounds had closed, something in her bearing had settled as well, and what remained was simply grace with patience wrapped around it.","\" For you to have your cute serious face on,\" she said, \" you must have made a lot of progress in obtaining information.\"","Noah gave a light nod.","\" THE ETERNAL PAX. \" He watched the skies as he said it. \" So in addition to the threat of THE Sealed One, there is also an organization intent on enslaving all those who utilize authority, wherever they deem the holder unworthy of it. And both sides are likely backed by Those Who Remain.\"","He glanced at her. \"I have only now come across a single Descendant of Those Who Remain belonging to THE ETERNAL PAX. But can I assume there are many, many Descendants making up that organization?\"","He looked at the exquisite lifeform before him and waited.","After all, she could not tell him too many things explicitly, since every revelation about what was to come cost her a piece of what she was. But he had learned the shape of their arrangement by now. He reasoned aloud, and came to his own conclusions, and she could simply do something small.","Thalia nodded lightly, with a smile.","And Noah thought about it for a moment.","Existence was vast and full of terrors, and enemies and adversity were not at all scarce. If anything, the count of them only grew the higher he climbed. So the path forward was not complicated, however long it was!","He needed to continue becoming unfathomably powerful at an increasingly faster pace. He needed to keep forcing the very weight of all existence onto his quarks, filling them with his Provenance and his Teloi, becoming a grander version of himself particle by particle, all while continuing to spread his rulership across everything his hands could reach.","That was the most straightforward way of raising his attributes and his Provenance alike. And when he held enough power, everything else would fall into place. It always had!","As he was thinking about all of this, Thalia had come around in front of him.","Her hand was outstretched, palm up, as if she was asking him for something.","Behind her, on the distant cliff above the radiant river, his mother sat with Seo-yeon, and neither of them was watching the water. They were watching the skies. Because above all of them, something utterly exceptional was occurring.","\" Focus on the present ,\" Thalia said softly. \" Focus on the now. Look up to the skies.\"","HUUM!","The skies of THE Infiniverse were blooming.","Dozens of Observable Existences were being born above them. Wherever his people unfurled the Genesis Tesseracts under his guidance, blue-white geometry unfolded and opened, and out of each unfolding a newborn vastness bloomed into being, foundations declaring themselves, nine Prime Causes seating true around the honesty of each founder.","One moment a stretch of sky held only endless blue, and the next it held a young existence turning its first light, radiant and enormous and new!","And after every passing second, another one bloomed. Another, and another, births stacking upon births until the heavens of his home were a garden coming up all at once, hundreds of beginnings unfurling in silence above a farmland, a river, and a fishing cliff.","Compared to any wonder Noah had witnessed across his climb, and he had witnessed many, this was the one that made his eyes shine brightest!","Yes. Even for him, this was surreal. He had stemmed from a single Observable Existence. Even further down, he had stemmed from a single, tiny world.","One world of green and blue among an uncountable many. And now the seeds of Observable Existences were things he conjured and handed to his people, hundreds at a time.","For a human, he had truly come far!","\" Regardless of what is happening around you,\" Thalia said, her hand still open between them, \" you need to be the only one who decides how your emotions are flowing. Whether to be happy, or angry, or calm, or just neutral. Not your enemies. Not your circumstances. Not an organization that believes it holds your leash, and not a future that frightened even me. We can fail. Even I failed after coming back here and seeing you again. But...\"","Her voice stayed level, and warm underneath. \"A man controls his emotions. My Man controls his emotions. My Provenance... controls his emotions.\"","The faintest curve touched her lips. \"So, to anchor you down. Do not leave me hanging too much, and take my hand. Dance with me, while above you, something as grand as Observable Existences constantly budding sits in the sky because of your hands.\"","Dance? At such a time?","Noah looked at this utterly graceful and exquisite lifeform, her open palm, her patient eyes, the whole composed immensity of her waiting on his answer. And perhaps that was precisely her point!","If a man could dance at such a time, then no time would ever own him!","He took her hands.","DUM! DUM! DUM!","Existence itself began to play a symphony.","The sound rose out of the surroundings with no source at all, a symphony, a melody, deep notes rolling through the grass and the river and the light, and Thalia led him into it.","She drew his hands into place and brought her body close to his, close enough that he could feel her vibrant breath filled with immensity against him, and her feet began to move across the stellar grass, unhurried and certain, and his moved with hers.","They danced.","Below skies budding with Observable Existences, two figures turned slowly through the stellar grass, red hair and crimson gold, while above them beginnings bloomed by the hundreds, and on a distant cliff a mother watched her son dance with a woman from a drowning future, and said nothing at all, and smiled.","And all the while, Noah’s body continued the art.","THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis did not pause for the music. In truth, it settled deeper into him because of it. The weight of existence came down as it always came, THE Primordial Source and Infinity and THE Argent Loom and Time and everything imperceivable, and he ushered it seamlessly through the anatomy of his eleven singularities and onto a single quark, and then the next, and the next, bearing and seating and stabilizing in rhythm now, the whole crushing procession moving through his frame without a single thread of pressure escaping outward!","The grass beneath their turning feet did not bend. The river did not tremble. A mountain of everything was landing on him, particle by particle, and from the outside there was only a man dancing.","Was it her doing? Partly, perhaps. With a Provenance Lifeform in his arms, he could feel that her movements were doing something, some quality in the way she turned him and steadied him that his senses could not fully name, and she offered no explanation of it, and he did not ask for one yet.","But between her reminder on emotions, and the art running seamless through him, his Inner Peace, and the power of THE Infiniverse rising by the second as hundreds of newborn existences fed her vastness, something within Noah began to gather!","The music played. The skies bloomed. Her hand rested in his.","And Noah’s eyes changed.","The crimson gold of them drained away, and the singularity pupils faded, and what remained was blue. Endless blue, with no pupils at all, deep and grand and ancient and early all at once, the eyes of something that had been present before frameworks learned their names. He danced on without missing a step, and within him, everything accelerated!","The Baryogenesis surged. Where the weight had moved quark to quark in steady rhythm, it now moved three times faster, four times faster, the bearing and the seating and the stabilizing flowing together into a single continuous motion. And more than the pace, the depth changed. Improvements arrived in him unbidden, one after another, small profundities blooming fully formed: a truer angle for the weight to land, a cleaner braid of Provenance and Telos in the seating, a temper in the remaking that left each Provenance Telos Quark immensely more powerful than the hundred thousand that had come before!","He was not merely converting anymore. He was refining the art while performing it, and the art was refining him back!","| You have entered a Unique State of Existence: THE PROVENANCE REVERIE.|","|A state spoken of among the first Provenance Lifeforms, and attained by the exceptional among them. It exceeds Inner Peace. Where Inner Peace is the absence of argument within an existence, THE PROVENANCE REVERIE is agreement so complete that the existence and its surroundings begin to move as one. Existence itself becomes part of your limbs.|","| Within the Reverie: all processes of your existence are accelerated. Cultivation, generation, comprehension, and refinement flow together rather than in sequence. Profundities and epiphanies arise constantly and unbidden, each one an improvement to what you are and what you practice. Your arts may be advanced in the act of using them. Your perception deepens, and what you perceive, you may briefly wield as though it were your own body.|","|The entry was threefold: a heart that alone decides its weather, an art in seamless motion, and the hand of another Provenance in yours.|","| Cost: the Reverie drains the light of your Provenance Essence and of your existence itself to remain active. To hold it for long is to spend what cannot be easily replaced, and among the first of your kind, the Reverie was a thing of moments, entered rarely and exited poor.|","|However. Your existence holds Infinite Sanguine Mana atop your limited Provenance Essence. No record exists of a Provenance Lifeform sustaining this state upon an infinite reserve. The duration available to you is ?????.|","Glorious prompts, arriving one after another while the music played!","Noah held Thalia tighter in his arms, and they turned together across the stellar grass as wonder bloomed within him and around him in equal measure, quarks igniting by the thousands in his depths, beginnings igniting by the hundreds above!","And through all of it, the symphony went on, old past any counting, filling the surroundings from nowhere and everywhere at once, as if existence itself had drawn near to bear witness to the emergence of something utterly immense!"]},{"number":5622,"title":"Chapter 5622: Chapter 5621: Dimensionality! I","paragraphs":["The dance continued and simply grew quieter!","Somewhere between one turn and the next, the symphony had settled into a slow old melody, and Thalia’s steps had eased to match it, and the two of them moved across the stellar grass in small unhurried circles beneath a sky still budding with beginnings.","Since the Reverie asked for an art in seamless motion, the dance itself had become part of the cultivation.","Within Noah, the epiphanies had begun to arrive in streams!","Of course, they did not arrive as answers. They arrived as better questions, one unfolding out of another, each profundity opening a door that three more waited behind. And as the weight of existence came down onto quark after quark, as his attributes rose in slow increments with every hundred thousand particles remade, his thoughts kept returning to a single word that had been circling his climb recently.","Dimensionality.","|1,000,000 Provenance Telos Quarks converted. The quality of quarks remade within THE PROVENANCE REVERIE exceeds all prior conversions.|","|Your attributes have risen. VERITAS: 17. PROVENANCE: 13. POTENTIA: INFINITE. PONDUS: 18.|","What was Dimensionality, truly?","He had been collecting pieces of it for a long while without assembling them. The Argent Loom could only be perceived and used by those of high Dimensionality, and the fused authority of Infinity and THE Primordial Source was chased precisely because the fusion elevated it.","Climb far enough and others stop perceiving you!","Then there was his own Solipsism, which rendered him imperceivable to any being whose VERITAS and PONDUS both sat below ten. And there was the quiet fact he had noticed in the cages of THE Serenaros, where a Primeval One’s panel read in the low tens while a True Gilded Lifeform read below one, though both were called mighty by everyone beneath them.","So the pieces were there. Within the Reverie, they finally moved toward each other.","Perhaps Dimensionality was not a measure of power at all. Perhaps it was a measure of depth. How much of existence a being actually occupied, and how much of existence could actually reach them.","Power asked how hard a thing could push. Dimensionality asked where a thing truly stood, and the two questions only looked similar from far away.","Compared against everything he had witnessed, the model held! When his attributes had passed ten, an entire layer of existence had opened to his senses, the Argent Loom’s white rivers appearing where nothing had been, and beings who once read as blanks unfolding into panels.","Others below that wall could not perceive him at all. It was not that they were weak. It was that he stood somewhere their existence did not extend to!","A fish did not fail to see the mountain because the mountain hid. The fish’s whole reach simply ended at the water.","Thus, the attribute walls were not merely thresholds of strength. Every ten, existence itself seemed to admit a being one tier deeper.","And uniqueness bent all of it.","Two beings could stand on the same tier of Dimensionality, and if one of them was unique enough, if the gap in the quality of their depth ran wide enough, the unique one could still slip beneath the other’s perception entirely. His Solipsism was precisely that: not a trick of hiding, but a Precept written from a truth so singular that ordinary depth could not hold onto it. Yrsa perceived him because her panel cleared the double wall. But would she still perceive him if his uniqueness widened further? How wide did such a gap have to grow?","And was that the real reason his sight slid off Mahishasura’s panel, rows of veiled unknowns where every other being had opened? Not concealment, but depth beyond his reach?","He did not know. Yet!","So, since he was a being who sought to understand everything, Noah began to build a ranking.","He kept the backbone of it plain, and he measured it against the only proxy his sight could count: attributes .","But the more the pieces settled, the clearer it became that the walls did not fall every ten. There were only two shores he could actually verify, and one more he could only guess at across the water.","Below ten attributes was one kind of existence entirely.","He had lived in it. Nearly everything alive still did. Mortals, Monarchs, most True Lifeforms, entire civilizations of the mighty, all of them held within the same vast layer, able to perceive one another, able to reach one another, and entirely blind to what ran above them.","And what defined that layer, when he truly weighed it, was that everything within it could be counted. Their power had edges. Their reach had ends. Their reserves ran dry, their senses stopped at walls, their lives closed on schedules, and the frameworks that fed them measured out authority in finite portions to finite holders!","A whole layer of existence, magnificent and teeming, and every single thing in it was a finished sum.","He would call it THE FINITE VERSE.","Above ten attributes, existence changed its agreement with a being.","He remembered the crossing in his own body. The white rivers appearing where nothing had been!","Beings below the wall losing the ability to perceive him at all. It was not strength that had changed first. It was standing. Existence had admitted him past the edges of the countable, into a layer where the old sums stopped closing. Beings here reached across distances that had no business being crossed!","They held reserves that replenished from sources the Finite could never see, wielded authorities that compounded rather than depleted, perceived rivers and layers that ran through everything.","They had gone beyond the finite without yet becoming boundless, deeper than any count and still, somewhere far above, countable by something. His own footing. Skallagrim’s twenties. Yrsa’s twenty-eight. Primevals at their height, and what he had seen of THE ETERNAL PAX so far, all of them sharing this same deeper water.","He would call it...THE TRANSFINITE VERSE.","HUUM!","And above that?","Here his weavings ran out of verified entries, and hypothesis had to carry the rest. Was there a third wall at thirty? He doubted it, since Yrsa’s panel sat within the twenties and she read to his senses as the same kind of being he was, only deeper. At forty, then? Perhaps. But when he weighed everything he had seen, the veiled rows of Mahishasura’s panel, the auras seated on the inner mountains, the beings existence itself was supposed to agree with, his reckoning kept settling on a higher number. Fifty?","A wall at fifty attributes or above, past which his every instrument of understanding simply failed. Not a deeper water. The end of water as a description. A standing that could not be measured, compared, or even properly spoken of in the language of counts at all, where his sight returned rows of veiled unknowns not because something was hidden, but because nothing in him yet existed that could hold the answer.","He would call that hypothesized shore THE INEFFABLE VERSE!"]},{"number":5623,"title":"Chapter 5623: Chapter 5622: Dimensionality! II","paragraphs":["And as he finished outlining the framework within himself, the Reverie took his taxonomy and set it into record, prompts unfolding one after another in plain confirmation.","|Your framework of Dimensionality has been recorded.|","| THE FIRST DIMENSIONALITY: THE FINITE VERSE . Attributes above zero through ten. The layer in which nearly all of existence resides, and the only layer most of it will ever know. Every being here is a closed sum: finite power, finite reach, finite perception, finite time. They perceive only their own layer. THE Argent Loom, and all beings standing deeper, are entirely beyond their senses, and what they cannot perceive, they cannot touch, resist, or flee.|","|Empires rise here, frameworks crown their chosen here, and entire histories of the mighty play out here, all within a vessel whose walls the Finite will never see. To the layers above, the grandest wars of THE FINITE VERSE are...ants fighting.|","| THE SECOND DIMENSIONALITY: THE TRANSFINITE VERSE. Attributes of ten and above. Existence admits these beings past the countable. The Argent Loom becomes visible. The Finite become unable to perceive them unless perception is granted. Reserves, reach, and authority here exceed every closed sum of the layer below, yet remain ordered, comparable, and climbable: within this Verse, depth continues to matter, and a wide enough gap in attributes or in uniqueness may still place one Transfinite being beyond another’s senses, as your Solipsism already demonstrates.|","|Your current footing, the Wardens and Enforcers of THE ETERNAL PAX, and Primeval Ones at their height all reside within this Verse. It is deeper than any count of the Finite, and it is still not the deep end.|","|THE THIRD DIMENSIONALITY: THE INEFFABLE VERSE . Hypothesized. Estimated to begin at fifty attributes or above. Unverified by your senses. If it exists, it is the standing at which measurement itself fails: no panel opens, no comparison holds, no count closes, and no language of attributes properly applies. The Ineffable would be that which water, depth, and shore were always insufficient words for. To them, THE TRANSFINITE VERSE may appear as the Finite appears to you, and existence may not merely admit them, but defer. Candidates: the summit of THE ETERNAL PAX. THE Sealed One, should he attain what he seeks should be far past this Dimensionality. Those Who Remain may be far, far above this Dimensionality. ?????|","|The framework is yours, and it will be refined as your perception deepens. Hypotheses are recorded as hypotheses.|","...!","There was one more rung, and it sat below all the others, and it was the one that unsettled him. The inhibited of THE Serenaros, pressed to decimals, a True Gilded Lifeform reading below one. The Pax did not merely chain its captives. It pressed them beneath even THE FINITE VERSE, down into a shallowness that existence had never intended for anything, where everything could perceive them and they could reach nothing at all. Perhaps that was the true cage, and the metal boxes were only furniture.","|2,500,000 Provenance Telos Quarks converted.|","|5,000,000 Provenance Telos Quarks converted. The pace of THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis continues to rise within the Reverie.|","WAA!","The dance turned. The sky bloomed!","Thalia’s hand rested in his, and her eyes were closed now, and if she could feel the storm of reckoning moving through the man she was dancing with, she gave no sign beyond the smallest curve at the corner of her mouth.","And the epiphanies moved on, from what Dimensionality was to what rulership was, because in truth the two had been the same question wearing different clothes.","Rulership over a large portion of existence, and tremendously high Dimensionality...seemed like something that went hand in hand .","But how did one actually spread rulership across something as vast as existence? For Existence was vast!","The obvious road was the one he had been walking: take Dimensions, take Observable Existences, seat authority over territory and let the territory answer to him. It worked. It was also slow, and loud, and it painted a target on every border he drew.","THE ETERNAL PAX had partly noticed him because he ruled a Dimension...alongside the fuckery of THE Sealed One. Territory was rulership that announced itself.","HUUM!","Another epiphany arrived, fully formed in the manner the Reverie delivered its best ones!","He did not need to rule Dimensions. He did not even need to rule Observable Existences.","He needed to rule lifeforms!","Humans. Beings. The living, wherever they stood, whatever framework fed them. Territory was only ever a container for them!","And the moment he thought it, another memory surfaced to meet it","THE Infinity Eater.","A Descendant of Those Who Remain that did not rule an inch of territory, so far as any record showed. And yet it was the source of Infinity itself for entire populations of Infinite Lifeforms, beings who drew their seas from threads the Eater lent, and most of them did not even know. They believed their Infinity was their own. They built lives and Pantheons and empires on a borrowed wellspring, and somewhere far away, a single being held the other end of every thread.","Was that not rulership of the deepest kind? No borders. No banners. No target painted anywhere, because the ruled did not know they were subjects. The Eater did not govern where its dependents stood. It governed what they were made of!","Could he not extend his rulership the same way?","The question opened, and the Reverie poured into it, and the pieces of his own existence began raising their hands one by one.","His Infinite Sanguine Mana. An inexhaustible ocean, generated from within, unperceivable to beings beneath his depth, already proven to pass through loomlight itself untouched. What was Infinity, to an Infinite Lifeform?","A reserve that answered when called. If threads of his mana could be spun fine enough, thinned past all perception, and set where Infinite Lifeforms drew their power, would their calls not be answered just the same? They would pull, and something would answer, and the something would be him!","He could become a source of Infinity, the wellspring beneath other beings’ seas.","And his Provenance Essence. Rarer, dearer, limited where the mana was not, but of a purity that predated frameworks entirely. THE Primordial Source was the other great root that Source Lifeforms drank from, dense foundational being itself.","Could refined essence, or the light it shed, stand in that place? Could he become a source of THE Primordial Source and Infinity, so that Infinite Lifeforms, Gilded Ones burning their Egos bright and Source Lifeforms deepening their patient cores were, at the very bottom of their draw, drawing on him?","Two wellsprings. One infinite, one precious. Between them, they touched nearly every variety of powered lifeform existence had produced!","Which left only the question of reach. How did one lay a wellspring beneath beings scattered across Dimensions and Observable Existences beyond counting?","For a moment he considered the Argent Loom, since the Loom already did something similar, invisible rivers threading all of existence, unperceived by everything beneath the Second Tier. But the thought discarded itself almost as quickly as it formed. The Loom was not his!","It was the Pax’s industry and, if Skallagrim’s theory held, an extension of the thoughts of Those Who Remain. Building his rulership on a borrowed road meant the road’s owner could close it, and he had rejected borrowed foundations once already, on obsidian sands, with an entire system watching.","No. The answer was already inside him, and it had been all along.","His Infinite Sanguine Mana was not perceivable by those beneath him. That was not a limitation. That was the entire mechanism. An infinite, self-generated, imperceivable substance, spun into threads finer than any sense that would ever check for them, spread outward across existence the way his blood already answered him across any distance, latching quietly onto the draw of every lifeform that reached for Infinity, for Source, for power it assumed was its own!","No conquest. No announcement. Every pull, answered. Every answer, a thread of rulership!","They would never even realize!","HUUM!","The dance turned once more beneath the budding sky, and Noah held that design in the endless blue of his pupilless eyes, complete and patient and enormous, and only one small question kept turning quietly at the edge of it.","The seat he intended to occupy already had an occupant. Somewhere across existence, THE Infinity Eater held the other end of countless threads.","And what did such a being do, he wondered, when it noticed a second hand on his rulership?","|10,000,000 Provenance Telos Quarks converted.|","|Your attributes have risen. VERITAS: 19. PROVENANCE: 16. POTENTIA: INFINITE. PONDUS: 19.|","...!"]},{"number":5624,"title":"Chapter 5624: Chapter 5623: Glory! Quintessence!","paragraphs":["His immensity rose rapidly as the Reverie went on, and within it, Noah had arrived at the edge of a decision!","The design was complete in him. Threads of Infinite Sanguine Mana, spun finer than any sense that would check for them, laid beneath the draw of lifeforms who believed their power was their own. All that remained was the first test, and the test had an obvious ground.","THE Ymnaros, fused and healing, where the folding of THE Vaelos had delivered millions of Infinite Lifeforms into his territory, weak and strong alike, every one of them pulling on seas they had never once questioned. He gathered the first threads at the edge of his existence, and prepared to let them go.","And THE Infiniverse shook at such a time.","HUUM!","It was not an attack, and he knew that within the first fraction of the tremor, because the shaking carried no wrongness in it at all. It carried the opposite. It moved through the grass and the river and the blooming skies in slow, enormous waves, and it felt, more than anything else, the manner in which a held breath feels when it is finally released!","Thalia’s hand tightened once in his. On the distant cliff, his mother had risen to her feet.","Prompts began to unfold, and they did not stop!","|More than 1,000 Observable Existences have now emerged within THE Infiniverse.|","|One thousand First Causes and foundations. Nine thousand seated Prime Causes and above, each declared true around its own founder, all of them rooted within a single containing existence. No record holds a precedent for this structure. The Causes do not merely reside within THE Infiniverse. They back her. A Dimension ordinarily stands upon its own foundation alone. THE Infiniverse now stands upon thousands.|","|Her Dimensionality has risen past all prior measure, and continues to rise.|","|A Unique Precept has arisen for THE Infiniverse: THE PRECEPT OF THE UNFOUND HEARTH.|","|Its truth: a home is not a place. A home is an arrival. What seeks THE Infiniverse as a place will never find her, for she has ceased to be findable in the manner of places. She may now traverse: gathering the whole of herself, every Realm, every nested Observable Existence, every life she holds, and crossing to elsewhere within reach of nearby Dimensions in a single unperceivable motion. These crossings are designated HEARTHSHIFTS. A Hearthshift emits nothing, disturbs nothing, and may not be perceived, predicted, or followed by any being of insufficient depth. Those within her will know they have moved only if she tells them.|","| THE Infiniverse is transforming. Designation: a UNIQUE TRANSFINITE DIMENSION.|","|She has crossed the wall your framework names. Her reserves no longer close. Her reach no longer ends. She is the first Dimension in your records to carry an Intent, a Precept, and a thousand rooted foundations at once, and existence has admitted her into deeper standing accordingly. The Finite may dwell within her without ever perceiving what holds them. The Transfinite may stand within her and still not find her edges.|","|And from the joining of her new depth with your Infinite Sanguine Mana, something is rising through her that belongs to no framework and no record.|","| Rivers of authority, unique to THE Infiniverse, are forming. Designation: THE CRIMSON WEFT.|","|THE CRIMSON WEFT runs through the whole of her: through every Realm, every nested Observable Existence, every life she carries. It is unperceivable to all beings and all instruments, at any depth, with a single exception: you. Its current is your Infinite Sanguine Mana. Its nature is binding: where the Weft touches an Observable Existence or a Dimension, within her or beyond her, it may latch, quietly and completely, and what it binds becomes reachable, anchorable, and holdable. A bound point may serve as an anchor for a Hearthshift. A bound existence may be fed, protected, or drawn upon through the Weft without ever perceiving the thread. Where THE Argent Loom is a road built by others and watched by others, THE CRIMSON WEFT is grown, and it is yours, and no eye in existence has been built that can see it.|","|The Weft deepens with every Observable Existence that takes root within her. It has only begun.|","...!","The prompts settled, and the changes began!","Across THE Infiniverse, the countless Realms answered her transformation one after another. Skies deepened in color, richer than any eye within them remembered. Rivers of light ran fuller. The thousand young Observable Existences turned brighter in their cradles, and between all of it, visible to exactly one being in all of existence, thin crimson rivers rose and began to thread themselves through everything, through farmland and citadel and sanctuary, through the roots of newborn foundations, unhurried and silent and everywhere at once.","Noah watched the Weft weave itself through his home, and on the far cliff, Seo-yeon laughed at something she could not see but could somehow feel, and the sound of it carried across the water.","Was this what the Pax had, when they looked upon their Argent Loom? He doubted it. The Argent Loom was inherited, and argued over, and possibly the extension of someone else’s thoughts. This had grown out of a mother and a bloodline and a thousand honest declarations, and there was no committee anywhere inside it!","So, with his home transforming around him and the Reverie still burning steady on its infinite subsidy, Noah released the threads.","His Infinite Sanguine Mana left him without sound or light. It passed out of THE Infiniverse along the first bound points of the Weft, crossed the dark, and entered the fused Ymnaros Dimension, and there it began to spread across the countless gigaparsecs where the millions of THE Vaelos lived.","Infinite Lifeforms beyond counting, from sovereigns commanding old escalations down to the young and thin whose infinities barely filled a valley, all of them going about the hours of a Dimension recovering from an incursion, grieving their dead, rebuilding their terraces, scared of a Blood-Crowned One most had never seen.","And beneath every one of them, unperceivable and patient, the threads arrived!","They simply settled where each lifeform’s draw of Infinity met its source, finer than any sense that would ever check, and waited for the next pull. And when the next pull came, as it always came, the seas answered as they had always answered, and the answering was subtly different now, and not one being in all those gigaparsecs noticed the difference!","Their Infinity felt fuller, if anything. Cleaner. A well that had always been theirs, running a little sweeter than yesterday!","They had begun to pull from another source. The source was him!","|Your rulership is extending along a road no instrument can register.|","|104,318 Infinite Lifeforms across THE Ymnaros now draw, in part, upon your Infinite Sanguine Mana as the wellspring of their Infinity. They perceive nothing. The count is rising.|","|418,772 Infinite Lifeforms now draw upon you.|","|1,296,439 Infinite Lifeforms now draw upon you. Every draw deepens the thread. Every deepened thread widens your standing. Rulership, as you have redefined it, is no longer a matter of territory: it is a matter of substance. You are becoming what your subjects are made of.|","Noah stood in the stellar grass with his eyes of endless blue, watching numbers rise that no border would ever contain, and it was at this moment, of course, that the two halves of him chose to hold a discussion!","\"It works ,\" THE Provenance of the Closed Crown said. \" So the only question left is pace. And I say we stop waiting for existence to get thirsty on its own.\"","\"Meaning what, exactly? \" THE Open Hand asked, though its tone suggested it already knew.","\" Meaning that a well nobody needs is just water in the ground.\" The Crown’s voice ran low and unhurried, and there was a great deal of patience in it, and none of it was gentle!","\" Listen. Every lifeform that pulls on Infinity, or Source, or any framework’s allowance, already depends on something. They simply depend on it invisibly, the same as they now depend on us. The Infinity Eater holds many threads. The frameworks meter out their portions. Those Who Remain built ladders and own every rung. Existence is already a web of wellsprings, and every one of them has an owner, and not one of those owners asked permission either. We would not be introducing dependence into a free existence. We would be competing for dependence in a market that has never once been free.\"","And here the Crown’s voice settled, and the whole Reverie seemed to lean in to listen. \" We become the best water in every valley. Wherever a framework rations its chosen, our thread runs a little fuller. Wherever a source runs thin, ours arrives without being asked. Wherever the Pax subtracts authority and leaves the mighty as beggars, we are the quiet spring the beggars find. We never demand. We never announce. We simply out-provide every wellspring in existence until pulling from us is not a choice anyone remembers making, because it will feel to every one of them the way breathing feels. And then, when enough of existence is made of us...\"","\" We never close the well. We give them free access to abundance, and everyone whose depths we run through will come to understand, slowly, in the marrow where understanding actually lives, that their next breath was always going to be drawn through us.\"","HUUM!","\"You do not rule beings by commanding their choices. You rule them by becoming what their choices are made of. That is tyranny perfected, and it requires no cage, no collar, and no Pax. Existence itself becomes the leash, and we never even have to pull it.\"","Silence held for a moment across the turning dance.","\" We make certain that what flows through the threads is genuinely better than what flowed before, \" the Crown said. \" Fuller Infinity. Cleaner Source...immensity! Glory! Quintessence!\"","The Hand did not answer that.","And Noah, turning slowly through the stellar grass with Thalia’s hand in his and a million threads deepening beneath a distant Dimension, listened to the tyrant half of his own Provenance lay out the road, and found, with no argument anywhere in his existence...","That he agreed!","Let them draw from him! And they would find their Infinity greater, their Source sweeter and grander!","His...would be the only source they would ever pull from as any other source would feel lackluster!"]},{"number":5625,"title":"Chapter 5625: Chapter 5624: The Severed Demesne!","paragraphs":["The dance ended the way it had begun, with her deciding!","The old melody wound itself down to a last few notes, and Thalia drew him close on the final turn, and rose onto her toes, and kissed him on the lips.","It was a single action, soft and brief and entirely unhurried, and it very nearly broke him out of the Reverie. Warmth moved through his existence with no permission asked, and the endless blue of his eyes flickered once, and steadied!","’ This woman...’","\"I can sense your Provenance pulsing with momentum, \" she said, still close. \" Continue with what you need to do. I will ensure all those who are potential targets of THE Sealed One finish the emergence of their Observable Existences. I will also introduce myself to Barbatos and the others.\"","A faint curve of her lips formed. \" And I will keep an eye on anything coming across Dimensions and Time.\"","She said such words, and then she moved away from him like a dream, unhurried across the stellar grass toward the distant cliff, and his mother and his daughter were already waving her over.","Noah watched her go.","Then, with his eyes still shining stellar blue, he spoke to the whole of his home.","\" Infiniverse...conduct your first Hearthshift. Take us from THE Ymnaros.\" He paused. \"I will leave one clone behind to brief Anaximander and the others...\"","|Understood, Master.|","HUUM!","And there was, of course, a strangeness in what came next, which was that almost nothing came at all!","No engines lit. No skies tore. Within THE Infiniverse, the rivers kept running and the thousand plus young Observable Existences kept turning, because a home does not tremble when it arrives somewhere new!","Only two beings in all of existence perceived the motion itself: a mother gathering the whole of herself, every Realm and foundation and life she carried, and stepping, once, across the dark.","|THE Infiniverse has conducted her first Hearthshift.|","|Departure: the fused Ymnaros Dimension. Nothing perceived her leaving. Nothing can follow.|","|Now drifting across Existence.|","WAA!","|Drifting...|","|Drifting...|","|Drifting...|","WAP!","| Arrival: a wandering Dimension, one of many sundered fringes of THE Source Lands that broke away across the ages over time. Local designation, drawn from the memory of its inhabitants: THE SEVERED DEMESNE.|","|Composition: Source Lifeforms, including True Source Lifeforms. Depth assessment: every living being within this Dimension resides within THE FINITE VERSE. None possess the standing to perceive you, THE Infiniverse, or THE CRIMSON WEFT, under any circumstance, even should you walk among them.|","A severed edge of THE Source Lands!","Noah found it quietly remarkable. He had stood in the Source Lands before. And yet here drifted a piece that had simply broken off it, ages ago, and gone on living alone, a limb that had outlasted its body’s memory of losing it.","’ How many such fragments are scattered across existence? How many pieces of eternal things?’","The Weft was already moving. Crimson rivers only he could see threaded out from THE Infiniverse and latched, quietly and completely, onto the drifting Dimension, binding it as an anchor, and through those threads his Infinite Sanguine Mana began to flow outward. But this time, the mana did not travel alone.","It carried glimmers of his Provenance Essence within it.","Since Infinity answered Infinite Lifeforms, and THE Primordial Source answered Source Lifeforms, and his essence was a thing of purity that predated frameworks entirely, the design followed plainly enough.","The mana would be the river. The essence would be what the river carried. And the Source Lifeforms of this Dimension, drawing as they had always drawn on the deep patient foundation of all things, would find their draw answered by something a great deal closer, and a great deal purer, than anything that had ever answered them before!","Noah went to see it done personally.","He appeared above a grand citadel floating in the open dark, and no alarm anywhere in existence stirred.","The citadel stretched beneath him in ordered tiers of pale stone and dense golden light, light years across from its outermost terraces to its radiant heart, and millions of Source Lifeforms moved through it, patient beings of settled luminance going about their hours, markets and sanctums and long contemplation halls where rows of the ancient sat in stillness with their cores glowing softly. And it was one citadel of dozens!","His senses counted them scattered across the Dimension, each one vast, each one old, an entire civilization built by beings who had never once perceived the walls of the vessel holding them.","He descended, and walked among them.","He passed through a market where a Source Lifeform haggled over crystallized Source foundations. He walked the length of a contemplation hall past a hundred seated ancients, close enough to touch the oldest of them, a being whose luminance had the deep worn steadiness of ages, and not one head turned, and not one sense so much as itched. To THE Severed Demesne, nothing at all was happening this afternoon!","And beneath all of them, the threads settled into place.","His Infinite Sanguine Mana, carrying its glimmers of essence, slid silently beneath the point where every Source Lifeform’s draw met its source, and replaced what answered. No pull was interrupted. No draw was denied. The next time each being reached for the foundation of all things, the foundation reached back, and it was him!","The old one in the contemplation hall opened his eyes.","\"...\"","Around him, one by one, the other ancients stirred from their stillness, and looks were exchanged down the long hall, wondering and quiet, because every one of them had felt the same impossible thing in the same second!","\" Elder... did you also...?\"","\"...THE Source seems Closer...\" The oldest one’s whisper barely left him. \" It feels... closer! Oh!\"","...!","THE Primordial Source felt closer than it had ever felt in the whole of their long lives. Grander. Warmer, if such a word could be used for the deep foundation of existence!","In the market outside, a lifeform sat down in the middle of the street and wept without knowing why, and across dozens of citadels and light years of dark, in a thousand halls at once, the Source Lifeforms of a severed fragment turned toward their own depths in wonder.","And for a rarer few, the change ran deeper still.","|Note: this Dimension contains True Source Lifeforms who also cultivate Infinity. 217 among them actively pursue the fusion of Infinity and THE Primordial Source.|","The fusion path!","Here at the Finite depth it was pursued the way the Finite pursued everything, blindly and bravely and mostly fatally, generations of True Source Lifeforms grinding at a joining that hurt nearly all who attempted it.","And in this hour, all 217 of them stopped what they were doing.","Because it had suddenly become so much easier! The two great currents they had spent lifetimes forcing toward each other now ran, at their deepest point of draw, out of a single wellspring, and currents from one source do not fight their joining. Across the Dimension, many bolted upright in their sanctums and began sensing their own existences with something between disbelief and reverence, feeling a lifetime’s impossibility soften in their hands!","Oh!","No war. No conquest. Not a drop of blood shed anywhere beneath him.","And Noah was extending his rulership grandly.","Minutes passed, and the permeation completed itself. His glimmering essence settled beneath every being in the Dimension that had ever touched THE Primordial Source, and his mana beneath every one that had ever touched Infinity, and where a lifeform cultivated both, both draws quietly became him.","|Your rulership has extended across THE SEVERED DEMESNE.|","|38,114,209 Source Lifeforms now draw upon your Provenance Essence as the wellspring of THE Primordial Source. They perceive nothing.|","|1,120 True Source Lifeforms now draw upon you. 217 now draw upon you through both currents at once. Their pursuit of the fusion has been eased beyond all precedent. Whether this proves a gift or a consequence is unrecorded.|","|Attention: your Provenance Essence is not infinite. Sustaining all current draws consumes 0.0000001% of your essence per second. The rate will rise with every Dimension claimed. As of now, the cost is negligible.|","...!","Noah looked at those last words for a long moment, and his shining eyes were tyrannically heavy.","The cost was nothing, today. But he had not designed this road for one Dimension. He had designed it for existence, and existence would multiply that small number by millions!","A wells that can run dry... is a throne with a crack in it.","So the answer was the same answer it had always been, the one running through his quarks at this very moment. Generate faster than existence could drink. Become a source that made the word finite a stranger!","\" Infiniverse ...\" he said quietly. \" Let us initiate the next Hearthshift. Let us...continue on.\"","| Understood, Master.|","WAA!","And as his home gathered herself for her second step across the dark, the Baryogenesis within him surged faster still. The weight of existence came down and his quarks drank it in accelerating rhythm, and he could feel his Dimensionality rising quicker for what he had done, as though existence itself were adjusting its opinion of where he stood, deepening the water around a being who had become the foundation beneath forty million others!","And at this moment...","HUUM!","His existence rang!","It was not pain and it was not power. It was fullness. Every corner of what he was drew taut at once, his singularities, his organs, his remade quarks, all of it arriving together at some shared brim, pressing outward against a boundary his senses could feel but not name, a membrane at the very edge of everything he currently was!","|100,000,000 Provenance Telos Quarks converted.|","| Your attributes have risen. VERITAS: 20. PROVENANCE: 20. POTENTIA: INFINITE. PONDUS: 20.|","|All of your attributes now stand at 20. None have yet crossed the wall.|","...!"]},{"number":5626,"title":"Chapter 5626: Chapter 5625: Cure-Giver!","paragraphs":["As his existence advanced and began to expand his rulership across Lifeforms...his body in one of the domains in THE ETERNAL PAX continued its role of a Prisoner.","There was a door in the back of Mahishasura’s workshop that did not look like it went anywhere important.","Yrsa walked him through it on his golden leash, Mahishasura leading with a host’s unhurried pleasure, and between one step and the next, the workshop was gone.","Sunlight fell from no sun.","White marble colonnades. Terraced gardens. Olive trees older than some frameworks, shallow pools mirroring a ceiling pretending to be sky, couches of carved marble circling long low tables, the smell of crushed herbs and old wine!","Compared to the cage-fields outside, it was a paradise. Compared to anything honest, a display case.","And lounging through the whole of it were Cursed Descendants.","’ Seven,’ Noah counted behind his cold expression. ’ And not one curse is the same....’","At the longest table, a mountain of a being ate. The table held enough to feed a citadel. He worked through it with both hands, steady, joyless, and the food replenished itself, and so did his emptiness!","By the largest pool, a slender Descendant lay with a wine bowl on her stomach and her eyes shut, two silent Shrouds refilling it, and her stillness had nothing of rest in it.","Near the entrance, a lean flushed figure declaimed poetry to three Shrouds that had not been built to applaud, his voice pitching louder whenever a living gaze drifted off him.","And at the farthest couch, apart from everything, one Descendant sat upright with his hands folded, watching the door they had just come through.","\" Brethren .\" Mahishasura’s soft voice carried without being raised. Every head turned. The eater paused with his hands full.","\" You have waited a long time, and you have heard me make a great many promises. Today, I have outdone them all as...The Pax Provides.\"","HUUM!","He stepped aside. He gestured to the leashed man, and made the gesture a small ceremony.","\"I have brought you... your cure.\"","Silence.","Then the wine bowl slid from the slender one’s stomach and rang against the marble, and she was sitting up, and the hall broke open with voices!","The mountain at the long table looked the leashed man up and down slowly, and did not stop chewing.","\"... Are we supposed to eat him?\"","\"Baelgrim.\"","\"It is an honest question. You say cure, and you point at a creature. \" He swallowed, and his voice came down flat and hard. \" That is a man on a leash, Mahishasura. The fuck is this?\"","\"I have brought you the being who unbound a recent Curse from our distant cousins in THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension.\"","The dice stopped rattling.","The poet’s mouth hung open mid-verse. The slender one rose from her couch entirely, and when she spoke, her voice had gone quiet and careful!","\" We heard only weavings of rumors of that. Nothing more.\"","\"Weavings of rumor are how such truths travel across Existence, across the thoughts of our Fathers.\"","Mahishasura drifted toward the couches, one hand trailing the marble. \"I confirmed it through memories Yrsa here obtained herself. A Cursed Descendant of THE Krazhor-Nul walks free of his sentence, alongside a rather unfortunate dead Steed that died for those memories to be obtained.\"","...!","Yrsa’s expression did not move.","His eyes quietly flashed, and the room unfolded into panels.","|Descendant Baelgrim|:: VERITAS: 24. PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 23. PONDUS: 26. Cursed by the ire of Those Who Remain: THE CURSE OF THE BOTTOMLESS TABLE. He has not felt full in eleven thousand years.","|Descendant Sylvaine|:: VERITAS: 27. PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 25. PONDUS: 24. Cursed by the ire of Those Who Remain: THE CURSE OF THE SHARED WOUND. Every harm she authors arrives in her own flesh first.","|Descendant Othrys|:: VERITAS: 21. PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 22. PONDUS: 20. Cursed by the ire of Those Who Remain: THE CURSE OF THE UNREMEMBERED NAME. Whoever looks away from him forgets him. His deeds remain; his name does not.","|Descendant Kharvel|:: VERITAS: 29. PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 27. PONDUS: 28. Cursed by the ire of Those Who Remain: THE CURSE OF THE UNSLEEPING WATCH. He has been made to require sleep and has not slept since the sentence was spoken. He sees more than he wishes to.","Each one was uniquely cursed as the curses themselves tremendously interested Noah!","\" Then why is the supposed thing capable of stripping away curses leashed? \" Othrys had crossed half the hall already, hungry-eyed, planting himself where the most gazes would have to pass through him.","\"If it can do what you say, it is worth more than...many, many things. Why is a thing like that wearing a collar? Or is thst precisely the reason why?\"","\"Because before he is the cure, he is the Pax’s prisoner. \"","Hungry gazes all honed in on Noah from many sides!","And then, from the far couch, without rising, a voice worn smooth by many sleepless nights.","\" What does it cost?\"","The hall quieted. Sylvaine glanced back at the watcher, then at Noah.","\" Everyone who gives something wants something,\" Kharvel continued, patient, terrible, calm.","\" Cure-Giver....What does your cure cost?\"","Every gaze in the pocket Dimension settled on the leashed man.","And at both sides of Noah’s head, his own voices echoed out in his mind!","\" Look at their power and standing, \" THE Closed Crown said, low and appreciative. \" We can cure their curses while applying our marks on them, being sure to entrench our Provenance Essence so deeply into their existences and code that they don’t even sense it. They will purposefully not get a high tier as at our choosing...we will command them to begin going against this domain and The Pax overall. Descendants...at our beck and call.\"","HUUM!","\" Brother ,\" THE Open Hand said, with something close to warmth, \" there are times I like you. This is a sound plan.\"","HUUM!","Both sides of him agreed!","So he lifted his gaze, chains ringing softly, and answered the only question that had been put to him.","\" Healing a Curse of Those Who Remain is unfathomably difficult work. What sits in each of you is not an illness. It is authored weaving of existence, braided through every clause of what you are.\"","His cold eyes traveled the couches, the pools, the mountain of food, the unsleeping watcher.","\" I will need access to the entirety of your existence while I do it. All of it. One of you at a time. And if I face any rejection from you while I am altering the weavings of your existence and releasing the curse... your existence itself could collapse.\"","He let that settle across the marble.","\" And in doing all of this is my freedom. Yes?\" His gaze moved, slow and level, to Mahishasura. \" Which means I will also need this collar to be removed so I can access my authority.\"","...!","The pocket Dimension went very quiet, and every Cursed gaze in it swung from the leashed man to their host, and their host’s composed face gave back nothing at all.","Silence held for one heartbeat longer.","Then Baelgrim laughed, huge and hollow, and shoved his endless table back with a scrape that rang down the colonnades.","He rose to his full mountain height. \" I will go first, Cure-Giver!\"","...!"]},{"number":5627,"title":"Chapter 5627: Chapter 5626: Curing and Shackling!","paragraphs":["Of course, the collar came off!","It was never truly a question, however long the silence had stretched after his demand.","Mahishasura had spent his credibility assembling this room, and made promises to every ruined lounger in it. What was a question, and an interesting one, was how frightened they would allow themselves to look while paying it.","\" Remove it,\" Mahishasura said.","\"....\" Yrsa’s eyes looked at Noah as if in a warning as she did not yet nove.","\" On my authority, and on my head, my dear Yrsa. \" The soft voice did not rise. \" Remove it.\"","She crossed to Noah without another word, and her pale eyes held his for one long moment, and then she reached out.","CRACK!","THE GILDED CLAUSE opened and slid from his neck, and the golden chains uncoiled from his wrists, and every being of power in the pocket Dimension pulsed at once!","Mahishasura’s immensity rose behind his composed face. Yrsa’s twenty-eight PONDUS leaned forward against the air. Along the colonnades, Loomwrought Shrouds turned their wrapped heads in perfect unison, and even the Cursed on their couches gathered themselves, seven ruined powers coiling, a whole hall of drawn bows aimed at one unbound man!","And the unbound man released... a silent pressure.","Nothing so crude as power. He simply stopped pretending to be nothing, and let a measured portion of something settle outward through the marble and the pools and the olive trees, presence without shape, weight without direction, and the drawn bows found there was nothing to loose at.","He watched them all hold their eruption and then he raised one hand and beckoned, calm as a man calling for tea.","\" Come.\"","WAA!","The mountain came.","He crossed the hall slowly, and sat where Noah pointed, and up close his curse was audible, a low ceaseless complaint from within him, eleven thousand years of a body demanding what it would never receive!","Noah’s wordlessly raised his hand as he didn’t care for small talk, he would find out everything he wanted soon enough!","Crimson gold rose from his palms and drew itself into blades, thin and precise and humming, and he set them to the Descendant’s existence and opened it, and the pocket Dimension held its breath.","What lay inside was a sentence.","One unbroken line of unreadable script, running backward through every ancestor to a hand that had spoken it before frameworks had names, and braided through it, black through gold, with a curse.","THE CURSE OF THE BOTTOMLESS TABLE!","Noah read it once, coldly.","Then he began to unwrite.","The blades moved. The curse fought, the manner in which all authored things fight their unwriting, clauses screaming as they came apart, and Baelgrim’s mountain body shook, and his hands crushed the marble bench beneath him to powder!","HUUM!","Noah was not at all gentle as the process took some time, the minutes rolling by a Descendant tried not to curse!","Clause by clause. Thread by thread. And beneath the visible working, in the same breath, in the same motion, invisible to every eye and every instrument in the pocket Dimension, his other work ran!","As each cleaned clause resealed, something else settled into the seal, written in the same unreadable script the lineage itself was made of.","|The counter-writing of THE CURSE OF THE BOTTOMLESS TABLE has been unwritten at the root.|","| The lineage of Descendant Baelgrim has been resealed. Within the seal, THE PROVENANCE BLOOD MARK has been written as grammar of the line itself. Designation: VEILED.|","|Nothing in existence perceives the Veiled Mark. It is not an addition to be found. It is the language the sentence is now written in.|","|Descendant Baelgrim: a VEILED BLOOD MONARCH. All bindings, boons, and options are withheld from expression until you call upon them. Available to you, at your choosing, forever: his senses. His memories. The option of command. The option of an ending.|","The blades withdrew. The opened existence closed!","And Baelgrim sat very still on the powdered remains of the bench, and his face went strange, and stranger, and his hands rose slowly to his own stomach.","\"...\"","\" Baelgrim?\" Sylvaine, half-risen across the hall.","\"It is... quiet .\" The mountain’s whisper cracked. \" My stomach... it is quiet.\"","His breath started coming ragged. \"All these years, and it is... it is QUIET in here!\"","He stood, and swayed, and looked at the endless table still heaped with food, and turned his back on it as he felt nothing!","Then Descendant Baelgrim, the Bottomless, put his face in his hands and laughed.","Mahishasura was already moving.","He circled the cured Descendant slowly, and his amber eyes had gone bright and sharp, and his long fingers traced the air around Baelgrim’s body, reading, testing, hunting.","This fucker was confirming that everything was normal and there was nothing they couldn’t see!","\" The Curse unwritten...haha, that is nuts!\" the Enforcer murmured.","He looked up at Noah, and smiled, and the smile held delight and something else. \" You do clean work, Cure-Giver.\"","\"I said what I take, I take from the curse. \" Noah’s voice stayed flat. \" Who is next?\"","...!","The next hours remade the room.","Sylvaine came to him with her eyes set, and left the working an hour later shaking, and stood in the middle of the hall, and drew the blade she had not truly used in an Age, and cut the air, and waited, braced, for the echo of harm that had answered every violence of her long life.","Nothing arrived!","She cut again. Again. Faster, wilder, a storm of edges in the marble hall, and nothing arrived, and she stopped with her chest heaving and tears running silently down her face!","Othrys could not sit still for his. He talked through the opening, talked through the pain, talked until the unwriting reached the clause that had eaten his name, and then he went silent for the first time since Noah had entered this Dimension.","When it was done, he stood, and looked around the hall at his gathered brethren, and asked...","\"...Look away from me. All of you. Look away, and then look back.\"","They did.","\" Othrys, \" Baelgrim said.","\" Say it again.\"","\"Othrys, \" said Sylvaine!","And the Descendant of the Unremembered Name sat down on the marble floor right where he stood and wept into his hands while his own name went on being said around him!","The three loungers from the deep couches came one after another, an hour apiece: a Descendant whose shadow had been cursed to strangle what she loved, a Descendant cursed to age one Age for every lie he spoke, a Descendant whose curse Noah did not name aloud, and unwrote just the same.","Each opened. Each unwritten. Each resealed, cured, and Veiled to the root of what they were, rising incredulous and radiant into a hall that grew louder and warmer with every rising.","|Descendant Sylvaine: a VEILED BLOOD MONARCH.|","|Descendant Othrys: a VEILED BLOOD DUKE.|","|Three lineages resealed. Three VEILED BLOOD MONARCHS.|","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing notes what is being given. Grand salvations, granted to beings of the Transfinite Dimensionality. What pools within the Tide has moved past its prior precedent, and continues to grow. It has not yet been asked for.|","And then only one remained.","Kharvel crossed the hall unhurried, upright, and awake. He sat where the others had sat, and folded his hands, and his unsleeping eyes held Noah’s from an arm’s length away, and for a long moment he said nothing at all.","\" One question, Cure-Giver. \" His worn voice came level. \" Before you open me. If I see something inside your cure that I was not meant to see and you wish to quiet me... what happens to me?\"","The hall’s warmth thinned. Across the marble, Mahishasura’s amber gaze sharpened, and Yrsa’s pale one, and the cured Descendants went quiet.","\" There will not be anything not meant to be or see ,\" Noah said.","\"I have not slept in many years. I see everything. It is the one thing I do.\"","Noah remained quiet and didn’t reply!","The unsleeping eyes searched him for one moment longer.","\"... Begin.\"","The blades rose. The existence opened. And this working ran longest of all, and Noah unwrote all of it, clause by clause by clause, while the hall stood silent and the grammar settled invisibly into every seal.","|The counter-writing of THE CURSE OF THE UNSLEEPING WATCH has been unwritten at the root.|","|Descendant Kharvel: a VEILED BLOOD SOVEREIGN. The Veil holds. Nothing perceives it.|","The blades withdrew. Kharvel sat still.","Then his shoulders came down from a height they had held for eleven millennia, and his unsleeping eyes blinked once, slowly, and blinked again, and a look of pure animal disbelief crossed the most watchful face in the pocket Dimension.","\"... Heavy ,\" he whispered. \" My eyes are... heavy.\"","WAA!","He did not make it to a couch. Descendant Kharvel, twenty-nine of VERITAS, the watcher of watchers, lay down on the marble floor of the hall right where he was, and closed his eyes, and slept for the first time in many years, and the sound that came out of him was a snore!","HUUM!","The hall broke into celebration around the sleeping body. Wine and roaring laughter and Othrys’s name still being said, Baelgrim’s empty quiet stomach toasted by the whole roaring hall, Mahishasura moving among his collected brethren accepting their gratitude with elegant modesty, every promise he had ever made them kept in a single day!","And at the edge of it all stood the Cure-Giver, unbound and uncollared, watching the celebration with eyes that had gone entirely cold.","’ Seven Descendants. Dance! Laugh! Rejoice! You are can be puppets or be killed...at any moment!’","...!","Apart from being able to collapse their Existence and control it, he could also peruse their memories!","Of course, he did not need their permission, and he did not need their waking, and no instrument in THE Serenaros would register so much as a whisper of what came next!","Somewhere beneath the laughter, along seven threads written into the language of seven existences, the option he had built for himself opened quietly for the first time.","Noah gazed at his cured, celebrating, unknowing Veiled.","’ Show me...your memories.’","And he began to read!"]},{"number":5628,"title":"Chapter 5628: Chapter 5627: The Unfinished Command!","paragraphs":["Seven libraries of memories opened at once.","Of course, from the outside, nothing at all was happening. The hall roared on around the sleeping body of Kharvel, wine moving, Othrys’s name still being said for the joy of saying it, and at the edge of the celebration stood the Cure-Giver with cold eyes and a stillness that read as weariness to anyone who bothered to look.","Inside that stillness, along seven threads written into the grammar of seven existences, Noah read.","And the first thing he learned was that memory has architecture, and one Descendant in particular had the clearest memory!","The others gave him texture. Kharvel gave him everything.","The structure of THE ETERNAL PAX assembled itself across his depths, memory by memory.","At the bottom, the Loomwrought Shrouds. Made, not born, grown in batch-halls around cores of refined Argent Loom, the labor and the soldiery and the furniture of the whole institution, and no one above them thought of them at all!","Above The Shrouds, The Wardens. And here the memories grew thick with ambition, because Wardenship was a career. Wardens earned their standing in counts: collars logged, collections completed, incursions closed without loss, every capture entered into ledgers that followed a Warden!","Wardens competed. Wardens were sponsored, patron Enforcers lifting promising collectors out of the field, and a Warden whose records ran long and clean enough might one day be raised to a mountain.","Because Enforcers like Descendant Mahishasura held mountains!","Each Enforcer of THE Serenaros kept a peak of the inner rings as seat and fief, with Wardens sworn beneath them and Shroud soldiers of their own!","Above the Enforcers sat an Arbiter , one to a Dimension, governor of the whole of it, and the memories of the Arbiter of THE Serenaros all shared one strange quality.","They dimmed near the center.","Every memory that approached the blinding heart of the inner rings lost its edges, detail sliding away the closer any Descendant had ever walked toward that radiance.","’ Even their memories avert. Interesting.’","And above The Arbiters, spoken of always in lowered voices, sat THE Still Conclave.","Nine seats. The summit of the whole Pax, its members almost never seen. Nine beings who answered to nothing beneath them and to only one thing above.","The Voice.","Kharvel had not been there at the founding. But Kharvel had watched a Descendant who had.","And the memory of the founding was a grand one!","A gathering of beings of terrifying depth assembled on a bare plain of purple gold, Descendants among them, Primeval things among them, and every one of them standing the way children stand when summoned. No figure appeared. No shape descended.","There was only the Voice.","It arrived without direction, from everywhere and from inside, and it was not loud and it did not need to be, and the memory itself still shook at its arrival!","\" Too many unworthy things are playing with authority.\"","Noah shuddered!","His actual body, standing in a marble hall gigaparsecs from any memory, shuddered, once, from the sheer registered weight of a voice heard thirdhand!","\" Reduce the count across existence, meaningfully.\"","’ Who .. .’ Even his thought came unsteady. ’ Which one of them is this?!’","But the memory did not know!","The Descendant who stood on that plain had never learned it. None of them had. The gathered terrors of that day had gone to their long lives and their eventual sentences without ever knowing which of Those Who Remain had spoken!","\" And only stop when you are told to.\"","The Voice ended. The memory ended.","And Noah stood in the celebration hall with cold sweat at his temples and rage arriving right behind it, rage at the fear itself!","He had shuddered from a voice of Those Who Remain!","He shuddered like a Finite thing in a storm as he was enraged!","’ How dare I feel fear from merely hearing the voice of such a being? They are not beyond existence. They are lifeforms! Grander Dimensionality, grander depth, and nothing more than that. Nothing more!’","HUUM!","And beneath the rage, he replayed the last message of whatever one of Those Who Remain had uttered","Only stop when you are told to.","He searched Kharvel’s archive for it as...","No stop order had ever come.","The whole towering machine of THE ETERNAL PAX, The Wardens and their records, The Enforcers and their mountains, the Arbiters and the Conclave and the cages running gigaparsecs in every direction, all of it was still executing the last sentence of a command spoken by one of Those Who Remain!","An unfinished command. An engine with no braking instruction, collecting existence piece by piece, waiting with perfect institutional patience for a word that no memory suggested was ever coming.","He internally shook his head as he continued.","The memories of their Lineages came next, because the cured seven carried three of them in their blood.","Descendants, the memories confirmed, did not descend from Those Who Remain generally.","Each line ran back to one architect, one specific being of that grander Dimensionality whose spoken sentence had become a bloodline, and the lines differed the way their architects differed.","Messages into the existence from Those Who Remain were rare for all of them, a fortune or a catastrophe once in a lifetime if it came at all. But the shape of the silence differed.","THE Sleepless Fiend, whose line Baelgrim and two of the couch-loungers carried, spoke seldom and transactionally, bounties and bargains, an architect who treated its own blood as a workforce.","THE Unblinking Shepherd, whose line ran through Kharvel and Othrys, never spoke at all. Its Descendants lived their whole spans inside the feeling of being watched, a pressure of attention with no message in it ever.","And THE Weeping Architect, whose line Sylvaine and the shadow-cursed one carried, sent no words either. Its messages arrived as griefs. A sorrow with no source, settling into a Descendant’s existence for a year or a century.","Three architects!","Noah held the pattern up against everything else he carried.","This was basically a workforce of Those Who Remain!","And then, in a certain memory, he found the exception.","The memory belonged to the liar-cursed Descendant as it told a grand story.","Wardens and Shrouds by the thousand, Inhibitors in racks, the single greatest collection operation the archive held. Target: the great Infinite Lifeforms of a far reach.","Among the targets: THE Infinity Eater.","And....the operation failed.","The only recorded failure of THE ETERNAL PAX!","And after it, the order had come down through THE Still Conclave, and the order was the true treasure:","Cease all operations against THE Infinity Eater. Cease all operations against the Infinite Lifeforms in specified areas!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly as he understood why!","Collaring Infinite Lifeforms stifled their draw of Infinity. And their draw of Infinity was the Eater’s harvest. Every great Infinite Lifeform the Pax subtracted was income subtracted from a fellow Descendant of Those Who Remain, and so the word had come down from somewhere above the Conclave, and the word was stop!","And right now...","Noah was drinking from the Eater’s protected watershed at this very hour, thread by imperceivable thread.","’ What does the farmer do when he notices a second hand on his crop?’","...!","One more thing surfaced before he closed the seven libraries, small and sharp, from the gossip that every institution carries.","Warden Yrsa.","The memories of the cured held her at ceremonies but always slightly apart, always slightly deferred as she was a...","Progeny of a Descendant and a Primeval One. And the Primeval One sat on THE Still Conclave.","One of the nine.","’ Well .’ Noah watched the plain woman across the hall, the woman who had broken his finger to check a seal, whose death he had decided on a battlefield gigaparsecs ago.","It didn’t fucking change a thing. She would still die!","Around him, the hall roared on as he...began seeing budding outline of a plan!"]},{"number":5629,"title":"Chapter 5629: Chapter 5628: Accountable!","paragraphs":["The celebration was winding down when Warden Yrsa appeared behind him with the golden collar open in her hands.","\" Your service has concluded, big guy\" she said. \" Protocol resumes.\"","Noah lowered his head slightly, and let her close THE GILDED CLAUSE around his neck, and the click of it rang through a hall that had gone quiet and uncomfortable at the sight, seven cured Descendants watching their miracle be leashed again.","\" None of that ,\" Mahishasura had said hours ago, about a shove.","He said nothing at all about a collar.","And within Noah, behind the lowered eyes of a compliant prisoner, his two halves were in session!","\" We have everything, \" THE Open Hand said. \" All the memories. The plan was information, and the plan is complete.\"","\" The plan has matured, \" THE Closed Crown answered. \" Look at the room, brother. Every asset of this workshop is standing in one sealable box. An Enforcer whose measure we now hold. A Warden whose blood ties to the ninth chair. Seven Veiled Descendants that answer to our commands. This opportunity will not reassemble itself easily\"","\"So...\"","\" Kharvel watched Mahishasura for two thousand years without blinking. \" The Crown’s voice echoed. \" The seven compared themselves to him constantly. Their reckoning agrees: deep, but not past the middle thirties in attributes. Four of them hold him for a breath. Seven hold him for longer. Seven, plus surprise, plus a sealed Dimension, plus us... hold him for as long as we need.\"","\" And Yrsa?\"","\" Yrsa ,\" said the Crown, \" is mine.\"","A pause, and then the Hand, quietly: \" Seal the box.\"","HUUM!","It began with nothing anyone could see.","Along seven threads written into the language of seven existences, options opened. Not commands, not yet, only readiness, and seven celebrating Descendants felt nothing at all as their bodies became pieces on a board they could not perceive!","Through the Weft-thread bound quietly to this pocket Dimension a while ago, crimson rivers only one being could see slid across every seam and door and fold of the marble abode, and latched, and held.","The box sealed. No signal would leave it. Nothing would leave it!","Then, gently, a thread pulled.","Baelgrim, laughing, waved Mahishasura over toward the long table. \" My friend! Come, sit with us. For years I could not taste food, only need it. Sit, and watch a man eat for joy.\"","And Mahishasura came, of course, smiling his composed smile, drifting into the heart of his collection’s happiness, accepting wine he did not drink, seating himself among cured brethren!","Sylvaine drifted to his left, telling him of the blade. Othrys took his right, making him say the name again. The three loungers closed in behind with their cups, warm, adoring, casual.","And across the hall, on the marble floor, Kharvel’s eyes opened from the first sleep of many millennia, clear and rested and calm, and he rose without a sound.","Yrsa noticed none of it. Why would she? A host among his grateful cured, a hall full of joy, a prisoner standing collared and docile at her side.","Seven Descendants moved in the same instant, in complete silence.","No shout. No flare!","Baelgrim’s arms closed around Mahishasura’s body from the side with the whole of a mountain’s mass behind them, Sylvaine’s blade was through his shoulder before the wine in his hand had finished falling, Othrys and the three took his limbs, and Kharvel arrived last and struck once, precisely, at a point below the Enforcer’s ribs where its lineage was written heavily, and the composed immensity of Descendant Mahishasura hit his own marble floor under the mass of his entire collection!","BOOOOM!","The pocket Dimension shook!","\"Wh-\" Yrsa’s wravings of protocol shattered!","Her pale eyes went wide, flicking from the pile of silent violence to the exits that were no longer exits, shock and horror arriving on a face that had never once worn either. \"What... what is-\"","And beside her, the collared prisoner rose from his docile stillness, unhurried, and rolled his neck against the golden band.","\" Crazy stuff, isn’t it?\" Noah said mildly. \" Existence is truly vast, and full of terrors.\"","...!","Yrsa turned to him very slowly, and the shock on her face cooled and hardened into something ancient.","\" This is your doing?!\"","Noah did not reply.","Instead, at the sides of his head, two small figures of stellar blue-gold stirred, and one of them, the cross-legged one, bowed out, and the other, arms folded, dark gold at its edges, opened its eyes for the first time.","\" My turn,\" said THE Closed Crown.","And it stopped being a figure at his temple, and became him.","HUUM!","The transformation rolled through Noah’s body from the marrow outward. His stature rose, broadened, settled heavier, shoulders widening beneath a mantle of pressure that bent the marble floor into a shallow bowl beneath his feet!","Dark gold bled into the crimson of his aura and hardened at its edges. His hair lifted and darkened at the roots, his features cut themselves a fraction crueler, and his eyes went deep burning gold with black singularity pupils, the face of the tyrant half worn openly at last!","THE GILDED CLAUSE, still locked around his neck, sat on him now the way jewelry sits on a king.","| THE PROVENANCE OF THE CLOSED CROWN has fully embodied your existence.|","|For the duration of the embodiment, the sundered half acts as the whole. All processes are surrendered to dominion.|","|Your attributes have momentarily exceeded the wall. For the duration: VERITAS: 25. PROVENANCE: 25. POTENTIA: INFINITE. PONDUS: 25.|","Yrsa looked at the tyrant standing in her prisoner’s place, at the collar doing nothing, at everything her records had recorded about him burning down in a single second.","She roared as she moved!","Hundreds of Loom-blades tore into being around her in layered orbits and fell on him as one, and the battle began, and it was cold and it was brutal!","He did not dodge. Dodging was for the light. His body had become unfathomably heavy, twenty-five of PONDUS packed into every limb, and he walked forward through the blade-storm as white edges rang off his frame and opened thin lines that closed before they finished opening, and his right arm rose and fell like an ancient hammer, reinforced in Provenance Essence.","BOOM!","The blow caught her shoulders and drove her through a colonnade, through a second, into the terraced gardens in a trench of shattered marble!","His Quarks were grand!","He was a Provenance fucking Lifeform!","He held IMMENSITY!","She rose spitting blood, blades reforming, and her calm was gone now, fully gone.","Blood drops rose around him, crimson gold with stellar light, and went out in fans. Detonations walked across the garden in even rows, eating her Argent Loom ring by ring, and she answered with a lance of woven white that took him through the shoulder and out the back, and he closed his hand on it and let his weight arrive.","CRACK!","The lance shattered. She was already behind him, both palms to his spine, and the pressure of twenty-eight PONDUS driven to its edge slammed him face-first through the garden and into the bedrock of the pocket Dimension itself!","She was still powerful!","\" You should have stayed a prisoner ,\" she breathed, pressing down, blades regathering above her back in a rising thicket. \" You should have-\"","\" Kharvel ,\" said the Crown silently.","The Descendant of the Unsleeping Watch had never stopped moving since his first strike. He came out of her blind angle and hit her exactly there!","It bought one moment of shock and horror from Yrsa!","The Crown used it whole. Noah’s body turned inside her broken body of blades, seized her wrist, folded her guard inward with a hammer-blow that collapsed her defense entirely, and plunged his hand into her chest.","Blood drops flooded in behind it. Crimson gold poured through her existence in rivers, drops seeded into every current of her, and with them went the Mark, gripping her Lifeline, closing around everything she was, and Warden Yrsa’s pale eyes went very wide and then very dim as her body seized and her orbits of white rained down dead around them both!","He did not withdraw his hand.","He walked, and dragged her with it, back through the ruined gardens, through the broken colonnades, into the marble hall where Veiled Descendants held a heavily injured Enforcer pinned to his own floor.","Mahishasura’s black-and-gold coat was torn, his pale gold hair was matted dark, and his amber eyes, sighting the tyrant coming on with the Warden’s body hanging from his buried hand, went grave, and then hateful, and stayed hateful.","Noah stopped above him, and stood over everything.","The sealed Dimension. The pinned collector!","The dead-eyed daughter of the ninth chair dragged forward like a settled account!","Seven Descendants kneeling!","Dark gold pressure rolled off Noah in slow tides that bent the wine pools flat, and when he spoke, the Crown gave every word the unhurried weight of a thing that had already happened.","\" You built a very reasonable case, Enforcer. I listened to all of it. The appetite subtracted. The vessels chained. \" He crouched slowly, bringing his burning gold eyes level with the hateful amber ones, Yrsa’s body settling on the marble between them with his hand still seated in her chest.","\" But your own Warden taught me the true doctrine of your Pax, on the day she took me. She stood over everything and she told me that followers are merely followers. \" His voice dropped lower, colder, final.","\"It is always those who lead... that need to be held accountable.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5630,"title":"Chapter 5630: Chapter 5629: Idols!","paragraphs":["His left hand was seated in the chest of a Warden!","His right hand rose, and sanguine blades gathered along it, and came down, and split the chest of Descendant Mahishasura open to the sentence beneath.","The Enforcer did not scream as his hateful amber eyes stayed locked on the tyrant working above him, seven of his own collection pinning his limbs to his own marble, and Infinite Sanguine Mana poured into two opened existences at once, rivers of crimson gold running left and right from a single unhurried figure, and as he worked, the Crown-embodied Emperor began to talk.","\"I once knew a guy who spent months carving an idol out of solid lapis lazuli.\" His voice ran calm, conversational, and almost warm. \" Every morning, without fail, he bowed before it. Utterly convinced it was something special.\"","The blades moved deeper!","\" Then one afternoon, another student struck it, and it shattered into a thousand ordinary blue pebbles.\"","Mahishasura’s jaw clenched. Yrsa’s dim eyes fluttered. The rivers ran on!","\" You see, we have this tragic, almost laughable habit of manufacturing idols out of common clay. But the weavings of existence are remarkably egalitarian. If something possesses a physical shape... if it was brought into being... and if at the end of its long, inflated day, it can die...\"","The blades reached the deepest clause, and held. \"... then it does not deserve a single knee bent in its direction. Reverence is an illusion sold to those too terrified to stand up straight.\"","His burning gold eyes came level with the hateful amber ones.","\" Those Who Remain are no grander than the dust settled on my feet. They do not deserve your worship. \" A pause, precise as a blade finding its seam. \" And frankly... neither do you.\"","BOOM!","The rewriting began.","Crimson gold flooded both opened existences at once, and within Mahishasura, the work ran the way it had run seven times this day, but inverted, because there was no curse to unwrite and no consent anywhere in the room. The blades held the lineage open against its bearer’s will, clause by fighting clause, and into every reseal the grammar went, written in the script the sentence itself was made of, and Descendant Mahishasura felt every word of his own remaking and could not stop one letter of it.","|The lineage of Descendant Mahishasura has been opened by force.|","|THE PROVENANCE BLOOD MARK has been written as grammar of the line. Designation: VEILED. Nothing in THE ETERNAL PAX will perceive the writing.|","|Obedience: absolute. Cognizance: intact, at your choosing.|","|Descendant Mahishasura: a VEILED BLOOD SOVEREIGN, bound to command.|","And within Yrsa, the flood found less to fight. Her defenses were already collapsed, her Lifeline already held, and the Mark closed over the whole of what she was, daughter of a Descendant and a ninth chair, and gripped it, and waited for its instruction.","The hall settled. The rivers stilled.","And Noah rose to his full embodied height above the two opened bodies, dark gold pressure rolling off him in slow tides, and across the sealed pocket Dimension, every Descendant knelt.","For the seven, it arrived as their own hearts rising. Gratitude, awe, the plain sense that kneeling to the being who had unwritten years of sentences was simply correct, and Baelgrim went down first with tears still drying on his face, and Sylvaine followed, and Othrys, and the loungers, and Kharvel last among them, each of them certain to the root of their resealed lines that the kneeling was a choice!","For Mahishasura, it arrived as a command.","His torn body gathered itself off the marble against every screaming instruction of his own will, and folded, and knelt, and his cognizance was entirely there for all of it, his composed face wrecked around eyes that blazed with pure unwilling hate, an Enforcer of THE Serenaros kneeling on his own floor with his chest still open, and knowing precisely why!","|Descendant Mahishasura|:: VERITAS: 34. PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 32. PONDUS: 33. A Descendant of ?????. He had never once been made to kneel. He is kneeling now.","The Crown read the panel slowly, savoring the last line, and then crouched again before the kneeling Enforcer, forearms on knees, casual as a man talking over a fence.","\" Now. From your own mouth.\" His voice stayed mild. \" Tell me just how I can fuck up THE ETERNAL PAX the most .\" He tilted his head. \" And you know what. I will not even call it that anymore. Because it is not something eternal, and it will not be something eternal. Just THE PAX will do.\"","Mahishasura’s jaw worked against the grammar, and lost.","\"... Slowly .\" The word came out of him dragged and furious . \"You do nothing loud. Nothing fast. The Pax is not a fortress you break. It is a Record you corrupt.\" His hands shook against his own knees.","\"I return to my mountain, cured brethren at my side, my credibility without limit after this day. And from that seat, I begin to extend... this. \" His eyes flicked with hatred toward his own opened chest.","\" Enforcer by Enforcer. There are those who owe me. Those who envy me. Those who will come to see the cured and want to know how. Each one drawn into a room like this room, one at a time. And when enough Descendants of my standing carry your grammar in their lines... when the Enforcers of enough mountains are yours...\" The grammar dragged the last of it out of him.","\"... then, and only then, do you reach for the Arbiters. One seat-Dimension at a time. And THE PAX will go on reciting its creed in perfect order, provides, protects, subtracts, never once perceiving that its own hierarchy has become your instrument, until the hour you decide it learns.\"","BOOM!","The hall held silence around the counsel. Seven kneeling faces shone with reverence at strategy they believed their savior had inspired.","Noah smiled calmly.","\" Good ,\" he said. \" You will begin tomorrow.\"","Then he turned his burning gold gaze down, to the body still hanging from his left hand, and the smile went away entirely.","\" And now, Warden. Your account.\"","He drew her up by the chest until her dim pale eyes hung level with his, her feet clear of the marble, blood-drop light pulsing softly through her seized frame.","\"I promised you a death, \" the Crown said. \" I decided it in the crossing-dark, over a headless steed. That promise stands. But your collapse would ring, Warden. A daughter of the ninth chair, ceasing, would be felt in rooms I am not ready to visit. So.\" His hand shifted slightly within her chest. \" You will be given another form of death. Quieter. Fuller.\"","Her dim eyes found his, and somewhere very far down in them, understanding surfaced, and with it, for the second time in one day, fear on a face that had never worn it.","\" Your memories. Your sense of self. Erased.\" He said it the way she had once said protocol. \" Warden Yrsa will continue to exist, to every eye of THE PAX. But Yrsa...\" The blood drops within her began to turn. \"... will no longer exist.\"","...!","\" You ...\"","\"I offered you salvation once. In the crossing-dark. I told you that moment was your fork in the road.\" The drops turned faster. \" You chose your cause. I am merely keeping to my word.\"","HUUM!","Within him, at the edge of the embodiment, THE Open Hand said nothing at all.","And the erasure ran.","It was not violent. That was the cruelest part of its craftsmanship. The blood-drop light moved through her existence in slow, thorough tides, and everything it passed through, it settled, and everything it settled, it emptied.","A childhood in the shadow of a ninth chair. The pride of a plain woman among terrifying blood, shacklings, one broken finger, one kept promise, one shuddering Voice, all of it dimming tide by tide behind her pale eyes while seven kneeling Descendants watched their savior work and a kneeling Enforcer watched everything with hate that had gone very quiet and very old.","|The memories of Warden Yrsa have been erased.|","|The sense of self of Warden Yrsa has been erased.|","|What remains: a body, a rank, an obedience, and your grammar. Warden Yrsa will answer to every eye of THE PAX. Yrsa will answer to you. Yrsa, as she was, no longer exists.|","The hand withdrew from her chest at last, and the wound sealed behind it without a scar.","She settled to the marble on her own two feet, swayed once, and steadied. Her plain face composed itself, feature by feature, and her pale eyes opened, and there was nothing behind them of what she used to be. No rules. No cause. No count!","And in the center of a sealed pocket Dimension, ringed by kneeling Descendants, beneath the burning gold gaze of THE True Human Emperor, the last body in the hall folded smoothly downward.","Yrsa knelt!","And she knelt without a glimmer of hesitation!"]},{"number":5631,"title":"Chapter 5631: Chapter 5630: Authorities and Fluff!","paragraphs":["The embodiment ended grandly.","Dark gold drained back out of the crimson, the tyrant’s stature settled into the emperor’s, and the burning gold eyes cooled to endless blue as THE Provenance of the Closed Crown withdrew to its small folded-arm seat at his temple, looking satisfied with itself.","| The embodiment has ended. All attributes have returned to 20.|","And behind that prompt, more rose, and they did not stop rising!","|Your VERITAS has risen tremendously. Your PONDUS has risen tremendously. Your PROVENANCE has risen tremendously.|","|Cause: your current actions, weighed as truth lived at the deep Transfinite, and THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis, which has not paused once through battle, embodiment, rewriting, or erasure. Quarks remade within THE PROVENANCE REVERIE continue to exceed all prior conversions.|","|Assessment: the wall past 20 was meant to be hard. It was meant to be arduous, and long, and to break most of those who ever reached it.|","|At your current pace, it will likely be climbed within the next few minutes. Hours, at most.|","Grand actions gave grand results!","And Noah, restored and unhurried, looked around the ruined celebration hall of a sealed pocket Dimension, at seven kneeling Veiled and one kneeling Enforcer and one kneeling instrument, and decided that since nothing could leave this box, nothing needed to leave it just yet.","There was one more piece of work to do here.","\" Up ,\" he said. \" All of you. And you...\"","He looked at the thing that had been Warden Yrsa.","\" Come here. Hands and knees.\"","She came, and folded, and Noah seated himself upon the back of the Warden of THE PAX the way kings seat themselves on thrones they have not finished judging, one ankle across the opposite knee, entirely comfortable.","Among the Descendants, no one objected. Why would they?","\" Now .\" Noah settled back. \" The battle was too fast. Multiple Descendants of Those Who Remain moved in my service and I saw perhaps a tenth of what any of you are. That will not do. I intend to know my instruments to the last thread.\"","His cold blue gaze traveled the hall. \" Show me your lineages. One at a time. Baelgrim.\"","The mountain grinned, and rolled his shoulders, and looked around the cluttered hall for something worth the showing.","He chose a Loomwrought Shroud.","\" My line runs from THE Sleepless Fiend ,\" he rumbled, walking toward the slumped artificial soldier. \" And our Father’s gift is simple, Cure-Giver. He owns everything he has ever touched.\"","Both huge hands closed around the Shroud’s wrapped frame. \" So do we. For a while.\"","HUUM!","White light shuddered through the Shroud’s body, and its core, a thing grown and keyed and sworn to THE PAX across centuries, simply changed hands. It stood at Baelgrim’s gesture. It knelt at Baelgrim’s gesture. It turned its wrapped head toward its own racks of collars with an obedience its makers had never installed, and Baelgrim released it, and the ownership drained away over a few breaths, and the Shroud slumped back into the Pax’s inventory none the wiser.","\" Touch, and tithe ,\" Baelgrim said. \" Weapons. Armaments. Authorities, if my grip is deeper than their seat. My cousins can do it to stranger things.\"","The two Fiend-line loungers demonstrated. The first laid her palm flat against the ambient dark and claimed the sliver of Infinity threaded through it, blue rising off her skin in a brief stolen sea.","The second pressed one finger to the marble floor, and for ten long seconds the entire terraced garden was his the way a hand is his, stone flexing when he flexed.","\" The Fiend’s blood claims...okay \" Noah observed from his seat.","\" Kharvel.\"","The watcher rose, rested and terrible!","\" My line runs from THE Unblinking Shepherd,\" he said quietly. \" And the Shepherd’s gift is that the flock is always found.\"","His eyes closed. And every Loomwrought Shroud in the pocket Dimension straightened at once.","\"I am seeing through all of them ,\" Kharvel said, eyes still shut. \" Forty-one Shrouds, nine functional. I am seeing through all of them.\"","His eyes opened, and they were pale-rimmed now, ringed in faint white. \" Anything that has ever been watched, my line can watch from. And anything I have marked...\"","He looked at Noah, and inclined his head slightly. \". ..I would find across Dimensions, until one of us ceased. The Shepherd does not lose sheep. THE Argent Loom itself is a trail to us.\"","Othrys followed his lineage-brother, and his display was the inversion of eleven thousand years of sentence. He walked the length of the hall and was not noticed doing it, not by the seven, not by the instruments, a presence folded out of every attention in the room at will, and then he stood at its center and unfolded, and every eye arrived on him at once.","\" They cursed me with the broken half of my own gift,\" he said, and for once he did not perform the words. \" Attention, with the ownership stripped out. Thousands of years of it.\"","He bowed low to the man seated on the Warden. \"It is mine again.\"","Noah nodded and looked at the next one.","\" Sylvaine.\"","She drew no blade. Instead she raised one hand, and reached into the unseen, and pulled.","Threads of THE Argent Loom came down into the visible.","White rivers, the same authority that ran the collars and the roads and the Inhibitors of the whole towering institution outside, gathered into her palms in obedient skeins, and she began to build. Blades first, a hundred of them, forged of braided loomlight.","Then the blades became ribs, and the ribs became an architecture, a vaulted lattice of white edges assembling itself above the hall, vast and precise and strangely beautiful, a cathedral-frame of pure cutting authority filling the pretend sky.","And it keened.","A low note ran through every strut of it, soft and unresolved, a construction that mourned its own standing, and Sylvaine looked up into her own work with an expression that held old questions.","\" My line runs from THE Weeping Architect, \" she said. \" We build with THE Argent Loom the way our Father built before us. And everything we build... grieves. We have never learned why. Our messages arrive as sorrows. Our works arrive singing them.\"","Her hand closed, and the lattice folded itself away into nothing, and the keening stopped.","The shadow-cursed lounger built after her, a fortress of layered dark raised and razed in half a minute, its walls weeping slow black light at every seam.","And through all of it, Noah sat on the back of a Warden and watched.","\" Claim, watch, build ,\" said the Crown. \" The Fiend takes, the Shepherd finds, the Architect makes. Three weavings, and THE PAX runs on all three of them...\"","At last, Noah’s gaze settled on the final kneeling figure.","\" Enforcer. Your turn.\"","Mahishasura rose with his torn coat and his quiet old hate, and did not choose a Shroud or a thread or a trick.","He simply opened his hands.","And the entire pocket Dimension’s Loom answered.","Every river of white in the sealed abode rose at once, out of the collars and the racks and the slumped Shrouds and the seams of the walls, an ocean of authority lifting into the air in perfect surgical order, and it turned above them all, and where it turned it worked: a broken Shroud on the far table unmade itself to threads and remade itself whole, the shattered colonnades of the Yrsa battle knitted stone by stone, hairline order sweeping the ruin out of the hall in a single conducted pass.","He closed his hands. The ocean settled home. The hall stood repaired.","\" My display,\" he said flatly, \" is that Those Who Remain use THE Argent Loom, and I understand it immensely. If not for being swarmed and sneak attacked, I would have not been defeated...\"","It was straightforward and grand!","Noah rose from his seat, unhurried, and stood at the center of the repaired hall, and delivered the lesson.","\" You have all shown me wonders, but...\"","\" Existence is terribly fond of novelty. It offers an endless, glittering weaving of abilities, authorities, and specialized tricks, all of it designed to make us feel clever. But in the grand, infinite weavings of existence, all those infinite variations are usually just theatrical fluff. When the curtain falls, the entity with the sheer, crushing weight of raw power wins the battle. Nine times out of ten... mass breaks nuance.\"","WAA!","\" Except, of course, for that rare, terrifying creature who carries the one authority that unmakes everything entirely. A truly unique authority will rewrite the rules before you even realize you have sat down at the table. \"","His endless blue eyes moved slowly across seven reverent faces and one hateful one and one empty one . \"I mean... look at what happened to all of you, when put against me. You were more powerful than me. You had more abilities than me. Every one of you, deeper, older, richer in gifts.\"","He spread his hands slightly, taking in the hall, the kneeling, the grammar none of them could see.","\" And here we are.\"","No one answered!","Noah looked down at the Warden still waiting on her hands and knees, patted her head once, twice, the maintenance of furniture, and turned for the sealed door with his hands loose at his sides.","\" Prepare, all of you. Soon, we begin corrupting THE PAX.\"","...!"]},{"number":5632,"title":"Chapter 5632: Chapter 5631: A Torn Wall!","paragraphs":["As Noah continued to scheme on exactly how things could unfold in THE Serenaros, he asked...","\" The vessels of THE Sealed One. Where are they kept?\"","Mahishasura stood beside the repaired long table with his hands folded behind his back, and answered.","\" Two are held in this Dimension. The others are distributed. THE PAX...does not warehouse its rarest stock in one vault.\"","\"Hmm...\"","Noah weighed it in silence.","Two of them, a short walk from this place. Pinned pieces of the enemy who, in some future, attained IT!","A visit would have to be made, and made carefully.","Could he learn anything more of THE Sealed One from shackled vessels? He would find out soon enough.","For now, Noah turned his gaze inward and far away, to THE Infiniverse, where one Hearthshift after another had been completed while a pocket Dimension held its coup.","And his own progress had been immense.","—","The fifth Hearthshift settled.","And a few hundred million lifeforms now pulled upon Noah Osmont without knowing his name.","A few hundred million was not large, as Dimensions counted the living. In a single Dimension there could be countless Folds, and within them countless Domains of Existence, and within those countless Cosmos holding Universes and Galaxies and Worlds beyond any counting, filled with decillions upon decillions of beings who held no connection to Infinity or THE Primordial Source at all, who would live and end without once touching mana or knowing it existed.","No. The few hundred million were something else entirely.","They were the powerful. The connected. The lifeforms in every Dimension with the immensity to effect tremendous change, the sovereigns and cultivators and ancients whose draws moved the fates of everything beneath them. Rulership of them was rulership of every hand!","And yet.","He was still THE True Human Emperor, and the decillions mattered to the title as much as the millions did. Because behind his wellsprings came his home.","The authority of THE Infiniverse flowed out across every bound Dimension in rivers of crimson that no eye would ever find, THE CRIMSON WEFT latching quietly onto Folds and Domains and Cosmos entirely, and even if none of them knew, even if not one being from the greatest True Lifeform to the smallest child in the smallest World ever learned it...","They were, effectively, under his rule. All of them.l","The fifth Dimension was blue.","Noah floated at the middle of it, and in every direction, radiant Infinity trees stretched away for light years. Yggdrasils of pure deep blue, trunks wider than Worlds, crowns of azure light spreading across the dark in canopies that whole civilizations navigated by, roots drinking from wells of blue so bright they made the void around them look painted.","Blue permeated everything here. The light was blue, the drifting seeds were blue, the very texture of the ambient dark ran blue at its edges, because this was a Dimension that had given itself to Infinity entirely.","And near the great trees, dozens of True Infinite Lifeforms floated with their eyes closed.","They hung still and reverent in the branches’ light, ancient beings wrapped in oceans of blue, and every one of them was sensing the same impossible thing!","The Infinity they had drawn upon for entire Ages, the Infinity they knew the way they knew their own names, had suddenly become... so much grander.","Sweeter in the draw and deeper in the well, and not one of them could say why, and not one of them could stop drinking!","Noah watched them from the open sky, unperceived!","|Your rulership has extended across multiple bound Dimensions.|","|89,412,506 Infinite Lifeforms of this Dimension now draw, in part or in whole, upon your Infinite Sanguine Mana as the wellspring of their Infinity. 84 True Infinite Lifeforms now draw upon you. 12 among them pursue the fusion of Infinity and THE Primordial Source, and their pursuit has been eased.|","|They perceive nothing. They will perceive nothing.|","|Total, across THE Ymnaros and five bound Dimensions: 396,208,441 lifeforms now draw upon you as the source beneath their sources.|","|Provenance Essence expenditure has risen accordingly: 0.0000009% per second. The rate remains negligible.|","And behind those prompts, the deeper count arrived.","|1,000,000,000 Provenance Telos Quarks converted.|","|THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis proceeds at the greatest pace yet recorded.|","| The wall at 20 is being torn apart.|","BOOM!","The breakthrough arrived, and no one saw it!","Across the blue vastness, not a single ancient stirred. No skies split for watching crowds. No phenomenon announced itself to the dozens of True Infinite Lifeforms hanging in the branches light years away, because the being at the center of it stood at a depth their senses did not reach, and what they could not perceive, they could not witness.","But existence itself attended.","Around the floating figure of Noah, rivers of Infinite Sanguine Mana rose out of him and coiled, crimson gold serpents of blood-light winding through the empty sky in slow colossal spirals, dozens of them, then hundreds, a storm of rivers turning around a single man.","Glimmers of Provenance Essence kindled among them, stellar blue-gold points igniting one after another until the space around him held its own constellation, and the weight of everything came down, THE Primordial Source and Infinity and THE Argent Loom and Time and all the imperceivable rest, pouring through his frame into quarks that drank and drank and did not burst.","His hair lifted in a wind that touched nothing else.","His endless blue eyes burned brighter, and the twenty singularities of his depths turned as one, and somewhere far beneath perception, a membrane that had been meant to hold for months or years simply came apart.","|Your attributes have crossed the wall.|","|VERITAS: 25.|","|PONDUS: 24.|","|PROVENANCE: 23.|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE.|","The rivers settled slowly back into him. The constellation dimmed and went home.","And in the branches of a blue yggdrasil light years away, one ancient True Infinite Lifeform opened her eyes and turned her head toward the empty middle sky, frowning faintly at nothing at all.","She closed her eyes, and went back to drinking from a well she did not know had a king.","| THE Infiniverse reports: her Dimensionality is rising at a tremendously rapid rate.|","|Cause: THE CRIMSON WEFT now binds her authority across many Dimensions, and Observable Existences continue to rise within her without pause. A Dimension that contains a thousand foundations and touches six more Dimensions is being weighed by existence as something no framework has a shelf for.|","|And her rising lifts you. Your Dimensionality now runs far higher than what your attributes express.|","|Effect: THE PRECEPT OF SOLIPSISM has deepened. You may now render yourself unperceivable to lifeforms whose attributes reach into the 30s.|","Noah read the last prompt twice, and a slow!","The 30s. Mahishasura himself sat in the low thirties. Which meant that as of this moment, the Enforcer could not find him if he did not wish to be found!","...!"]},{"number":5633,"title":"Chapter 5633: Chapter 5632: Rage. Rage. Rage!","paragraphs":["The wall was torn, and Noah was already thinking past it.","His current level of immensity was a floor, not a ceiling, and the road to raising it rapidly had already proven itself five Dimensions over.","More Hearthshifts. More wells laid beneath more draws. More rulership extended along roads no instrument could register, until the count beneath him stopped being millions and started being measured the way Dimensions were measured!","The plan needed no revision. It only needed repetition, and time, and he held infinite quantities of exactly one of those.","But at such a time... something connected to him trembled!","HUUUM!","It was not an attack. It was not the Weft, and it was not a thread of rulership, and for one strange moment he could not place it at all, because the trembling came from a connection he had given away.","It came from THE Infiniverse.","From the bubble chamber. From the backbone of THE Infinite Scales he had cast out on obsidian sands, the framework he had built across a small time in mimicry of Vakochev’s Scales of Existence, the ladder his old power had climbed before Provenance replaced every rung of it.","He had been thinking, only recently, about how to reframe that cast-out skeleton under his Provenance!","And at this moment, she sent her message through.","| Master. Weavings of a grand record are being sent through your old scales of existence.|","|A record that seems to stem from... Vakochev himself.|","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes shone with a terrifying brilliance.","\" Send it through.\"","He closed his eyes. And within a corner of his consciousness, a grand record was passed inward, and it bloomed!","His consciousness gave the record a stage, and the stage was an endless stellar blue sea.","Noah’s body manifested upon the still water, whole and standing, and opposite him, something else arrived.","A shrouded figure, seated.","It could not entirely be observed. The shape of it slid away from direct perception, and around it, obsidian waves rolled, black lightning crawling through them in slow crowns, immensity manifesting in tides that the blue sea absorbed without complaint!","A being that had covered Observable Existences and Dimensions and vast reaches of THE Infinite Carcosa and THE Source Lands with a single framework, rendered down into a recording, and still too grand to look at directly.","And then it spoke, and its voice boomed through the whole of Noah’s consciousness!","\"I am Vakochev.\"","The obsidian waves rose with the name.","\" And I am reaching out to all those who tried to do what I tried to do. I send this message through my Scales and other Scales, to the few with Boundless Potential.\"","The shrouded head lifted.","\"I tried to go against Those Who Remain. I tried to level the playing field, for all of us. And I have failed. I have to retreat. I have come to the conclusion that this is not something I can do alone... because Those Who Remain are not alone.\"","The lightning stilled for a moment, and the voice came lower.","\"I retreat in defeat. And I persevere. And you, who seek to do the same as me... Persevere. They are coming for me, and they will come for you. They will try to stifle every life and every possibility that could one day topple them. So forgive me, for the adversity you are about to have.\"","The figure’s shrouded gaze seemed to find him, across a recording, across existence.","\" But even adversity is part of existence. If you die, this is also a part of existence. If you are brought into their folds, this too is a part of existence. So Persevere. Do not go gentle into the night.\"","The obsidian waves rose into a storm.","\" Rage.\"","The sea shook.","\" Rage.\"","The sky of his consciousness split with black light.","\" RAGE!\"","BOOM!","The figure stood, and the standing alone drove the stellar sea outward in a ring, and then it shot upward, a pillar of obsidian and lightning climbing out of the record and out of perception entirely!","And where it had sat, something remained.","A single obsidian crystal, small and dark and perfectly still, settling down through the blue water of Noah’s consciousness.","|The record has concluded.|","|Something has been left behind. Its nature is ?????.|","Noah opened his eyes, shock still moving through him, the crystal settling somewhere deep and the last word still ringing in every corner of what he was!","He grasped the crystal, and all it had were question marks!","And in the next moment, all of existence began to shake.","The Dimension he stood in shook. And far across the dark, even THE Infiniverse began to shake, a Unique Transfinite Dimension trembling in her own step between Dimensions","It...was not isolated.","---","In a quiet Inner Dimension far across THE Infinite Carcosa, a man who wore the body of Achilles Adrastia was breaking a promise slowly, and doing it face to face.","\" Until I am certain, \" he said, \" that I control my existence... that this hand is mine when it moves, and this voice is mine when it speaks... I may have to leave you, Rose.\"","The woman before him had green hair that fell in loose waves, and a beauty so vivid it made the quiet garden around her seem painted was pained.","She was about to reply when...","Existence shook.","The garden swayed. The light bent. And the man who was half Achilles Adrastia and half something sealed and ancient had already appeared to wrap his arms around Rose as he looked around for any threat coldly!","—","Far away.","In an unknown Dimension of black stone and burning skies, THE Creature was at war.","Two Primeval Ones circled him, vast and old and bleeding, and his obsidian flames ran threaded with white-gold as THE MAW hung open at his shoulder and the shapeless Pantheon wore the battlefield itself. One of the Primevals struck!","Then existence shook.","All three ancient things stopped, mid-violence, in perfect unison.","And THE Creature turned his head upward, toward a sky that was not the source of anything, and the swirling white rivers in his eyes narrowed.","\"...Hm.\"","—","In a grand citadel of gold and glory, a thousand True Gilded Lifeforms looked up at once.","Not one after another. At once, in a single synchronized motion, a thousand brilliant heads tilting toward the ceiling in the same heartbeat, because not one of the motions was their own. Their amplified Egos burned in perfect, identical rhythm, an ocean of glory moving as one instrument.","For they were under the collective control of THE Great Usurper.","And around them, existence shook!","—","And in THE Serenaros, the shaking rolled through everything.","The purple gold mountains swayed upon their clouds. The cage-fields rattled for light years, columns of stacked prisons groaning, despondent captives lifting their heads.","And inside a pocket Dimension that was sealed against all of existence, the shaking arrived anyway.","The marble hall trembled. Wine pools shivered. Cured Descendants were on their feet in an instant, staring upward at a pretend sky, and the empty instrument that had been Yrsa stood placidly in the swaying hall awaiting instruction, and Descendant Mahishasura gazed around coldly.","Noah stood at the center of the trembling marble.","He looked around slowly and somberly as he thought about Vakochev’s words!","Rage. Rage. Rage!"]},{"number":5634,"title":"Chapter 5634: Chapter 5633: The Provenance of Existence! I","paragraphs":["The shaking deepened.","And beneath it, running under the quake of every surface, there came a sound that was not truly a sound!","A sensation of something cracking. Something vast and old and everywhere at once, fracturing along its whole length!","Noah looked around slowly. Across the trembling marble hall, the Descendants were doing the same, seven cured faces and one hateful one all tilted toward a pretend sky, because every one of them was feeling it too!","|A vast structure is breaking across existence.|","| Certainty is not possible, but weighed against everything in your records... that may be the fracturing of Vakochev’s Scales of Existence.|","...!","The prompt was a heavy one, and existence went on quaking around it!","The Scales. The framework that covered Observable Existences and Dimensions and vast reaches of THE Infinite Carcosa and THE Source Lands. The ladder that even free beings paradoxically kept climbing, the measure so old that entire civilizations had never conceived of standing anywhere else!","He had heard its maker’s voice minutes ago, wrapped in obsidian lightning, admitting defeat. I retreat. I persevere. Rage!","And now the ladder itself was coming apart across the whole of everything.","At such a time, Noah heard nothing at all.","But through the Descendants his existence controlled, through seven Veiled lines and one bound Sovereign whose senses were his to share... he heard it.","A voice, echoing out within the lineages themselves. Booming and serene at once, feminine, filled with an immensity that made the fracturing sound small, arriving not through any air but through the blood, through the unbroken written lines running back through every ancestor, a message into existence itself of the kind that Descendants received once in a lifetime if they were fortunate.","Every Descendant in the hall went rigid as one.","| Rejoice, O Progeny of Immense Ones.|","|For you will be first to learn of the coming of the new Ruling of Existence itself. No Scales shall sit above anything ordained by THE Immense Ones, by Those Who Remain. There is only our Rulings, that all of existence shall follow and thrive from.|","|There is only, and will only be... THE Provenance of Existence.|","...!","Noah’s gaze became terribly heavy.","Vakochev’s message, and then this, in the same hour!","That grand lifeform had failed at whatever his plans had been, had broadcast his defeat through a specific few, and Those Who Remain had answered his retreat by making their move at last!","A replacement of the measure of everything!","Just what did it entail?","THE Provenance of Existence.","They had taken the word Provenance!","The name of what THE First Lifeforms were, the name of what he was, the name of the one power in all of existence that owed nothing, borrowed nothing, and was granted nothing... and THE Immense Ones had taken it!","The voice went on. And what it delivered next, only the Descendants of all existence would receive freely!","Every other lifeform across every Dimension would feel the Ruling settle over their lives tonight and be given nothing at all, left to learn its shape by stumbling through it for Ages.","|Hear the mechanics of the Ruling, O Progeny.|","|Existence is woven of MANTLES. They have always been there: roles woven through the living since the living began. The Ruler. The Peasant. The Tyrant. The Mender. The Shield. The Blade. The Watcher. The Betrayer. The Wanderer. The Usurper. Every age and every Dimension has worn them, and until this day, wearing them earned nothing.|","|As of this day, the Ruling answers those who wear them.|","|When a lifeform wears a Mantle so truly, and for so long, that its own weavings and the Mantle’s weavings can no longer be told apart, existence shall record the union. That recording is an ORDINATION. The Ordained draw standing, power, and depth from the Ruling itself, owing nothing to any framework of authority, and so the humble may rise through their roles where no ladder of power would ever have carried them. This is the gift.|","Around the marble hall, seven cured Descendants stood frozen inside a message only their blood could hear, and Mahishasura had gone very pale!","\" They have never done this before...\" he said softly, to no one. \" In all the records of all the lines. They have never once addressed us all!\"","HUUM!","The voice was not finished.","| And know the two roads of the Ruling, for every lifeform shall walk one.|","|THE ORDERED are those who live their roles in service of the ordained order. Their EXISTENTIAL MOIRAI shall gather steadily: the favor of existence itself, chance leaning toward their steps and the door that opens at the needed hour. Their Dimensionality shall rise with their observance, slow and without ceiling. Existence favors stability. The Ordered ARE stability. They shall thrive from the Ruling, and the Ruling shall thrive from them.|","|THE WILLFUL are those who wear their roles for their own ends, or worse, who refuse all roles and author themselves. To them the Ruling gives its other face. Existence also has the undeniable fact of instability and entropy. Their power shall come fast and grand. And their Moirai shall burn or flicker without notice, and chance shall lean away from them like the unstable things they are. They shall thrive from the chaos of Existence. The Willful are permitted. The Willful are even needed.|","...!","The hall was silent inside the quaking.","And Noah stood at the center of it, unheard-of things assembling themselves behind his cold eyes!","They had built an order that rewards its own believing and likely benefitted Those Who Remain!","His eyes flashed, and he turned THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard on the nearest Descendant.","| Descendant Baelgrim|:: VERITAS: 24. PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 23. PONDUS: 26. MOIRAI: 14. No role.|","There it was. A new line!","He swept the Regard across the hall. Sylvaine, MOIRAI: 11. Othrys, MOIRAI: 9. Kharvel, MOIRAI: 22!","Mahishasura, MOIRAI: 31, an Enforcer of order weighed richly by an order he had never heard of until this minute.","And then, slowly, Noah turned the Regard inward, upon himself.","|VERITAS: 25. PONDUS: 24. PROVENANCE: 23. POTENTIA: INFINITE.|","|MOIRAI: ?????|","|The Ruling has attempted to weigh you unsuccessfully. The Ruling is still attempting.|","...!"]},{"number":5635,"title":"Chapter 5635: Chapter 5634: The Provenance of Existence! II","paragraphs":["The quaking had begun to settle, but the questions had not.","A system did not become real by being announced. It became real by being tested, and Noah had a hall full of instruments, a bound Enforcer with thirty-one Moirai already weighed upon him, and no intention of learning the Ruling’s shape the way the rest of existence would learn it, by stumbling.","So he turned to the most richly weighed being in the room.","\" Mahishasura . What have you done across your long life? What are you doing still? Proclaim it, and let us see what this new Ruling makes of you.\"","The Enforcer straightened his torn coat, and lifted his chin, and spoke!","\"I am Mahishasura, Enforcer of THE Serenaros. \" The soft voice carried through the marble hall, and something in it began to resonate!","\" I have held a mountain, and from that mountain I have ordered the Wardens sworn beneath me out into the reaches of existence. At my word, they have stripped the authority from countless lifeforms unworthy of holding it. I weighed them, and I found them unworthy, and I had them subtracted.\"","His amber eyes did not waver!","\"I have taken the mighty out of the hands of the helpless. I have emptied the skies of appetites. I have caged what could not be reasoned with and carried it away from everything it would have eaten.\"","...!","The hall held still.","And then, from above, out of a pretend sky that had no above to offer... a golden shield descended!","HUUM!","It was vast and slow and utterly silent, a sigil of deep gold in the shape of a great shield, turning gently as it came down through the air over the Enforcer’s head, and light poured off it in soft sheets, and every being in the hall felt existence itself lean toward the marble floor where one bound Descendant stood proclaiming.","| The Ruling has heard a proclamation, and weighed it against a life.|","|Descendant Mahishasura has been recognized. He now wears the Mantle of THE SHIELD.|","| THE SHIELD: the Protector’s role, worn by all who stand between harm and the held . What THE SHIELD guards, existence shall help him guard. His EXISTENTIAL MOIRAI shall gather from his actions and from the results of his actions: every harm turned aside, every held thing that endures, shall be weighed and paid. While he acts in accordance with his role, his power shall be amplified tremendously. And should a wearer of THE SHIELD face an opposing role in contest, existence itself shall lean, and probability shall bend, to ensure the victory of one of THE ORDERED.|","|Should Descendant Mahishasura truly and fully live his Mantle, deed upon deed upon deed... he may one day be granted his own unique Ordination.|","...!","The golden sigil settled, sinking into the air above his shoulders until it hung there faint and turning, a quiet crest that did not fade. And Mahishasura stood beneath it surrounded by a grand descending light, gold pouring over the torn black coat and the pale hair, and for a moment the bound, hateful, coup-broken Enforcer looked almost exalted, a figure existence itself had chosen to illuminate!","Noah looked at him, and slowly shook his head.","His eyes flashed.","| Descendant Mahishasura|:: VERITAS: 40 (34). PROVENANCE: 0. POTENTIA: 40 (32). PONDUS: 40 (33). MOIRAI: 31, and gathering. He wears the Mantle of THE SHIELD.|","Forty. Across the board!","The parentheses held what the Descendant truly was, and the Ruling had simply written larger numbers over them, granted for nothing more than proclaiming a life and being found in accordance with a role.","His cold gaze swept the hall. \" The rest of you. All of you. Proclaim what your existence has been doing so far! Let us see just what role, just what archetype, each of you holds!\"","WAA!","Baelgrim went first.","\"I am Baelgrim ,\" the mountain rumbled. \" I have no grand record of order. I have only this. For all my Ages, when something came for my kin, it found me in front of them. Before the curse, I stood in front. That is all I have ever done.\"","HUUM!","A second golden shield descended, vast and slow, and settled turning above the mountain’s shoulders, and Baelgrim looked up at his own crest with wonder.","|Descendant Baelgrim has been recognized. He now wears the Mantle of THE SHIELD.|","|VERITAS: 30 (24). POTENTIA: 30 (23). PONDUS: 30 (26). MOIRAI: 14, and gathering.|","Sylvaine stepped forward with her eyes set, and proclaimed a harder life!","\"I was made to end things. I have ended tyrants and ended innocents and ended whatever my masters pointed me toward, and when the ire of THE Immense Ones made me feel every wound I authored, I authored them anyway, when the cause was worth the cutting. I am not a protector. I am the thing protectors send. I am the edge that goes where shields cannot.\"","...!","No shield came for her.","Instead, a slender sword of white gold descended point-down through the pretend sky, keening one soft note as it came, and hung turning above her head.","| Descendant Sylvaine has been recognized. She now wears the Mantle of THE BLADE.|","|THE BLADE: the Ender’s role, worn by those who cut what must be cut and carry the cost of the cutting. Her Moirai shall gather from every ending that spares a greater one. While she acts in accordance, her power is amplified tremendously.|","|VERITAS: 30 (27). POTENTIA: 30 (25). PONDUS: 30 (24). MOIRAI: 11, and gathering.|","Kharvel did not step forward at all. He proclaimed from where he stood, quiet and level.","\"I have watched. Nothing under my watch was ever lost that I did not see lost. Nothing approached that I did not see approach. I have been the one who does not look away, in a hall of beings who could afford to.\"","An unblinking eye of pale gold descended over him, lidless and serene, and hung turning.","And it did not stop pouring.","Where the others’ lights had settled, Kharvel’s deepened, gold flooding down over the watcher in sheet after sheet, and the whole hall turned to look as the amplification visibly climbed!","| Descendant Kharvel has been recognized. He now wears the Mantle of THE WATCHER.|","|THE WATCHER: the Witness’s role. What he watches, existence shall keep watchable. His Moirai shall gather from every warning that arrives in time, and every truth that is seen before it is suffered.|","|His life and his role can scarcely be told apart. The Ruling has weighed this, and paid accordingly.|","|VERITAS: 35 (29). POTENTIA: 35 (27). PONDUS: 35 (28). MOIRAI: 22, and gathering.|","...!","Thirty-five, where every other cured had been given thirty!","Noah’s cold gaze narrowed slightly at the parenthesis and what sat outside it, and the mechanic assembled itself plainly enough. The Ruling... paid alignment.","Othrys proclaimed next.","\"I have wandered. No home held my name. No road kept my footprints. I walked out of every memory I entered.\"","A staff of worn gold descended for him, a traveler’s staff, turning slowly.","| Descendant Othrys has been recognized. He now wears the Mantle of THE WANDERER.|","|THE WANDERER: the Roadless role, worn by those who belong to the going rather than the arriving. Ways open for him. His Moirai shall gather from every path walked that no other could have walked.|","|VERITAS: 30 (21). POTENTIA: 30 (22). PONDUS: 30 (20). MOIRAI: 9, and gathering.|","The shadow-cursed lounger proclaimed the years she had wrapped her dark around her loved ones, before her curse taught the dark to strangle, and a third golden shield came down for her, and she wept beneath it.","The quiet lounger, the one whose curse Noah had unwritten without ever naming it aloud, proclaimed softly of a long life spent putting broken things back together, beings and bonds and Dimensions cracked by wars she had not started, mended with hands the record never thanked. A golden thread descended for her, stitching slowly through a ring of light.","|Shenara now wears the Mantle of THE MENDER.|","|THE MENDER: the Restorer’s role. What she mends, existence shall help hold mended. VERITAS: 30 (22). POTENTIA: 30 (21). PONDUS: 30 (23).|","And another one of the 7 Cured Descendants proclaimed grandly, at length, of deeds and stands and sacrifices.","And...","Nothing descended.","The hall waited, and nothing happened as it seemed that one still needed to have had significant actions to back their claims, and could not simply bullshit their way to a Mantle!","Which left one being in the hall unaccounted for.","\" Warden .\" Noah’s voice stayed level. \" Proclaim what your existence has done.\"","The empty instrument that had been Yrsa stepped forward at the command and proclaimed in a voice with no resonance in it at all.","\"I am Warden Yrsa of THE PAX. I hold the rank of Warden. I execute collections. I maintain Records. I obey .\"","The hall waited.","Nothing descended again!","|The Ruling has weighed this proclamation.|","|It has found no one.|","...!","Noah held the prompt in his cold gaze for a moment.","So the Ruling did not weigh bodies, or ranks, or obediences. It weighed selves!","And where a self had been erased, the grandest system Those Who Remain had ever imposed looked into a standing, speaking, breathing being... and found no one home to give a role to.","Noah watched the hall wordlessly after that.","Three Shields, a Blade, a Watcher, a Wanderer, a Mender. Golden crests turning over seven of his nine, one Descendant unweighed, one instrument unfounded!","Existence itself leaned into the room the way a patron leans into a shop it has decided to fund.","The boosts were terrifying! Under these new scales, these new Rulings of Those Who Remain, a proclaimed life was worth more, and if a wearer met one of the Willful in contest, probability itself would take a side.","Even he, standing outside every framework existence had ever offered him, looked at the boons... and was tempted.","But no.","He had cast out borrowed thongs and he had not done it to kneel at a newer, grander one. He had to generate something of his own. Even if he tapped into this vastness, and he might, because this was a new makeup of existence itself that even he could not deny, it would be on his terms, through his own works, worn as nothing existence could revoke.","Because that was the fact under all the gold: existence itself... deferred to this new system.","And even now, watching the crests turn above the proclaimed, Noah felt he was only beginning to grasp what Those Who Remain had imposed upon all of existence.","...!"]},{"number":5636,"title":"Chapter 5636: Chapter 5635: For Stability!","paragraphs":["Noah thought about it for a while.","A new system had been laid over all of existence, and existence itself deferred to it.","He wanted to see...how far he could push it.","\" Mahishasura .\" He turned to the Shield. \" We...are going to visit another mountain. And when we arrive, you are going to make a proclamation of your own.\"","The amber eyes watched him with attentiveness at this time!","\" You will tell the Enforcer of that mountain this. That for the stability of existence, your role as THE SHIELD requires more Enforcers and more Wardens acting directly beneath you, so that you may gather the Moirai to stabilize existence further as you see fit.\"","\" Which means that Enforcer must bend the knee to you. And should they refuse... \" He let it settle. \"... then they stand against the stability of existence itself. And a Shield, in accordance with its role, is permitted to correct that.\"","Mahishasura understood as he shook his head with incredulity, because the plan was monstrous and elegant and used his own new Mantle as the knife!","—","They set off across THE Serenaros.","The Weft carried them, unseen, crimson threads bearing an emperor and his Shield out over the purple gold mountains and the cloud-seas and the gigaparsec cages stacked on each other, and Noah watched the Dimension move beneath them as they went.","It was in chaos, quietly.","The Ruling had settled over THE Serenaros the same hour it settled over everything, and even here, in the seat of the ones who served THE Immense Ones, no one had been told more than the Descendants had.","Many were trying to grasp this new system!","The masters of order, Noah observed, were as disordered as anyone tonight.","A little while later.","A mountain rose ahead of them, ringed in its own cages, and Mahishasura brought them down before its gates and called out.","\" Enforcer Vorlag.\"","His soft voice carried across the terraces, and after a moment, powerhouses came out!","An Enforcer first, a broad Descendant with stone-gray skin and a brow-mark split like cracked stone, flanked by his Wardens. Noah’s eyes flashed across them as they emerged, cataloguing without a word.","One of the Wardens was a Descendant like her master. The rest were progeny, the mingled blood of Descendants and Primeval Ones, of Descendants and Infinite Lifeforms drawn in deep blue, of Descendants and old Source things, the mixed and mighty middle ranks that ran the machinery of THE PAX.","\" Mahishasura !\" Vorlag’s gray face was bright!","\" You felt and heard the glorious change our Fathers have laid down?! Haha, even we are trying to figure it out right now!\"","Mahishasura spread his hands, and the golden shield-crest turned faintly above his shoulders, and he made his proclamation.","\" Yes, Existence has a new Ruling, Vorlag. You have felt it. I have grasped it .\" The crest brightened as he spoke in accordance with his role!","\"I wear the Mantle of THE SHIELD, and my role is the protection of the ordained order, and the Ruling has shown me that to stabilize existence further, I require more hands acting beneath mine. More Enforcers. More Wardens. Yours among them.\"","His voice stayed courteous and warm.","\" So bend the knee, and act beneath me for the stability of existence. Or refuse, and stand revealed as a thing that opposes stability itself.\"","BOOM!","Vorlag’s bright face began to darken toward anger.","\" You have lost your damn mind! The fuck are you talking abou-...!\"","Mahishasura attacked.","No further word. No warning!","The Shield simply moved, and the whole of THE Serenaros seemed to move with him!","Noah watched from the open air, and as the Shield struck, prompts rose before his eyes alone.","|A wearer of THE SHIELD is acting in full accordance with his role.|","|Descendant Mahishasura has framed this contest as the set order against a thing that opposes it. The Ruling has accepted the framing. Existence has begun writing a narrative around his existence and his role.|","Mahishasura crossed the distance in an instant, and his fist took Vorlag across the jaw. Forty attributes behind the blow, against a being who stood in the low thirties, and worse, far worse, existence itself leaned into it as it landed!","Noah watched probability bend in real time. Vorlag’s guard came up a fraction too slow. Every small chance that might have saved him tilted, quietly and completely, toward the wearer of THE SHIELD.","| Probability has bent to favor THE ORDERED. Result achieved: an opposing role staggered.|","|EXISTENTIAL MOIRAI of Descendant Mahishasura: 33.|","The Ruling was helping. It had chosen a side the instant Mahishasura framed the fight as order against disorder, and it did not choose halfway!","He fought with everything he was at once. His lineage gift woke, and where his hands passed, the mountain’s own defenses answered him instead of their master!","THE Argent Loom rose to him the way it rose to no one else alive, white rivers pouring up out and gathering into his open hands and hardening into weapons, into walls, into a hundred white blades that orbited him and struck where he looked!","Loom, and lineage, and forty attributes, and existence itself tilting the floor beneath his enemies!","It was not a fight. It was a demonstration of what THE ORDERED were built to be.","Vorlag went down alongside his forces as nobody else had to make a move!","Mahishasura floated there, gazing at his own hands as if he couldnt believe what he had done!","|Result achieved: an opposing cohort broken. Harm turned aside from the ordained order.|","|Existence continues to favor the accordant. EXISTENTIAL MOIRAI of Descendant Mahishasura: 33 to 37.|","|He is playing out his role to perfection.|","...!","Oh!","In under a minute, Enforcer Vorlag and every Warden of his mountain lay broken across their own terraces, alive, ruined, uncomprehending.","Mahishasura turned toward Noah, breathing hard, and on his face as right now he showed...euphoria!","\" Lock this place down .\" Noah’s voice went sharp and quick as he began to move towards the defeated!","The Veiled moved as darkness flowed all around.","And Noah descended toward the broken Enforcer and his broken Wardens, and his sanguine blades were already blooming along his hands, crimson gold and humming.","He crouched over the ruined Enforcer, blades bright, and got to the work of taking him.","It seemed that new possibilities were rising!","He could attain his goals much faster amidst the chaos of this new system...while also utilizing it and the terrifying power behind it to achieve his aims!","He would use this new Ruling of existence they had imposed to fuck them over tremendously, if he could!"]},{"number":5637,"title":"Chapter 5637: Chapter 5636: Roles! I","paragraphs":["Although the battle for the mountain had ended, the absolute weight of order remained heavy in the air.","Noah floated silently before the broken forms of Enforcer Vorlag and his cohort of Wardens, who all knelt in the ruined courtyards of their own fief after he had placed his Markers into them.","Around Noah, the veiled figures of Mahishasura, Kharvel, Sylvaine, and the other cured Descendants floated in immaculate stillness!","Noah looked at the kneeling forms, his eyes exceptionally bright as his mind catalogued exactly what had just occurred.","In truth, he was thinking more and more about THE Provenance of Existence and how this new system could be stretched, weaponized, and ultimately drained.","The most glaring vulnerability this Ruling came with was the Mantles, and the absolute reality that if an existence truly and fully played out their designated role, existence itself would side with them.","It was represented by Moirai. It acted akin to a localized destiny backing a lifeform simply because of what they stood for. Thus, Noah reasoned through the implications.","Could he design a grand narrative role for someone like Mahishasura to perform? Could he effectively turn the Descendant into a lead actor on a grand stage? Would the Moirai bend nearby existence to aid him in living out this newly authored role?","To truly fulfill this architecture, he needed complete operational control!","Noah did not speak a command aloud. Instead, he sent a concentrated portion of his own consciousness directly into the veiled weavings of Mahishasura, taking total, seamless control of the Descendant’s body and power.","Stepping into the vessel of a Descendant was a remarkably strange sensation.","Noah felt the unbending sentence written into the very blood of the lineage, humming with the cold dictation of Those Who Remain.","He felt the innate, effortless connection to THE Argent Loom, perceiving the boundless white threads of authority that stitched the Dimension together.","But most surprisingly, he felt the Existential Moirai surrounding this body. It was a buoyant, upward pressure.","It made him feel as though the physical surroundings themselves were actively lifting him up, eager to support whatever action THE SHIELD decided to take!","While his consciousness anchored into Mahishasura, Noah’s actual body moved backward.","He waved his hands casually, pooling crimson gold Sanguine Mana infused with stellar blue light to form a high, bloody throne.","Sitting back upon it, THE Precept of Solipsism washed over him, rendering him entirely unperceivable to anyone whose attributes fell below his own, and more due to his immense Dimensionality.","Below his throne, the Descendants lined up like perfect soldiers, an arrangement that allowed Noah to comfortably bask in the ambient awe and Moirai without ever exposing his own hands.","From the mouth of Mahishasura, Noah looked down at Enforcer Vorlag and the vastness of thid place. He needed to truly unleash the Mantle of THE SHIELD, and to do so, he required a speech that existence itself could not ignore!","\" There was once a mortal man attempt to hold up a collapsing roof with a single wooden beam,\" Mahishasura spoke, his voice echoing with a soft, precise, courteous lecturing warmth that carried an iron menace beneath.","\" Many go on believing that a shield is just a piece of metal you hold in front of your own chest. But a true shield is an architecture.\"","Mahishasura paced slowly through the white threads of THE Argent Loom.","\" To truly fulfill my Mantle as THE SHIELD, my ability is fundamentally limited if I cannot control all members of THE PAX across the entire Serenaros Dimension. To guard the order, I must bring every Enforcer on this Dimension under my fold. I must take control of the Arbiter. Except, the architects of this Dimension are terribly fond of their current, flawed design. They hoard authority while the roof collapses.\"","Mahishasura stopped pacing and opened his arms toward the purple gold skies, his amber gold eyes blazing as he addressed the firmaments of Existence directly!","\" Will existence side with one of its children who stands faithfully as one of THE ORDERED? Will existence back me in this arduous accounting?!\"","He lowered his gaze back to Enforcer Vorlag, his tone dropping the cosmic grandeur for a flat, terrifyingly simple conclusion.","\" They do not deserve to hold the line. And frankly... neither do you.\"","BOOM!","The results arrived instantly. All of surrounding existence buzzed with a deafening, resonant frequency as the skies of THE Serenaros seemed to physically lean downward!","Cascading waves of pure Moirai gushed from the skies, pouring directly into the body of Mahishasura like a breaking dam!","Information flooded into the Descendant’s existence, a raw Existential validation that Noah immediately translated into crisp prompts within his own vision.","|You are one of the foremost existences utilizing THE Provenance of Existence to its fullest.|","|You are the first to trigger a Narrative of Existence.|","| THE Narrative of Existence, Political Crusade, has been triggered as you are one of the central Mantles.|","|Political Crusade: A triggered internal conflict to usurp rule against those deemed unworthy of their stations. Mahishasura, THE SHIELD, has been deemed The Leading Crusade. All Narrative Moirai flows around him, strengthening his existence and the Crusaders behind him to guarantee the highest probability of a successful crusade.|","|Existential Moirai begins to bud aggressively in THE Serenaros. If enough participants arise, and if different Mantles and roles join in this Narrative, an interested gaze from one of THE Immense Ones may be drawn over. Leading participants will gain unfathomable Existential Moirai in return.|","The returns were ridiculously out of his expectations!","Sitting unperceivable on his bloody throne, Noah gazed at the prompts through the eyes of Mahishasura, processing the sheer volume of Moirai exploding around the vessel. It was an absolute validation of his siege architecture!","The Ruling was not just paying for actions anymore; it was paying for the entire theatrical campaign!","|Descendant Mahishasura|:: VERITAS 41 / PROVENANCE 0 / POTENTIA 42 / PONDUS 43","Every attribute had crossed the threshold of forty, fueled entirely by the momentum of the crusade.","Noah felt the overwhelming density of the Descendant’s new standing, and he did not waste a single second of the narrative high.","Operating through Mahishasura, he raised one pale gold hand and pointed toward the distant, hazy silhouette of the next mountain in the inner ring.","\"We march ,\" Mahishasura commanded, his voice carrying the amplified, undeniable weight of The Leading Crusade. \" We bring the order to the next peak. Anyone who resists is an enemy of stability itself!\"","The Veiled Descendants moved in perfect unison, their figures snapping in the wind as they rallied behind their newly empowered vanguard.","And far behind this terrifying, righteous force, Noah rested his chin on his fist atop his throne of Sanguine Mana, directing the entire crusade from the absolute safety of the unseen!"]},{"number":5638,"title":"Chapter 5638: Chapter 5637: Roles! II","paragraphs":["<THE Creature>","Although the shaking of existence had paused the war for a brief moment, the violence in the unknown Dimension of black stone and burning skies was far from settled.","Two Primeval Ones circled THE Creature. They were vast, old, and bleeding, shimmering with hoarded authority, and entirely unaware that the foundation of their power had just rotted away beneath them!","In truth, existence had just undergone a violent restructuring.","When Vakochev’s Scales fractured across reality, the lineages of Descendants heard a booming voice delivering the new laws of THE Provenance of Existence. THE Creature heard nothing at all!","He did not need to hear a voice.","His Pantheon of All Existence was the surroundings themselves. When the physical and conceptual rules of the burning skies and black stone changed, the new grammar inscribed itself directly into his flesh and his Intent.","He felt the death of the old ladder. He felt the birth of Moirai. He understood instantly that existence was now weighing roles, measuring lives against Mantles, and preparing to fund those who played their parts perfectly!","The two Primeval Ones prepared to unleash their accumulated Ages of power. They still believed they were the apex of a static hierarchy!","THE Creature looked at them, his face a mask of cold obsidian flames threaded with white-gold.","\"A true ruler does not float above the weight of his domain,\" THE Creature spoke, his voice flat and unhurried, carrying the absolute density of inevitable payment.","\" He places himself beneath it. He carries the cost of every life, every death, and every broken law. You have sat in the dark and hoarded authority without ever bearing its consequences.\"","He took a single step forward, and the black stone groaned.","\"I am the one who carries ,\" he continued, his tone devoid of any rising passion. \"I am the one who pays the cost. And I am the one who will dictate the order of what remains.\"","Existence listened!","Without a single visual notification or floating text as of now, a profound and heavy knowledge blossomed inside THE Creature’s mind.","Existence had weighed his life, his suffering, and his unyielding thesis of bearing, and it found him absolutely in accordance.","He felt an invisible, crushing weight of validation pour into his Pantheon!","He received the Mantle of THE RULER!","Pure Existential Moirai flooded his being. It did not arrive as a number he could read. It arrived as a localized destiny, a physical sensation of the surrounding Dimension actively lifting him up and bending its own probability to guarantee his success.","He was now one of THE ORDERED, and existence itself would lean to ensure his victory in this contest.","The Primeval Ones struck!","The black stone vanished in a blinding storm of dense golden Primordial Source and roaring blue Infinity. The two ancients poured the entirety of their hoarded Ages into a combined beam of annihilation meant to erase him from the Records entirely!","THE Creature did not dodge.","BOOM!","The annihilation beam struck the space inches from his chest and simply fractured, skipping off his aura like a thrown stone off a frozen lake.","The probability of their strike landing had been bent away by the Moirai of THE RULER. The Primeval Ones stared in absolute shock as their guaranteed execution failed to even singe his robes!","They did not understand the new Ruling. They did not know that authority was no longer enough!","They needed Roles!","THE Creature raised his hand.","THE MAW opened simultaneously in the burning sky, the obsidian floor, and the very air between the two Primevals. The invisible jaws clamped down on their flowing blue Infinity, devouring their attack and their Intent in a single, unhurried motion.","\" Payment is due ,\" THE Creature murmured.","THE Blank Caudal of the Unwritten Primeval whipped out from behind him wrapped with tendrils of THE Argent Loom.","The white-haired tail crossed the distance in a fraction of a nanosecond, carrying the amplified, undeniable weight of his new Mantle. It slammed into the chest of the first Primeval One with the force of countless collapsing Observable Existences!","CRACK!","The ancient lifeform folded perfectly in half, its Trueness rupturing outward as it was driven straight into the black stone floor.","The second Primeval One turned to flee, finally realizing that the rules of engagement had been entirely rewritten!","THE Creature extended his arm and applied THE Burden of Existence.","Every era of grief, every ounce of suffering he had ever carried, and every slaughtered life he had witnessed transferred instantly into the fleeing Primeval’s soul.","The ancient being screamed, its unblemished existence buckling under a weight it had never been trained to carry. It collapsed, crashing into the stone beside its broken companion.","THE Creature walked slowly toward them, his steps echoing in the sudden quiet of the burning domain.","He looked down at the two shattered ancients, their bodies trembling as they struggled to understand the insurmountable gap that had just opened between them.","He did not kill them. He had a use for their weight!","\" Bend the knee ,\" THE Creature commanded, his voice cold and final, \" and you will be my first generals to form a grand Rule.\"","The two ancient beings, broken by the sheer disparity in standing, slowly pushed themselves up onto their trembling knees. They bowed their heads, shockingly pledging their very existences to the entity standing above them!","These were Primeval Ones, mind you!","Oh!","As their submission set into reality, two colossal, illusory statues carved of gray stone materialized within the borders of THE Creature’s existence. The Pantheon of All Existence was expanding its Hoard, turning their pledged weight into permanent fixtures of his domain.","THE Creature waved his hand.","\" Rise.\"","Because his Dimensionality ran unfathomably deep due to the massive statue within him, he could perceive the white threads that stitched reality together and use them now. He reached into the unseen layer and commanded THE Argent Loom.","Brilliant white rivers of authority flowed from the surrounding Dimension directly into the shattered bodies of the two Primeval Ones, knitting their Trueness back together and reinforcing their broken frames with ancient density.","The two generals stood, their wounds bound by glowing white threads.","\" Tell me everything you can regarding this Dimension ,\" THE Creature instructed."]},{"number":5639,"title":"Chapter 5639: Chapter 5638: Roles! III","paragraphs":["The two Primeval Ones looked at each other, the terror of their defeat still fresh in their glowing eyes. The larger of the two bowed its head respectfully.","\" This is THE Vhelgaros ,\" the General spoke, its voice carrying the heavy rumble of shifting tectonic plates. \" It is a vast and ancient domain, filled with Primevals and True Lifeforms scattered across dozens of Observable Existences. But none of us rule it.\"","The second General continued, shivering slightly. \"A terrifyingly powerful Primeval One stands atop this Dimension. And worse, he is married to a Descendant of THE Immense Ones. Together, they hold an absolute monopoly.\"","THE Creature listened. A Primeval One claiming rulership simply by holding a Descendant’s hand, hoarding authority while demanding tribute from the lesser existences scattered below.","It was exactly the kind of unearned peace he despised.","\"It seems... like the rulers of this Dimension need to change,\" THE Creature said absentmindedly.","BOOM!","The instant the words left his mouth, existence seethed. The burning skies roared with a resonant frequency as cascading waves of pure Existential Moirai surged down, pouring directly into THE Creature’s body!","A flood of information blossomed in his mind. The Ruling had heard the declaration of THE RULER, and it was bending reality to accommodate his campaign.","The information came as behind THE Creature, the massive statue others couldn’t see smiled brutally as it translated the information into text!","| You have triggered a Narrative of Existence.|","|THE Narrative of Existence, The Grand Succession, has been triggered as you are one of the central Mantles.|","|The Grand Succession: A triggered external conflict to usurp a seated ruler through the sheer weight of bearing and territorial dominance. You have been deemed The Leading Conqueror. All Narrative Moirai flows around you, strengthening your existence and the generals behind you to guarantee the highest probability of a successful succession.|","|Existential Moirai begins to bud aggressively across THE Vhelgaros. If enough participants arise, and if the seated rulers are drawn into the contest, an interested gaze from one of THE Immense Ones may be drawn over. Leading participants will gain unfathomable Existential Moirai in return.|","THE Creature floated grandly above the black stone, his obsidian and white-gold flames expanding as he took all the information in!","He turned his masked face toward the two Generals standing beside him.","\"Let us go gather more Generals so this Dimension can have its first Great Ruler.\"","WAA!","---","<Achilles Adrastia>","Although the quiet garden in THE Infinite Carcosa was meant to be a sanctuary, existence itself refused to remain still.","Achilles wrapped his arms tightly around Rose, feeling her tremble against his chest as her green hair fell in loose waves and the very light of the surroundings bent out of shape.","He felt the monumental changes through a bizarre, half-assimilated bridge in his soul.","Because one of the countless vessels of THE Sealed One was a Descendant, the booming serene feminine voice of the new Ruling echoed straight down the lineage and bled directly into Adrastia’s mind.","He learned of THE Provenance of Existence. He absorbed the sudden absolute laws of Mantles, of Ordination, and of the invisible currency known as Moirai!","Adrastia looked down at Rose, his thoughts cementing around his overwhelming desire to protect her and to secure his own identity. To ensure he remained himself, he knew he had to rely entirely on his own Trueness and his own expanding Dimensionality.","\"I...will not be erased by the weight of an ancient ghost,\" Adrastia spoke aloud, his voice steady and carrying the absolute certainty of his own survival.","\"A man is not defined by the size of the ocean he drinks, but by the strength of the vessel that holds it. I assimilated a piece of a monster, and I am still standing. No matter how deep its Dimensionality runs, no matter how true its history claims to be, what truly matters is my own existence. I could assimilate the whole of existence itself, and I would still be Achilles Adrastia.\"","HUUM!","Existence buzzed with a deafening frequency in immediate response!","Because he outright refused to serve an imposed order and claimed a role purely for his own ends, cascading waves of invisible Moirai crashed into him, burning and flickering unstably as they recognized his defiance.","Crisp prompts bloomed across his vision, delivering the exact measure of his rebellion.","|You have taken a Mantle of THE WILLFUL.|","|You have claimed the Mantle of THE USURPER.|","|Due to being one of the first lifeforms to stand among THE WILLFUL, and possessing a unique connection to a Lifeform whose name is already etched in Narrative History (THE Sealed One), you have drawn the gaze of one of Those Who Remain.|","| THE Sealed One was among the first to be Ordained, bearing the Unique Ordination: The Zenith of Subjugation.|","| THE RAVENOUS ARCHITECT looks upon you with dark amusement. Support is granted to see how much you can devour before you break.|","BOOM!","A terrifying gaze landed heavily upon Adrastia, burning his entire existence as though he had stepped into a furnace!","Yet, instead of turning to ash, he felt his Dimensionality rapidly beginning to rise. He understood the mechanics immediately from the stolen memories of THE Sealed One, feeling his own existence gradually becoming more and more clear amidst the burning pressure.","But as his own standing deepened, he also felt the connected weavings of THE Sealed One shudder with unfathomable growth!","Far away, the monster was rising up tremendously in its own Dimensionality, benefiting from this new system of THE Provenance of Existence more than almost any other being.","Boundless Narrative Moirai surrounded THE Sealed One due to the heavy history it had established Ages ago and the conquests it was establishing now. Existence would heavily defer to the ancient terror, bending probability at every turn to help it achieve its aims!","Adrastia held Rose ever closer, his mind turning terrifyingly cold as he decided exactly what he had to do.","He was more closely connected with THE Sealed One than many others, having already successfully assimilated a portion of the being’s vessel. At this point, there was no room for doubt or fear. He would try to assimilate even more of this terrifying entity!","BOOM!","Moirai exploded around him, the unstable flames of THE WILLFUL flaring wildly as another prompt arrived.","|You have begun building a heavy Narrative Momentum. THE RAVENOUS ARCHITECT is delighted at this choice and watches on with high expectations.|","...!","With shining eyes, he planned!"]},{"number":5640,"title":"Chapter 5640: Chapter 5639: Ruling! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Although the ongoings of existence had shattered every precedent, the quiet that followed inside THE Infiniverse was remarkably serene.","Noah floated silently atop the verdant blue-gold hills of his own domain. Far above him, the skies continued to bud and bloom with more and more Observable Existences, a cascading expansion that his people were granted access to open with the direct help of THE Infiniverse.","He looked out over the sprawling, nested realms, his vision piercing the boundaries of space to see the countless millions of humans, the exemplifiers, and his core party settling into their newly elevated stations.","In truth, a profound asymmetry hung between him and everyone else. While he was a Provenance Lifeform who generated his own standing, all of his people were not. They remained situated on the established weavings of existence, subject to the same frameworks and laws as all others.","Because of this, his people would inevitably be affected by THE Provenance of Existence. He had chosen to personally deny the new measure, refusing to kneel at a borrowed ladder!","Yet, he still needed to decide how he could utilize the way existence had violently changed to his own absolute advantage.","After all, Those Who Remain had just rewritten the rules so that roles and archetypes of existence were now the critical decider of power and standing. The imposition of Mantles meant that playing a part perfectly was now the heaviest currency in reality!","Noah considered his own history. He already possessed his own weavings of THE Protagonist. He had assigned many roles to himself long before this mandate ever arrived!","He even held the word PROTAGONIST locked firmly within his Osmontian Tongue. Operating under that absolute linguistic anchor was both THE Aura of THE Protagonist and THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard.","If Mantles and archetypes truly began acting as the heavy decider on the flow of existence, would he not be able to potentially bring the archetype of THE Protagonist to the forefront?","HUUM!","His entire existence buzzed at the thought alone!","This was a concept that was already his, generated from his own actions and his own identity, belonging to nobody else!","As he continued to turn the possibility over in his mind, he also knew he had to begin preparing heavy defensive measures.","The words and actions of Vakochev hung fresh in the air. The maker of the old Scales had explicitly warned that \"they will come for you\" before he retreated in defeat.","Furthermore, there was the obsidian crystal of unknown nature currently sitting silent and unmoving within Noah’s consciousness, left behind after Vakochev disappeared. There were lots of things to figure out but...","If Noah truly could bring forth THE Protagonist as a Mantle and force existence itself to support him, it would create an insurmountable bulwark. To have the sheer conceptual weight of THE Protagonist backed by the narrative weight of existence itself would allow him to weather whatever Those Who Remain sent his way!","Another piece of his vast arsenal clicked into place as there was also his True Declarative Human Ruling.","It was a supreme authority granted by THE True Distinction of THE True Human Emperor, an asset he had carried but never found a proper use for, nor truly known what to do with.","And now, Those Who Remain had imposed a vast, overarching Ruling that was THE Provenance of Existence!","How astounding the symmetry of reality could be. It felt like many disparate pieces of his existence were suddenly clicking together!","He could now enact a grand vision with tools that had merely been waiting for the proper stage.","The thought alone filled him with an overwhelming immensity. He did not waste another second in contemplation. He instantly commanded his stellar blue Provenance Essence, letting his weavings ring out with absolute tyranny!","\" Bring forth my weavings of the Protagonist as a Hidden Mantle ,\" Noah commanded, his voice echoing across the verdant hills with the weight of an unbroken sovereign.","\"I will finally utilize my True Declarative Human Ruling to usher in something that can interact with and benefit from THE Provenance of Existence, without ever being privy to Those Who Remain. A Mantle akin to a cheat in their own system, one that they do not know about. Generate them from the core of who I am, what I have been doing across existence, and what I am doing now.\"","WAA!","Existence answered him, not with the booming voice of an Immense One, but through the silent, generated authority of his own blood and will!","A cascade of grand and glorious prompts flooded his vision, detailing a grand ruling that stitched itself seamlessly into the fabric of reality while entirely bypassing the watchful eyes of the system’s architects.","|TRUE DECLARATIVE HUMAN RULING INITIATED.|","|Your unique weavings of THE Protagonist are being weaponized against the ambient laws of THE Provenance of Existence. You are bypassing the standard assignment of roles to carve your own definition into the Records of reality.|","|A Hidden Mantle is born. It is integrated into the flow of existence, yet utterly excluded from the gazes and attention of Those Who Remain. You will draw upon their established mechanics without ever registering on their ledgers.|","...!","|Because you have lived as a Protagonist so truly, and because your very existence has always moved in perfect accordance with this role, you are not merely granted a Mantle. You gain your Ordination in this very instant.|","|ORDINATION ACHIEVED: THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist.|","|THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist: You are not merely an actor upon the stage of existence; you are the one who recognizes the script and holds the pen. Existence will aggressively defer to your narrative direction. You are granted the following initial grand capabilities under this Ordination:|","|1. Narrative Override: You possess the capability to change the Narrative of any character who holds a Mantle into one that you choose. You may redefine an enemy’s role mid-battle, stripping them of their Moirai by forcing them into a script they cannot fulfill.|","|2. Existential Plot Armor : Any lethal strike, overarching curse, or sequence-ending event that does not align with the continuing story of THE Protagonist will be categorically refused by existence. Probability will bend to near absolute zero to ensure your narrative survives to its intended conclusion.|","|3. Scene Dictation : You may declare a localized region of space to be a closed narrative act. While this capability is active, all external interference, reinforcements, and ambient dimensional laws are nullified until THE Protagonist resolves the scene on his own terms.|","...!"]},{"number":5641,"title":"Chapter 5641: Chapter 5640: Ruling! II","paragraphs":["The sheer audacity of the prompts caused the air around Noah to grow heavy and dense!","He had taken the supreme measure of THE Immense Ones and generated his own name over the top of it, securing the benefits of their cruel currency without ever submitting to their authority!","BOOM!","The verdant hills shook violently as the physical manifestation of his new Ordination arrived.","Obsidian gold rivers of Osmontian Moirai surged into being from the empty air, roaring around him in a torrential, swirling storm of localized destiny.","Unlike the standard Existential Moirai that paid the obedient servants of the Pax, this Moirai belonged solely to him. It carried the dark, fiendish weight of his blood, completely superseding the normal rules of probability!","Noah stood at the center of the obsidian gold rivers, feeling the staggering upward pressure of a reality that was now actively conspiring to ensure his victory.","He breathed in the heavy, intoxicating current of his own generated destiny, his eyes glowing with quiet, unyielding dominance!","Although the obsidian gold rivers of his newly generated Osmontian Moirai had settled into a quiet, terrifying orbit around him, Noah did not let his momentum rest.","He remained suspended within the absolute clarity of his Reverie, floating atop the verdant hills of THE Infiniverse while the skies above him rippled with endless potential!","In truth, he was still dissecting the staggering capabilities granted by his Ordination as THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist. The prompt detailing Scene Dictation sat heavily at the forefront of his mind.","If he could declare a localized region of space to be a closed narrative act, nullifying all external interference and ambient dimensional laws until the scene resolved on his own terms, he possessed the ultimate absolute defense!","Of course, a scene required an ending. He needed a resolution condition so impossible, so unfathomably distant, that the scene would effectively never end until he explicitly chose to end it.","Noah looked up at the boundless skies of his domain.","\"A true defense... is not a barrier of force. It is a boundary of script. If you want to keep the storm out, you do not build a higher roof. You simply write a play where the rain is not permitted to fall until the final act. I have the pen now. And I... am writing the walls.\"","WAA!","His tone dropped its warmth for flat, tyrannical certainty.","\"I declare THE Infiniverse to be a closed narrative act. And this scene will only be resolved when THE Infiniverse obtains IT. The IT that THE Sealed One and all others seek will be the single, absolute condition that resolves this closed narrative!\"","BOOM!","The response from existence was immediate and deafening!","A shockwave of pure narrative authority erupted from his fingertips, expanding outward at speeds that made light look entirely static!","The skies of THE Infiniverse did not physically alter their color, but a profound, unyielding conceptual lock clamped down over the entire Unique Transfinite Dimension.","The boundary of reality thickened noticeably. The rivers of Osmontian Moirai surged upward, weaving themselves into the very fabric of the space, turning the atmosphere heavy with the undeniable weight of an authored script!","Crisp, staggering prompts cascaded down his vision.","|SCENE DICTATION INITIATED.|","|THE Infiniverse has been declared a Closed Narrative Act.|","|Resolution Condition: The acquisition of IT by THE Infiniverse.|","|Effect: All external interference, hostile reinforcements, and ambient dimensional laws authored by Those Who Remain are categorically nullified. No authority, no Enforcer, and no Immense One may pierce this space or alter its internal logic until the Narrative Act reaches its stated resolution.|","...!","Noah observed the flawless execution of his command, the sheer security of it filling his existence with a cold satisfaction!","The fortress was sealed tight against the prying eyes of ancient monstrosities. He felt an overwhelming urge to continue riding this soaring momentum, to fully capitalize on the sequence of unbroken victories he had carved out over the past hours.","After all, he had done a staggering amount of giving recently.","He had reached into the cursed lineages of Baelgrim, Sylvaine, Kharvel, and the others, granting them an impossible cure and absolute freedom from their ancient sentences.","He had forced the proudest Enforcers to kneel. He had even weaponized the new Ruling to gift a Narrative of Existence directly to Mahishasura, setting the Descendant as the lead actor in a grand epic of political crusade!","He had given grandly. And according to his Foundations, what he gave always returned to him grander.","\" Release all the collected boons of THE Tide That Owes Nothing from my recent actions,\" Noah declared into the quiet air.","He already knew exactly what he wanted the prizes to be. With the sheer volume of his people currently settling into their new power across his domain, he needed more space, more realms, and more structural foundation. His intention for the collected boons was entirely focused on THE Genesis Tesseracts, because with more Tesseracts, more Observable Existences could bloom within his protection!","...!","The stellar blue-gold light of his Provenance Essence flared as the Tide answered his call, calculating the sheer weight of his recent salvation and conquest.","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing recognizes the salvation of ancient Descendants, the upending of established mountain fiefs, and the genesis of a grand Narrative of Existence among many acts of giving.|","|Calculated Boon Yield: 4,000 Genesis Tesseracts.|","|Wait. Anomaly detected within your Ordination.|","Noah narrowed his eyes slightly as the prompts flickered, shifting from the standard gold of the Tide to the dark, obsidian-gold hue of his Osmontian Moirai.","| Your Hidden Mantle of THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist has inherently triggered the Narrative Archetype of EXISTENCE BLESSED.|","...!","|EXISTENCE BLESSED: Existence itself actively conspires in THE Protagonist’s favor. Natural disasters happen at the exact moment you need a distraction. Rare opportunities drop directly into your lap without effort. Lethal attacks miraculously miss your vitals by a hair’s breadth. Existence bends to ensure your continued rise.|","|For you, the boon of the Tide has been tripled.|","|12,000 Genesis Tesseracts have been brought to fruition.|","BOOM!"]},{"number":5642,"title":"Chapter 5642: Chapter 5641: Ruling! III","paragraphs":["The heavens above THE Infiniverse shattered into a display of unfathomable, dazzling beauty!","Twelve thousand hypercubes of deep blue-white light bloomed into existence simultaneously, hanging against the skies!","They spun slowly, humming with the raw, unshaped potential of entire Observable Existences waiting to be unpacked.","The sheer density of the gathered Tesseracts cast a brilliant, oscillating glow over the verdant hills, illuminating Noah’s face as he looked up at the staggering harvest!","It was a level of wealth that defied all logic, paid out by an Existence that was now mechanically forced to favor him!","As Noah watched the hypercubes drift in their majestic, silent orbit, the space beside him rippled gently.","Thalia Vasiliou stepped onto the grass, her white-blue robes shifting in the wind. She did not look at the magnificent display of Tesseracts right away. Instead, she looked at Noah, her expression clouded with a heavy, troubled weight.","She looked around at their surroundings, taking in the suffocating security of the Scene Dictation and the dazzling lights above, before she finally spoke.","\" The Ruling of THE Provenance of Existence... was not supposed to be enacted until much later, \" Thalia said, her voice quiet but strained.","\" In the future, you mentioned something to me about Vakochev right before everything came down. Did Vakochev reach out to you already? Because even that was supposed to happen much later.\"","...!","Noah turned his gaze away from the blooming stars to look at the dazzling woman beside him.","His endlessly blue eyes shone brightly as he listened to her words.","They held terrifyingly heavy implications!","If THE Provenance of Existence was not supposed to come down right now, it meant Vakochev was not supposed to have lost his war so early. The maker of the Scales had retreated prematurely, triggering the Immense Ones to impose their new order long before the timeline dictated they should.","Why would things be playing out differently?","Noah evaluated the variables with cold precision. Did any of this have anything to do with his own aggressive actions across THE Krazhor-Nul and THE Ymnaros? Or did it stem from Thalia herself coming back across Dimensions and Time?","His recent movements against Those Who Remain could not have possibly triggered things to start playing out differently, right?","The past could not be changed. The loops of existence were closed, meaning everything that was happening now was exactly as it was always supposed to happen.","Yet, her clouded expression told a different story. If the loop was closed, why was she surprised by the timing?","Noah considered the paradox silently.","Existence was a script. If his actions were rewriting the timeline in real time, then the rules of causality she relied on were already breaking under his weight!","And if the rules were broken, then the future she was trying to prevent was no longer the future they were walking into.","Nothing was set in stone!","What she knew could or could not happen!","\"...\"","---","<THE Infinity Eater>","Existence is terribly fond of the illusion of freedom!","Terribly!","But the truth of any harvest is that someone always owns the field.","Many ancient beings believed they were the masters of their own domains. They cultivated boundless blue Infinity, climbed Vakochev’s Scales, and raised grand citadels across the observable and unobservable realms. In truth, they were merely crops left to fatten in the sun!","THE PAX existed to prune the weeds that grew too tall and disrupted the soil. THE Infinity Eater existed to reap the harvest when the season finally ended.","He sat in the center of a dying Dimension. It was a hollowed-out realm of gray dust and silent, hovering structures. Rivers of pure blue Infinity flowed continuously into his pale, elongated form, drawn from thr countless decillions of True Lifeforms scattered across adjacent Dimensions.","He did not look like a monster. He looked like a weary scholar draped in immaculate white robes, his eyes solid blue spheres without pupils .","He looked up at the tearing sky. Above him, the boundary of the Dimension was folded backward, revealing an eye that spanned the entire horizon. It was a presence that crushed the very concept of depth. It was one of THE Immense Ones.","\" The new Ruling is remarkably loud,\" THE Infinity Eater spoke. His voice was smooth and polite, carrying the precise annoyance of an accountant finding an error in the Records.","\" You have handed Mantles to the absolute dregs of reality. You are paying them in Moirai for playing out their little roles. Why flood the market with currency when the old system kept them so predictably obedient? Vakochev was actually not so bad.\"","The eye above did not blink. A serene, feminine voice resonated directly within the structure of his existence, carrying the weight of ancient architecture.","\"A river that never floods leaves the soil to turn to dust.\" Her voice sounded like grinding tectonic plates softened by velvet. \" The water must be allowed to rise so that we may see what knows how to swim.\"","\"It is inefficient ,\" THE Infinity Eater countered. He raised a pale hand, observing the golden sign of his own Mantle rotating slowly above his palm. It was the shape of a curved scythe.","He had been weighed and Ordained in the very first nanosecond the Ruling descended. He held the Mantle of THE HARVESTER.","It was a role he had played for Ages, perfectly in accordance with the design of Those Who Remain. Existential Moirai flooded him constantly, a localized destiny ensuring that whatever he sought to consume would inevitably fall into his mouth.","\"I have farmed these Dimensions for you since the earliest epochs, \" he continued. \"I let them build their Egos and their True bodies. Then I drink their Existence ever so slowly and send the yield upward. This new Provenance of Existence gives them hope in these roles. It gives them the illusion that they can author their own standing. Hope is a notoriously difficult crop to manage.\"","\" Hope is not a crop,\" the serene voice answered, shifting the pressure in the gray air. \" Hope is the plow. It turns the earth. It makes the roots dig deeper. When the roots are deep, the fruit is heavy.\"","THE Infinity Eater frowned. The answers of THE Immense Ones were never truly answers. They were simply pronouncements of weather from beings who lived above the clouds!","He knew better than to ask for a plain explanation. He merely needed to ensure his own quota remained undisturbed.","\"As long as my fields are protected, you may play whatever games you wish with their Existence, \" he said calmly.","He closed his solid blue eyes and reached out through his unfathomable senses, checking the intake valves of his vast, invisible network. He monitored the deep, hidden tethers that connected him to the countless decillions of Lifeforms across all Dimensions he had his network.","He expected the familiar, rushing torrent of blue Infinity.","He felt...less.","THE Infinity Eater opened his eyes. The serene composure broke for a fraction of a second, revealing the terrifying, endless void beneath his pale skin.","He checked the invisible tethers again. The lifeforms were still there. They were still drawing on a wellspring of power, still generating massive amounts of weavings of existence.","But the source they were drawing from was no longer him. It was no longer a current he owned!","Someone had seamlessly slid beneath his architecture. Someone had replaced his water with their own, turning his entire crop into dependents of a new, unknown wellspring!","\" The fruit is suddenly growing on someone else’s tree ,\" THE Infinity Eater murmured.","He looked back up at the colossal eye spanning the broken sky.","\" Did you authorize another collector in the eastern Dimensions? \" he asked.","\" The wind blows where the pressure drops ,\" the feminine voice replied softly. \" If a house falls, it is because the wood was ready to break.\"","THE Infinity Eater let out a slow, cold sigh. These monstrous beings never gave straight answers!","He stood up. The gray dust around him swirled into a violent vortex as the immense pressure of his Dimensionality flared outward. The scythe of his Mantle pulsed with demanding, hungry gold light.","\"I am THE HARVESTER ,\" THE Infinity Eater declared. His polite tone completely vanished, replaced by the sheer, absolute gravity of a predator whose territory had been breached.","\" And I have to go find out who is stealing from my farm of lifeforms and replacing me as the source.\"","The colossal eye above slowly faded into the dark, offering no blessing and no warning.","THE Infinity Eater stepped forward and vanished into the crossing, leaving the hollow Dimension to quietly collapse behind him."]},{"number":5643,"title":"Chapter 5643: Chapter 5642: Power!","paragraphs":["<Descendant Alcaeus>","A great number of lifeforms believe peace is the ultimate reward of a long life.","They would be ridiculously wrong.","The truth of any cage of peace is that eventually, the prisoner will beg for a war.","For those who lived across the deepest expanses of reality, stagnation was the only true death.","They climbed through the tiers of existence, gathered their authority, and built their citadels. Yet, when a being possesses the lifespan of an entire epoch, the quiet becomes an unbearable weight. To answer this endless boredom, certain Dimensions were authored exclusively for the harvest of violence.","THE Morior Dimension was one such place.","It was a vast, blood-soaked arena where the progeny of the highest authorities went to prove the weight of their lineages. Deaths that occurred upon its rusted soil were not recorded in the Records as permanent endings. The Dimension itself was a miraculous testing ground where shattered flesh and spilled Trueness were simply collected and remade, allowing the strong to fight without the inconvenient finality of a true death. It was a slaughterhouse that functioned as a stage.","In the center of a jagged canyon, Descendant Alcaeus stood like a monument to absolute brutality.","He was a colossal, muscular titan draped in the thick, golden pelt of a slaughtered Primeval beast. His skin was scarred bronze, and his eyes burned with a terrifying, unyielding joy. He did not care for politics or anything else. He cared only for the glory of battle!","Of course, the rules of his favored game had recently changed.","When Vakochev’s Scales fractured across reality, THE Provenance of Existence had descended. Alcaeus had not questioned the booming, serene voice that spoke into his lineage. He had simply proclaimed his life of violence loudly to the empty air. Existence had weighed his endless battles, measured his absolute devotion to conflict, and found him perfectly in accordance.","A golden sign shaped like a roaring lion’s visage hovered above his head. He was Ordained. He held the Mantle of THE CHAMPION.","Because of his staggering accumulation of victories, he had already triggered a Narrative of Existence. The information that resonated in his mind called it THE Endless Crucible . It was a triggered external conflict that paid him for every drop of blood he spilled. He did not need to retreat to a quiet peak to cultivate his power. He simply needed to fight, and the Ruling would fund his rise.","Existential Moirai surrounded him in a thick, golden aura. It acted as a localized destiny, actively lifting him up and bending probability to ensure his continued survival in the canyon.","He was not fighting alone.","Far above the rusted cliffs, the sky was not a sky at all. Three massive eyes hovered in the purple firmament, unblinking and terribly ancient!","They were three of THE Immense Ones, looking down to observe the proving grounds of their children. They watched the bloodsport in total silence, their mere presence crushing the air below.","\" Come on!\" Alcaeus roared, his voice shaking the canyon walls. \" Is this all the depth you can muster?!\"","Hundreds of other Descendants charged him from all sides. They carried massive weapons and roared with THE Argent Loom!","Alcaeus laughed joyfully.","He did not draw a blade. His Dimensionality ran terrifyingly deep. He understood that true power was not about how hard a thing could push, but where a thing truly stood!","He reached his massive hands up and physically grabbed the white threads of THE Argent Loom that stitched the air together.","Alcaeus grabbed the threads and pulled them down into his palms by brute force. He mixed the pristine white authority of The Argent Loom with his own roaring, bronze-colored power, and then flooded the mixture with the heavy golden Moirai granted by his Mantle.","He pressed his massive hands together.","The sheer, unfathomable PONDUS required to compress such authorities was staggering, but his muscles merely bulged as he forced the mixture to collapse inward!","The threads, the power, and the destiny condensed into a sphere no larger than a fist. It was a small, screaming, condensed dimension of pure kinetic force.","He formed a miniature Dimension with his own hands!","Alcaeus threw the compressed dimension directly into the charging army.","BOOM!","The miniature thing expanded instantly upon impact. It swallowed fifty Descendants in a localized singularity of white light and crushing pressure. Armor shattered. Weapons turned to dust. The roaring of his enemies was simply snuffed out as their bodies were unmade and swept out of the arena to be reconstructed later.","The survivors leaped through the settling dust, their power aimed at his neck and chest.","Alcaeus moved into the fray.","A spear of THE Argent Loom thrust toward his throat. Existence leaned. The Moirai of THE CHAMPION bent the probability of the strike away, causing the spear to glide harmlessly past his skin!","He caught a falling sword of THE Argent Loom with his bare hand, the blade biting into his palm. He squeezed his fist, shattering the weapon into fragments, and punched the owner so hard the air itself screamed.","He threw another compressed dimension!","BOOM!","The battlefield became a canvas of absolute destruction. For an hour, the canyon shook with the sounds of unmaking. Alcaeus fought with the chaotic, unyielding rhythm of a being who knew he could not lose. He did not fight to survive. He fought because fighting was the only language he truly understood.","When the dust finally settled, Alcaeus stood alone in the center of the crater.","The corpses of hundreds of defeated Descendants remained scattered across the broken ground, waiting for the Dimension’s laws to pull them back into the cycle. Those few who had survived in the periphery had already turned and run, their morale broken by the sheer, insurmountable depth of THE CHAMPION!","Alcaeus threw his head back and roared his triumph to the empty sky!","OOOOH!","The response from the new Ruling was immediate and staggering. Moirai gushed down from the heavens like a golden sea, pouring directly into his body. The sheer volume of the reward washed over his attributes, feeding his existence and solidifying his Mantle even further. He felt the heavy, intoxicating rush of am Existence that was actively paying him for his violence.","As he stood basking in the golden downpour, the sky changed.","One of the three massive eyes above him suddenly pulsed. It was a bloodshot, terrifying gaze that represented THE SLEEPLESS FIEND.","The atmosphere in the canyon dropped to an absolute, freezing silence. The other two eyes slowly drifted backward, allowing the Fiend’s gaze to dominate the firmament.","Alcaeus stopped laughing. He fell to one knee, bowing his head in sudden, total reverence.","The message did not arrive as a sound. It bypassed his ears completely and burned directly into the obsidian brow-mark on his forehead. It carried the impersonal, heavy weight of a Father addressing a useful tool.","| Something has grown bold enough to rewrite my curses.|","Alcaeus grimaced as the sheer density of the thought pressed into his skull.","|It has passed through THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension and THE Ymnaros Dimension. A Cure-Giver.|","The image of a broken curse, of Steeds running unchained, and of lines of writing being forcibly altered flickered through his mind. The Fiend was searching for the source of an impossible rebellion.","| Find it for me and ask it for me... what made it so bold?|","HUUM!","The burning sensation in his brow slowly faded. The massive eye in the sky stopped pulsing and drifted back into its silent, unblinking watch alongside the others.","Alcaeus remained kneeling for a long moment, the dust settling silently around him. He processed the weight of the command. A hunt!","A target that had somehow managed to undo the authored punishments of Those Who Remain. A being that operated across THE Krazhor-Nul and THE Ymnaros.","He looked up at the sky as a wide, terrifying grin spread across his face.","He laughed joyfully, the sound echoing through the canyon of corpses. He did not care about the politics of curses, or the implications of a broken sentence. He only cared that a target capable of such impossible feats would undoubtedly provide the greatest battle of his entire immortal life.","\"As THE SLEEPLESS FIEND deems,\" Alcaeus said.","Oh!","Existence was vast and filled with terrors .","One couldn’t even begin to imagine just what terrifying wonders were out there that they didn’t even know about!"]},{"number":5644,"title":"Chapter 5644: Chapter 5643: A Thousand Origins","paragraphs":["<A Thousand Origins>","What could not be perceived by the vast majority was always the most pristine.","Down in the mud of the lower frameworks, authority was loud. Egos clashed against each other in open displays of light and force.","Dimensions bled. Observable Existences were shattered to prove a point. Up in the terrifying depths of true Dimensionality, existence was a perfectly still lake!","To stand at the absolute summit of reality was not to shout. It was to become a ghost to everything beneath you.","In fact, there existed domains so deeply seated in the unseen layers of reality that even strong True Lifeforms and ancient Primeval Lifeforms could not perceive them. If a Cenozoic or Mesozoic master somehow managed to fly through the coordinates of such a place, they would see only empty space and silent dark.","THE Concord of a Thousand Origins was exactly one of these places.","It was a vast, staggering architecture that defied every natural law of existence!","Exactly one thousand individual Dimensions were clustered together into a single, breathtaking metropolis. They were bound to one another by colossal, physical bridges woven from pure white threads of THE Argent Loom.","From a distance, it looked like a Dimensional reef.","An axis Dimension of pure, shining purple gold sat at the center, acting as the anchor. Bolted onto its edges were realms of entirely different natures.","A Dimension consisting entirely of endless blue oceans was grafted directly into a Dimension of burning black obsidian. A realm of floating crystal towers fed seamlessly into a sprawling jungle of petrified wood.","Of course, a city built of a thousand Dimensions did not house peasants.","The thoroughfares of THE Concord of a Thousand Origins were filled with the absolute apex of Existence!","Colossal Primeval Lifeforms pulled massive barges of tribute across the void between realms. Ancient True Lifeforms traded the fates of lower Observable Existences as casually as mortals traded coins.","Most importantly, it was the supreme gathering place for the children of the architects. Descendants of every conceivable lineage mingled, schemed, and operated across the sprawling bridges.","This place was the original forge. It was known in hushed rumors as one of the primary locations where many Descendants were engineered, stitched together, and born in the earliest epochs . It was a sprawling laboratory of authority, acting as one of the few places in all of reality where Those Who Remain could actually be reached!","To step foot in a place like this was to have won in existence.","Since the fracture of Vakochev’s Scales and the descent of the new Ruling, THE Concord of a Thousand Origins had become a blinding storm of fate and destiny. Because it was heavily populated by the highest concentration of the Ordained, complex and grand Narratives of Existence had begun to bloom in every sector.","Existential Moirai poured down from the space in localized systems. Above the crowds, golden shields, white swords, and travelers’ staves hovered proudly over the heads of the most devoted actors .","Rival lineages fought proxy wars of succession. Grand crusades were funded by the very air they breathed. The entire cluster of a thousand Dimensions was vibrating with the euphoria of a place that was finally paying its rulers for their cruelty!","Despite the sheer, suffocating density of authority crowding the white bridges, some of the true apex of the Concord was entirely ignored.","In a bustling central region, a dazzling woman walked through a courtyard surrounded by towering Descendants. She moved with absolute, gliding silence. Her white-blue robes shifted gently in the ambient wind.","She was followed closely by a second woman.","The follower wore plain, unadorned gray garments. She radiated absolutely no power. She carried no Intent, no roaring blue Infinity, and no trace of THE Primordial Source or Argent Loom!","Yet, she held a terrifying pressure that physically warped the air inches from her skin. The sheer weight of her bearing was so immense that if she allowed even a fraction of it to express itself, the courtyard of Descendants would have been flattened into paste.","The Descendants around them did not even know they were there!","A colossal, bronze-skinned Descendant wearing the Mantle of THE TYRANT stepped directly into the path of the two women. He did not bump into them. He simply passed right through the space they occupied, completely unaware that he had just walked through the projected shadows of two beings whose depth made him look like a drawing on a piece of paper.","The Dimensionality of these women was that high!","Because they generated their own standing and did not rely on the ladders built by Those Who Remain, their power rendered them absolute ghosts in the most crowded room in existence.","The follower stepped closer to the dazzling woman in white-blue. Her voice carried a quiet, lethal edge that ignored the surrounding noise of the market entirely.","\" Queenling Thalia, what are we doing in a vile place like this? \" the follower asked. \" Descendants frolick and Those Who Remain choose places like this to do whatever vile things they want. What is there for us here?\"","...!","Queenling Thalia!","Thalia Vasiliou stopped walking. She reached up with a calm, unhurried motion and brought her hood down.","Her striking, freckled face and deep red hair were exposed to a crowd of ancient monsters who could not perceive a single detail of her beauty!","She looked around the courtyard, taking in the golden signs hovering above the Ordained and the heavy, intoxicating smell of Moirai in the air.","She raised her hand to eye level.","Her pale skin was flickering. The edges of her fingers blurred in and out of existence, vibrating violently as if the hand was attempting to disappear. It looked as though her physical form was trying to merge with another version of her that absolutely should not be here!","Moving across Dimensions and Time carried an unfathomable cost. The rules of causality did not appreciate a closed loop being pried open!","The paradox of her presence was beginning to exact its toll, fraying the very edges of her Provenance.","Thalia looked at her flickering hand with complete, composed indifference.","\"I have to talk to one of Those Who Remain in this place who owes us a favor,\" Thalia said smoothly, her voice betraying none of the physical degradation she was enduring. \" He can answer some of my questions regarding Vakochev and THE Provenance of Existence.\"","...!","Two Provenance Lifeforms had appeared in this place.","It was not the first time such an impossible event had occurred in the deep history of existence, but it was certainly not something that happened openly. The sheer audacity of walking into the very forge where Those Who Remain engineered their children was a testament to the absolute grandness of their standing!","Vakochev had retreated too early. The new Ruling had descended long before the timeline dictated it should. The events she had traveled back to prevent were suddenly rushing forward, reacting to an existence that refused to play by the established script.","She needed to know why the timeline was breaking. She needed to know what the architects were rushing to prepare for.","Her aim here was a singular one!","Thalia lowered her flickering hand and moved forward, walking straight through the illusions of the mighty!","---","When an existence possesses the authority to rewrite reality and fears absolutely nothing, its appetites do not diminish as they actually inflate. The architects of existence, Those Who Remain, did not sit in quiet contemplation of Existence. They indulged!","They treated lower Dimensions like personal vineyards and ancient Primeval Lifeforms like disposable playthings, engineering lineages of Descendants out of sheer boredom and base desire.","Thalia Vasiliou walked through the deeper sectors of THE Concord of a Thousand Origins, her expression composed perfectly over a rising disgust.","She and her gray-robed escort passed through bridging Dimensions that showcased the absolute debauchery of the architects. They walked over a realm consisting entirely of oceans of wine where colossal Primeval Lifeforms drowned themselves for sport. They bypassed a floating continent where generations of Descendants were bred and discarded in endless, violent revelry.","Eventually, the dazzling lights of the Concord faded. Thalia arrived at the edge of a Dimension composed of pure, suffocating darkness.","In the center of the black expanse sat a towering temple of jagged obsidian. The grounds outside the temple were packed with thousands of kneeling Descendants. They pressed their knees against the cold stone, their bodies trembling in absolute reverence toward the open doors.","Thalia did not kneel as she walked straight through the kneeling masses, her white-blue robes cutting a pristine path through the dark, her escort following silently behind her.","They entered the temple.","The air inside was so dense it felt like walking through solid earth. There were no walls and no ceilings, only a central dais that defied all optical logic. Thalia stared directly into the center of the temple and saw what looked like countless event horizons stacked on top of one another!","The overlapping singularities leaked an air of terrible, suffocating power that warped the very concept of distance.","A voice echoed out from the stacked event horizons. It sounded wet, heavy, and slithering with ancient amusement.","\"A Provenance Lifeform steps into my domain without an invitation.\" The voice pressed against the stone floor, forcing the ambient darkness to ripple.","\"It is a rare thing for one of your kind to dare to come see one of THE Immense Ones unplanned.\"","Thalia stood perfectly straight. She did not let a single ounce of pressure force her gaze downward.","\" You have worked with my Father before,\" Thalia spoke, her voice ringing clear and cold through the suffocating temple . \"I can do something as simple as seeking an audience. On behalf of my Provenance Lineage, I came to call upon the favor granted by THE SECRETIVE DEFILER ages ago.\"","HUUM!","The event horizons spun faster, grinding against one another as the being inside listened.","\"I seek to know of the conflict involving Vakochev, \" Thalia continued, her tone completely devoid of fear.","\" Nobody heard any musings of the battle that was supposed to occur. Nor did anyone predict the premature descent of the Ruling of THE Provenance of Existence, which was only a rumor for all of us until it happened. I seek to know what happened.\"","...!","The darkness inside the temple deepened.","The stacks of event horizons began to part. THE Immense One materialized from the crushing gravity, forming into a hazy, colossal humanoid outline. Two massive obsidian horns curved upward from its shifting head!","The face held no distinct features, save for two eyes burning with a sickening, absolute power that devoured the light around them.","THE SECRETIVE DEFILER gazed down at Thalia’s pristine figure. The burning eyes dragged slowly over her white-blue robes, lingering with a heavy, unmistakable hunger.","\" Vakochev simply could not measure up to the Narrative he sought to take down,\" THE SECRETIVE DEFILER rumbled, his voice dripping with base desire.","\" And the new Ruling fell. You wish to know the mechanics of all this...?\"","The hazy, horned giant leaned forward.","\"I will tell you everything I can regarding what happened, \" THE SECRETIVE DEFILER said, a cruel amusement lacing his words.","\" Because things definitely got interesting. But knowledge of this depth requires a toll, little Queenling. Present yourself to me as a gift. Be given the honor to lay with me for a thousand years, and breed to produce at least a hundred Descendants for my halls. Do this, and you will have your answers.\"","...!","A wave of absolute, freezing cold washed over the obsidian temple!","The gray-robed escort standing behind Thalia did not speak, but the terrifying pressure radiating from her frame spiked. The ambient darkness of the temple buzzed under the sheer weight of the escort’s anger, the stone floor spiderwebbing with hairline cracks beneath her plain shoes!","HUUM!","Thalia looked up at the hazy, horned outline of the ancient architect. Her freckled face was a mask of pure, absolute distaste.","\"I would rather unmake my own Provenance and scatter my essence into the void.\" Thalia declared, her voice carrying the unyielding frost of an absolute sovereign!","And THE Immense One laughed as if he found this profoundly entertaining!","\" Keep your secrets. I will find the truth from something that does not crawl in the mud.\"","She did not wait for a dismissal. Thalia turned on her heel, her white-blue robes sweeping over the fractured stone as she and her escort walked toward the exit.","THE SECRETIVE DEFILER did not strike her. He simply watched her go, his burning eyes narrowing with a cold, predatory amusement.","\" Walk away, Queenling ,\" THE SECRETIVE DEFILER boomed. \" But do not forget that Provenance Lifeforms do not sit above THE Immense Ones. Do not forget who needs to suckle at the feet of whom.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5645,"title":"Chapter 5645: Chapter 5644: The Arbiter!","paragraphs":["<The Arbiter>","The new ruling imposed by Those Who Remain was presented as a measure of stability.","It was, and yet any sudden freedom will simply removes the mask many wore before.","The Provenance of Existence did not merely grant people power as it allowed them to be exactly who they truly were and amplified it, regardless of how ugly that truth happened to be.","For the Arbiter of THE Serenaros Dimension, the truth was exceptionally ugly.","He stood as the leading figure of THE PAX across the entire Dimension. He held Mahishasura and many other Enforcers beneath his command. Yet, his private reality was far removed from the cold bureaucracy of the Shrouds!","For a while, he had maintained a habit of silently causing entire sections of locked-up Inhibited Lifeforms to disappear from the vast cage-fields.","He took them into his own sealed Pocket Dimension and devoured them.","He did not eat them like a beast. He crushed the physical bodies and the very existences of Inhibited True Lifeforms and Primeval Lifeforms into a fine, sparkling powder. He then snorted this powder directly through his nose!","In fact, his Intent was specifically shaped to transform the pulverized existence directly into his nerve receptors, allowing him to feel the condensed terror, power, and final emotions of the ground-up lifeforms all at once.","It gave him an unfathomable high. He was, fundamentally, an existential addict.","Since THE Provenance of Existence came down, he had been increasing the number of lifeforms he ground to dust. He had loudly claimed his vile habits and received a Willful Mantle. He was THE DECADENT!","The euphoria he received from the new currency was immense, and his power was rising up faster than it had in an entire Age.","Inside his private Dimension, the Arbiter stood over a struggling cluster of Gilded True Lifeforms. They were stripped of all authority, their Egos screaming as his crushing Intent wrapped around them.","CRACK!","The Gilded Lifeforms shattered. Their brilliant Trueness and their lingering blue Infinity were pulverized instantly, turning into a line of stellar white dust suspended in the air.","The Arbiter leaned forward and inhaled sharply.","HUUM!","\"Ahhh....!\"","The white dust rushed into his system. The pristine white threads of THE Argent Loom mixed with his Intent and his faint Pantheon, causing his entire body to seize and vibrate. His eyes rolled back into his head as he tweaked with absolute, unadulterated euphoria!","At exactly that moment, a dark-haired Descendant Enforcer stepped into the domain. She looked at the tweaking, shivering leader of her Dimension and kept her gaze perfectly straight, acting exactly as if she saw nothing unusual.","\" Arbiter ,\" the Enforcer addressed him smoothly. \" Mahishasura seems to have taken the emergence of THE Provenance of Existence too literally. He is currently taking all other Enforcers under his banner. He seems to have received a terrifyingly strong Mantle, as the surrounding existence is heavily supporting him. What shall we do? More than half of all Enforcers within this Dimension now follow behind him like a unified force.\"","...!","The Arbiter breathed in sharply, a harsh rattling sound echoing in his throat. He blinked his bloodshot eyes rapidly, his pupils dilated to the size of coins.","\" Gather all the Enforcers remaining under me,\" the Arbiter voiced out, his words rushing together in a frantic, manic rhythm. \"I didn’t expect rebellion within our own home! Other Arbiters of THE PAX don’t have to worry about this shit. But... haha!\"","A wide, terrifying grin stretched across his face, exposing teeth stained with Existential dust.","\"I can use this conflict as an excuse to grind down more and more Inhibited Lifeforms! If more than half of the Inhibited we hold were to suddenly disappear... nothing much would change in the Records during such chaotic times! Haha, let’s go! I actually need to thank Mahishasura for bringing this conflict to my door. Gather all those remaining!\"","The dark-haired Enforcer bowed and stepped back, leaving the madman to his devices.","The moment she left, the Arbiter waved his hand frantically.","Dozens of massive metal prisons materialized in the air, filled with hundreds of defenseless True Lifeforms. The captives looked out in absolute terror at the tweaking giant.","The Arbiter did not hesitate as his Intent shot out like a collapsing Dimension, pulverizing the defenseless beings in a single, deafening crunch! They screamed, and then they were dust.","He snorted what their existence used to be with utter euphoria, his body violently shaking as he exhibited the base, desperate behaviors of an addict while simultaneously wielding the unfathomable power of a dimensional ruler. It was a horrible, grotesque combination!","As he consumed the harvest, the atmosphere of his pocket Dimension buzzed.","A flood of information erupted down his vision. He had triggered a Narrative of Existence!","|You have triggered a Narrative of Existence.|","| THE Narrative of Existence, The Hedonist’s Defense, has been triggered as you are one of the central Willful Mantles.|","|The Hedonist’s Defense: A triggered Willful Narrative centered on standing true to your ideals, your greed, and your absolute lust for existence’s highest pleasures. Those who seek to usurp your domain and take your harvest are your greatest enemies.|","|The more lifeforms you burn and pulverize while carrying out this narrative, and the more violently you clash against the incoming crusade, the more Existential Moirai will be generated for your Mantle.|","The Arbiter threw his head back and laughed. But the Ruling was not finished paying him!","Even more information cascaded down, carrying a suffocating, heavy weight that made the hairs on his arms stand up!","|One of THE Immense Ones is interested in your Narrative.|","|THE ECSTATIC FLAYER has begun to observe your movements.|","|If you put on a good show of pleasure and death, you will be granted even more power.|","The Arbiter stared at the final waves of information, his chest heaving as the ultimate high washed over him. The architects of existence themselves were watching his binge, and they were bringing more powder!","More! More! MORE!"]},{"number":5646,"title":"Chapter 5646: Chapter 5645: Narrative Vs Narrative! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Noah floated in the unseen layers Dimensionality, seated comfortably upon a high, bloody throne of crimson gold Sanguine Mana. Below his suspended position, Mahishasura cut a heroic and terrifying figure!","The golden shield of his Mantle turned slowly and proudly above his head. He floated as a righteous vanguard, surrounded by the broken, unconscious bodies of hundreds of Descendants that were Wardens and Enforcers who had dared to stand against his glorious political crusade!","Of course, a grand crusade required a constant influx of soldiers. As the defeated members of THE PAX fell, Noah simply extended his fingers from the absolute safety of his throne.","He did not need to step down and issue verbal commands. Crimson gold blades of Sanguine Mana, laced with brilliant stellar blue light, slipped silently through the air. They cut effortlessly into the chests of the unconscious Enforcers and Wardens. Noah bypassed their physical flesh entirely, diving straight into the rigid, authored sentences written into their Descendant lineages.","He flooded them with his own grammar, ruthlessly cutting away their old loyalties to Those Who Remain and binding their existences directly to his will. They rose only moments later as perfectly Veiled puppets, their eyes devoid of any rebellion as they joined the growing, unified force standing behind THE SHIELD!","In truth, Noah was deeply contemplating exactly how far he could push his own newly generated architecture.","He now held the Hidden Mantle of THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist. Since he possessed the supreme capability to override narratives and dictate closed scenes, he wondered how he could best weave this conceptual power into the current war.","Could he completely author the outcome of Mahishasura’s crusade without ever drawing a weapon himself? Would existence itself continue to fund his conquest if he simply wrote the right script from the shadows?","The sheer momentum of his recent actions answered him with a heavy, surging weight within his own body. He felt the unpaused cycle of THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis roaring through his quarks, lifting his true standing tremendously with every passing second.","He called upon his own Regard to measure the exact depth of his rise.","|VERITAS: 28|","|PROVENANCE: 27|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 29|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 35|","|Hidden Mantle: THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist|","|Capabilities: Narrative Override, Existential Plot Armor, Scene Dictation|","Every attribute was rushing aggressively toward thirty. Furthermore, his Osmontian Moirai had already reached thirty-five. Unlike the standard Existential Moirai that paid the obedient servants of the order, this dark and fiendish currency was generated solely by his own Quintessential weight!","He was growing at a pace that defied all established measures of reality, his power compounding in total silence!","The crusade moved forward. Mahishasura led his newly acquired army of Veiled Enforcers into the sky, marching toward the next towering purple gold mountain in the inner ring.","They arrived to find the vast courtyards entirely empty.","There were no Wardens. There were no Loomwrought Shrouds. The mountain was a silent, hollow peak, completely devoid of the suffocating order that usually defined THE PAX.","Then, a booming voice echoed out from the distant, hazy clouds.","\" Haha, Mahishasura, when did you grow so bold?\"","The voice carried a manic, wet rattling sound that vibrated with pure instability. It did not sound like a composed ruler of order. It sounded exactly like a desperate addict finding a fresh vein!","\" And who... is that fucker behind you on a throne? Is this your narrative, or his?\"","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes pulsed violently!","Someone had seen him! A lifeform had peered right through the Unique Precept of Solipsism! Because his true Dimensionality ran so deep that it blinded even beings in the upper thirties, this meant whoever had just spoken possessed a depth that touched the absolute summit of Transfinite Dimensionality. No Enforcer had seen him so far. He had remained entirely unperceivable to the masses!","Noah squinted his eyes, peering intently through the purple gold skies to see what anomaly had arrived.","The distant clouds parted violently as...The Arbiter of THE Serenaros floated into view.","He was a towering, terrifying Descendant. His robes were immaculate, but his face was an absolute horror of twitching muscles and heavily dilated pupils. A layer of stellar white dust coated his upper lip and the fine collar of his garments. He shivered violently in the air, tweaking with an uncontainable, frantic energy that made the surrounding space warp and groan.","Behind him floated hundreds of elite Enforcers and Wardens, backed by thousands of perfectly silent Loomwrought Shrouds. They formed a massive, terrifying army, yet all of them kept a cautious distance from their own leader.","The moment he appeared, The Arbiter did not bother addressing Mahishasura again. He simply waved his pale, shaking hands toward a series of massive metal cages hovering in the periphery of the clouds.","Inside the cages, hundreds of defenseless Inhibited True Lifeforms looked up in sheer, unadulterated terror. They were Gilded and Source and Infinite lifeforms who had been stripped of their authority, their weavings completely silenced by their leashes!","The Arbiter smiled, exposing teeth stained with glowing white residue.","His Intent shot forward grandly. It slammed into the cages, crushing the physical bodies and the boundless Trueness of the captives in a single, deafening motion.","BOOM!","The defenseless lifeforms screamed for only a fraction of a second before they shattered entirely. They were instantly pulverized into a long, swirling line of sparkling white existential dust.","The Arbiter leaned forward and inhaled sharply. He waved his hands, guiding the pulverized existence of hundreds of beings directly into his nose. He snorted the crushed remains of the True Lifeforms with an expression of utter, deranged euphoria!","His entire body seized. Pure pleasure washed over his twitching face as the white threads of THE Argent Loom mixed directly with the stolen existences inside his veins. His power spiked visibly, his aura tearing at the fabric of the Dimension as he laughed at the sheer, overwhelming high of the consumption!","He was a being of unfathomable power exhibiting the lowest, most pathetic behaviors of a street addict!","Noah watched the display from his bloody throne.","His gaze turned impossibly cold. To witness such senseless cruelty, to see living, thinking existences treated as nothing more than an inhaled stimulant, offended the very core of his Quintessential human nature.","The sheer waste and indignity of it made the stellar blue light in his Sanguine Mana flare dangerously!","He did not move to strike. Instead, he activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard.","The details of the tweaking monster instantly cascaded down his vision.","|The Arbiter of THE Serenaros|","|VERITAS: 48|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 45|","|PONDUS: 49|","|EXISTENTIAL MOIRAI: 50|","|Mantle: THE DECADENT (Willful)|","|Narrative of Existence: The Hedonist’s Defense|","|A triggered Willful Narrative centered on standing true to your ideals, your greed, and your absolute lust for existence’s highest pleasures. Those who seek to usurp your domain and take your harvest are your greatest enemies. The more lifeforms you burn and pulverize while carrying out this narrative, and the more violently you clash against the incoming crusade, the more Existential Moirai will be generated.|","Noah read the prompts with absolute, unblinking focus. But the Ruling was not finished delivering its terrible truths. Another heavy prompt descended, carrying the suffocating weight of the architects themselves.","| Through him, the gaze of one of THE Immense Ones has been drawn.|","|THE ECSTATIC FLAYER observes this Narrative of Existence with high expectations. If this Willful actor puts on a sufficient show of pleasure and death, he will be granted even more power.|","The situation had just become extraordinarily fragile!","The Arbiter was not merely a powerful addict hoarding authority. He was a lead performer on an existential stage, and one of Those Who Remain was sitting directly in the audience!","THE ECSTATIC FLAYER was actively watching this exact mountain, funding the slaughter with invisible currency.","If Noah stepped out from the unseen layers and executed The Arbiter himself, he would immediately draw the direct, unfiltered gaze of an Immense One.","He may expose his own generated standing, his Osmontian Moirai, and his hidden presence before his dimensional fortress was entirely complete!","He had to be extremely careful how he moved.","For now, this had to remain Mahishasura’s play. It had to be the grand epic of The Leading Crusade clashing violently against The Hedonist’s Defense.","Noah rested his chin on his fist, his expression smoothing into a mask of pure, tyrannical calculation.","He would use his own Mantle to scheme and steer from behind the scenes. He would pump Mahishasura full of hidden Sanguine Mana to bridge the massive attribute gap. He would use Narrative Override to quietly erase The Arbiter’s advantages, slowly starving the addict of his Moirai without ever stepping into the spotlight!","He would take control of this entire Dimension. He would claim this entire limb of THE PAX!","And he would do it while THE ECSTATIC FLAYER watched, completely unaware that the play they were enjoying had already been hijacked by a hidden director."]},{"number":5647,"title":"Chapter 5647: Chapter 5646: Narrative Vs Narrative! II","paragraphs":["Noah observed the absolute chaos erupting across the purple gold skies of THE Serenaros.","The Arbiter of THE Serenaros struck out as he did not fight like a collected general of THE PAX. He fought like a rabid beast terrified of losing its next meal!","His body trembled violently as the stellar white dust of pulverized existences burned through his veins. He threw his arms wide, and his terrifying Intent erupted outward.","It exerted his own illusory Pantheonic Dimension directly onto the physical surroundings. Space and time warped sickeningly around him! Within a radius of a million light years, the flow of time dilated and stretched, designed expressly so that any pain inflicted upon his enemies would be experienced for what felt like an entire epoch.","\"I am the peak of the high!\" The Arbiter roared, his voice a manic, rattling shriek. \" Give me your depth!\"","HUUM!","He reached his pale, twitching hands into the pristine white rivers of THE Argent Loom that stitched the sky together. With a violent, tearing motion, he ripped the white threads from the fabric of reality and fused them with his own Intent.","The resulting manifestation was horrific!","Hundreds of massive, spinning vortexes of razor-sharp white Loom-threads materialized in the air, churning with the corrosive white dust of consumed existences. They swept forward like grinding wheels of slaughterhouse, shredding the purple gold clouds and annihilating the mountain peaks below. Every spinning vortex carried a PONDUS in the high forties, heavy enough to erase many simply by passing near it!","Descendant Mahishasura floated in the path of the onslaught.","The golden shield of his Mantle flared with brilliant, defiant light. He did not retreat!","Operating entirely within the role of THE SHIELD, Mahishasura raised his hands and projected a colossal fortress of woven Loom and golden Existential Moirai. Behind him, the Veiled Enforcers and Wardens poured their own boundless Intents and Dimensionality into his back, reinforcing the barricade!","The spinning white vortexes slammed into the golden fortress.","BOOM!","The impact shattered the local weavings of existence. Reality cracked like fragile glass, revealing the absolute dark of the crossing between Dimensions. Mahishasura grunted, his pale gold hair whipping wildly as the sheer kinetic weight of the Arbiter pressed down on him!","The gap in their attributes was simply too massive. Mahishasura sat in the lower forties, while The Arbiter brushed against the absolute summit of fifty. The golden shield began to fracture, hairline cracks spreading across the Mantle’s projection.","Noah watched the fracturing shield with a cold, unblinking gaze.","He could not allow The Arbiter to break the siege. If Mahishasura fell, the grand epic of the political crusade failed, and Noah would be forced to step out and handle the addict personally while an Immense One watched.","He leaned forward on his throne of Sanguine Mana. It was time to pull the strings of the play!","Noah activated one of the supreme capability of his Hidden Mantle, THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist. He targeted the active script of The Hedonist’s Defense, isolating the specific narrative beat that granted The Arbiter his terrifying momentum.","The addict was drawing power from the continuous consumption of existence. To starve him, Noah simply needed to rewrite the accessibility of the harvest.","| NARRATIVE OVERRIDE INITIATED.|","|Target: The Arbiter of THE Serenaros. Narrative: The Hedonist’s Defense.|","|Override Parameter: The script dictates that the hedonist’s stash is compromised. The existential dust of his harvest shall no longer yield euphoria, but ash. His reaches will find only the void.|","As the prompt locked into reality, The Arbiter laughed maniacally and reached his shaking hand toward another cluster of distant metal cages filled with Inhibited Lifeforms. He intended to pulverize them to fuel a second wave of Loom-vortexes.","His crushing Intent slammed into the cages. The bodies of the captives shattered perfectly, turning into a swirling line of stellar white dust. The Arbiter inhaled sharply, his eyes rolling back in anticipation of the overwhelming high.","The dust rushed into his nose, but the expected euphoria never arrived.","\"...?!\"","Because Noah had authored a local plot override, existence itself categorically refused to process the transaction. The pulverized existence turned into inert, tasteless ash the moment it entered The Arbiter’s veins. It carried no white threads of THE Argent Loom, no condensed terror, and absolutely no power.","The Arbiter choked. He coughed violently, his eyes snapping wide open in sheer, unadulterated panic as the sudden, agonizing withdrawal hit his system like a physical blow.","\" Where is it?!\" The Arbiter shrieked, clawing at his own throat. \" Where is the emotion?! The immensity?! The high?!\"","HUUM!","With the addict momentarily crippled by his own rewritten narrative, Noah shifted his focus to his vanguard. He extended his fingers, sending invisible, razor-thin threads of crimson gold Sanguine Mana directly into the back of Mahishasura’s neck.","He did not merely feed the Descendant raw power. Noah actively laced his dark, fiendish Osmontian Moirai directly into the golden Existential Moirai swirling around Mahishasura. The obsidian gold and pure gold blended seamlessly, masking Noah’s generated destiny inside the Ruling’s own currency.","Down in the sky, Mahishasura gasped.","He felt an unfathomable, terrifying surge of weight flood his limbs. He did not question the source, assuming the Ruling itself was paying him an absolute fortune for holding the line. His amber gold eyes burned with newfound tyranny.","\" The Pax protects!\" Mahishasura roared, his voice echoing with an unnatural, overlaid resonance.","Mahishasura pushed both hands forward before the opposing Enforcers and Wardens could even move, and it was hard for them to move due to the narrative storm that none of them had a hand in!","The golden fortress of his Mantle exploded outward as an offensive singularity. He compressed an entire gigaparsec of THE Argent Loom into a single, blinding white javelin wrapped in golden Moirai, and hurled it straight at the choking Arbiter.","The javelin crossed the distance instantly, carrying the full, amplified weight of Noah’s hidden backing and the ongoing Narrative!","CRACK!","The strike pierced straight through The Arbiter’s chest. The towering Descendant was thrown backward, crashing through three floating purple gold mountains before finally slamming into the grand, floating archive-peak of his own domain!","He lay pinned in the rubble, bleeding thick white existential dust and crimson Trueness, his body shivering uncontrollably from the wound and the narrative starvation.","Noah rested his hand back on his throne. The play was proceeding flawlessly. The Hedonist was breaking, and THE Political Crusade, The Leading Crusade, was standing tall!","But...existence rarely allowed things to work entirely undisturbed.","High above the broken mountains, the fabric of the sky suddenly ceased its natural movement. The purple gold clouds froze in place, and a sickening, heavy pressure descended over the entire Dimension. It was a pressure so dense that the ambient Infinity in the air physically plummeted to the ground!","Noah’s eyes narrowed as a cascade of heavy prompts flooded his vision.","| THE ECSTATIC FLAYER has deemed the performance of The Hedonist’s Defense to be lacking.|","|THE Immense One refuses to let a favored play end in starvation.|","|Direct interference detected. THE ECSTATIC FLAYER bypasses the standard generation of the Ruling and injects raw, unfiltered Existential Moirai directly into the Willful actor.|","|The Narrative is being forcibly mutated.|","The skies above the pinned Arbiter tore open like a weeping wound. A torrential sea of pure, blinding gold Moirai crashed down from the firmament, mixed with a sickening, vibrant purple light. It did not fall gently. It struck the broken addict with the force of an ocean dropping from orbit!","\" YES!\" The Arbiter screamed, his voice bubbling and distorting as the raw power of an Immense One flooded his empty veins. \" GIVE IT TO ME! OH, GIVE IT TO ME!!!\"","Noah watched in absolute, cold silence as the direct interference of Those Who Remain tore apart the established rules of their own system.","The Arbiter’s body underwent a grotesque, terrifying transformation. The immaculate robes of his office shredded into ribbons as his flesh expanded exponentially. His pale skin tore open to reveal weeping, fleshy tendrils of raw tissue that pulsed with an agonizing, ecstatic light.","Dozens of jagged, unhinged mouths ripped themselves open across his chest, his arms, and his elongated neck. His eyes swelled into massive, bloodshot orbs that radiated pure, concentrated madness.","He had become a towering, multi-limbed beast of absolute hedonism, a physical manifestation of a high that could never be satisfied.","The monstrous Arbiter let out a roar that shattered the eardrums of every Warden within a million miles. He did not look toward Mahishasura first. Instead, his dozens of mouths snapped wildly at the air, starving for immediate consumption.","He lunged backward into his own ranks.","The elite Enforcers and the thousands of perfectly silent Loomwrought Shrouds that had floated cautiously behind him had no time to react. The Arbiter’s fleshy tendrils whipped out, snatching hundreds of his own loyal soldiers. He shoved Enforcers, Shrouds, and Wardens into the jagged mouths across his chest, chewing through their physical flesh and their Trueness with horrifying, wet crunches!","\" More !\" the beast gurgled, its voices overlapping in a sickening chorus as it devoured its own army to fuel its mutation. \"MOTHERFUCKER, I NEED MORE!\"","BOOM!","With every lifeform he consumed, the purple-gold light around him flared brighter. The monstrous Arbiter turned his massive, bloodshot eyes back toward Mahishasura, his tendrils thrashing the sky as he prepared to leap across the void!","His gaze became purely tyrannical. The stellar blue light within his Sanguine Mana burned with a lethal, absolute intensity!","He had authored a clean, tactical starvation, and an Immense One had simply dumped an ocean of raw currency onto the board to ruin it.","If he had closed off external intervention, he would have then definitely been locked onto by THE Immense One.","\"...\"","He activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard, his eyes scanning the mutating horror below.","The details that cascaded down his vision confirmed the terrifying reality of the Immense One’s interference.","| The Mutated Arbiter of THE Serenaros|","|VERITAS: 52|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: NULL|","|PONDUS: 55|","|EXISTENTIAL MOIRAI: ????? (Overloaded)|","The attributes had shattered the ceiling of fifty. The Arbiter had been artificially inflated past the bounds of THE TRANSFINITE VERSE...well, maybe. Noah still could not confirm if 50 was the bounds of THE TRANSFINITE VERSE!","And the POTENTIA had changed to NULL after this forced change. Did that mean the weavings of elevation of this lifeform were now...done?","Noah looked closely at the roaring beast. Before his very eyes, the physical form of the monstrous Arbiter began to flicker. One moment he was a towering mass of flesh and mouths, and the next, his edges blurred into the white threads of the Loom, rendering him completely transparent.","He was half-there and half-not, his existence vibrating at a frequency that was actively escaping the perception of normal reality.","His Dimensionality had been pushed so incredibly deep by the injection of Moirai!","Down below, Mahishasura raised his golden shield, his amber gold eyes widening as the unperceivable weight of the beast pressed down on him. Even with Noah’s hidden backing, the sheer density of an existence in the mid-fifties was enough to crack the foundation of his Mantle just by standing near it.","Noah did not move from his bloody throne. He did not panic!","He looked at the flickering, monstrous addict, and he looked at the weeping purple wound in the sky where THE ECSTATIC FLAYER watched its favored pet.","Noah reasoned that if Those Who Remain wanted to break their own rules to put on a better show, then he would simply have to step onto their stage and break the fucking actors!"]},{"number":5648,"title":"Chapter 5648: Chapter 5647: Narrative Climax!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","When an existence touches the absolute borders of another VERSE entirely, the physical Existence actively struggles to hold its shape.","Noah remained seated upon his bloody throne of crimson gold Sanguine Mana, his chin resting on his fist as he looked down at the tearing sky of THE Serenaros. He did not issue a command. He simply observed the horrific, impossible physics of a lifeform whose attributes had just been artificially inflated past fifty!","The mutated Arbiter did not move through the air. His flickering, transparent form simply updated its position, bypassing the space between points entirely.","He appeared directly in the center of Mahishasura’s formation. Dozens of jagged, unhinged mouths snapped open across his chest, and his terrifying Intent erupted. It imposed his own illusory Pantheonic Dimension directly onto the physical surroundings.","Gravity inverted instantly. The flow of time thickened into a suffocating, gelatinous sludge.","\"I AM THE PEAK! \" The Arbiter gurgled, his overlapping voices vibrating with the absolute, unearned weight of an Immense One’s backing.","The monster reached his fleshy tendrils into the pristine white rivers of THE Argent Loom. He did not weave the authority as he ripped it out by the roots, mixing the white threads with torrential oceans of THE Primordial Source and endlessly blue Infinity, and cast the resulting fusion outward.","Hundreds of spinning, corrosive vortexes of white and blue materialized across the sky. They acted like hungry singularities, pulling everything toward their grinding centers!","The Veiled Enforcers and Wardens fighting behind Mahishasura had no time to retreat. The time-dilation of the Arbiter’s Pantheon held them perfectly still as the vortexes swept over them!","CRACK!","Ten Veiled Wardens were shredded instantly, their physical flesh and their Dimensionality erased into fine ash!","Five elite Enforcers raised their weapons, only to have their arms and chests devoured by the tearing white threads. The sheer PONDUS behind the Arbiter’s attacks was suffocating, as its Dimensionality was crushing the local laws of reality into dust!","Descendant Mahishasura did not panic.","He was an unwilling instrument bound by a tyrant’s grammar, but he remained a perfectly composed general of THE PAX. His amber gold eyes tracked the flickering movements of the beast with cold calculation. Operating entirely within the role of THE SHIELD, he pushed his hands forward, drawing heavily on the euphoric rush of Existential Moirai the system was feeding him.","\" The shield does not break! \" Mahishasura roared, his voice carrying the resonant, amplified weight of his Mantle.","He condensed the surrounding Argent Loom into a massive, multi-layered phalanx of ethereal golden-white shields. He launched them forward like a continuous, explosive barrage. The ethereal shields crashed into the spinning vortexes, detonating in blinding flashes of blue and gold that shattered the time-dilated space.","But the gap in their standing was simply too vast!!","The Arbiter’s fleshy tendrils whipped through the explosions, shattering Mahishasura’s projections. A tendril struck the golden shield hovering above Mahishasura’s head, cracking the Mantle itself. The Descendant was thrown backward, coughing up crimson Trueness as he smashed into the ruins of a floating archive-peak.","Up in the unseen layers, Noah watched his pieces fall.","His expression remained a mask of pure, tyrannical calculation. He was losing Veiled soldiers, but he accepted the cost without a fraction of hesitation. Merely Descendants!","A player did not win an existential board game by refusing to trade pawns. However, he could not allow his pieces to fall while THE ECSTATIC FLAYER watched from the bleeding purple sky.","If he wanted to break the addict without stepping onto the stage himself, he had to change the script yet again!","Noah activated the grand capability of his Hidden Mantle, THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist. He targeted the active, mutated Narrative of The Hedonist’s Defense. The Immense One had injected raw currency to keep the monster fighting, but injected power was not earned power. In any grand epic, a villain bloated by an ancient power’s unearned blessing always succumbed to the very weight of the gift.","Noah simply authored the trope into reality.","|NARRATIVE OVERRIDE INITIATED.|","|Target: The Mutated Arbiter of THE Serenaros.|","| Override Parameter: The Trope of the Unstable Core. The power the beast wields is borrowed, and a borrowed ocean eventually drowns the vessel. The more authority the hedonist exerts, the faster his internal weavings will fracture. His own consumption shall become his rot.|","BOOM!","The prompt locked into the fabric of the Dimension.","Down below, The Arbiter laughed maniacally and prepared to unleash another wave of blue and white singularities. He drew heavily upon the unfathomable Moirai THE ECSTATIC FLAYER had granted him, his dozens of mouths opening to consume the ambient authority of the battlefield.","But the moment he pulled the power inward, his transparent, flickering body seized violently.","Because Noah had fundamentally altered the mechanics of his narrative, the Arbiter’s existence could no longer process the unearned weight. The pure gold Moirai inside his veins turned volatile. His flesh began to bubble and hiss. One of the massive mouths on his chest violently ruptured, spewing boiling white dust and stellar blood across the sky!","It was so fucking effective that even Noah had to lean forward to watch!","Holy shit, was he becoming tremendously overpowered once more?!","\" What is this?!\" The Arbiter shrieked, his tendrils thrashing wildly as his own Pantheonic Dimension began to collapse inward, crushing his own limbs. \" THE YIELD BURNS! IT BURNS!\"","Noah did not give the monster a second to recover. He shifted his focus to the ruins of the archive-peak.","He extended his fingers, sending a concentrated, invisible surge of his own dark Osmontian Moirai directly into Mahishasura, wrapping it seamlessly beneath the system’s own currency. He laced it with a heavy influx of crimson gold Sanguine Mana and a bit of Provenance Essence, fueling the Descendant with a wellspring that defied the limits of his power!","In the rubble, Mahishasura gasped.","His amber gold eyes flared with a terrifying, absolute light. The cracked golden shield above his head instantly repaired itself, expanding into a blinding, oppressive sun of pure authority. He felt the staggering, impossible weight flooding his limbs, and he weaponized it instantly!","Mahishasura shot into the sky, moving faster than the collapsing time-dilation could register.","He compressed the entirety of his golden Moirai, the white threads of THE Argent Loom, and the hidden crimson gold power into a single, titanic guillotine of light.","\" The Pax subtracts!\" Mahishasura declared smoothly, his voice devoid of all hate, carrying only the absolute certainty of an executioner.","He brought both hands down.","The guillotine of light sheared through the sky. It bypassed the Arbiter’s frantic, thrashing tendrils entirely and struck the direct center of the monster’s bubbling, unstable mass.","CRACK!","The impact sounded like a dying Dimension snapping in half. Because the Arbiter’s core was already rotting from Noah’s Narrative Override, the beast possessed no foundation to resist the strike. The guillotine cleaved the mutated Arbiter cleanly in two!","The monster did not even have time to scream. The sheer kinetic force of the blow detonated the volatile Moirai trapped inside his flesh!","BOOM!","The Arbiter of THE Serenaros exploded into a massive, expanding shockwave of THE Argent Loom and white dust, his existence utterly erased from the Records!","\"...\"","Silence slammed back into the purple gold mountains.","Mahishasura floated in the settling dust, his chest heaving as the golden shield of his Mantle pulsed proudly above him. Below him, the surviving Veiled Enforcers rallied, their weapons raised in silent victory.","Further out, scattered across the surviving courtyards and floating islands, hundreds of the Arbiter’s Descendants, Wardens, and Shrouds looked up at Mahishasura in absolute shock. Their leader was dead!","Sitting unperceivable on his throne, Noah’s eyes shone with a cold, tyrannical light!","His immediate instinct was to extend his fingers and flood the hundreds of defeated Descendants with Sanguine Mana, marking them all and claiming the entire seat of power in one breath. But his hand remained perfectly still on the armrest of his throne.","He looked up at the sky. The weeping purple wound where THE ECSTATIC FLAYER had injected the Moirai was still open. The Immense One was still watching.","Noah knew that moving now would expose his grammar. He held his patience, perfectly content to wait in the shadows while Existence processed his victory.","The systemic harvest arrived immediately.","Because he had stood in the shadows of a proxy war against the direct interference of an Immense One, the sheer adversity of the conflict fed his Dimensionality and transforming Quarks to an unfathomable degree.","| VERITAS: 30|","|PROVENANCE: 30|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 30|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 40|","Every attribute had crept and arrived menacingly toward thirty. His generated destiny swelled, the dark Osmontian Moirai wrapping around him in thicker, heavier currents.","But the true prize arrived deep within his soul.","|The adversity of the closed scene has generated immense Osmontian Biomass.|","|Threshold reached.|","|The Nine Foundations have begun their passive elevation to SS-Rank Oir.|","Noah breathed in slowly as a profound, settling weight anchored itself in his quarks. The Unkneeling Crown, The Tide That Owes Nothing, and the rest of his core Foundations began to shift. SS-Rank Oir represented finished craft and exact making. He did not need to retreat to a cave to cultivate the change; his body simply began to forge the absolute mastery of his laws in the background, a passive transformation that would soon elevate his existence entirely.","He had won the battle, secured the dimension’s capital, and triggered his grandest elevation, all without a single lifeform knowing he was there.","Then, the sky finally reacted.","The weeping purple wound began to close, but the firmament buzzed with a deafening, heavy frequency. A cascade of prompts flooded Noah’s vision, carrying the bored, terrifying weight of the architects themselves.","| THE ECSTATIC FLAYER withdraws its gaze in mild disappointment.|","|The Hedonist has burst. The actor lacked the necessary capacity, and the play failed to deliver the required tragedy.|","|However, the stage itself shows undeniable promise. The Leading Crusade has proven entertaining.|","| THE Serenaros Dimension, and all lifeforms residing within it, have been marked as participants in a budding Narrative of Existence.|","|This Narrative is being actively designed for the pleasure and entertainment of multiple Immense Ones. It shall serve as a grand convergence, pulling in multiple young promising significant Mantles and Ordained Figures across Existence to contest for ultimate standing. All extremely old and powerful are left out to give a semblance of a chance for others.|","Noah’s eyes narrowed sharply.","The prompts continued, dropping the names of the incoming terrors like falling executioner’s blades!","|Current pulled participants of this Narrative include, but are not limited to:|","|THE SHIELD (Descendant Mahishasura)|","|THE GOLDEN CHILD(???)|","|THE SON OF EXISTENCE(???)|","|THE DARK LORD(???)|","|THE HARVESTER (THE Infinity Eater)|","|THE ASSASSIN(???)|","|THE WRITER OF MYTHOS(???)|","|THE ZENITH OF SUBJUGATION (THE Sealed One)|","|THE CULLING BLADE(???)|","|THE USURPER (Achilles Adrastia)|","|THE CONTINUUM PARADOX (?????)|","|Let the actors gather. Let the play commence.|","The purple light vanished entirely from the sky, leaving THE Serenaros quiet and bathed in normal sunlight.","Noah remained perfectly still on his bloody throne. He read the list of names again, his mind dissecting the sheer magnitude of what had just been declared as he was shocked by the names that appeared!","Adrastia! He came to be considered so grand?","THE Infinity Eater was coming. THE Sealed One, the ancient terror who had taken his home and who was currently seeking IT. And there was a participant named THE CONTINUUM PARADOX whose details were completely redacted among others.","Noah considered the implications with unyielding focus.","For countless Ages, Those Who Remain had ruled by proxy. They sat in the dark, issued unfinished commands to their Descendants, and let existence grind itself into dust. They had never taken a direct hand like they currently were.","But with the fracture of Vakochev’s Scales and the emergence of THE Provenance of Existence, their entire methodology had shifted.","Why?","Noah rested his hand against his cheek, the stellar blue light of his Sanguine Mana casting long shadows across the unseen layers.","An ancient, untouchable king only began moving his own pieces by hand when he realized the board was no longer safe. They were rushing the play because they were preparing for something. Or, perhaps, they were terrified of something that had already arrived.","Or...all of that was wrong and he simply did not have enough information yet!"]},{"number":5649,"title":"Chapter 5649: Chapter 5648: Elsedimensions!","paragraphs":["The skies of THE Serenaros Dimension settled into a deceptive calm following the Arbiter’s explosive death, but the fabric of reality at the borders had already calcified.","An unfathomable narrative power wrapped around the entire Dimension, locking the gates of space and time with absolute, systemic authority. Nobody could leave!","The budding Narrative of Existence was simply waiting, gathering its assigned actors across the crossing-dark, and it would only raise the curtain once a sufficient number of confirmed lifeforms were embroiled in it.","Up in the unseen layers of existence Noah Osmont observed the weeping purple wound in the sky finally close completely. The terrifying gaze of THE ECSTATIC FLAYER retreated, leaving the broken mountain peaks to the survivors.","He had given rains to THE Closed Crown before.","Now that the Immense One was no longer watching the board, he wanted to see exactly how the other half of his newly sundered Provenance would act. He let his intent slip backward, allowing the peaceful manifestation to take the throne.","Stellar blue-gold light washed over the bloody throne of Sanguine Mana. The crimson gold hardened edges softened into flowing, gentle currents. Noah’s posture shifted seamlessly, his legs crossing and his hands resting open on his knees. His expression smoothed into an ocean of profound, terrifying peace.","He had become THE PROVENANCE OF THE OPEN Hand.","Down below, Mahishasura floated above the ruined courtyards of the Arbiter’s archive-peak. Thousands of surviving Enforcers, Wardens, and Loomwrought Shrouds looked up at him in absolute wonder, their weapons lowered as they awaited the judgment of the conqueror.","Mahishasura did not strike them as he spread his arms, his voice carrying the courteous, lecturing warmth of his nature, completely devoid of the Arbiter’s manic cruelty.","\" The Arbiter was a rot upon the order,\" Mahishasura proclaimed, his voice echoing across the inner rings, officially claiming his absolute leadership over THE Serenaros and this local Chapter of THE PAX!","\"I am the cure. Do not draw your authority. Stay perfectly still, and the very same power that brought me to this peak shall flow through you.\"","...!","From the unseen layers, THE Open Hand went to work.","It moved like a master physician. Endless rivers of crimson gold Sanguine Mana, laced heavily with brilliant stellar blue light, drifted down from the sky like a gentle, cleansing rain.","The mana bypassed physical flesh entirely. It slipped effortlessly into the rigid, authored sentences of the many Descendants here!","Instead of tearing the grammar apart by force, THE Open Hand mended the gaps, soothing the panic of the lineages as it rewrote their loyalties with supreme kindness . In seconds, a few Hundred Descendants across the entire Dimension were seamlessly cut open, altered, and marked.","They blinked, their eyes losing the frantic terror of the Pax and settling into the calm, absolute obedience of the Veiled.","These were Descendants, mind you!","Each one was either equivalent to...or grander than a Primeval Lifeform! Each one traced back in some way or another...to an Immense One.","And...","The harvest of claiming an entire Dimension’s forces in one breath was staggering!","Because the conquest was enacted with perfect peace and total efficiency, Existence rushed to validate his standing. A cascade of prompts flooded his vision, detailing a surge in his internal architecture that defied all precedent.","|50,000,000,000,000 Provenance Telos Quarks converted.|","| VERITAS: 31|","|PROVENANCE: 31|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 31|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 42|","Every attribute shattered the marker of thirty!","Noah grasped the immensity of the change, feeling his Dimensionality rise deeply!","And while the Open Hand secured the staging ground of THE Serenaros, his true focus remained anchored elsewhere.","---","In THE Infiniverse, another body continued to follow its unperceivable Hearthshifts across the void.","Noah floated atop the verdant blue-gold hills of his own domain, fully submerged in THE PROVENANCE REVERIE. His eyes were endless blue, completely devoid of pupils, radiating the absolute agreement between his existence and his surroundings.","He waved his hands, utilizing the 12,000 Genesis Tesseracts gathered from THE Tide That Owes Nothing.","The hypercubes of deep blue-white light shot upward into the skies of THE Infiniverse. They detonated silently, expanding into massive, sweeping wonders! Observable Existences bloomed like the birth of new stars, knitting themselves into the expanding boundaries of the Unique Transfinite Dimension.","As the realms expanded, his people also opened more of their own. Their own localized stability generated even more Observable Existences in a cascading, exponential loop of creation, feeding the sheer size and Dimensionality of THE Infiniverse to unfathomable heights!","Thalia Vasiliou stood on the stellar grass beside him, watching the sky ignite. Her white-blue robes shifted gently in the winds of newborn Observable Existences, her expression clouded with a heavy reality.","\" You are building your fortress beautifully, my Provenance, \" Thalia said, her voice quiet but strained.","\"But with things moving like they are, and with so many unknowns rushing the stage... you might have to pay a visit to THE Provenance Elsedimensions early.\"","Noah’s endless blue eyes turned to her. He simply listened as she explained the inevitable cost of her paradox.","\" My existence in this current timeline will not survive long with me standing here,\" Thalia continued, a sad smile touching her freckled face.","\" The two of my Existences in this flow of time will merge soon. It is the only way existence can reconcile the loop. A trip to the Elsedimensions may provide us with some more answers, and it will allow you to truly understand your nature as a Provenance Lifeform.\"","Noah was silent for a moment as he grasped the immensity of her words.","\" What are Provenance Elsedimensions? \" He asked smoothly.","Thalia looked up at the budding wonders, her eyes reflecting the boundless blue light of his domain.","\"When a First Lifeform generated enough of its own essence, it realized that the physical frameworks of existence...The Rulings, the Dimensions, the crossing-dark...were simply too rigid to hold it,\" Thalia explained.","\" So they stepped sideways . Provenance Elsedimensions are not places you travel to by flying.\"","She turned back to him, her gaze serious.","\" They are vast, overlapping Warrens of raw, unshaped reality layered beneath the skin of existence. They are realms authored entirely by the Provenance of those who live there, completely untethered from THE Argent Loom and relatively free from the influence of Those Who Remain. To walk in an Elsedimension is to walk inside the minds and the laws of beings who answers to nothing. It is dangerous, but it is the original estate. It is the only place left where the architects’ eyes do not easily pierce.\"","Noah considered the tactical advantage of a realm where THE Immense Ones held no jurisdiction. Well, relatively.","He considered the sheer depth of knowledge waiting in the Warrens of his own kind, of Provenance Lifeforms, and how that knowledge could be put to use.","\" Okay ,\" Noah said."]},{"number":5650,"title":"Chapter 5650: Chapter 5649: Primeval!","paragraphs":["<THE Aureate Matriarch>","In the deepest spans of the crossing-dark, existence does not bother hiding its age.","There was a Dimension that was one among many which held a rather large number of...Primeval Ones.","This Dimension was known as THE Vhor-Mhal Dimension, and it held a unique disposition unlike many others.","THE Vhor-Mhal Dimension was an architecture built entirely of corpses . A central, floating landmass stretched for gigaparsecs, formed from the petrified, interwoven roots of the very first Observable Existences that had failed to bloom.","The first Observable Existences that had failed to bloom! What a wonder such a thing was as it was the home of some of the more ancient Lifeforms!","Standing upon this unfathomable graveyard were thousands of Primeval Lifeforms. They were the earliest children of reality, beings of staggering Dimensionality whose sheer mass warped the local laws of space into screaming loops!","Some were towering, chimeric beasts woven of starlight and bone, while others carried the amplified, weeping Egos of Superbius, Luxuria, and Ira, and a whole lot more. They were ancient, they were unfathomably deep, and they were grand!","At the head of this particular massive tribunal stood THE Aureate Matriarch.","She was a Primeval One who looked exactly like a colossal, unmoving golden statue. Her form was immaculate and perfectly proportioned, draped in the shifting, invisible weight of harvested eras. Above her head, the golden sign of her Ordination turned slowly in the dark. She carried the Mantle of THE ELDER.","She did not shout to be heard over the groaning Dimension. She spoke, and her cold, calm voice simply became the only truth the air was permitted to carry.","\" My children. My brothers. My sisters,\" THE Aureate Matriarch spoke, her golden eyes sweeping over the thousands of assembled ancients.","\" Some have the habit of ignoring the foundations they stand upon. They look at the millions of Observable and Unobservable Existences scattered across the dark, and they believe these realms simply happened. They believe authority is a hammer they just found in the dirt.\"","She paced slowly across the petrified roots, every step ringing like a tolling bell.","\" They forget who planted the seeds. We are the Primeval Ones. We did not merely watch the First Lifeforms. We steered the formation of Existence. We harvested and utilized the backing of millions of Causes, stacking the burdens of existence upon our own backs to ensure Existence did not collapse. Our methodology of power is so deeply rooted that even Those Who Remain look at our Causes as a weight that can rival THE Argent Loom, or the volatile fusion of Infinity and THE Primordial Source.\"","Her golden eyes narrowed, the only movement on her pristine, statue-like face.","\" Our place in existence is grand. And yet, portions of our brethren are being treated like nothing. A faction of Descendants, clutching the borrowed authority of Their Fathers, is shackling our kin. They lock Primeval Lifeforms in metal cages and inhibit their power, treating the architects of the eras like common Bounded Lifeforms, or worse. They believe they can prune us.\"","HUUM!","The Matriarch raised one massive golden hand toward the firmament.","\" Will we stand for this?!\"","WAA!","The tribunal of thousands shook with absolute, unyielding rage!","The light of boundless Causes erupted across the petrified roots in blinding flashes of crimson, gold, and violet. Primeval beasts roared, their terrifying Intents expanding to crush the void. Beings of Superbius and Ira unleashed their Egos in shockwaves that physically tore the firmament of THE Vhor-Mhal apart, their fury echoing like the dying screams of a hundred Dimensions!","The Matriarch lowered her hand, letting the fury wash over her unmoving form.","\" The fracture of Vakochev’s Scales was merely a symptom of a rotting house. But THE Provenance of Existence has descended, and it paves a way for us. The new Ruling pays for roles. It funds the actors. With it, we can impose the oldest Narratives in existence upon these ignorant children. For who holds grander Narratives than those who have seen the births and guided the weavings of millions of Observable Existences and Unobservable Existences?\"","She stepped forward, her voice rising with tyrannical certainty.","\" We will allow the emergence of countless Narratives. We will ensure that THE Pax, and all those who hide behind cages, learn exactly what we are. The Descendants are not the only ones with the support of Those Who Remain! Existence is vast, and full of terrors. Existence is vast... and full of us.\"","BOOM!","Far above the gigaparsec landmass, the sky vanished.","The dark firmament was replaced by the crushing, terrifying weight of four massive eyes. Four of THE Immense Ones had opened their gazes to look down upon the tribunal.","Boundless, pure Existential Moirai rushed down from the eyes like breaking oceans!","The localized destiny wrapped around the thousands of Primeval Lifeforms, feeding their Egos, stabilizing their Causes, and amplifying their terrifying Dimensionalities.","THE Aureate Matriarch bathed in the falling currency, her golden form shining like a newborn sun. As the Moirai washed over her, a message bypassed her ears and burned directly into her ancient consciousness. It carried the bloodshot, breathless weight of THE SLEEPLESS FIEND.","|The stage is expanding, O First Children.|","|A budding Narrative of Existence involving many is blooming. It gathers the Ordained. It gathers the unique anomalies.|","|Select your youngest. Select those among you who carry the grandest Mantles, and send them to the stage. They shall participate. They shall establish the Narratives of the Primeval Ones across the bodies of the arrogant, and they shall be funded beyond measure.|","THE Aureate Matriarch looked up at the four weeping eyes in the sky. She felt the absolute validation of Existence backing her claim, the very architects of reality handing her a stage to unleash the wrath of her kin.","\" Let the young ones sharpen their fangs, \" the golden statue murmured, a cruel smile finally breaking her pristine features.","They were grand, and they were old. Who the fuck did others think they were to step over them?!"]},{"number":5651,"title":"Chapter 5651: Chapter 5650: THE Dimensional Provenance Train! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","A conquered Dimension usually requires time to settle its borders. THE Serenaros was granted exactly none!","Noah remained seated upon his bloody throne of crimson gold Sanguine Mana, resting his chin on his fist as he observed his newly acquired dominion. Down below, Mahishasura floated over the archive-peak, projecting the composed authority of THE SHIELD while the surviving thousands of Descendants and Enforcers knelt in grand obedience!","In fact, Noah was already calculating the weavings of permeating the entire Dimension with his Sanguine Mana when the sky changed.","The purple gold skies of THE Serenaros did not tear open like it had for THE ECSTATIC FLAYER. Instead, the entire sky began to shine with an oppressive, blinding light. The ambient Infinity in the air froze completely. The weight of multiple Immense Ones descended simultaneously, bypassing the physical borders of the Dimension and pressing directly into the authored lineages of every Descendant present.","Down in the courtyard, Mahishasura stiffened violently, his amber gold eyes going wide as information flooded his existence.","Because Mahishasura was bound to Noah’s grammar, Noah did not need to wait for the Descendant to speak. He simply read the incoming broadcast straight through the Sanguine threads anchored in Mahishasura’s lineage.","Waves of glorious, complex information rushed into Noah’s vision as prompts. They detailed the architecture of the budding Narrative of Existence, and the sheer scale of the design was breathtaking!","The architects of existence were literally linking entire gigaparsec-wide Dimensions into a connected, unstoppable sequence.","|THE Narrative of Existence has commenced.|","| Title: THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence.|","|THE Serenaros Dimension has been coupled as a Dimensional Cabin alongside an unknown number of other Dimensions that will move across Existence. It is now bound to the linear tracks of the Narrative Moirai.|","Noah sat up slightly, his eyes narrowing as the prompts continued to build the rules of the terrifying stage.","|The Moving Sequence: The core of this continuous narrative lies in the absolute finality of its momentum. Geography across the crossing-dark becomes a linear gauntlet. Time and survival are now measured by forward progression.|","|The Tyranny of the Tracks: The Narrative Moirai dictates the path of these chained Dimensions.|","|The Hostile Periphery: Existence outside the dimensional boundaries is actively lethal as of this moment for all lifeforms within THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence. It is an endless void of crushing temporal anomalies and predatory storms of the power of Immense Ones. The coupled Dimensions actively fend it off, making the outside a terrifying canvas of abstract annihilation whizzing past at breakneck speeds. Any lifeform thrown past the boundaries of any of the connected Dimensions faces certain death by the combined might of THE Immense Ones.|","Noah read the rules with cold, unyielding focus!","For they were fucking heavy!","Dimensions...connected together to form a Dimensional Provenance Train rushing across Existence? Anything that left the bounds of the Dimensions would collapse instantly?!","|The Convergence of Thresholds: The systemic boundaries between these chained Dimensional Cabins will not remain permanently sealed. At dictated intervals, the dimensional doors separating the Cabins will open. Lifeforms may cross over into neighboring Dimensions to conquer, or prepare to be conquered.|","|The Spoil of the Stage: To spur the actors, Narrative Treasures will bloom at random intervals within each Dimensional Cabin . These treasures contain unfathomable seas of Existential Moirai among other things waiting to be claimed by those bold enough and powerful enough to seize them.|","|The Dimensional Hierarchy: The physical layout of the chained Dimensions perfectly mirrors a rigid hierarchy of standing. The Engine Dimension at the front houses the absolute elite and the heaviest apex predators. As you move toward the back Cabins, the Dimensions become structural battlegrounds for the desperate as those in the back are weaker.|","| THE Serenaros Dimensional Cabin has been deemed...one of the weaker Dimensions on the back of THE Dimensional Provenance Train|","WAA!","The intricacies of the play were staggering. The overarching tension would circle back to survival and conquest. When the doors opened, a neighboring Dimension full of terrifying enemies would simply spill into their own.","BOOM!","The moment the final prompt locked into the Records, THE Serenaros physically jolted.","The sensation was entirely different from the smooth, unperceivable step of a Hearthshift. Noah felt the sheer, raw kinetic force of an entire Dimension violently coupling onto a track of pure white Argent Loom and golden Moirai!","The purple gold clouds above them suddenly streaked horizontally. The borders of the Dimension crystallized into thick, translucent barriers, revealing the absolute dark of the void whipping past at speeds that defied the laws of anything one new.","A deafening, structural groaning echoed across the sky as the Dimension settled into its perpetual forward momentum.","Noah rested his hand on his bloody throne, his expression a mask of pure, tyrannical calculation.","The Immense Ones had done something ridiculous!","And why oh why did they even do this?!","Just to watch? Just as a Narrative?","He was placed at the very back of a rigid hierarchy, expected to be ground into dust by the Dimensions opening their doors ahead of him.","But...","He did not view this Dimensional Train as a cage. He viewed it as a perfectly arranged buffet.","The architects had kindly lined up every major threat, every rival Mantle, and every hoarded authority in a perfectly straight line!","They had saved him the trouble of hunting them down across the vastness of existence, and they were even going to drop Narrative Treasures filled with Moirai directly into his lap while he marched!","Well...maybe.","Existence was vast and full of terrors. Who knew just what terrifying things were swept up in it?","---","<THE Writer of Mythos>","A completed story is, by its very nature, a dead thing.","In the deepest vaults of existence, where the crossing-dark gives way to the hidden sanctuaries of the architects, there existed a Dimension built entirely of paper and silence.","It was a realm where geography did not consist of mountains or oceans, but of countless floating pages. The pages were woven from the pristine white threads of THE Argent Loom, and the text upon them was inscribed with a mixture of endless Infinity and dense golden Source.","They fluttered in a perpetual, silent cyclone, recording the histories, the tragedies, and the grand epics of thousands of Observable Existences.","At the absolute center of this storm of literature sat Descendant Calliope.","She was a vision of profound, heartbreaking grace. Her long, silver-white hair floated around her like spilled ink in water. Her skin was perfectly pale, untouched by the crude violence of the lower frameworks, and her fingers were permanently stained with the deep blue residue of raw authority.","Her presence was entirely serene, radiating a terrifying, absolute calm that could pacify a raging Primeval beast with a single glance.","Above her head, a grand, golden sign shaped like an open book and a quill rotated slowly. It was her Ordination, granted flawlessly by THE Provenance of Existence. She was THE WRITER OF MYTHOS.","Yet, despite her staggering standing and the endless wealth of her domain, her eyes held the dull, suffocating weight of absolute boredom.","High above the cyclone of floating pages, the firmament of the Dimension began to warp. The sky parted effortlessly, and a single, colossal eye gazed down at her. It was the eye of an Immense One, radiating a calm, suffocating pressure that forced the floating pages to perfectly align themselves in midair.","\" The board shifts violently, my child ,\" the Immense One spoke, its voice carrying the resonant, tolling depth of ancient bells. \" The Provenance of Existence has flooded the frameworks. The actors are moving, and the currency flows like water. Existence is yours for the taking. With your Ordination, you can write Narratives at the same level as Vakochev or any Provenance Lifeform. You can author the rise and fall of entire epochs with a flick of your stained fingers.\"","Calliope did not bow and ahe did not even look up immediately. She simply let a single, blank page drift into her palm, staring at its emptiness with a profound gaze.","\" But why should I?\" Calliope asked, her voice impossibly smooth, carrying a melancholic echo that defied her sheer power.","\"In existence, why should I bother? All the Mythos I’ve written are grand. I have authored the tragic ends of many Lifeforms. I have written the glorious ascensions of entire realms. But none of it has scratched my itch recently. It is all so terribly... predictable.\"","The colossal eye above gazed down. The silence between them stretched for a long, heavy moment before the Immense One finally answered.","\" You suffer the malaise of the untouchable ,\" the ancient architect rumbled gently. \" Listen to me, Calliope. Long before you were born, and long before the Scales were ever weighed, there was a Provenance Lifeform known as The Willful Traveler.\"","Calliope raised her gaze slightly, her silver-white hair drifting as the Immense One wove a story into the fabric of the Dimension itself.","\" The Willful Traveler had no predetermined shape and no authored lineage. It possessed only its own generated standing, and the absolute desire to walk forward. For Ages, it walked through the raw, unshaped crossing-dark, braving the tearing storms and the lethal quiet. One day, the Traveler came upon a domain authored by one of Those Who Remain...a being known as The Maker of Cages.\"","The pages around Calliope began to glow, automatically recording the fable as it spilled from the Immense One’s lips.","\" The Maker of Cages had built a flawless, glass sphere, \" the Immense One continued. \" Inside the sphere, there was no pain. There was no fatigue, no hunger, and no uncertainty. The Maker offered the sphere to The Willful Traveler, saying, ’Why do you walk in the cold dark? Step inside my cage. Here, you will never lose. You will never fade. You will rule over all that you see in perfect peace.’\"","\" The Traveler was weary from the endless storms. It accepted the offer and stepped into the glass sphere. For a million years, the Traveler sat in perfect, unchallenged peace. It authored grand illusions within the glass, creating anything it desired with a single thought.\"","Calliope’s stained fingers twitched slightly. She recognized the shape of the mirror being held up to her.","\" But after a million years ,\" the Immense One said, its voice dropping to a terrifying, intimate whisper, \" The Willful Traveler began to suffocate. Because it controlled every variable, there was no friction. Because there was no friction, its own generated power had nothing to push against. The Traveler began to shrink.\"","\"So, The Willful Traveler tore out its own heart. It used its own fiendish, ancient blood to corrode the flawless glass, burning a hole straight through the perfection. It stepped back out into the freezing, lethal crossing-dark. The Maker of Cages was furious. It asked, ’Why would you choose the pain of the cold over the peace of perfection? Why bleed just to leave?’\"","\" The Willful Traveler looked back and answered: ’A cage that guarantees victory is a cage that denies purpose. The pain of the cut is the cost of the ink. Without the ink, there is no story. Without the possibility of failure, there is no ’Why’. There is only the box.’\"","HUUM!","The story settled heavily into the dimension. The millions of floating pages hung completely static in the air.","\" You are suffocating in your own glass sphere, Calliope ,\" the Immense One declared softly. \" You are bored because you are the absolute master of your domain. You cannot scratch the itch because you already know how every story ends before you write it. You lack the friction of the unknown.\"","Calliope stared up at the colossal eye, a faint, dangerous spark finally igniting within the dull depths of her gaze.","\"If you seek a grand Mythos, \" the Immense One commanded, \" then you must step onto a stage where you cannot control every variable. Go to THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence. It is a budding Narrative pulling in terrors and anomalies that defy even our predictions. There, you will find beings of unimaginable depth Existence has produced. There, you will find the possibility of your own ending. There... you might find new inspiration.\"","...!","Calliope breathed in slowly. The sheer, intoxicating concept of a Narrative where she was not the author, but a participant forced to fight for the pen, sent a sudden, violent thrill through her rigid lineage.","A story where she might actually lose!","She raised her head, her beautiful, serene face breaking into a very small, very terrifying smile.","She nodded lightly.","BOOM!","The instant her agreement was registered by the records, her entire Dimension buzzed with a deafening, structural frequency!","The cyclone of millions of pages was violently sucked inward, compressing into dense, physical walls of white Argent Loom and purple-gold authority. The limitless boundaries of her quiet sanctuary crystallized, locking into thick, translucent barriers that revealed the sudden, terrifying blur of the crossing-dark whipping past at breakneck speeds!","The physical force of an entire Dimension coupling onto a linear track slammed through the realm!","Her sanctuary was no longer a hidden vault. It had just been forcibly coupled to the rushing momentum of the architects’ grand design. It had become one of the many Dimensional Cabins of THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence!","Calliope stood in the center of her accelerating Cabin, feeling the localized gravity shift as the Narrative Moirai dragged her domain forward into the ultimate, inescapable gauntlet. She raised her ink-stained fingers, her silver-white hair whipping in the new, violent winds of the moving Dimension.","She finally had a blank page worth writing on!"]},{"number":5652,"title":"Chapter 5652: Chapter 5651: THE Dimensional Provenance Train! II","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","The Provenance Realm of the First Lifeform had expanded unfathomably since Noah first stepped through its doorway. The verdant blue-gold hills rolled endlessly into the distance, carrying a profound, untouchable peace. The river of light holding quiet star-pools ran deeper and wider than before. But the most staggering change hung directly above him.","The serene sky was no longer marked by a handful of stars. Over thirty manifested singularities of stellar blue-gold Provenance Essence hung in the space above.","Noah had returned here alone before setting off for the Elsedimensions as he floated just above the stellar grass. His eyes were endlessly blue, completely devoid of pupils. He remained submerged in THE PROVENANCE REVERIE, and simply existing within the boundaries of his own realm fed him a continuous, effortless stream of profound epiphanies.","He analyzed the sheer velocity of the board shifting around him.","THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence was a masterstroke of systemic cruelty. It was a linear gauntlet designed to force conflict, stripping away the vastness of the crossing-dark to lock apex predators in a hallway. Soon, he would leave to seek out the Elsedimensions Thalia had mentioned, the hidden Warrens of his own kind, supposedly free from the piercing gazes of the architects.","He wondered of far too many things.","He wondered if his people were finally safe from the creeping reach of THE Sealed One. They were securely nested inside THE Infiniverse, actively drawing upon his localized wellspring, and backed by thousands of newly rooted Causes from the blooming Observable Existences. But safety was a fleeting, fragile illusion in Existence.","Dimensionality kept proving that there was always a deeper layer, an unseen tier of authority waiting to crush the unprepared.","Noah reached into the void of his inventory and pulled out the physical remnant of his most recent mystery.","A single obsidian crystal settled into his palm. It caught the light of the thirty singularities above, absorbing the stellar blue-gold glow without reflecting a single beam back. It was the object Vakochev’s manifestation had left behind before retreating into the dark. It was a heavy, quiet thing, carrying the desperation of an ancient scale-maker who had realized he was outmatched by Those Who Remain. The crystal sat in his hand, full of unresolved questions.","As he turned the dark stone over in his fingers, the crown of Sanguine Mana and Provenance floating above his head suddenly shone with a brilliant, warm light.","The authority condensed, dripping downward to form a physical shape beside him. Ruination materialized as a flawless humanoid figure draped in elegant, flowing crimson-gold robes laced with stellar blue light. She sat down directly beside him on the grass and gently leaned her head against his shoulder.","|Master is a bit introspective,| Ruination spoke, her voice carrying a rare, consoling warmth that perfectly matched the peace of the realm.","|Existence is rapidly changing around you, and you are adapting fast and doing everything you should.|","Noah smiled, the endlessly blue light in his eyes softening. He reached up and gently patted her head.","\" Tell me about you and your sister, \" Noah asked quietly.","Ruination did not move from his shoulder, but crisp, concise prompts cascaded down his vision as she delivered her accounting.","|THE Circlet of the Quintessential Ruin and THE Infiniverse are advancing harmoniously. Because my weavings flow through both you and her, I benefit tremendously from your rising Dimensionality.|","|The continuous flow of your Infinite Sanguine Mana and Provenance Essence is actively elevating my nature. I cannot clearly place my own Dimensionality on any known framework, but I feel a profound shift in my capabilities. I can now alter and control the flow of information across any Dimension or domain I occupy.|","|I am capable of hijacking the localized transmissions that Descendants receive within their lineages. I can even present myself as information originating from THE Immense Ones, overriding the surrounding existence with forged truths before they reach the ear.|","|I call this...THE PRECEPT OF THE UNWRITTEN FREQUENCY.|","|My Dimensionality seems to be forming entirely toward how I can best support you. After all, rewriting the words of ancient terrors is far more efficient than swinging a sword at them.|","Noah let out a soft breath of wonder.","|As for THE Infiniverse,| Ruination continued, |everything you cast out for her to hold has only made her more immense. She is actively managing the cast-out backbone of THE Infinite Scales. We have begun streamlining them, preparing to potentially have all those within THE Infiniverse adopt a localized, perfect version of the Scales that answers only to us.|","|Furthermore, we have analyzed the mystery of Causes. It remains deeply illogical that Those Who Remain would eradicate an entire race like the Laestrygonians simply for bearing them, only for THE Sleepless Fiend to build his own cursed lineage backed by that exact same power. To understand this, I have mapped out the genetic markers of Damodred.|","|With your permission, and a significant allocation of power from THE Tide That Owes Nothing, I can begin pulling those markers to bring forth more Laestrygonians within THE Infiniverse. This is not merely out of the kindness of our existence. It allows us a thorough, controlled study of Causes, which will directly benefit the seating and growth of your own Teloi.|","|Authorities, Intents, Tongues, Causes... existence is crowded with systems of power. With continued focus, we should soon grasp the true immensity of Causes and finally understand why THE Sleepless Fiend fears them enough to eradicate an entire species.|","Noah listened in comfortable silence. He nodded, letting out a quiet sigh as he leaned backward, lying flat against the verdant gold hills of his realm.","He looked up at the skies. Over thirty manifested singularities hung above him, a staggering testament to an existence that was tearing through boundaries without pause. He slowly raised his hand toward the skies, his fingers curling slightly as if he wanted to grasp something sitting just behind the veil of the sky, but did not know exactly what it was.","His eyes swirled with boundless Provenance. He evaluated his arsenal with ruthless precision. His Provenance. THE Osmontian Tongue. Infinite Sanguine Mana. THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist Mantle. The nine SS-Rank Foundations.","Would it all be enough?","He was preparing to move amongst the oldest monsters in existence, to step into the Warrens of Provenance Lifeforms, and to eventually face Those Who Remain when the time was right, because they could now squish him like a bug.","He wanted to understand everything. He wanted to experience the absolute profundities and immensities of reality without a single chain holding him back.","But he could doubt. He could wonder. Because he was fundamentally, quintessentially human.","Lying on the grass, surrounded by the staggering weight of his own generated power, Noah simply wondered about the future and what it truly held for him and his people.","\" Existence... has always run on the illusion of scarcity,\" Noah murmured to the quiet sky.","\" Gilded Ones. Infinite Lifeforms. Source Lifeforms. Primeval Ones, Descendants... they spend their entire lives scrambling up ladders built by someone else. They now fight over roles and Moirai minted by the architects, utterly convinced that authority is a finite resource they have to beg for.\"","He lowered his hand.","\" But true standing is not something you catch in the rain. It is something you bleed. My Provenance was not handed down from a weeping sky. I generated it. I am the wellspring. Let them hoard their borrowed authority and ride their little tracks. Let them do what they wish...as I will do what I wish. We will see what happens to their unyielding train when it slams into an existence that refuses to move.\"","Noah rose up from the stellar grass. He stretched his arms casually, the joints of his Provenance Body popping with deep, resonant sounds that echoed across the hills like dying stars.","\" Let’s fuck shit up.\"","...!"]},{"number":5653,"title":"Chapter 5653: Chapter 5652: THE Dimensional Provenance Train! III","paragraphs":["<Descendant Alcaeus>","Descendant Alcaeus stood upon the rusted, jagged cliffs of THE Krazhor-Nul. It was a hostile, unforgiving realm defined by a lethal ambient density that could effortlessly crush the life from weaker beings.","But for Alcaeus, who held the golden Ordination of THE CHAMPION, the crushing gravity was merely a comforting weight.","He had come to this Dimension on a direct mandate. THE SLEEPLESS FIEND, had issued a bloodline-wide bounty of the anomaly known only as the Cure-Giver. Alcaeus had wanted to see the remnants of broken curses and shattered authorities, so he came here.","To witness where The Cure-Giver had been!","Alcaeus loved a prey that fought back.","He was preparing to leap into the foamy space between Dimensions to follow the trail toward THE Ymnaros when the red skies above him suddenly froze.","The ambient light of the Dimension snapped into a blinding, oppressive brilliance. The weight of multiple Immense Ones descended simultaneously, pressing directly into his authored lineage.","Waves of information rushed into his mind, detailing the commencement of THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence!","BOOM!","THE Krazhor-Nul physically jolted. The sensation was violent. The rusted cliffs cracked, and the red firmament streaked horizontally as the entire Dimension was violently coupled onto a linear track of Narrative Moirai.","The borders of the realm crystallized into thick, translucent barriers, revealing the abstract, lethal annihilation of the crossing-dark whipping past at breakneck speeds.","Alcaeus did not panic as the Dimension settled into its perpetual forward momentum.","Because he received one last piece of information.","| THE Cure-Giver may be within this Dimensional Provenance Train.|","HUUM!","He stood up slowly, the sign of his Mantle pulsing above his head.","Alcaeus threw his head back and laughed, his joyful roar echoing over the rushing noise of the tracks. The hunt had just become a scheduled execution!","<THE Infinity Eater>","THE Infinity Eater sat in the center of THE Ossuary of Gluttony. It was a terrifying, suffocating Dimension built entirely of half-digested Primeval ribs and sprawling lakes of corrosive, digestive acids.","He maintained the appearance of a weary scholar draped in immaculate white robes, his eyes solid blue spheres without pupils.","Above his pale head, the golden sign of a curved scythe turned slowly. He was THE HARVESTER.","He was preparing to mobilize his absolute standing to descend upon THE Ymnaros after his passage here when...","The suffocating pressure of the architects flooded this realm. Information cascaded down, announcing the architecture of the budding Narrative of Existence!","BOOM!","The Ossuary of Gluttony shuddered violently.","The colossal ribs of dead Primeval Lifeforms groaned and snapped as the Dimension was wrenched onto the linear tracks of the Narrative Moirai. The acidic lakes sloshed heavily against the newly crystallized, translucent borders of the Dimensional Cabin.","THE Infinity Eater gripped the arms of his bone-carved throne, his solid blue eyes narrowing as he read the rules of the sequence.","He sensed that many Lifeforms he used to draw from...may just be within this Train as well.","Did that mean the thief would be here too?","\"...\"","He leaned back, his pale fingers drumming a lethal rhythm on the bone armrest. He did not need to launch an expedition across the void.","The Train’s forward momentum would inevitably bring the usurper of THE Ymnaros right to his doorstep!","Maybe!","<Kaelen, THE Dark Lord >","Every grand epoch eventually demands a villain to justify its bloodshed.","Kaelen stood upon a balcony of frozen black ash, looking out over THE Umbral Wastes. It was a Dimension of perpetual twilight, jagged obsidian glaciers, and silent, monolithic citadels that pierced the dark clouds like spears.","He was an ancient, towering entity whose biology defied the standard frameworks. His skin was the color of cracked basalt, and his multi-jointed limbs moved with a heartbreaking, weary grace.","He was not a creature of base malice, but a being of absolute, suffocating tragedy. His very existence was an Intent that froze THE Primordial Source into heavy, immovable black ice.","When THE Provenance of Existence descended, the Ruling had weighed his long, bloody history of subjugation and handed him a Mantle he had never asked for.","Above his horned head floated the jagged, weeping crown of THE DARK LORD.","\" They author the play, and they assign the knives,\" Kaelen murmured, his voice sounding like grinding tectonic plates.","Below his balcony, millions of Source True Lifeforms stood in perfectly ordered, silent legions. They were bound to his shadows, their existences preserved in the freezing dark. They were his army, his burden, and his curse.","The twilight sky suddenly ignited with an oppressive, blinding light. The weight of the Immense Ones pushed down, freezing the ambient Source that drifted through the falling ash.","The broadcast of the Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence burned directly into his ancient consciousness.","BOOM!","THE Umbral Wastes violently lurched. The obsidian glaciers shattered, and the monolithic citadels swayed as the Dimension was forcibly coupled onto the track. The borders of the Wastes turned to thick glass, and the abstract, lethal terror of the crossing-dark began to scream past the edges of his domain.","Kaelen gripped the railing of his balcony, the black stone cracking under his massive fingers.","He had been designated as a prime obstacle. His Dimension was placed securely in the middle of the Train, a brutal checkpoint that the desperate and the \"righteous\" would have to overcome to reach the front. Narrative Treasures would bloom in his frozen wastes, drawing Ordained beings like moths to a flame.","He closed his eyes, a profound exhaustion settling over his basalt features. He did not care for the Moirai, and he did not care for the entertainment of the architects. But he would not let arrogant Descendants or rushing upstarts burn his silent kingdom.","\"If they wish to play at being heroes ,\" Kaelen rumbled to the frozen legions below, \" then we will give them the dark they require.\"","<The Front>","Far ahead of the rusted cliffs of THE Krazhor-Nul, ahead of the frozen ash of the Wastes, and ahead of the acidic lakes of the Ossuary, the Engine of the Narrative roared through the void.","It was not a single realm, but a breathtaking, staggering cluster of a thousand gigaparsec-wide Dimensions, all stitched together by the pristine white threads of THE Argent Loom.","This was THE Concord of a Thousand Origins!","It served as the absolute forefront of THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence.","The Concord was a reef of impossible wealth.","Oceans of pure Infinity fed directly into Dimensions of burning obsidian, which seamlessly grafted into sprawling jungles of petrified wood. It was the supreme gathering place for the children of the architects, heavily populated by the highest concentration of the Ordained!","Here, the track was not a constraint; it was a throne carried by the rest of existence!","The colossal Primeval Lifeforms and the ancient True Lifeforms and Descendants that walked the white bridges of the Concord felt the massive jolt as dozens of lesser Dimensions were violently coupled behind them.","They looked back toward the rear of the Train, their golden Mantle signs flashing with anticipation.","Above the Concord, the sky did not show the crossing-dark. It showed the unblinking, terrifying gazes of multiple Immense Ones, watching their grand Engine pull the entire weight of the narrative forward!","The doors between the Dimensional Cabins remained sealed for now. The tension was building, a ticking clock of existential proportions. The elite at the front sharpened their weapons and gathered their Moirai, preparing to even leave their opulent standing to go down to hunt!","The Train had commenced its journey and there were no fucking brakes!"]},{"number":5654,"title":"Chapter 5654: Chapter 5653: What Was Promised! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Stepping off the edge of the map requires an entirely different set of keys than simply conquering the board.","Noah stood within the verdant blue-gold hills of his own Provenance Realm, watching Thalia Vasiliou prepare the doorway. She did not weave the white threads of THE Argent Loom, nor did she attempt to draw upon THE Primordial Source or Infinity or Causes or any Tongues.","Instead, she reached out with her bare, pale hands and physically grasped the fabric of his self-generated domain.","Her existence flickered violently, caught in the paradoxical strain of moving across Dimensions and Time, but her movements were flawlessly precise. She pulled her hands apart, tearing a seam not through space, but through the conceptual layer of existence itself.","\" We are leaving the established frameworks entirely,\" Thalia said, her voice quiet against the hum of the opening tear. \" Hold my hand. If you step incorrectly here, you do not fall into the crossing-dark. You simply cease to be recorded...well, somewhat. You are strong enough to survive.\"","Noah took her hand without a fraction of hesitation.","They stepped through the tear.","The transition did not carry the raw kinetic violence of THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence, nor the unperceivable slide of a Hearthshift. It felt like walking from a crowded, deafening auditorium directly into a silent, boundless cathedral.","They arrived in a domain that defied every metric of existence held dear!","Towering arcs of moss-draped stone hung suspended in the sky, anchored only by localized, swirling gravities.","Colossal trees with trunks the width of continents spiraled upward, their canopies scraping an atmosphere that glowed with a deep, bioluminescent violet light. The air itself tasted pure!","\" Within the Provenance Elsedimensions are scattered domains known as Elseworlds,\"","Thalia explained, her white-blue robes shifting in the strange, vibrant winds.","\" We have just arrived at the Vasiliou Elseworld. It is the original estate where the Provenance of the Vasiliou Provenance Lifeforms runs the strongest.\"","...!","Noah swept his gaze across the breathtaking, alien horizon, his endlessly blue eyes analyzing the underlying architecture of the realm. A series of crisp prompts cascaded down his vision, confirming the sheer wonder of where they stood.","|You have entered an Elsedimension.|","|The underlying weavings of THE Argent Loom are virtually nonexistent here.|","| THE Provenance of Existence has a loosened grip upon this territory. The Rulings of THE Immense Ones are severely delayed and lack immediate enforcement within this Elseworld.|","|You stand in a blind spot of the architects.|","It was a staggering realization. The Immense Ones could force entire Dimensions into a linear gauntlet, but they could not easily peer into the sovereign Warrens of those who generated their own standing.","Thalia did not linger to admire the scenery. Her physical form vibrated with a sickening frequency, the paradox of her existence reaching a critical, breaking point. She held Noah’s hand tighter, leading him away from the towering stone arches and down toward a much lower, more intimate basin of the Elseworld.","The geography shifted into a serene, unfathomable expanse of water.","Endless, crystalline lakes spilled into one another over colossal cliffs, generating slow-motion waterfalls that caught the bioluminescent light. Floating atop the vast, perfectly still waters were massive luminous blue-gold lotuses, some the size of entire islands. The air here was heavy with a fragrant, ancient peace.","Thalia led him onto the surface of one of the grandest lotuses.","Waiting for them in the absolute center of the massive flower was another body.","Noah’s footsteps slowed. Sitting quietly on the blue-gold petals was a second Thalia Vasiliou. She wore the exact same white-blue robes, her striking, freckled face turned upward, her deep red hair cascading down her back as she looked...magnetic.","The seated Thalia looked at Noah with a soft, breathtaking smile.","\" Existence does not like things moving across time, \" the seated Thalia spoke. \"I sensed my future self arrive in this era the moment she did. We have both been pulled towards each other ever since, destined to merge as one to close the loop.\"","The Thalia holding Noah’s hand stepped forward, her flickering form aligning perfectly with her seated counterpart.","\"I may not have all my memories afterward ,\" the flickering Thalia continued, her gaze dropping slightly. \" But I may be able to talk more about what I remember as I will no longer be as bound. And... I may not even survive the resulting friction. For this, I need your help. I need an Anchor to hold my existence together in the way that my Provenance considers absolute.\"","Noah listened in total silence!","\" And what my Provenance considers absolute... \" Thalia finished calmly, though a rare, unmistakable shyness touched her features, \" is an act of giving myself to My Provenance. You are my Provenance... so I do need you to anchor me and guarantee my survival as my present and future merge, okay?\"","...!","Noah looked at the two women in utter astonishment.","She was entirely serious. He evaluated the request with the same absolute focus he applied to any existential conflict. He was not a man who needed to be told such things twice!","He had not known her for a tremendous length of time in a linear, measurable sense. But time was a metric for mortals and the governed. She had known him in the future. She had bled for him, she had guided his mother, and she had looked at his daughter with genuine warmth.","Seeing how seamlessly she had integrated into the core of his existence, Noah found that every single reservation he might have held had completely vanished.","\"I am right here ,\" Noah said softly.","The flickering Thalia stepped into the seated Thalia.","The two bodies overlapped, and the merge commenced!","Immense, golden waves of Provenance began to seethe and erupt around her figure. The sheer force of the paradox collapsing in on itself threatened to tear her physical form apart!","Thalia looked up at Noah, her eyes misty with the agonizing strain and an overwhelming, desperate hope.","\" My Provenance ,\" Thalia whispered, her voice trembling under the weight of closing time itself. \" Will you stabilize my Existence? Will you take what is yours now and in the future?\"","Noah felt the call of her existence pulling at his own. He had to exert absolute, tyrannical control over his true depth, calling upon every single one of his billions of Provenance Telos Quarks to suppress his crushing Dimensionality and Egos!","He moved to her slowly, dropping to his knees on the blue-gold petals, and took her into his arms.","As their existences met, the massive golden lotuses around them reacted. The colossal petals folded upward, curling over them. They sealed the center of the lake in a dome of radiant light, ensuring that even the surrounding Elseworld would not bear witness to the act occurring within!"]},{"number":5655,"title":"Chapter 5655: Chapter 5654: What Was Promised! II","paragraphs":["And seconds began to pass.","In the middle of a grand act to anchor a Provenance Lifeform, to ensure her survival as the loops of time snapped shut, Noah’s mind suddenly exploded with a staggering influx of information.","His Provenance Essence flared violently. He was connected to the grand Provenance of another in an unfathomable way, and his existence was beginning to read the deepest, most heavily guarded secrets buried at the very root of her lineage.","Grand, blinding prompts surged into his vision!","|The existential union has reached the root. Two Provenance existences have touched where existences are not meant to touch. Something long-ripening has noticed the better vessel.|","|A latent Provenance stirs within Thalia Vasiliou. It has been ripening across the entire history of her lineage. It is not yet fully hers. It has never fully belonged to anyone. It has only been... awaited.|","Noah held Thalia closer, his breathing steady as he read the sheer scale of the revelation.","|THE Vasiliou Lineage has cultivated toward this Provenance for its entire existence. Generation upon generation refined, narrowed, and aimed, so that one day one vessel might be born able to hold it. That vessel is Thalia Vasiliou. She is their Queenling. She is the apex the whole lineage was a ladder toward.|","| And one of THE Immense Ones laid claim upon this Provenance before Thalia was ever born.|","|Looking down the length of the lineage’s potential, one of Those Who Remain reserved the harvest for itself. When the apex ripened, it would be taken. The Vasiliou were unwilling to part with or share such a Provenance, but conceded after many grand promises. A promise was made between one of Those Who Remain and The Vasiliou Provenance Lineage.|","The architects of reality had bred a harvest outside their own frameworks, and they had claimed it before it even had a name!","|You are not the vessel it was bred for. You are a purer, younger one.|","|The Provenance seeks the existence most able to bear it, and it has found one the lineage never designed and the claimant never accounted for: an existence of boundless potential, generated rather than granted, un-weighable, owing nothing to any framework. It reaches for you.|","| You may receive it. Doing so takes the purity of a Provenance reserved for one of THE Immense Ones. The claim will be broken by being fulfilled elsewhere. The awaited harvest will be reaped by a hand it was never promised to.|","Noah’s eyes burned with a terrifying, stellar blue-gold light in the enclosed dark of the lotus petals.","To take from Those Who Remain. To steal the reserved prize of the architects simply because his own generated existence was a superior, flawless vessel.","He did not even delay!","He held Thalia fiercely, accepting the union completely and drawing the latent, ripening authority directly out of her lineage and into his own unyielding Existence!","He felt his Provenance surge explosively, anchoring down something it absolutely should not anchor, claiming a theft of glorious proportions!","HUUUUM!","The surrounding existence outside the lotus petals trembled violently! The serene waterfalls shattered. The bioluminescent sky of the Vasiliou Elseworld flickered as if sensing the sudden, uncontainable rage of a distant, unimaginable terror!","It was the rage of one of Those Who Remain as however far they were...something they had claimed was being stolen!","But...it had no power here!","|An Immense One senses a severed claim.|","|A prize promised for Ages has been taken by an unknown hand.|","And in the midst of the shaking surroundings, as Noah secured the survival of the woman in his arms, the final, heaviest prompt locked itself permanently into his Records.","| THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign has settled into your existence.|","To steal from an architect is a crime. To steal a harvest reserved for an Immense One before they can even reach down to pluck it... is a genesis!","Noah knelt within the sealed, radiant blue-gold dome of the colossal lotus, holding Thalia Vasiliou tightly against his chest. The surrounding Vasiliou Elseworld was still shaking from the severed claim, but inside the petals, a far more terrifying violence was unfolding.","The latent authority drawn from Thalia’s lineage...the ripening prize that Those Who Remain had bred and waited Ages for, crashed into Noah’s existence like a falling Dimension.","It was a heavy, untamed weight. It carried the conceptual density of a sovereign right to rule, designed expressly to sit within the impossibly deep frameworks of the architects. But Noah did not possess their frameworks. His existence was entirely self-generated, owing nothing to any system.","So, when the unfathomable weight of THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign struck his core, it did not find a waiting throne. It found a grinder.","Noah’s endlessly blue eyes flared with absolute tyranny!","He called upon THE Hunger That Refines and THE Sovereign Existence. He refused to let this foreign, promised authority dictate his biology. Instead, he weaponized the sheer, crushing mass of the stolen harvest, using it as the ultimate catalyst for the grandest art he had ever authored.","THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis required the weight of existence to press down on his foundational particles, forcing them to survive and remake themselves into Provenance Telos Quarks. He had been converting them steadily, but the sudden influx of an Immense One’s prize acted like a billion Observable Existences detonating inside his veins all at once!","HUUM!","The first cycle of Baryogenesis accelerated infinitely.","Noah felt the agonizing, euphoric tearing of his own fundamental building blocks. It was a sensation of being unmade and perfectly reassembled in the same nanosecond.","The sheer friction of his body arguing with the size of the stolen Provenance caused his crimson gold Sanguine Mana, laced with stellar blue light, to erupt from his skin. It wrapped around Thalia, protecting her merging form while his own body became a crucible.","The count of converted quarks blurred past comprehension!","Fifty Decillion!","One Hundred Decillion!","One Hundred and Ninety Decillion!","Every single particle of his physical flesh, his bones, and his blood was subjected to the unyielding pressure of THE Immense Sovereign’s weight, and every single one of them survived!","BOOM!","A shockwave of absolute, unadulterated purity blasted outward, flattening the blue-gold petals of the lotus!"]},{"number":5656,"title":"Chapter 5656: Chapter 5655: What Was Promised! III","paragraphs":["Grand, cascading prompts flooded Noah’s vision as Existence rushed to record the birth of an anatomy that defied all established limits!","|The first cycle of THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis is complete.|","|All 200 Decillion Quarks have been successfully converted into Provenance Telos Quarks.|","|The First Tier of the Provenance Body has been forged.|","BOOM!","| THE Quintessential Provenance Skin is active. You have become structurally pristine.|","....!","Existence was far from finished!","Because the 200 Decillion Quarks had been forged using the catalyst of the stolen harvest, THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign did not just settle into his existence.","It was violently digested, integrated, and repurposed by his Quintessential nature!","Noah gasped, his arms tightening around Thalia as a completely new, terrifyingly complex understanding of life itself bloomed in his mind.","He was suddenly looking at existence through a lens no ordinary True Lifeform or Primeval One could ever access. He could see... the literal, genetic markers of reality. He could see...he could see!","| THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign has been fully integrated and elevated by your unique architecture.|","|Capability Unlocked: EXISTENTIAL LIFELINE REVISION AND MARKER ATTAINMENT.|","|You have attained the authority to reach into the very genetic and existential markers of a lifeform. By utilizing THE Osmontian Tongue and your Infinite Sanguine Mana, you may completely edit, splice, isolate, or rewrite the foundational sequences of their existence.|","|You may extract and forge Genetic Markers of Existence. These sequences of Existential Code can be spliced into any lifeform and elevated to higher states of Dimensionality.|","| Initial isolations include the Infinity Genetic Marker, THE Source Genetic Marker, THE Provenance Genetic Marker, the Intent Genetic Marker, and THE Infinite Tongue Genetic Marker.|","| You and the Provenance Lifeform connected to you at the root may now act as PROVENANCE PROGENITORS.|","WAA!","The prompts carried a weight that shattered every known ceiling!","|You possess the sovereign right to author a new taxonomy of life. You may rewrite the existences of the bound and the shackled, stripping away their reliance on any other authority.|","| Through your editing, you may usher in Nova Provenance Elselifeforms. These are beings whose markers are entirely re-sequenced to generate their own standing, completely free from the frameworks of Those Who Remain.|","WAA!","To be a Progenitor!","Noah realized the sheer, unfathomable immensity of what he had just stolen. One of Those Who Remain had honed in on the Vasiliou lineage for Ages specifically to harvest this exact capability. It was the power to perfectly design, edit, and control the genetic foundation of existence itself. And Noah had simply snatched it from the vine and made it his own!","He could isolate the Infinity Genetic Marker and splice it into a being, allowing their existence to carry boundless Infinity without any rejection or the inevitable madness of the void! He could insert THE Source Genetic Marker to anchor them to the dense golden weight of THE Primordial Source, or THE Infinite Tongue Genetic Marker to grant them the capacity for supreme grammar. They were literal sequences of Existential Code, ready to be written, elevated, and deployed.","As this supreme authority settled into his newly forged Skin, his attributes violently adjusted to the new baseline of his existence.","| VERITAS: 45|","|PROVENANCE: 40|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 45|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 60|","His numbers had skyrocketed, crushing the limits of the mid-thirties and surging terrifyingly close towards whatever end of THE TRANSFINITE VERSE was. His Osmontian Moirai, the dark and fiendish currency generated by his own weight, hit sixty!","Within his arms, the golden waves of paradox surrounding Thalia finally settled!","The loops of time had snapped shut. Her present and future selves had merged perfectly, anchored by the sheer, unmovable gravity of Noah’s existence...and Dual Cultivation!","It saved lives!","Because their Provenances had touched at the absolute root during the theft, she had shared in the baptism of the Immense Sovereign’s integration.","Thalia Vasiliou took a long, trembling breath.","She opened her eyes, and the dim, scattered singularities within her depths had ignited into a blazing, unified constellation of pure authority. She looked up at Noah, her striking, freckled face flushed with a terrifying new vitality.","\" You did it, \" Thalia whispered with brilliant wyes of adoration. \" You anchored me. And... you took it all.\"","Noah did not speak immediately. He looked down at his own hands, and then at hers.","They had both physically changed.","The integration of the Progenitor authority had left a visible, breathtaking mark upon their pristine vessels. Orbiting the outer edges of Noah’s endlessly blue irises was a microscopic, floating double-helix of stellar blue-gold light . It looked exactly like a glowing genetic sequence, constantly unzipping and reweaving itself in real-time!","The exact same ethereal sequence orbited the irises of Thalia’s eyes.","But it was not confined just to their gaze.","Hovering a fraction of an inch off the skin of their wrists were delicate, glowing bracelets of the same blue-gold helix-weavings . The runes within the floating genetic strings pulsed with the undeniable, sovereign authority to create, edit, splice, and unmake life at the most fundamental level.","They no longer simply looked like powerful lifeforms. They looked like the architects of a brand new era. They looked like true Progenitors!","Noah slowly ran his thumb over the floating helix-weaving above Thalia’s wrist. The microscopic blue-gold runes shifted playfully under his touch, answering exclusively to his will.","He considered the tens of thousands or even hundreds of thousands of Descendants locked in the Dimensional Cabins, the lineages serving THE PAX, and the ancient Primevals.","He thought of his people.","He now held the literal, genetic keys to rewrite all of them into Nova Provenance Elselifeforms. He could build an army of un-leashed, self-generating terrors armed with spliced Existential Code that Those Who Remain would not even be able to read in the Records!","Noah’s lips curled into a slow, devastating smile.","The Vasiliou Elseworld outside the massive blue-gold lotus was still vibrating from the severed claim of THE Immense Ones. Inside the sealed petals, however, the violent golden waves of the time-loop closure had finally settled into a profound, breathless peace."]},{"number":5657,"title":"Chapter 5657: Chapter 5656: What Have You Done?","paragraphs":["Thalia Vasiliou remained in Noah’s arms. Her striking, freckled face was flushed with the vitality of a fully stabilized Provenance Lifeform, but a sudden, heavy vulnerability clouded her expression. The microscopic, blue-gold genetic helix orbiting her irises spun slowly as she looked up at him.","\"I am sorry ,\" Thalia whispered, her voice cracking slightly in the quiet space . \"I asked you to anchor me, and in doing so, I forced you to make a direct enemy of one of Those Who Remain. They will not forgive what you just took.\"","Noah looked down at her. He evaluated the sheer weight of her apology and found it entirely unnecessary. His expression remained an ocean of calm, tyrannical certainty.","\" You did not force me to do anything ,\" Noah said smoothly. \" And nobody would have been allowed to take my Provenance. What was inside you was always going to belong to us. Let them be angry. I seem to be building a habit of offending them anyway.\"","Thalia stared at him. The sheer, unbothered arrogance of his claim broke right through the ancient tension weighing on her shoulders!","Small, crystalline tears spilled over her eyelashes. She did not bother wiping them away. A breathtaking smile broke across her face, carrying the profound relief of a woman who had spent her entire existence running from a predetermined cage. She reached up and embraced him tightly, burying her face into his shoulder.","Noah smiled softly. He wrapped his arms around her, his Sanguine Mana washing over them in a warm, protective current.","He allowed the silence to hold them for a long moment. He was human, and it was human to relax for a bit knowing of the coming storm. But his mind was already turning the newly acquired keys of their shared authority.","Noah pulled back just enough to look at the delicate, glowing bracelets of blue-gold helix-weavings hovering off the skin of their wrists.","\" How much of this Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign can you utilize?\" Noah asked.","\" These Nova Provenance Elselifeforms....and everything else relating to these new possible weavings of existence.\"","Thalia took a slow breath.","\" The lifeforms we can produce...they will be a bridge ,\" Thalia explained, her voice regaining its melodic, resonant power. \" They are not entirely Provenance Lifeforms, because their origin still requires our hands to edit and seat their foundations. And they are not entirely anything else that the Records currently hold.\"","She gently traced her fingers over the glowing helix on Noah’s wrist.","\" To be a Nova Provenance Elselifeform is to be severed from the scales of all others but us. What you can do...I can do. I think...\"","Noah looked at the floating genetic strings, thinking of Mahishasura, of Skallagrim, of the countless humans.","There was...boundless possibilities to think of!","He kept his arms wrapped protectively around Thalia Vasiliou. The golden waves of her stabilized time-loop had just settled. The microscopic blue-gold helixes orbiting their irises pulsed with the unfathomable authority of Progenitors.","For a fraction of a second, Existence belonged entirely to them.","It was...peaceful.","Then, the absolute peace within the lotus petals simply ceased to be.","HUUUM!","There was no spatial tear. There was no fluctuation of THE Argent Loom or ambient Infinity. Noah’s newly elevated Dimensionality, backed by attributes sitting heavily in the mid-forties, did not register an approach.","A woman simply materialized inches away from them, as if she had been standing there for the last epoch and had only now chosen to make herself visible.","Noah’s endlessly blue eyes snapped toward the figure, the stellar blue-gold Provenance Essence in his blood flaring dangerously before it calmed!","Because...","The woman looked like an older, terrifyingly grand version of Thalia. She possessed the same striking, deep red hair, though hers was woven with streaks of liquid gold. She was draped in immaculate, imperial white robes that seemed to carry the physical weight of entire Dimensions. Her posture was flawless, radiating a suffocating, ancient absolute.","But it was her eyes that commanded the space. They were filled with an immense, crushing disappointment as she looked down at the two of them.","Noah immediately activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard.","A heavy panel cascaded down his vision, bringing with it a profound realization of just how deep the Warrens of the Elsedimensions truly went!","|Rosalia Vasiliou|","|VERITAS: ?????|","|PROVENANCE: ?????|","|POTENTIA: ?????|","|PONDUS: ?????|","The entire panel was a wall of redacted ignorance!","Aside from her name, his sweeping authority could not weigh a single fraction of her existence. She was entirely unreadable, a being of such staggering age and depth that she bypassed the frameworks of his perception completely.","Rosalia Vasiliou did not even gaze at Noah. She kept her imperial eyes locked entirely on Thalia, her voice carrying a resonant, melodic sorrow.","\" My child.. .\" Rosalia whispered, the words vibrating through the very conceptual layer of the Elseworld. \" What have you done?\"","Thalia stiffened in Noah’s arms, the vibrant flush of her recent stabilization draining slightly from her freckled face.","\" You think that generating your own standing means you owe nothing to the soil that grew you ?\" Rosalia continued, her tone admonishing and heavy with reprimand.","\" But those with Provenance do not just think about themselves. Your lineage bled for Ages to cultivate the vessel you just broke. You acted only for yourself. You were selfish, Thalia, and in your selfishness, you have endangered every single Provenance Lifeform of our line.\"","Noah remained perfectly still as his eyes began to shine dangerously.","\" Do you know what THE Immense Ones value above all else?\" Rosalia asked, her voice dropping to a terrifying, intimate lecture. \"It is not authority. It is not the Scales. It is their honor. It is their dignity! To lose a promised bride, to have a reserved harvest stolen from their grasp... that is a slight that cannot simply be pushed aside! In existence, everyone has to make sacrifices. I made mine. Your father made his. We bent so that the Vasiliou could survive the architects.\"","She looked at the glowing blue-gold helix orbiting Thalia’s wrist, her disappointment deepening.","\" How could you do this?\"","Thalia slowly pulled herself out of Noah’s immediate embrace. She did not cower!","The time-loop had closed, and she had seen the absolute end of the road. She stood up on the blue-gold petals, her white-blue robes shifting as she met her mother’s imperial gaze.","\" We are Provenance Lifeforms,\" Thalia stated respectfully, but her voice had a grand, vibrating frequency that pushed back against her mother’s oppressive aura.","\" We decide our fate. We decide our existence! Even Those Who Remain cannot definitively stand above us unless we bow our heads and offer them our necks!\"","Thalia took a step forward, the stellar blue-gold light in her eyes flaring with the unmistakable, sovereign arrogance of a Progenitor.","\"I am a Provenance Lifeform, mother. Are you?\"","BOOM!","The words struck the inside of the lotus like a physical detonation!","It was a borderline blasphemous accusation, striking directly at the heart of Rosalia’s compromises! Thalia was angry. She was furiously rejecting everything!","Rosalia did not shout as her reaction was impossibly calm.","She simply turned her head, acknowledging Noah’s existence for the very first time.","Her unreadable, ancient eyes measured him up and down, dismissing his brilliance with a single, sweeping glance.","\"A newly budding Provenance Lifeform who has attained what... the First Tier or Second Tier of the Provenance Body?\" Rosalia mused coldly, her voice devoid of any actual curiosity. \" Such a being beside you, or one of Those Who Remain. If you had both of them presented before you, the choice is clear.\"","Thalia did not miss a beat. Her voice rang out grandly, filled with absolute, unyielding pride!","\" And I made that choice! \" Thalia declared. \" Between one of Those Who Remain and him... I have chosen him again and again! Across all Provenances, across time! As he would say in his own words... it is merely one of Those Who Remain. So what?!\"","BOOM!","Noah looked up at Thalia in pure astonishment!","She had weaponized his exact arrogance and thrown it directly into the face of a terrifying, ancient matriarch!","She had defended him with a ferocity, standing between him and the oldest fears of her own bloodline.","Rosalia Vasiliou stared at her daughter for a long, heavy moment. The disappointment in her eyes finally hardened into a cold, pragmatic resolve. She shook her head as she let out a long, exhausted sigh.","\" What is done is done,\" Rosalia said flatly.","\" And it cannot be taken back. So let us go. I have to convene with your father and the others of our Lineage to find a solution that does not involve your death, and all of our deaths. We may even have to reach out to the few friendly Immense Ones our Lineage shares some weavings with, to try and ensure that thing does not bring its unyielding rage down upon us.\"","She took a step closer, her imperial aura pressing against Noah’s Skin.","\" We have to do all of this because the one you chose... cannot protect us ,\" Rosalia stated.","She turned her eyes back to Noah, finally addressing the Emperor of THE Infiniverse directly. \" Or can you do that?\"","Noah felt the crushing weight of her unreadable Dimensionality pressing into his lungs.","\" What can you do?\" Rosalia asked, her cold words slicing through the absolute peace of the lotus. \" What can you do better than one of Those Who Remain?\"","...!","Noah looked at this woman, his tyrannical mind momentarily amused by the sheer absurdity of existence. He never thought he would find himself facing down a disapproving mother!","He wanted to remain respectful. Thalia had just merged her existences, and this was her family. But Noah was fundamentally incapable of bowing his head to anyone who demanded it.","Noah rose to his feet. He brushed off his crimson-gold robes, his endlessly blue eyes locking directly onto Rosalia’s unreadable gaze. He did not flex his attributes, and he did not scream about his capabilities. His reply was calm, unhurried, and perfectly tyrannical.","\"I will look at her, and all others of my people, as if they are equals, \" Noah said smoothly.","\" Not like they are playthings that mean nothing. I will treat your daughter with respect. Not like a tool to be traded for a few Ages of peace from a master who only sees you as a harvest.\"","He stepped up beside Thalia, his shoulder brushing hers.","\" That is what I do better.\"","Rosalia stared at him. The coldness in her eyes did not melt, and she did not seem remotely impressed by his declaration of humanity.","She simply harrumphed.","\" Respect doesn’t mean shit if she is dead,\" Rosalia snapped.","\"Let’s go.\"","...!","Rosalia Vasiliou simply waved her imperial hand.","A storm of blinding, ancient golden light raged instantly around them! The massive blue-gold petals of the lotus were violently blown backward as the sheer, conceptual force of her unreadable Dimensionality gripped both Noah and Thalia!","In a fraction of a second, the light swallowed the basin entirely, and all three of them disappeared from the Vasiliou Elseworld!"]},{"number":5658,"title":"Chapter 5658: Chapter 5657: Nova! I","paragraphs":["Respect doesn’t mean shit if she is dead.","The matriarch’s words followed Noah out of the lotus and across the Elseworld.","One body of him was gone with Thalia now, swallowed by golden light, carried deeper into the Warrens to be measured by a lineage older than the Scales.","He thought about Rosalia as he went.","She had looked at him and seen a First or Second Tier Provenance Body, a budding thing, a boy who had wandered into a house too old for him!","Him! A boy!","She had weighed him against one of Those Who Remain and found the scale tilted so far that the comparison was almost a courtesy. And she had not been wrong about the numbers.","By any measure of Ages and depth and accumulated dread, he was the smaller sum by an unfathomable margin.","The thing was, Noah had never once believed the numbers!","Standing before an Immense One, standing before the whole grim procession of Those Who Remain with their honor and their harvests and their bent and broken lineages, he had never for a single breath felt himself the lesser being.","He believed in himself that much!","And well. Sometimes a man had to fake it until he made it.","He almost smiled at that.","He had another one of his bodies sent into his Provenance Realm again as this body had come here for something quieter, and it was time to stop delaying it.","He called for his children.","They came into the Provenance Realm the way he opened for them, and the Realm’s blue-gold hills folded up around the three of them, and for a moment the war and the matriarch and the Train grinding through the crossing-dark were all somewhere else, and there was only this.","Henry arrived unhurried, blue-gold hair catching the light, wearing his father’s face years younger and none of his father’s weight. Seo-yeon arrived at a run and stopped short a pace away, her small face gone still and strange.","\" You feel...a bit wrong, Aba \" she said.","Noah crouched. \" Wrong how, kiddo?\"","She frowned, searching.","\" Not bad wrong. Far wrong. Like you’re standing so far away from us in positioning...or existence. Ah, its hard to say!\"","Noah smiled lightly at such words as he patted her head.","\"I am a bit far, but I am also here, don’t worry.\"","Noah stood, and opened his hand, and looked at his son and daughter the way he now looked at all living things. All the way down.","Their Lifelines lay open to him.","It was still the strangest sight he had been given, and he had been given a great many. Henry’s existence unspooled as a long line of light, an unbroken code of Existential Markers running the whole length of what the boy was, and every locus of it was legible to him.","Here the marker that made him human. Here the marker of his birth, the Osmontian blood carried one generation forward, thinning and brightening through a single life. And here, all down the length of him, the markers of every gift he had ever accepted.","Beside him, Seo-yeon’s Lifeline ran shorter and stranger and, to a father, unbearably lovely, threaded through with the quiet marker that let her feel dying Causes.","Noah looked at the two of them laid open as editable grammar, and felt no hesitation, only a care that had sharpened itself to the finest edge he owned.","\" This will not hurt, \" he said. \" Hold still.\"","HUUM!","He began with what he was.","His Sanguine Mana rose off his hands, crimson gold laced with stellar blue, and it wrote. Under the guidance of THE Osmontian Tongue, the blood drew itself into a shape that had not existed in all of existence a moment before, because he was forging it now, in the open air of his own Realm, out of the deepest truth of himself.","| You are forging a Genetic Marker of Existence.|","|Source truth: your Nine Osmontian Causes, seated as Teloi through the whole of your matter. You are isolating the sequence that lets an existence carry Causes of its own. Aimed. Owned. Answerable to no framework.|","The marker turned between his fingers, a small helix of blue-gold light, and it hummed with the whole weight of what he was.","| THE OSMONTIAN CAUSES GENETIC MARKER has been forged.|","|It carries the rankings of Dimensionality as all things do. FINITE. TRANSFINITE. INEFFABLE. What you seat, you may seat at the depth the vessel can bear.|","He forged the second from the part of him that owed nothing to anyone.","|You are forging a second Marker.|","|Source truth: THE Provenance Essence you generate from within. You are isolating the sequence that makes an existence a source unto itself. Generating, not granted. Standing on nothing borrowed.|","| THE PROVENANCE GENETIC MARKER has been forged.|","Two markers turned above his open palms, one and then the other, the Causes and the Provenance, the aim and the source, the two truths that had made Noah more than a man who had merely been given things.","Henry watched them with his composure entirely gone. Seo-yeon reached toward the light without thinking, and Noah caught her small hand and folded it gently closed.","\" Hold on,\" he murmured. \" The eldest one first.\"","...!","He came to his son first.","Noah pressed the turning markers toward Henry’s open Lifeline, and where the light met the code, he wrote. The Tongue moved through him, not in Letters this time nor in Words but in the finer grammar beneath them, the grammar of splicing, and he excised as he wrote.","The dependence went first. Anything to do with Scales or external power!","His son felt many things leaving as he did not question!","Into the emptied ground, Noah wrote the new truth. THE Osmontian Causes Genetic Marker settled into the root of his son, and THE Provenance Genetic Marker settled beside it, and the boy became a man of wonder!","Because he had become a source.","Henry’s blue-gold hair blazed white at the roots. His existence, stripped of everything borrowed and reseeded with everything self-made, began to sing at a register it had never touched, and he threw his head back and breathed like a man surfacing from deep water as Causes woke inside him for the first time. His own!"]},{"number":5659,"title":"Chapter 5659: Chapter 5658: Nova! II","paragraphs":["|Henry Osmont is being rewritten.|","|External dependence excised. Borrowed frameworks removed. THE Osmontian Causes Genetic Marker and THE Provenance Genetic Marker seated at the root, at the deepest his vessel can bear and still have room to grow.|","|He no longer draws his standing from what he was given. He generates it.|","| The Markers he holds stand at the Finite Dimensionality Stage. The potential to grow is Average, the Attributes that can be reached are 10 at Maximum, and the growth rate is slow. The Markers can evolve with his own hand from being unfathomably true to himself, or from devouring Existential Treasures or Lifeforms as in every single Genetic Marker lies a passive Osmontian Devouring, a capability that allows it to bear the weight and devour thr surrounding Existence to grow.|","BOOM!","The light settled. Henry stood breathing in the blue-gold hills, and looked at his own open hands as though they belonged to someone he had just been introduced to, and around his irises, faint and unmistakable, a small helix of light had begun to turn.","|A NOVA PROVENANCE ELSELIFEFORM has been born. The first of its kind.|","Henry was quiet a long moment.","\"I can feel...the Causes. Even closer than those backing me in THE Infiniverse...\"","His eyes blinked with wonder as he looked at his father!","Noah only nodded at him and allowed him to feel as he knelt to his daughter.","Seo-yeon looked up at him with a trust so total it had never once occurred to her to withhold it.","He forged her rewrite gentler. What made her herself he kept with a care, and he wrote the new truth around it rather than over it.","\" This one is yours,\" he said, low, seating THE Provenance Genetic Marker into her first. \" So that nothing you ever feel again can reach inside you and take.\"","He began splices thr two markers calmly as he slowly got the hang of rewriting genetic codes!","|Seo-yeon is being rewritten.|","|Native gift preserved and deepened. THE Provenance Genetic Marker and THE Osmontian Causes Genetic Marker seated at the root, at a Fine depth.|","| Another NOVA PROVENANCE ELSELIFEFORM has been born. The second of its kind.|","The helix kindled at the edges of her small eyes, matching her brother’s, matching her father’s, and she turned a slow circle on the petals to watch the light chase her gaze, smiling too damn happily as changes bloomed.","Noah stood between his two remade children, and existence answered what he had done.","|You have created the first two Nova Provenance Elselifeforms in existence.|","|Both descend from you at the root. Both carry your forged Markers. You are recorded not as a lifeform, but as a Progenitor with living descent.|","His Provenance Essence answered without being called.","It rose in him, seething upward from his newly pristine core!","|Assessment: Progenition generates. To seed a source is to prove yourself an origin, and the proof feeds the origin. Your Provenance Essence rises, and will rise with every lineage you author.|","|The more of existence that descends from you, the more of a source you become.|","Noah felt his own immensity lift as he smiled, his expression carrying a terrifying, unhurried absolute as he looked up toward the boundary of the realm. His secondary body had finally stopped moving. The storm of golden light across the Vasiliou Elseworld was dissipating.","They were arriving.","\" Get acquainted with your new foundations,\" Noah instructed his family, his voice dropping to a cool, commanding tone .","He had to go meet inlaws who very likely did not like him much!","But even as this occured, events in THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence also finally began to pick up.","---","<THE Serenaros Dimension>","A prison... only functions if the inmates actually believe the walls are solid.","Noah remained seated upon his high, bloody throne of crimson gold Sanguine Mana. Down below, the surviving Wardens and Enforcers knelt in absolute, Veiled obedience, their lineages seamlessly overwritten by his grammar.","Mahishasura floated just above the kneeling masses, projecting the composed, golden authority of THE SHIELD. He looked up toward the unseen layers, delivering his tactical assessment to the hidden emperor.","\" We have confirmed the perimeters of the coupling ,\" Mahishasura reported, his voice echoing with disciplined absolute!","\" There are two massive thresholds at either end of the Dimension. The doorway behind us leads to a lower Dimensional Cabin in the rear. The doorway ahead leads to a higher Cabin toward the front. So far, neither threshold has shown any fluctuations.\"","Noah nodded slowly, his chin resting on his fist.","He was already running simulations on how to best hijack the momentum of THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence. He controlled an entire Cabin. He had the literal, genetic keys to rewrite lifeforms into Nova Provenance Elselifeforms. He was simply waiting for the perfect moment to deploy his newly acquired taxonomy.","But the architects of reality were not known for their patience.","HUUUUM!","The entire gigaparsec-wide Dimension suddenly buzzed with a deafening, structural frequency!","Noah sat up, his endlessly blue eyes narrowing as the rusted courtyards directly in the center of THE Serenaros violently fractured. The pristine white threads of THE Argent Loom snapped. The ground tore open, and a geyser of thick, obsidian crimson blood bubbled out from the very core of the Dimension!","It did not pool on the ground as the obsidian crimson blood shot upward, weaving and hardening into the shape of a massive, colossal stellar tree!","The blood-tree pulsed with a terrifying, ecstatic air of power and immensity. It radiated the undeniable, suffocating scent of an Immense One’s direct interference. It was an authority so heavy and ancient that the moment it bloomed, the thousands of Descendants and Wardens across the Dimension began to tremble!","Their physical bodies seized. The natural, instinctual response of their authored lineages commanded them to drop their heads and press their knees into the dirt. They wanted to kneel to the sheer, crushing weight of the architects!","But they did not.","WAA!","A brilliant, stellar blue light flared from beneath the skin of every single Veiled Enforcer and Warden!","Because Noah’s Infinite Sanguine Mana had already cut open their existences and rewritten their loyalties, his Quintessential absolute violently rejected the compulsion! The crimson gold threads in their blood roared to life, locking their knees and holding their spines perfectly straight! The Veiled did not bow to external beings!","Up on his throne, Noah’s gaze turned sharp as waves of heavy, blinding information rushed into the minds of everyone present.","|An Immense One has cast a seed upon the board.|","|Pure Blood Essence of an Immense One has been scattered across select Dimensional Cabins.|","|Within the center of THE Serenaros, the Essence has taken root. It will soon mature into a Pure Blood Fruit. If consumed, this Fruit will heavily elevate the Dimensionality and physical foundations of the victor.|","|To ensure a worthy harvest, the Pure Blood Essence releases a heavy, undeniable scent across all connected Dimensional Cabins.|","|Let the contenders gather.|","Noah read the prompts with a cold tyrannical smile.","A treasure and a poison had just bloomed within their Dimensional Cabin! The Immense Ones were not just waiting for the Cabins to fight; they were actively dropping bait to force a bloodbath!","And the bait worked flawlessly.","Almost the exact moment the obsidian crimson tree fully formed, a terrifying sound echoed from the front of THE Serenaros Dimension!","The massive, translucent doorway leading to the higher Dimensional Cabin ahead of them began to buzz violently! The thick, crystallized barriers separating the realms screamed under a sudden, overwhelming pressure!","BOOM!","|The Walls between Dimensional Cabins are coming down.|","The prompt dropped like an executioner’s blade!","The translucent doorway at the front of THE Serenaros began to slide open, and a heavy, suffocating aura immediately bled through the gap! It was a dense, crushing Intent that carried the weight of an apex predator who had smelled the Pure Blood Essence and was coming to claim it.","Down below, Mahishasura raised his golden shield, his amber gold eyes locking onto the opening doorway as the Veiled Enforcers raised their authorities in perfect unison!","But up in the unseen layers, Noah watched.","His endlessly blue eyes swirled with boundless Provenance. He had just finished transforming all 200 Decillion of his fundamental building blocks into Provenance Telos Quarks! He had just forged the First Tier of the Provenance Body and activated THE Quintessential Provenance Skin! He was structurally pristine, generating an Osmontian Moirai that sat heavily at sixty!","Noah looked at the opening doorway, feeling the suffocating weight of whatever was stepping through to claim the Immense One’s prize.","He was not afraid as instead, he was genuinely, intensely curious.","He simply wondered... just what level of Dimensionality could he withstand before he even had to try?"]},{"number":5660,"title":"Chapter 5660: Chapter 5659: I Think, Therefore I Am! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","At times, the deepest shock of a breached door is rarely the monster you do not know. It is the presence you have already bled alongside!","Noah had his eyes locked on the front threshold of THE Serenaros Dimension. The thick, crystallized barriers separating their Dimensional Cabin from the one ahead were sliding open. He expected an apex predator, drawn by the undeniable scent of the Immense One’s Pure Blood Essence that was currently bubbling into a colossal stellar tree in the center of his rusted courtyards!","But as the heavy, suffocating aura bled through the gap, Noah’s eyes pulsed with sudden incredulity!","He felt the signature of life outside that door even before the physical bodies stepped in. He felt it because the weavings of his infinity, however cast out, were silently braided into the existences walking into his Dimension!","The doorway parted fully, and boundless waves of obsidian Paradox spilled into the realm.","Two figures emerged from the roaring abstract storms. The first was a massive obsidian titan, towering with the crushing density of a Primeval beast. Existence itself actively distorted and warped around his massive frame. Beside him walked a humanoid dressed in the threadbare rags of a peasant, his entire body burning quietly with faint, obsidian flames of pure anomaly.","They were beings Noah knew intimately, though they carried an entirely different weight at this moment.","It was THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Paradox! The student and the teacher were both here!","Noah activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard, taking the measure of their growth across the different flows of time.","|THE Living Paradox|","|VERITAS: 11|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: Undefined|","|PONDUS: 12|","|THE Primordial Paradox|","|VERITAS: 15|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: Undefined|","|PONDUS: 18|","Of course, attributes sitting in the teens carried a profound, lethal weight for any standard True Lifeform. But even more astonishing than their arrival was the immediate realization that the heavy aura of oppression did not stem from them.","The true, suffocating weight came from the shadow walking behind them.","An old man stepped through the threshold. He wore the loose, immaculate garbs of an ancient philosopher, his bearing entirely devoid of the fanaticism of THE PAX or the primal rage of the Primeval Ones. He radiated a boundless regality and an intellect so sharp it felt physically abrasive!","His eyes were unfathomably deep, holding a paradoxical certainty that forced the surrounding laws of existence to quietly submit to his presence.","Noah gazed at him once, and the Records answered with a heavy weight.","| Descartes, THE Continuum Paradox|","|VERITAS: ?????|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 62|","|PONDUS: 65|","|EXISTENTIAL MOIRAI: 85|","An existence sitting deep in the sixties, carrying a VERITAS completely obscured by questions marks!","The moment this philosopher appeared, he swept his sharp gaze across the Dimension. He completely ignored the towering blood-tree budding at the center of the courtyards. He ignored the endless cages filled with inhibited lifeforms hovering in the sky. He instantly locked his gaze directly upon the unseen layers, finding Noah immediately.","The old man stared at the Progenitor, and he frowned.","Before the tension could escalate into a conflict of Rulings, a boisterous voice boomed out and shattered the quiet.","\" Haha, Youngest? Youngest! How are you here? It has been months!\"","The titanic figure of THE Primordial Paradox rushed forward, his obsidian body vibrating with genuine, unfiltered joy. Even the prideful and calculative visage of Erwin cracked with shock, the peasant-garbed anomaly offering a small, rigid nod of acknowledgment toward the bloody throne.","Seeing an old friend, a title that could truly only be applied to THE Primordial Paradox, as Erwin had once been an enemy he nearly killed, Noah waved his hand.","Down in the courtyards, the thousands of Veiled Descendants immediately stood down. They lowered their authority and stepped backward, every single one of them moving with the deliberate, synchronized precision of chess pieces as they formed neat, silent rows behind their emperor.","Noah rose from his throne.","He descended through the unseen layers, his crimson-gold robes trailing stellar blue light as he stepped onto the rusted ground. He met THE Primordial Paradox in the center of the courtyard, and the two of them dapped up!","HUUUM!","The physical collision of their hands caused the surrounding existence to violently buzz! Bursts of localized, obsidian paradoxical storms raged outward from their grip, clashing uselessly against the invisible barrier of Noah’s Quintessential Provenance Skin!","\" Man, I still cannot see your depths,\" THE Primordial Paradox laughed, pulling Noah into a heavy, crushing hug. \"I thought with time moving differently across Dimensions, I may have pulled ahead of you just a little, but it doesn’t seem like it. Oh...\"","At that moment, THE Primordial Paradox scratched his massive obsidian head. He turned around, his boisterous demeanor instantly shifting into a posture of profound respect as he looked toward the old man behind them.","\" Continuum Master ,\" THE Primordial Paradox announced cleanly, \" this is an old friend and benefactor of both of us. THE Youngest, Osmont!\"","...!","Continuum Master?","Noah was genuinely astonished. THE Primordial Paradox, an entity of absolute arrogance who had warred against the weavings of existence itself, actually referred to another being as his Master?","Noah looked closely at the old man. Descartes was filled with unfathomable power, yet he carried no greed. He had ignored the Immense One’s treasure entirely to focus his complete attention upon Noah.","Descartes looked back at him calmly. His voice, when he finally spoke, hd devastating weight of absolute logic.","\"I think, therefore I am ,\" Descartes stated evenly. \" Do you think, Youngest?\"","HUUM!","It was a simple question.","Yet shockingly, Noah felt his Provenance Essence violently pulse! An unbearable conceptual weight slammed down upon his shoulders, testing the very foundation of his identity. He felt entire seas of unfathomable paradox pressing down around him, seeking to measure the exact depth of the truth he claimed to hold!","His physical existence demanded a response. His 200 Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks screamed to defend him, urging him to erupt with Infinite Sanguine Mana and violently shatter the incoming suppression.","But his mind recognized the nature of the pressure. It was not a physical strike. It was a philosophical measurement!","Noah stood perfectly still under the crushing weight, his endlessly blue eyes locking onto the philosopher, and he replied using the absolute, undeniable root of his own Tongue.","\"I AM!\"","BOOM!","Instantly, the heavy, suffocating weight pressing down upon him faded away into nothingness.","Descartes held Noah’s gaze for a long moment, the sharp intellect in his eyes cooling slightly. The old philosopher gave a single, slow nod, finding the answer perfectly adequate!"]},{"number":5661,"title":"Chapter 5661: Chapter 5660: I Think, Therefore I Am! II","paragraphs":["Descartes stood quietly in the center of the rusted courtyard, his unfathomable eyes sweeping away from Noah.","The old philosopher looked at the thousands of Veiled Descendants standing in perfectly ordered rows, and then he looked up at the massive floating metal cages filled with Inhibited True Lifeforms. He observed the grim, suffocating machinery of THE PAX without a fraction of shock.","\"It is a logical inevitability ,\" Descartes said smoothly.","\" Those who forge chains for others are simply building the very links that will eventually bind them. To suppress another’s existence is to admit that your own standing is too fragile to survive their freedom. The masters of this order built an entire system of cages, and now they find themselves locked. A perfect, symmetrical consequence.\"","He turned his head slightly, addressing his towering obsidian disciple without raising his voice.","\" Catch up, \" Descartes instructed THE Primordial Paradox, waving a perfectly calm hand. \" We will move soon, as I am... interested in your friend here.\"","...!","Descartes did not wait for an acknowledgment. He turned his back on the budding stellar blood-tree and the heavy aura bleeding through the vanguard doorway. He walked slowly toward the distant prisons, his hands clasped behind his back, and began to observe the Inhibited Lifeforms locked within the cages.","Noah watched the philosopher walk away.","His endlessly blue eyes shone with a profound, terrifying realization. He had just integrated THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign, elevating his attributes tremendously and establishing himself as a Progenitor. Yet the old man walking across the courtyard carried a density of paradox that made the surrounding physical laws actively submit to his footsteps.","\" How the hell did you come to be a disciple of another?\" Noah asked. \" And to someone like that?\"","Despite the sheer arrogance THE Primordial Paradox usually carried, the obsidian titan did not bristle at the question. He let out a heavy, rumbling breath that sounded like grinding tectonic plates.","THE Primordial Paradox offered a grim smile and shook his massive head. He looked over at Erwin, who stood quietly in his threadbare peasant rags, faint obsidian flames of anomaly burning across his skin.","\" All this guy’s fault ,\" THE Primordial Paradox said dryly. \" As THE Information Paradox, when we were at our absolute wits, he pulled upon all information across the continuum and instead called upon... our Master there.\"","The titan raised his massive hand. \" Ah, best if I just show you.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox waved his fingers, condensing a heavy singularity of obsidian light. He tossed the record directly to Noah.","Noah reached up and caught the singularity calmly. He allowed the condensed information to slip past his Quintessential Provenance Skin, and the scenes instantly began playing out across his mind!","The rusted courtyards of THE Serenaros faded. Noah’s vision plunged into the abstract, tearing violence of a different timeline.","He saw a cluster of Observable Existences burning in the void. Countless Gilded Lifeforms lay shattered across them. Standing in the center of the ruin were THE Primordial Paradox and Erwin. Both were heavily wounded, their obsidian authorities flickering and failing!","\" We were hunting a cluster of Gilded Lifeforms,\" THE Primordial Paradox narrated directly into Noah’s consciousness, his voice completely stripped of its usual boisterous warmth. \" And we stepped too deep. The noise drew the masters of the soil.\"","The space behind the two anomalies violently tore open. Three Primeval Lifeforms emerged from the crossing-dark. They were towering, impossible titans woven of raw Egos and petrified bone, carrying Egos of Superbius that crushed the remnants of the Observable Existences into dust simply by arriving.","\" They were old, \" the narration continued. \" They were heavy. We were completely outmatched and about to be collapsed into nothingness.\"","In the record, the Primeval Ones unleashed a tsunami of conceptual weight. Erwin dropped to his knees. The peasant-garbed anomaly reached his bleeding hands directly into the fabric of the continuum. He weaponized his own failing existence, spreading his paradoxical information across the furthest reaches of reality in a desperate, blind summons.","The void answered.","Descartes did not arrive with an explosion. The philosopher simply appeared between the dying anomalies and the raging Primeval Ones, wearing the exact same immaculate robes.","The Primeval Ones drove their massive, starlight-woven limbs downward, bringing the full, lethal weight of their Causes and THE Argent Loom directly onto the old man!","Descartes looked up, and he did something unique.","| The Continuum Paradox has rejected the sensory data of the attack.|","|He temporarily denies the certainty of the physical world. He doubts the existence of the blazing egos and the crushing bone.|","Because Descartes refused to acknowledge the physical reality of the strike, the unfathomable depth of his paradox forced Existence to agree with him!","The Primeval attacks struck his position and simply ceased to be true. The kinetic force and the conceptual weight passed entirely through him, rendered as nothing more than hollow, empty illusions!","The three Primeval Ones roared in absolute confusion!","Descartes countered. He simply spoke to them, applying the cruelest, most absolute logic existence could bear.","\"You beasts rely on authority and Egos,\" Descartes said in the memory, his voice echoing with devastating clarity. \" But if an illusion deceives your eyes, and authority and emotions cannot strike true, what are you? I think, therefore I am. Do you think, or do you merely consume?\"","|THE Continuum Paradox asserts absolute existence while eroding the certainty of the enemy. Without their power, the Primeval Lifeforms cannot prove their own cognition. Their existences begin to waver.|","The Primeval Ones shrieked as their massive bodies began to flicker. Their Causes unspooled!","Descartes stepped forward and delivered the execution!","|THE Continuum Paradox divides reality into two distinct substances: the non-physical thinking mind and physical extension in space.|","|The dualism is imposed violently upon the targets.|","Descartes segregated their minds from their matter. He tore their non-physical consciousness directly out of their physical forms!","The massive titans collapsed instantly. Their minds were cast adrift into the abstract void, completely severed from reality, while their towering bodies of Egos and bone rotted into dead, inert matter in a single second.","No physical blows were struck. No raw authority was exchanged. It was pure, lethal philosophy.","\" Since that day that we were saved ,\" THE Primordial Paradox concluded the narration, the obsidian singularity fading entirely from Noah’s mind. \" We have been learning from him. Because when it comes to Paradox... none of us can compare.\"","BOOM!","Noah blinked, the rusted courtyards of THE Serenaros snapping back into focus.","His tyrannical mind raced, processing the sheer terror of an existence that weaponized existential doubt to unmake ancient beings. To simply deny an attack the right to be true, and to sever a mind from its flesh through absolute logic... it was a methodology of power that was unfathomably unique.","Noah turned his head, looking past his Veiled army.","He refocused his endlessly blue eyes on the distant, unbothered lifeform. Descartes was standing in front of the massive metal cages, calmly engaging the terrified, Inhibited True Lifeforms in conversation! Casually!"]},{"number":5662,"title":"Chapter 5662: Chapter 5661: I Think, Therefore I Am! III","paragraphs":["Descartes entered and left cages freely.","The sealed dimension was supposed to be completely under Noah’s lock and key. Yet, from the very cages that held the collected trophies of Mahishasura and others, he simply traversed in and out as by the time he was done...","Descartes approached Noah.","\" Let us talk.\"","The voice was calm, holding no trace of any known authorities like Infinity or the dense Primordial Source.","Before Noah could formulate a response, the space rippled as two other figures stood on the periphery.","THE Primordial Paradox tilted his head and pointed toward Erwin.","\" Continuum Master, can we listen in?\"","Descartes did not turn around. He merely spoke to the empty air.","\" Listen in, if you are able to. We are here, and not here.\"","The moment the words left his mouth, a shift occurred. To the perception of everyone else present in the dimension, Descartes and Noah vanished. They were simply subtracted from the perception of reality, entering a depth of Dimensionality that defied observation!","THE Primordial Paradox sighed with heavy frustration. Behind him, Erwin also sighed.","\" Will that monstrous anomaly steal the show again? And here I thought we were making progress.\"","THE Primordial Paradox shook his head.","\"We made tremendous progress. Just some beings in existence can be utter monsters. Come on, let us try to listen in as they should be here.\"","Noah looked at the two paradoxes with shining eyes. They truly could not perceive them simply from the words of Descartes.","Descartes settled his gaze on Noah.","\" Do you agree with what Vakochev did? And the fact that he failed?\"","BOOM!","The question carried the conceptual weight of a collapsing Dimension. Noah remained outwardly still, but astonishment cascaded through him. He analyzed this impossible entity. How did this being know about the failure of Vakochev? Was he also among those that the final message reached? Did he hold an obsidian crystal of his own?","Noah met the gaze of the strange man.","\"It is only human to fail, and one can only try again.\"","He did not offer a defense of Vakochev, nor did he condemn him. He simply stated the bare reality of ambition. Then, Noah asked the only question that mattered.","\" Who are you, really?\"","\"I am just a thinking thing.\"","The philosophical reply hung in the air, dense with an unreadable depth.","\"Could I ask you a few questions, Young Friend?\"","Noah nodded lightly.","Descartes began.","\"If you completely strip away your name, your home, your family expectations, and your social status, what remains of the you that you are trying to be true to?\"","Noah blinked did not answer immediately. He let the question sink into the bedrock of his existence. If he was not THE True Human Emperor, if he was not Amelia’s son or Henry’s father, what was left? He looked inward.","\"A... tyrannical desire to thrive. What remains is the sheer, unadulterated will to impose its own order on a chaotic void. What remains is a hunger that refuses to let anyone else hold the pen that writes my story.\"","Descartes accepted the answer without judgment. He asked the next.","\"How do you know that your passions, cravings, and deepest desires are actually your own, rather than mere mechanical reflexes and chemical tricks of your physical body?\"","Noah found himself genuinely thinking. It was a terrifying concept, the idea that his very drive might be a scripted chemical reaction. He weighed it against his own choices. He decided on his truth.","\"Because I am the one who pays the price for them. If my body tricks me into a desire, I devour the trick. I take ownership of the reflex. A craving is only a trick if you are a slave to it. If you weaponize it to climb to the peak of existence, it becomes a tool. And tools belong to the hand that wields them.\"","\"A heavy claim, \" Descartes mused. \" But consider this. If an invisible force or internal psychological bias is actively deceiving you into believing a beautiful lie about your character, how do you verify that your self-image is not a complete illusion? What objective proof do you have that your authentic self is a reality and not a comforting ego defense mechanism?\"","Noah felt the weight of the question pressing against his VERITAS!","Objective proof. Was there such a thing?","\"There is no objective proof. Existence is terribly fond of novelty, and it will offer you a thousand mirrors to show you a thousand different lies. My proof is not found in a mirror. My proof is found in consequence. If my authentic self is an illusion, I will enforce that illusion upon reality until existence itself has no choice but to accept it as the ultimate truth. The proof...is the reality I leave behind.\"","Descartes offered a slow nod.","\"When you are fast asleep and dreaming of a completely different life, body, and existence, which version of you is the true one, and why do you prioritize the waking one?\"","Noah thought of the endless crossings, the dimensions, the lives he could have lived.","\"The true one is the one that wakes up. I prioritize the waking one because it is the one that has to bear the weight. The dreaming one gets to escape. I have been a Dreamer. I have met Great Dreamers. I have even dreamed an endless Dream, but I always wake up. The waking one has to protect its people, face THE Immense Ones, and build a home. The waking one is true because it does the work.\"","WAA!","By the time he finished answering the final question, a pristine state of clarity washed over him. The very fabric of his existence resonated!","|VERITAS: 46|","|VERITAS: 47|","|VERITAS: 48|","His Trueness began to shoot up, tearing through the walls of the forties. Just from thinking about and answering questions about himself!","Descartes looked upon the blooming stellar blue light.","\" To be true to oneself in existence is more than enough to overcome everything. It is how Those Who Remain became so powerful. Whether vile or good, whether they built sanctuaries or slaughtered Existences, they lived so absolutely true that now, even existence cannot argue with them.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5663,"title":"Chapter 5663: Chapter 5662: How To Kill An Immense One? I","paragraphs":["Descartes looked at Noah calmly.","\" Do you know what you are, Youngest?\" Descartes asked. \" Not your titles. Those are decoration. I mean the rare thing. The thing that makes an old creature like me cross a threshold to look at you.\"","Noah met the deep eyes and said nothing.","\" You are one of the few who wants to change the shape of things. \" Descartes clasped his hands behind his back.","\" That is rarer than you would believe. Existence is vast beyond any counting, and it is packed corner to corner with the mighty, and almost none of them want anything more than a larger portion of exactly what already is. A deeper cage. A higher rung. A wider vineyard. They climb and they climb, and not one in a billion ever lifts his head to ask whether the ladder should exist at all.\"","\" And of that one in a billion who does ask, who does look up and hate the ladder and dream of tearing it down, almost every single one lacks the power to so much as scratch it. They rage. They write manifestos in their own blood. They die small, and existence does not so much as pause to note the passing. Vakochev was rare, Youngest. He was one of the ones who both wanted it and nearly had the means. And you already know how that ended.\"","\"He failed ,\" Noah said. \" And retreated.\"","\"He failed and retreated. \" Descartes nodded, unbothered, as though failure were simply a data point and not a tragedy.","\" Which brings me to my question. Forget the Scales. Forget the Ruling and the Train and the whole grinding pageant the architects have arranged for us. Set all of it down, and answer me one thing.\"","The old philosopher’s gaze sharpened to a point.","\" How would you kill an Immense One?\"","HUUM!","The question landed with weight! It pressed on the concept of the thing, on the sheer blasphemy of the sentence spoken aloud, and Noah felt the subtracted space around them tighten as though existence itself had leaned in to hear.","Noah’s eyes sharpened.","And then he shook his head.","\"I don’t have enough information to answer that confidently,\" he said. \"I don’t know .\"","Descartes smiled, and it was the first warm thing his face had done.","\" Good ,\" the philosopher said. \"A man who claims to know is a man who has stopped thinking. But you should know. So let me give you the information you lack .\"","\"To understand how to kill one of Those Who Remain,\" Descartes began, \" you must first stop thinking of them as a wall, and start thinking of them as a kind. And to know their kind, you must set them beside the only thing in existence that shares their nature. You must set them beside a Provenance Lifeform.\"","He began to walk a slow circle in the nothing, hands behind his back, and Noah turned with him.","\" They are not so different as the frightened believe. Both generate their own standing. Both owe nothing to any framework. Both are answered by existence rather than answering to it. The difference between an Immense One and a Provenance Lifeform is not a difference of kind. It is only a difference of degree, and of one other thing. But before I name it, for you to truly understand, I would rather tell you a story.\"","Noah inclined his head. He loved old monsters who talked freely and gave him lots of information!","\" Long ago ,\" Descartes said, and the subtracted dark seemed to deepen and settle around the telling, \" so long ago that the rulings had not yet been weighed and the architects were young, there walked a company of Provenance Lifeforms. A grand company. They generated their own light, and they wanted for nothing, and they moved through the early dark as sovereigns of themselves, which is the only true sovereignty there is.\"","\" One day, they came upon another of their kind, sitting alone against a stone. He was dying. His light had thinned to almost nothing. His generation had faltered, his essence had begun to scatter, and by every measure the company could take, he had perhaps a handful of years left before he unwove entirely.\"","\" Now, a Provenance Lifeform does not die easily, and does not die often, and to see one of their own kind fading against a stone moved the company deeply. They gathered around him. They offered him their own generation, their own light, the deepest gift one sovereign existence can offer another. They told him they would not let him die. They had the means to arrest his fading, to prop him up, to buy him Ages he could not buy himself.\"","Descartes paused in his slow circle.","\" And the dying one refused.\"","\"He looked up at them, and he told them no. He said that his fading was his own. He said that the shape of his existence had brought him here, to this stone, at this hour, and that this too was part of what he was. To be propped up by another’s light, he said, would be to become a thing that was held together from outside. And he would rather scatter as himself than persist as something borrowed. He wished only to live true to the last, and his death was part of his truth, and he would not trade the truth of his ending for a longer, falser life.\"","Noah listened without moving!","\" The company of Provenance Lifeforms thought this a great shame, \" Descartes continued. \"A waste. They were sovereigns, and to them the refusal of help looked like pride hardened into foolishness. They argued with him, and he would not be moved, and at last they did the only thing left to do. They left him food. A store of it, enough for the years he had left, so that whatever he had chosen, he would at least not fade in hunger against his stone.\"","\" And then they moved on. And in the vastness of existence and the length of Ages, they forgot him. As one does. As all things do.\"","...!"]},{"number":5664,"title":"Chapter 5664: Chapter 5663: How To Kill An Immense One? II","paragraphs":["\" Ages passed. The company of Provenance Lifeforms prospered, and grew, and became a lineage, and the lineage spread its light across the early dark. But existence does not let the sovereign prosper unwatched. There came a day when that lineage crossed another company of Provenance Lifeforms, and this second company was not alone. Behind them stood the aura of one of Those Who Remain, an architect who had taken them as its own, and lent them the edge of its immensity.\"","\"It was not a contest as much as it was an extermination. The lineage that had once shown mercy to a dying stranger was driven to the edge of unmaking, cornered, their light guttering, an entire bloodline of sovereign existences about to be scattered into the dark with an Immense One’s weight pressing down to make certain none survived.\"","Descartes stopped walking.","\" And then another aura rose.\"","\"It came out of the deep dark, vast beyond the reckoning of anyone present, and it was the unmistakable, existense-bending weight of a second Immense One. It fell across the doomed lineage and it stood between them and their end, and the enemy company broke and fled, and the architect that had backed them, an Immense One in its own right, took one look at the aura that had risen to oppose it, and it fled as well. It fled, Youngest. One of Those Who Remain looked at what had come to defend a handful of sovereigns, and it chose flight over ruin.\"","\" The lineage was saved. And they looked up at their impossible savior, this Immense One who had scattered their doom, and they waited to see the face of the architect who had chosen, for reasons none of them could fathom, to spend its immensity on their behalf.\"","Descartes let the silence stretch to its breaking point.","\"It was the dying man. The one from the stone. The one they had fed and forgotten Ages before.\"","BOOM!","The word landed soft and landed heavy, and Noah’s endlessly blue eyes had gone very still!","\" He had not died,\" Descartes said quietly. \" He thanked them. Can you imagine it. An Immense One, a thing that architects now flee, and the first words out of it were thanks, for a store of food left against a stone in a forgotten Age. And the lineage, on their knees before the being that had saved them, asked him the only question that mattered. The question you would have asked. The question I asked, when I first heard this tale. They asked him how. How does a dying sovereign, fading against a stone, refusing all help, become in a few short Ages a thing that Those Who Remain flee from?\"","\" And he gave them an answer of four words, or near enough, and it is the answer I have carried across every Age since.\"","Descartes turned to face Noah fully.","\" He said: I lived truly. Unfathomably. To exactly who I was. I was true.\"","BOOM!","The subtracted dark rang with it, and for a long moment neither of them spoke.","Noah understood, now, why the old philosopher unmade Primevals with doubt, why he asked a man to prove his own waking life, why he had raised Noah’s own Trueness simply by making him examine it. It was all one lesson. It had always been one lesson!","An Immense One was not a different kind of thing from a Provenance Lifeform. It was a Provenance Lifeform that had lived so completely, so unfathomably true to the whole of what it was, that existence itself had stopped being able to argue with it. That was the difference of degree. That was the only difference there was. The architects were not born above the sovereign!","They had simply out-truthed the sovereign, across Ages, until their truth became the floor everything else stood upon.","And Descartes watched the understanding move across Noah’s still face, and he nodded, satisfied, and delivered the point of the whole long telling.","\" So .\" The old man’s eyes glittered with a cold, absolute logic. \" You asked me how to kill an Immense One, and I told you I could not answer that until we had simplified the equation. Now we have simplified it. An Immense One is only a Provenance Lifeform that has gone all the way. So the question is no longer a blasphemy. It is no longer even a large question. It has become a small one, and a plain one, and I will now ask it of you, since you are the one thing in this room built to answer it.\"","He leaned in, and the weight of it pressed against the very root of Noah’s existence.","\" How does one kill a Provenance Lifeform?\"","BOOM!","\"Would you be able to tell me that, O Provenance Lifeform?\"","The words hung in the subtracted dark, unbearably heavy, and Descartes simply waited, patient as stone, for the being he had crossed a threshold to test to reach for its own throat and describe how the cut was made!","At times, there is a moment in any real question when the person asked stops looking for the clever answer and starts looking at himself.","He wasn’t surprised that this being found out he was a Provenance Lifeform. So he instead thought about what anseer he could give.","Noah did not rush it.","\" There are two ways that I’ve thought about ,\" he said finally.","Descartes said nothing. He only waited!","\" The first is the obvious one. You cannot out-power a Provenance Lifeform. Not really. Pour enough weight onto one and you flatten the body, but the body was never the thing. A Provenance Lifeform generates itself. It is a well. And you do not kill a well by emptying the bucket, because the bucket fills again from below. So the first way is not to strike the water. It is to strike the source. You have to reach past everything it has made and get your hand around the act of making itself, and you have to convince it, at the root, to stop.\"","He turned the thought over as he spoke.","\"A Provenance Lifeform is a thing that answers to nothing outside itself. That is its glory and its single flaw. Because if nothing outside can command it, then the only thing that can stop its generation is the thing inside. You do not conquer a sovereign. You make the sovereign issue the order against itself. You corrupt the well at its head so that it poisons everything it pours. You get it to doubt its own truth for one full breath, and in that breath, its generation turns on itself, and it unmakes what it was still in the middle of making. It does not die of a wound. It dies of a contradiction. It becomes a thing that is generating and un-generating in the same instant, and it tears itself apart trying to be both.\"","Descartes’ eyes had gone very still!"]},{"number":5665,"title":"Chapter 5665: Chapter 5664: The Thing Beneath The Fruit! I","paragraphs":["\" That is the clean way,\" Noah said. \" The philosopher’s way. You would like it. It is almost bloodless.\"","\"And the second?\"","Noah’s endlessly blue eyes cooled.","\" The second is not bloodless at all.\"","\" A Provenance Lifeform is true. That is what it is, all the way down, a truth that generates itself and owes nothing. But a truth is only a truth as long as it is whole. So the second way is not to argue with the truth. It is to divide it. You do not try to overpower a sovereign existence and you do not try to trick it into doubt. You get inside the one indivisible thing it is, and you split it into two things that are each almost it, and then you make those two halves true against each other.\"","His voice stayed level.","\" Because a Provenance Lifeform cannot be commanded from outside, but it also cannot survive being two sovereigns in one skin. Set half of its own truth against the other half. Make its generation fight its generation. It will pour its entire infinite wellspring into winning a war against itself, and it will win, and in winning it will have spent everything it was on destroying half of what it was, and what remains will be a sovereign that has already killed the thing it most needed to stay whole. You make it the murderer and the murdered at once, and you simply wait for the survivor to notice it cannot live as half a truth.\"","The dark was silent.","\" One way corrupts the source until it poisons itself,\" Noah finished. \" The other divides the truth until it wars with itself. Both of them work the same way underneath, if you look. You cannot kill a thing that answers to nothing. So you make it the only authority it will ever obey. You turn the sovereign into its own executioner, and you get out of the way.\"","Descartes nodded.","\" Yes ,\" the old man said simply. \" Those are...theories and possibilities, but they are possibilities. Keep them in mind, Youngest. Keep them very close, for what is to come.\"","He turned his face away, toward nothing, toward the whole grinding architecture of the Train that lay beyond.","\" You and I should never have met,\" Descartes said. \" In all the vastness of existence, the odds of two beings like us occupying the same small Dimension at the same small hour are so thin as to be a joke. We are ants. Rare ants. The kind of ant that might one day look up at the boot and decide to bite. And existence is very large, and it scatters its rare ants very wide, precisely so that they never meet, never talk, never add themselves together into something the boot has to actually fear.\"","He gestured, one slow hand, at the sealed borders of the rushing Dimension.","\" And yet here we are. Because THE Immense Ones have a way of undoing their own precautions. They cannot help themselves. They gathered us. This Train they built, this grand moving pageant of chained Dimensions, they call it a Narrative, and the young ones aboard it believe they have been offered a stage to win glory on. They have not. It is a prison. You and I have been swept into a prison.\"","Descartes’ voice grew heavier with every word!","\" And it is not even a prison, when you look at it plainly. A prison keeps things alive. This is not built to keep. It is grounds of an execution, and we are the condemned who have not yet been told the sentence, marched together down a hallway that only runs one direction.\"","Noah listened without a word, and his mind was already moving ahead of the old man’s mouth!","\" That tree,\" Descartes said.","Noah’s gaze had already gone to it.","\" Some may think it is a prize. Existence told everyone it is a prize, a Pure Blood Fruit, a ladder to greater Dimensionality, a treasure worth crossing doors and killing for. And it is those things. But that is not why it is here. \" The philosopher’s eyes glittered.","\"It is a lure and it is a net at once. Pure Blood is the blood of the architects. It calls to what is like it. Get near that tree, reach for it, consume it, and the thing wakes and it knows. It knows that something of Immense blood, or something with the audacity to reach for Immense blood, is standing in this Cabin. It is not a fruit. It is a nose. The architects planted a nose in your Dimension to smell whether anything worth executing had washed up in the back of their Train.\"","\"Or so it should have worked,\" Descartes murmured. \"A quiet nose, sniffing for one thing at a time. Except.\"","He almost smiled.","\" Except that I am here. Standing beside you. Two of us, in one small confined space, both of us the exact thing that tree was set to smell. And a nose built to catch a single scent, given two at once, in the same room, does not simply catch them. It grows suspicious. It begins to wonder whether it is being tested, or fooled, or walked into. And even if its suspicion is entirely wrong, even if it decides there is nothing here at all...\"","The old philosopher’s calm did not waver, but something in it went very cold.","\"I have found, across a great many Ages, that Those Who Remain are thorough. They do not investigate a suspicion. They resolve it.\"","HUUM!","The words finished, and the dark released them back into the world, and Noah’s gaze was already fixed on the distant tree.","He watched it change, and it had been changing this whole time as it wss supposed to be producing a fruit!","At first it was only the light. The slow ecstatic pulse that had rolled off the crimson canopy stuttered, dimmed, and then went out entirely, as though something had closed a hand around the tree’s heart. The obsidian crimson of the trunk darkened past crimson, past black, into a color that had no honest name, and the canopy began to draw inward.","Then the tree buzzed.","BOOM!","The trunk split, not broken but unfolding, and the blood inside it stood.","Obsidian crimson blood rose up out of the tree and held its own shape in the air, thickening, hardening, gathering into a body that had never been meant to walk.","It climbed on limbs that formed as they climbed. Four of them, vast and jointed wrong, each one ending in a single tapering claw as long as a spear, four spear-claws unfolding from a torso of dark wet crimson that drank the light and gave nothing back.","It rose over the courtyards, and it kept rising, until it stood taller than the mountains, a fiendish crimson thing of obsidian sheen and terrible cold stillness, and along the ridge of its featureless head, nine eyes opened.","Nine flat gold eyes, evenly spaced, each one holding no rage and no hunger and no thought that any living being would recognize, only a cold and total attention. They opened one after another down the length of that awful head, and when the last of them opened, all nine turned, slowly, and looked down at everything in the Dimension at once.","The cold that came off it was a judgment!","Every Veiled Descendant in the courtyards went rigid, and this time Noah’s Sanguine Mark did not fully steady them, because the thing gazing down was not asking for reverence. It was taking a measurement, and being measured by it felt like being read for a sentence.","Noah stood on his ground and looked up at it, and he turned the full weight of THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard upon the thing, demanding to know what had just uncoiled out of an Immense One’s bait.","And the Records answered him with almost nothing.","|?????|","|VERITAS: ?????|","|PROVENANCE: ?????|","|POTENTIA: ?????|","|PONDUS: ?????|","Question marks. A wall of them, the way there had been for Rosalia. But beneath the blank attributes, where a name should sit, the Records gave him one thing, and only one after a little while!","| THE Sundered Scion of Sovereign and Immense.|","Noah’s eyes very still.","A Scion. A child!","Not a Provenance Lifeform and not an Immense One, but a thing born where the two had been forced together, the sovereign and the architect bred into one body and one blood, and something in the making had gone wrong, had come out sundered, had come out as this cold nine-eyed abomination that the architects grew on a tree and used as a nose.","They had not planted a fruit in his Dimension.","They had planted their own broken child, and told it to smell the room, and now it had smelled two of the exact thing it was made to find, and nine gold eyes were looking down at a company of the condemned with the cold and total patience of a thing that had been made for exactly this and nothing else.","Descartes, standing at Noah’s side, exhaled softly, and it was almost weary.","As if this old man...was truly tired.","\" Ah ,\" the old philosopher said. \" There it is. I did tell you they were thorough.\""]},{"number":5666,"title":"Chapter 5666: Chapter 5665: The Thing Beneath The Fruit! II","paragraphs":["Noah stood on the mountains of THE Serenaros, his endlessly blue eyes locked on the colossal, nine-eyed abomination towering above them. THE Sundered Scion of Sovereign and Immense looked down, its flat gold eyes radiating a cold, unyielding judgment!","Then, the terrifying silhouette of the beast began to blur.","Noah narrowed his eyes. THE PRECEPT OF SOLIPSISM normally blinded others to his depth, but this was the exact inverse. The Scion possessed a Dimensionality so unfathomably deep that it was physically slipping out of Noah’s perceptive frameworks. It was descending into an unseen layer of reality that Noah had not yet breached!","Descartes gazed up at the fading horror. The old philosopher clasped his hands behind his back.","\" This will be a difficult one,\" Descartes said calmly. \" The solution will be with the two it wants to kill. Both you and I will have to find what makes this thing tick, and kill it. Those Who Remain act with boundless power, but there are also restrictions. Even in an impossible situation, there is always a chance of survival.\"","The subtraction of their presence ended. Descartes and Noah instantly became perceivable to the rest of the Dimension once again.","THE Primordial Paradox and THE Living Paradox floated up to them immediately. The two obsidian anomalies did not carry their usual arrogance.","Their heavy gazes were fixed on the sky, and their bodies trembled under a sudden, crushing oppression that demanded they kneel!","Descartes did not look at his students. He kept his eyes on the blurring Scion.","\" Stay close to me,\" Descartes instructed them. \" And under no circumstances are you to be in one state of existence. Be alive and dead. Be here and not. Exist on a continuum of paradox. Should you slip a single fraction, I may not be able to save you.\"","...!","The command only deepened the gravity of the space.","Noah focused his utmost attention on the blurring sky. His Provenance churned, drawing on the weight of his 200 Decillion Quarks!","At that exact moment, the nine gold eyes of the beast focused entirely on Noah.","His existence rang with deafening alarm bells!","The sheer, concentrated intent of the Scion bypassed the physical air and spoke directly to the conceptual foundation of the Dimension, proclaiming a single certainty over reality itself!","DEATH .","In the next instant, THE Sundered Scion completely disappeared from Noah’s perception.","Noah did not think as he moved on pure, tyrannical instinct!","He raised his left hand, and millions of Sanguine Blood Drops instantly bloomed into existence on his side. They formed an overlapping, impenetrable wall of crimson gold and stellar blue event horizons, designed to eradicate any approaching physical or conceptual force!","A fraction of a nanosecond later, all millions of his Blood Drops simply evaporated.","BOOM!","They were snuffed out completely!","An unseen force bypassed the Sanguine Mana entirely and smashed directly into his raised hand.","Cracks formed.","His glistening flesh fractured! THE Quintessential Provenance Skin broke!","BOOM!","|THE Quintessential Provenance Skin has been truly tested for the first time.|","|Limits identified. Your pristine vessel is strained against lifeforms that exceed 60 Attributes, even though your own attributes are much lower. Nothing below 60 Attributes can effectively harm you.|","|What has hit you this time is a force carrying an unfathomably higher Dimensionality.|","|WATCH OUT!|","Noah absorbed the sheer, concentrated kinetic impact of countless Dimensions.","For the first time since his transformation, his focus broke!","His body was launched backward with impossible violence. He was smashed across the entire length of THE Serenaros, tearing through the rusted mountains and the heavy purple gold clouds as everything on his path turned into dust!","He slammed directly into the outer barrier of THE Dimensional Provenance Train!","The thick, crystallized glass of the border shrieked under his weight. He was inches away from shattering the boundary and being thrown out into the abstract, lethal annihilation of the crossing-dark!","His Provenance seethed violently. A vast sea of Infinite Sanguine Mana bloomed against the glass, acting as a final cushion to arrest his momentum.","Noah stabilized his broken hand and bellowed into the rushing void.","\"I AM!\"","BOOM!","His 200 Decillion Quarks rang with maddening grandeur. They roared with absolute tyranny, stitching the fractured skin of his hand back together in a wash of stellar blue-gold light!","Noah breathed out in genuine astonishment. A single hit by an enemy he could not even see had nearly cost his newly forged body its life.","This was the raw, unmitigated product of THE Immense Ones. Vakochev had warned those of boundless potential that they would be targeted, and the architects had not sent a messenger. They had sent an executioner!","SKEEE!","A fearsome, metallic cry clapped across the entirety of THE Serenaros Dimension.","The sound carried a horrid, conceptual weight as up in the skies, the massive floating metal cages rattled violently. Every single Inhibited True Lifeform and Primeval One trapped inside those cages with attributes sitting below 10...simply ceased to exist. They turned into puffs of red mist.","Down in the courtyards, the catastrophe spread. Mahishasura and the Veiled Descendants dropped to their knees, bleeding profusely from their eyes and ears. Several of the controlled Descendants lost consciousness entirely and plummeted from the sky!","Noah felt his own existence ring violently against the noise.","|The sound waves of THE Sundered Scion carry THE Provenance Cause of Existential Terminus.|","|You are immune to its effects due to the propagation of your Teloi across the whole of your matter.|","|Lifeforms without sufficient backing of their existence are extinguished.|","...!","BOOM!","Noah stabilized his footing, his endlessly blue eyes heavy with coldness.","He looked across the gigaparsecs of his Dimension. Countless spots of mist drifted where ancient lifeforms had hovered just a moment before. The scream of the unseen enemy continued to tear the purple gold skies apart!","In the far distance, Descartes stood calmly near the ashen, flickering figures of his two paradoxical students. The old philosopher did not raise a weapon, but his unfathomable eyes hardened.","\" To kill senselessly is the crutch of the unimaginative ,\" Descartes stated, his voice slicing cleanly through the deafening screech.","\"A sovereign ends what stands in its way. But only a terrified architect murders the audience just to clear the stage.\"","Descartes raised a single, immaculate hand.","Existence seethed. Billowing clouds of dense, obsidian smoke manifested out of nowhere, wrapping around a specific coordinate in the sky. The paradoxical smoke forced the unseen layers to overlap with the physical world, stripping away the Scion’s concealment and rendering it barely visible again.","But the massive, nine-eyed abomination was not in the sky above the mountain.","Noah felt the air freeze at his back.","The Scion had already crossed the Dimension. Its position was right behind Noah!","Its colossal jaws were opened impossibly wide, and its nine cold gold eyes locked directly onto THE True Human Emperor!","Before the jaws snapped shut, Noah heard a cold, featureless voice echo from the mouth of the abomination.","\" Death is human. Be...human.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5667,"title":"Chapter 5667: Chapter 5666: Heavy! Heavy! Heavy!!!","paragraphs":["A roar was a promise of violence. A spoken word was a promise of comprehension, a signal that the monster understands exactly what it is destroying.","The colossal jaws of THE Sundered Scion closed around Noah!","There was no time to step through the unseen layers. There was no margin to call upon the Weft or fold space. The nine gold eyes locked onto him and simply asserted that his existence was caught.","Noah did not attempt to dodge as he raised both hands, pushing the absolute maximum output of his PONDUS outward, commanding his 200 Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks to hold the line against a creature whose Dimensionality defied the Records!","BOOM!","The collision occurred.","Cracks spiderwebbed across the air. The physical space of THE Serenaros shattered into absolute white static.","Noah’s Quintessential Provenance Skin tore open.","His forearms fractured under a conceptual weight that carried the mass of ten thousand Observable Existences pressing down onto a single point. Crimson gold blood laced with stellar blue light sprayed across the rusted mountains. The agony was instantaneous and absolute, a blinding physical trauma that sought to unravel his Trueness at the root!","He was being chewed by an abomination!","But he did not break.","The moment his blood spilled from malicious foreign authority, hus existence elevated violently in direct proportion to the injury!","The more his pristine flesh tore, the more tyrannical his generation became. His Infinite Sanguine Mana erupted in a blinding crimson tide, forcing the crushing jaws open just a fraction of an inch.","A quiet, devastating voice cut through the violence.","\"A beast that lectures on humanity understands neither death nor life.\"","Descartes stood on the ground far below. The old philosopher did not raise his voice, yet his words bypassed the deafening destruction and struck the conceptual foundation of the Scion.","Descartes applied...Methodological Doubt directly to the beast’s bite.","| THE Continuum Paradox rejects the sensory reality of the jaws.|","|He dictates that the physical extension of the Scion’s teeth cannot be proven true. He doubts the bite.|","Existence was forced to agree with the philosopher. The colossal, obsidian crimson jaws clamping down on Noah suddenly lost their physical density. The crushing kinetic force vanished, turning the teeth into hollow, harmless shadows passing harmlessly through Noah’s body.","Noah dropped from the sky, landing heavily on the ground.","He breathed out, his blood immediately flowing backward to stitch his fractured forearms together. He looked up at the towering abomination.","The Scion did not roar in frustration as it simply adapted.","If its physical bite was denied by philosophy, it would weaponize its architecture!","WAA!","The obsidian crimson flesh of the nine-eyed titan pulsed. For the first time, the absolute darkness of its hide shifted, revealing the anatomy of its making.","Running down the center of its colossal chest, wrapping around its incorrectly jointed limbs, were thick, blindingly bright seams of pure white authority.","THE Argent Loom.","The architects had not birthed this creature naturally. Noah could begin to theorize and see glimpses!","Glimpses of what an Immense One had done!","They had taken the unfathomable blood of an Immense One and forcibly stitched it to the unyielding core of a Provenance Lifeform, using the pristine white threads of the Argent Loom to hold the incompatible truths together.","\"Now that...is a contradiction ,\" Descartes announced, his sharp eyes reading the blinding seams. \" Two things forced into one skin, held by the strings of its masters. It is not whole.\"","WAA!","The Scion moved.","Its nine flat gold eyes glowed with a sickening, heavy light, and it unleashed multiple Provenance Causes simultaneously.","A Cause slammed down upon the courtyard, seeking to freeze the kinetic motion of everything below. A Cause followed immediately, painting the air a dull, dead gray that turned everything into drifting ash.","The sheer scale of the bombardment was catastrophic. It was the brute-force extermination tactic of an entity that did not need to aim!","Noah’s endlessly blue eyes turned cold.","Philosophy alone would not endure an endless barrage of raw architect mass. Brute force would only shatter against a Dimensionality that sat completely outside the established frameworks.","Noah needed to change the rules of the engagement.","He reached into his own depth and activated a mantle he had kept completely hidden from many.","| THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist Mantle has been invoked.|","|You assert narrative dominance over the immediate domain.|","Noah raised his healed hand, his Sanguine Mana flaring as he began to write the reality of the battle.","\"A monster built by others always carries the flaw of its makers,\" Noah declared. \" It attacks blindly because it believes its power requires no precision.\"","|The Trope of the Arrogant Goliath is authored.|","|You dictate that the Scion’s overwhelming bombardment lacks focus. Probability bends to enforce the narrative.|","The gray wave of a Provenance Cause tore through the courtyard, annihilating everything in its path. But because Noah had authored the trope into existence, the wave split precisely around him and Descartes and two Paradoxes.","The destruction leveled the mountains behind them, yet left them standing perfectly untouched in a narrow sliver of spared reality!","The Scion tilted its massive head. Its cold gold eyes narrowed.","It recognized the narrative interference. The white seams of THE Argent Loom across its body flared violently, actively combating Noah’s authorial control!","|THE Sundered Scion utilizes THE Argent Loom and multiple unknown Provenance Causes to reassert the literal reality of its power.|","|Narrative Override contested.|","BOOM!","The backlash of the contested narrative struck Noah directly in the chest!","Pain! Shockingly, he felt actual pain as it wss surreal!","He coughed up a mouthful of stellar blood, his ribs fracturing under the impossible strain of arguing with an Immense One’s direct design!","Provenance Causes! Were these the study and product of THE Immense Ones like THE Sleepless Fiend?! Did thid thing Generate its own Causes, or were they false and instilled in it?","Noah only had such a thought as the battle degenerated into a brutal, grueling meat-grinder.","There was no elegance to the exchange. The Scion brought down one of its massive, spear-like claws. Descartes stepped forward, his face pale with exertion, and applied his unique power to the limb.","He forcibly separated the Scion’s intent to strike from the physical matter of the arm, causing the colossal spear-claw to veer wildly off course and impale the ground miles away.","But the Scion simply ripped the limb free, THE Argent Loom stitching the metaphysical tear back together in an instant.","It fired beams of pure, concentrated Loom-light fused with unknown Provenance Causes from its nine eyes.","Noah answered with Sanguine Blood Drops. He manifested millions of event horizons, stacking them into a dense, crimson gold shield. The white beams struck the shield, and the two authorities ground against each other in a deafening, reality-tearing screech!","The heat of the exchange boiled the purple gold clouds above them away completely.","Noah’s arms shook. His skin cracked and healed in a continuous, agonizing loop!","This fight was one of the worst ones as the enemy he faced exceeded him in almost all ways!","The fight pushed his POTENTIA to staggering heights, allowing him to endure impacts that would have instantly erased a Descendant like Mahishasura.","He was bleeding heavily. His crimson gold robes were shredded.","Descartes was faring no better. The old philosopher’s immaculate robes were scorched. Blood dripped from his nose as he continuously weaponized a weaving Noah affirmed as a Cogito to prevent the Scion’s aura of Existential Terminus from snuffing out their lives.","Cogito, meaning I Think! Descartes continued to think to ensure they werent snuffed out as after some time...","\" The seams!\" Descartes shouted over the roar of the destruction. \" The white threads. They are the only thing keeping it from tearing itself apart!\"","Noah heard the philosopher. He analyzed the towering abomination through the blood pouring into his eyes.","The bloody way.","To kill a Provenance Lifeform, one must divide its truth and make it the murderer and the murdered at once.","Noah dropped his defensive posture. He allowed a glancing blow from the Scion’s tail to smash into his side, shattering his hip and launching him into the air. He used the violent momentum to carry himself directly toward the colossal chest of the beast.","He ignored the pain. He ignored the alarm bells screaming across his 200 Decillion Quarks.","He extended his right hand, condensing his Infinite Sanguine Mana and the absolute weight of his VERITAS into a single, razor-thin blade of crimson gold light.","He did not aim for the obsidian crimson flesh. He aimed exclusively for the blinding white seams of THE Argent Loom holding the chest together.","| THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist Mantle is pushed to the absolute limit.|","|You author The Trope of the Fatal Flaw.|","|You dictate that the architect’s binding is brittle.|","Noah crashed into the chest of the abomination.","He drove the Sanguine blade directly into the thickest seam of white thread.","\"I AM!\" Noah roared, unleashing the foundational Letter of his Tongue directly into the wound.","CRACK!","The sound was not loud, but it resonated with a catastrophic finality.","The Sanguine blade severed the primary knot of THE Argent Loom.","The reaction was instantaneous and apocalyptic. Without the white threads forcing compliance completely, the Immense blood and the Sovereign blood within the Scion recognized each other as foreign, incompatible truths.","The abomination shrieked!","It was a sound of pure, unadulterated agony. The Scion stopped attacking Noah and Descartes entirely. Its massive spear-claws reached up, tearing at its own chest as the two conflicting authorities inside its body began to wage a war of mutual annihilation!","Obsidian crimson blood erupted from the severed seam in a geyser that painted the sky.","The Scion staggered backward, its nine eyes rolling wildly as its generation turned on itself. It was destroying half of what it was to save the other half.","Noah fell back toward the courtyard, landing in a ruined heap of shattered metal and rusted ash. He did not bother standing up immediately. He simply lay there, breathing heavily, his Provenance slowly mending his ruined bones.","\"Fuck!\"","He couldn’t help but curse in pain and frustration as today, he may have very well died!","Descartes walked over to him slowly. The philosopher wiped the blood from his own face, his unfathomable eyes fixed on the shrieking, self-mutilating titan thrashing in the distance.","The beast was not dead. Its Dimensionality was too vast to collapse from a single severed seam. But it was severely wounded, fully occupied with its own internal civil war.","They had taken an impossible executioner sent by the architects, and they had made it bleed.","Noah spat a mouthful of blood onto the rusted ground. He looked up at the old philosopher, his eyes burning with a cold, exhausted tyranny as this old man said...","\" We are thinking things,we just have to outhink this ridiculous beast a bit more to ensure its collapse. Ready?\"","...!"]},{"number":5668,"title":"Chapter 5668: Chapter 5667: Never Fair!","paragraphs":["THE Sundered Scion of Sovereign and Immense did not die from the severed seam. It shrieked, thrashing in the ruined courtyards of THE Serenaros, but it did not collapse. The abomination simply adapted to the tear in its own reality.","It abandoned the elegance of its executioner protocols. It stopped trying to erase Noah and Descartes cleanly. Instead, the Scion wrapped its colossal obsidian crimson body in three unknown Provenance Causes simultaneously, pulling dense, blinding waves of THE Argent Loom directly from the surrounding crossing-dark to act as a physical cast over its broken chest.","It turned itself into a battering ram of pure, unadulterated mass!","In a single nanosecond, THE Sundered Scion attacked forty times.","HUUM!","Noah met the onslaught with his own body. He did not step back. He threw himself directly into the blinding white and obsidian storm, his 200 Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks screaming under the sheer kinetic impact of an entity bred by the architects.","CRACK!","A spear-claw the size of a mountain ridge smashed through Noah’s. The blow shattered his left shoulder, tearing the crimson gold flesh away and exposing the stellar blue-gold marrow beneath.","Noah did not retreat as he weaponized the agony!","He drove his unbroken right fist directly into the Scion’s lower eye, his knuckles wrapped in countless localized event horizons of Sanguine Mana.","The eye burst in a spray of thick, unreadable fluid.","The Scion retaliated instantly, sweeping a Loom-wrapped tail across Noah’s ribs. The impact shattered his ribcage.","Noah spat blood, his endlessly blue eyes burning as he activated his immensity!","|THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist Mantle is invoked.|","|You author The Trope of the Unyielding Bastion.|","|Probability bends. The lethal trajectory of the enemy’s strikes is forced into a predictable rhythm.|","He forced the Scion to fight on his tempo. Descartes stood on the periphery, bleeding, yet the old philosopher never stopped working.","Whenever the Scion raised a limb to deliver a killing blow, Descartes applied Methodological Doubt. He denied the physical reality of the specific joint, causing the colossal arm to stutter and lose its density for a fraction of a second.","Noah exploited every single stutter.","He drove Infinite Sanguine Blood Drops into the joints. He tore away plates of obsidian crimson flesh with his bare hands. He absorbed catastrophic damage, allowing his pristine vessel to be pulverized and restitched in a continuous, grueling loop of destruction and generation!","He grew stronger and stronger through the brutal battle!","Minutes passed.","Against a creature possessing a Dimensionality that defied the Records, a minute of direct physical combat felt like an epoch of uninterrupted torture. The rusted mountains of THE Serenaros were entirely pulverized. The ground was melted into a sea of slag and stellar blue-gold light.","Finally, Noah saw the opening.","Descartes stepped forward, raising both hands, and applied a massive, concentrated burst of The Cogito directly to the Scion’s fractured mind, forcing it to question its own existence for a single, devastating moment.","The beast froze.","Noah launched himself from the sea of slag. He poured the absolute maximum output of his Infinite Sanguine Mana into his right leg, executing a descending strike that carried the localized weight of THE Infiniverse itself.","THE Infiniverse, now holding the weight of Thousands of Observable Existences! Its immensity filled him!","His heel cleaved through the dense white Loom-cast and smashed directly into the top of the Scion’s head.","BOOM...CRACK!","The impact drove the abomination face-first into the ruined ground. The remaining eight gold eyes rolled upward, the cold light within them dimming into nothingness. The massive limbs went entirely slack as Authority and Causes fizzled out as if they could no longer endure!","The sheer, oppressive aura of THE Sundered Scion faded!","Noah dropped to the ground, his chest heaving. He was covered in his own blood, his pristine skin marred by dozens of gory, exposed fractures that were currently knitting themselves back together.","He looked at the fallen beast.","He did not let his guard down as stupidly...","WAA!","A blinding, impossible light erupted from the corpse of the abomination!","The dim gold eyes did not reopen. Instead, the white seams of THE Argent Loom across its body violently multiplied. They tore through the obsidian crimson flesh, rewriting the biological structure of the beast in real-time.","From its massive, ruined back, two colossal, extending wings of pure white Loom-light burst outward!","|A hidden Provenance Cause has been triggered within the vessel of the enemy.|","|THE Cause of the Undying Cycle is active.|","|The architect authored a second life into their executioner. The physical parameters have been reset and elevated.|","The winged Scion rose from the slag, its form now a terrifying, pure horror of white light and obsidian blood.","Noah stared at the prompt, his endlessly blue eyes narrowing into slits. He spat a mouthful of stellar blood onto the ground.","\" Are you fucking kidding me? Hey! Come on!\"","HUUM!","The winged Scion did not wait for them to recover. It beat its colossal wings once, and the sheer kinetic force of the motion tore a vacuum in the center of the Dimension.","The second phase of the battle was infinitely worse than the first.","The Scion was faster. Its strikes carried the added conceptual weight of the Undying Cycle. Noah and Descartes were pushed to the absolute brink of their existences.","Descartes was forced to abandon his calculated philosophical strikes and simply erect walls of absolute doubt, denying the space between them and the Scion to prevent them from being physically erased. Noah fought with a brutal, unhinged ferocity, his Infinite Sanguine Mana flooding the Dimension until the air itself was a thick, suffocating ocean of crimson gold.","They tore it down piece by piece.","Noah lost his left arm. He regenerated it in a burst of rage and drove his newly formed hand directly through the wing’s joint, snapping the Loom-construct entirely. He was a gory, mutilated butcher, his regal crimson robes reduced to bloody rags, but he refused to yield a single inch of ground.","Another grueling, brutal set of minutes dragged on.","Noah realized that cutting the seams was not enough. To kill this thing permanently, he had to separate the sovereign from the architect entirely. He had to ruin its truth beyond any capacity to heal!","He waited for Descartes to create a window.","The philosopher dropped his hands, allowing the Scion to lunge forward, and applied something familiar now that noah affirmed to be Mind-Body Dualism to the creature’s forward momentum, severing its spatial awareness. The beast missed Noah by a fraction of a millimeter.","Noah stepped directly into the Scion’s side.","He reached out with both hands, his fingers digging deep into the ruined, severed chest cavity he had opened in the first phase. He grabbed the thickest clusters of THE Argent Loom in his left hand, and he grabbed the raw, pulsing obsidian crimson flesh of the Immense blood in his right.","He braced his feet against the beast’s ribcage!","He called upon his 200 Decillion Quarks, his PONDUS, his VERITAS, and his absolute Teloi!","\"I AM!\"","WAA!","Noah pulled his hands apart.","He did not just tear flesh. He physically and conceptually ripped the two halves of the abomination’s existence away from each other!","CRACK!","The sound defied description. It was the noise of a fundamental truth being broken over a knee.","Noah tore the Scion entirely in half!","The white wings and the Loom-weavings shrieked and dissolved into useless, scattered threads of light. The obsidian crimson half collapsed into a dead, rotting pile of inert Primeval matter. The contradiction was resolved. The truth was divided!","BOOM!","Noah was flung backwards like a ragdoll as grand, cascading prompts rushed into Noah’s vision, bathing his ruined, bloody body in the light of an impossible victory!","|You have successfully divided the truth of an architect’s creation.|","|THE Sundered Scion of Sovereign and Immense has been permanently eradicated.|","|A profound act of generation through destruction has occurred. You have survived the direct, unmitigated weight of Those Who Remain, and you have shattered it with your own hands.|","|Your Trueness cannot be argued with.|","|VERITAS: 51|","|PROVENANCE: 49|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 49|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 75|","His VERITAS tore through the wall of fifty! His other attributes sat heavily at forty-nine, ready to spill over the edge.","Noah dropped the chunks of dead matter from his hands.","He stood in the center of THE Serenaros, his chest heaving, his breath coming in ragged, bloody gasps. He looked around!","The Dimension was torn to absolute waste. There were no courtyards left. The purple gold mountains were gone. The sky was an empty, scarred void. The ground was replaced by a vast, churning sea of his own Infinite Sanguine Mana, littered with the shattered fragments of reality.","He swept his gaze across the ruin.","The millions of Inhibited True Lifeforms were gone, erased by the Scion’s opening scream. The thousands of Veiled Descendants, the Enforcers, and the Wardens he had planned to use to corrupt the Pax were completely eradicated.","There was only one survivor from the army he had claimed.","Far in the distance, kneeling on a floating chunk of rusted metal, was Mahishasura. The Descendant was bleeding from every orifice, his amber gold eyes dull, his pristine coat ruined. He had survived only because his Ordination of THE SHIELD and his depth had allowed him to barely weather the conceptual eradication.","Everyone else was dead.","An army of Descendants, an entire mountain of assets, shredded without even having the chance to strike a single blow.","Noah looked at the lone survivor, and a cold, heavy realization settled and was affirmed as something he already knew into his bones.","Anything apart from him was useless.","He could claim armies. He could weave entire Dimensions into his fold. But when the true weight of existence descended, when the architects actually looked down and sent their tools, numbers meant absolutely nothing. The followers would only ever be ash in the wind.","As a human, even though it could be terribly lonely, one had to always rely on themselves.","Noah looked over at Descartes. The old philosopher was leaning heavily against a shattered pillar, his immaculate robes ruined, his breathing shallow. THE Primordial Paradox and THE Living Paradox were ashen around him in constant paradoxical states.","Descartes had fought brilliantly as his handicap were protecting his disciples too. He was a monster in his own right. It was human to work together, and Noah respected the old man!","But he could never rely on him. He could not rely on Thalia. He could not rely on any others!","The tools of Those Who Remain alone had been enough to almost kill him today. If he wanted to survive all that was coming, he had to become the only variable that mattered.","Because this was existence.","And existence was never fair!"]},{"number":5669,"title":"Chapter 5669: Chapter 5668: Dreamer!","paragraphs":["The center of the gigaparsec-wide Dimension was reduced to a churning, ruined sea of crimson gold Sanguine Mana and shattered reality.","Descartes stood at the edge of the destruction. The old philosopher kept his unfathomable gaze fixed on his two disciples. THE Primordial Paradox and Erwin flickered violently, trapped in a constant, agonizing state of paradox.","Descartes fed them his own authority, ensuring they remained simultaneously alive and dead, here and not, refusing to let the residual Provenance Cause of Existential Terminus claim their existences.","Once he stabilized them, Descartes turned and floated over the sea of blood to stop near Noah.","\" Existence loves and loathes Those Who Remain for the exact same reason ,\" Descartes said.","\"It loves what they can do, and it loathes what they can do. They have free reign to author the epochs, but they also have restrictions. They can succeed, and they can fail. They failed here.\"","The philosopher looked at the scattered, rotting ash of the Scion.","\" What do you think they will do?\"","Noah stood amidst the ruin of his own making, his shattered skin still knitting itself together.","\" They’ll simply try again ,\" Noah replied calmly.","\" Yes ,\" Descartes nodded. \" But they are not omniscient. They do not know many things, and they only know some things. If they fully and truly knew about you or I, we might not be alive much longer.\"","Descartes clasped his hands behind his back, looking up at the shredded, empty sky of the moving Dimensional Cabin.","\" But we also cannot remain in the place where one of their tools has died. That will just give them free information when they send others to check. We are lucky none were watching this Dimension directly... or perhaps it is not luck at all. Perhaps it is a part of their restrictions. If they already had one of their cards on the field, existence demands balance. They could not also watch. Even I do not know.\"","The old man sighed, the weight of countless epochs settling into his shoulders.","\" There are many profundities about existence, about Provenance Lifeforms and Those Who Remain, that remain a complete mystery. Vakochev tried to peer through these mysteries and change things. Even someone as grand as him failed. That alone should have told all of us to not even try.\"","Descartes looked back at Noah, the corners of his eyes crinkling with a sad, ancient warmth.","\" But we are thinking beings, and we dream. Oh, we love to dream.\"","To dream.","To Dream!","HUUM!","Noah felt his entire existence violently buzz!","The words of the old philosopher did not just land in his ears. They struck the very bedrock of his identity like a physical trigger!","His entire existence vibrated with an unfathomable frequency, and it was his Provenance Essence that buzzed the absolute loudest.","To dream!","It was only human to dream. All humans always dreamed. They dreamed of a better life. They dreamed of a better spouse, a better home, a better anything and everything. The capacity to imagine a reality grander than the one they were handed was the defining trait of humanity.","As THE True Human Emperor, was Noah not the grandest dreamer of them all?","He dreamed of coming out on top against monsters who had lived for Ages. He dreamed of surviving and butchering the exact architects that Vakochev had failed against. Even standing in the wreckage of a nearly impossible battle, bleeding from a dozen fresh wounds, he still dared to dream. He still dared to believe.","At the absolute core of his existence, this was who he was. A human who dreamed of a better life.","Dreams almost always remained dreams for the vast majority of existence. But some humans fulfilled them. Noah wanted to be among them. He wanted to succeed against impossible odds, and he wanted to drag his people to the summit with him.","Noah raised his hands.","He looked at his palms, and small, crystalline tears spilled over his eyelashes. He smiled, a genuine, breathtaking expression of pure humanity breaking through his tyrannical composure.","Deep inside his pristine vessel, his forty-nine singularities of Provenance Essence stopped spinning.","They melted.","The forty-nine dense, stellar blue-gold stars dissolved into a blinding, infinite sea of blue-gold light that began to flood and spread across his entire existence!","They had gained a true, generated identity.","From his union with Thalia Vasiliou, he had generated the weavings of THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign. That was a borrowed, integrated Provenance with a very specific identity. It allowed him to edit genetic markers and usher in Nova Provenance Elselifeforms.","But his own Provenance Essence had remained blank. It was just Quintessential. It was just Infinite. It had no defined role other than being his.","At this moment, it picked up an identity. It anchored itself to a critical, core human quality.","The quality to dream.","WAA!","Golden blue clouds of raw, conceptual authority erupted from Noah’s skin!","His physical body became completely surrounded by the billowing light. His existence started to become hazy, blurring at the edges as if he were stepping into a reality that had not yet been authored.","Descartes took a sharp step back, his unreadable eyes widening in profound shock.","THE Primordial Paradox and Erwin paused their agonizing flickering, staring at the True Human Emperor with absolute disbelief.","Grand, heavg prompts cascaded down Noah’s vision!","| THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer has attained a level of Maturity.|","|You dream of a better life. You dream of prosperity, and at times, fear drives your dreams. But you are Human, and you are a Dreamer.|","|Your Provenance Essence takes on the identity your existence has selected for it.|","|Capability Unlocked: PROVENANCE DREAMS.|","|At any time of your choosing, you may initiate your Provenance to experience Provenance Dreams. This will form a Provenance Dream Body that can appear anywhere across time and existence as you dream, allowing you to seek out the tools for a better life.|","|A Provenance Dream can last for seconds or for years, but any power, authority, or knowledge you attain within the Dream remains yours even after the Dream has ended.|","|WARNING: This capability narratively approaches weavings similar to extremely unique Provenance Lifeforms and Those Who Remain. Existence loves and loathes such a thing. There may be unknown dangers and restrictions yet to be accounted for.|","|As your Provenance accepts the quality and identity of Dreams, other capabilities are budding as you can exert and utilize your Provenance on your surroundings and on other lifeforms for you to bring forth what you Dream externally in real time. If what you can envision and Dream is grand enough, you could potentially dream your enemies Dead, and existence may just be forced to agree.|","BOOM!","| Much more analysis is being done on your Provenance as details will follow.|","Noah read the prompts as the golden blue clouds swirled around him.","He had just generated a capability that allowed him to project his ambition across time and space. He could dream himself into unfathomable places and time and harvest power without his true body ever taking a single physical step.","He wiped a tear from his cheek, the smile on his face hardening into an expression of unyielding, terrifying resolve.","He wanted to understand his Dream and His Provenance and act upon it!"]},{"number":5670,"title":"Chapter 5670: Chapter 5669: THE Human Dreamer! I","paragraphs":["When an existence fundamentally redefines its own nature, the physical vessel is the last thing to catch up.","The golden blue clouds of raw, conceptual authority billowing from Noah grew infinitely dense. The regal, blood-soaked rags of his crimson gold robes simply burned away into nothingness!","He did not manifest new clothing or armor. He stood in the ruined center of THE Serenaros as a muscular, flawless humanoid figure forged entirely of stellar blue-gold light.","He was technically naked, yet he was clothed entirely in the unbearable brilliance of his own generated Trueness.","Hazy blue-gold clouds wrapped around his limbs and flooded the surrounding air. To the perception of the physical existence, he began to blur. He was becoming imperceivable to the surrounding existence, slipping into a depth of reality that was authored entirely by his own mind!","Descartes stood at the edge of the ruined blood-sea. The old philosopher watched the golden blue clouds expand, his unfathomable eyes analyzing the sheer conceptual weight of the phenomenon.","\"It seems you have made a tremendous advancement,\" Descartes said quietly. \" And found a way.\"","Noah looked at his own glowing hands.","He found a way?","The phrase felt unbearably small. He had found something so unfathomably grander that the established grammar of even the Verses of Dimensionality he had put up himself could not even contain it.","He felt...fundamentally different. The way his neurons fired, the way his 200 Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks processed reality, and even the way the words left his lips had entirely changed.","When he spoke, he felt like his words were... detached, analytical, and heavily burdened by the sudden ability to observe far too many things.","\"A way implies a path that was already there,\" Noah stated, his voice resonating with an eerie, echoing absolute that made the surviving space of the Dimension tremble. \"I did not find a path. I simply...closed my eyes and began to dream.\"","HUUM!","Noah lowered his hands, looking through the golden blue clouds at the scattered ash of the executioner.","\" What is a dream? \" Noah asked, his tone entirely filled with a unique passion","\" A Dream is a biological organism’s desperate attempt to rearrange a hostile reality. A human closes their eyes and constructs a localized simulation. They dream of warmth when they are freezing. They dream of survival when they are being hunted. They dream of prosperity when they have nothing.\"","He took a slow step forward, the stellar blue-gold light of his skin illuminating the ruined dark.","\" But humans fail to achieve their dreams because existence is rigid. The physical continuum does not care about the electrical impulses of a fragile brain. The dream remains trapped inside the skull. The dreamer wakes, and the world is exactly as cruel as it was when they slept.\"","Noah turned his endlessly blue, glowing eyes toward Descartes.","\"I am no longer trapped in a skull. I am THE Human Dreamer. My thoughts are backed by the weight of Quintessence. By the weight of my Provenance. When I close my eyes and construct a simulation, existence does not ignore me. It is forced to listen. It is forced to obey. And because I can exert this Provenance externally... I can do many more things.\"","WAA!","A blinding cascade of prompts rushed into his vision, detailing the exact nature of the authority he had just reasoned into existence!","| Capability Unlocked: THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM.|","| You may exert THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer upon the physical continuum in real time.|","|By weaponizing your generated standing, you may bring forth what you Dream externally. You impose the localized simulation of your mind directly onto the canvas of reality. If the conceptual weight of your Dream exceeds the True standing of your surroundings, existence is forced to agree with the simulation.|","|At the absolute apex of this authority, if your vision is grand enough, you may potentially Dream your enemies dead. If their existence cannot argue with your Trueness, they will simply cease to be.|","Noah read the details of THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM with cold, analytical perfection.","He did not celebrate as he immediately put the authority to the test.","He looked at the empty space above the sea of his own blood.","\"I am looking at THE Sundered Scion, \" Noah continued, his voice grand and devastatingly calm.","\"It is dead. Its components are rotting primeval ash. But in my mind, the white threads of THE Argent Loom are weaving together. The wings are extending. The nine eyes are opening.\"","As he spoke, he focused the absolute weight of his newly identified Provenance on the empty air.","\" Attributes are merely the foundation of the house. They are the stone. They are heavy, and they are real. But a stone does not build a house, and a stone does not execute a king. It requires motion. It requires a hand. Moirai. Mantles. Unique authorities. These are the hands that throw the stone. The Scion was heavier than me. Its basal authority was higher. Yet, it tore itself apart because its truth was fractured. If one holds a truly unique authority, they can ignore the stone entirely. They can make the impossible happen.\"","He raised his glowing blue-gold hand.","\" Like this.\"","BOOM!","Shining in brilliant blue and gold waves, the space above the blood-sea violently distorted!","The abstract simulation in Noah’s mind was forcibly written over the physical reality of the Dimension! A colossal, winged, nine-eyed abomination materialized out of thin air. It looked exactly like the second transformation of THE Sundered Scion, but it was forged entirely from stellar blue-gold Provenance Essence.","It radiated the exact same horrific, oppressive aura as the original architect’s executioner. By all laws of existence and authority, this was a living nightmare. And Noah had simply dreamed it into being.","|THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM is active.|","|You have generated a localized simulation of an unreadable entity.|","|20 Provenance Essence is consumed and held in reserve to sustain the physical manifestation of this Dream.|","Noah activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard and looked at the thing he had just dreamed.","|THE Sundered Scion of Sovereign and Immense (Dream Construct)|","|VERITAS: 62|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 65|","|PONDUS: 65|","The attributes sat heavily in the sixties. The construct was numerically deeper and stronger than Noah himself. But Noah looked at the staggering numbers and felt absolutely nothing. His own power was no longer merely a collection of attributes. The fact that his identity could produce a dream of this magnitude made him so much grander than the numbers could ever express.","He analyzed the glowing blue-gold titan hovering obediently before him.","He knew its shape. He knew its weight. But he did not know the exact weavings of the unknown Provenance Causes it had used to heal itself during the battle.","Noah closed his eyes. He dreamed that he knew.","|You are dreaming of variables you do not know.|","|10 Provenance Essence has been temporarily drained.|","|The authority of your Provenance is actively pulling knowledge from all facets of the continuum to fill the gaps in your simulation. The Records of existence are flowing into your Dream to make it true.|","...!","Noah gasped softly.","He felt the sudden, crushing infusion of raw, ancient information pouring directly into his mind. The fundamental weavings of THE Cause of the Undying Cycle and THE Cause of Conceptual Eradication unspooled across his consciousness. Existence was literally handing him the secrets of the architects simply to ensure his dream remained accurate.","He sighed with a profound sense of marvel!","In the distance, THE Primordial Paradox and Erwin stared at the True Human Emperor as if they were looking at a completely foreign, alien entity!","The sheer absurdity of a being manifesting an executioner that was just killed out of thin air shattered their understanding of paradox entirely.","Even Descartes was silent. The old philosopher watched the blue-gold Scion beat its wings, his unreadable eyes perfectly still.","Noah opened his glowing eyes.","\" Dreams can make many things possible,\" Noah murmured, his voice echoing across the shattered Dimension. \"I am a human. I possess the capacity to imagine an ending.\"","He looked at the ruins of THE Serenaros, and then he looked up at the empty sky, his mind reaching far past the physical borders of the Train.","\" Could I dream of a billion Descendants dying... and it happens?\" Noah asked the quiet dark. \" Could I dream of an Immense One dying... and existence simply agrees?\"","HUUUM!","Noah asked the heavy question, and the unperceivable fabric of reality trembled in response.","He knew the answer. To force existence to agree to the death of an architect, his Provenance of THE Human Dreamer had to become unfathomably grander. He needed more weight. He needed more depth!","But for the first time since he had stepped into the heavy weavings of Dimensionality, the death of Those Who Remain was no longer a theoretical exercise. It was simply... a dream waiting to be had in time.","And everything would happen...in its own time."]},{"number":5671,"title":"Chapter 5671: Chapter 5670: THE Human Dreamer! II","paragraphs":["Deep within THE Provenance Realm of the First Lifeform, far from the churning ruin of THE Serenaros, a secondary body of Noah Osmont stood upon the verdant blue-gold hills. The transformation that had claimed his main body cascaded perfectly across the connection.","The regal crimson robes burned away into nothingness. The physical vessel reformed. He stood on the grass as a flawless, muscular figure of stellar blue-gold light. Hazy blue-gold clouds drifted off his shoulders, blurring his edges into the surrounding reality!","He was not merely a body. He was a localized simulation of a completely unreadable depth.","And because THE Provenance Realm was an extension of his own generated identity, the Realm itself answered his transformation.","The verdant blue-gold hills inhaled!","The grass blades elongated and shifted into vibrant, physical strands of golden blue dreamscape. The river of light flowing at the base of the hills dissolved its liquid properties, turning into a churning current of materialized possibilities and unwritten timelines. The standing stones dotting the orchards restructured themselves, growing into towering, geometric obelisks of crystallized thought.","Up above, the unmoving stars in the sky of the Realm violently fragmented and split into blinding blue-gold suns, matching the newly melted identity of his Provenance Essences. Hazy, vibrant stellar clouds flooded the horizon, turning the sterile sanctuary into an endless, breathing canvas of his own mind!","Noah raised his hands, observing the glowing blue-gold digits against the backdrop.","He did not feel awe as...awe was a product of encountering something larger than oneself. He was currently observing himself, and he found the mechanics perfectly logical!","He felt unique as if he wanted to study himself and existence...and he wanted to articulate it.","He wanted to affirm and articulate all thst he did as he found his transformation and newly budding nature far too unique!","\"I am.\"","I.","He found this letter of his Osmontian Tongue to best describe how he was constantly feeling something new!","He smiled as he began, hoping he wouldn’t grow annoyed with his own new voice as he affirmed and analyzed this reality...and dream.","\"I am standing on the grass ,\" Noah said aloud, his voice devoid of temperature, echoing with a detached, analytical nature. \"I am observing the fundamental particles of this space. They are waiting for a thought. I am...providing the thought.\"","WAA!","The space beside him distorted. Because he was THE Human Dreamer, and because he was within his own sovereign Realm, he did not need to follow the rigid protocols of the outside existence.","He dreamed his opposing manifestations awake.","Two identical figures of stellar blue-gold light stepped out of his hazy silhouette.","On his left stood THE Open Hand. Its edges were soft, radiating a quiet, gathering light. On his right stood THE Closed Crown. Its edges were sharp, radiating a dense, tyrannical gravity.","All of them were Noah. All of them perceived the continuum with the exact same terrifying, detached clarity.","\" We are isolated ,\" THE Open Hand stated smoothly, looking at the sky. \" The environment has been customized. It is the optimal condition for an observation.\"","\"An observation implies we do not already know the outcome,\" THE Closed Crown corrected, its voice entirely flat. \" We are merely confirming the inevitable result of our own architecture.\"","Noah looked at the river of materialized possibilities flowing at the base of the hill.","\"I am observing... the memory of THE Sundered Scion and breaking down the structure of THE Cause of the Undying Cycle. A Provenance Cause is a rigid machine. It executes a single function without the capacity for variation. It is... a command.\"","Noah turned his endlessly blue, glowing eyes toward his own chest.","\" We do not hold Causes. We hold Teloi. A Telos is not a command. It is an aim. It is the destination of a journey. We have 200 Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks, each carrying a grain of our nine aims.\"","\"A command is finite, \" THE Open Hand observed.","\" An aim is infinite,\" THE Closed Crown finished.","...!","Noah raised his right hand.","\"I am exerting THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM upon our own anatomy and isolating the Telos of Chaos. I am projecting it externally. I am dreaming an aim into a physical law.\"","HUUM!","I am! I am! I am!","He continued these affirmations as they anchored him to his reality and dreams!","The blue-gold clouds around Noah thickened.","He simply imposed a simulation of absolute Chaos onto the physical dream-grass ten meters away from him.","|You are utilizing THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM upon your own Teloi.|","|The Osmontian Provenance Telos of Chaos is given external extension.|","The space ten meters away simply unraveled.","The grass forgot how to be grass. The blades turned into liquid light, then into solid geometric shapes of screaming obsidian, and then into a vacuum of silent white cold. The concepts of gravity, time, and molecular cohesion actively argued with each other within a three-meter radius!","It was a phenomenon far grander than a Provenance Cause. A Cause would have simply destroyed the matter. Noah had forced the matter to fundamentally misunderstand its own existence.","\"It is beautiful ,\" THE Open Hand said. \" It is the absence of structure.\"","\"It is inefficient ,\" THE Closed Crown countered. \" It lacks a ruler. We must impose order upon the anomaly to extract value.\"","Noah lowered his hand. The localized Chaos simply ceased to exist, returning to perfect blue-gold dream-grass in an instant.","\" We extract value by understanding the mechanism ,\" Noah stated. \"I am now moving on to... analyzing the human condition. I am looking at why we dream.\"","He waved his hand over the grass again.","\" Humans dream because the present is insufficient,\" Noah continued \" They are cold, therefore they dream of fire. They are dying, therefore they dream of immortality. The dream is a symptom of a flaw.\"","|You are simulating a localized human timeline.|","|2 Provenance Essence is held in reserve.|","Tiny, glowing blue-gold constructs emerged from the soil. They were microscopic simulations of humanity. Noah, THE Open Hand, and THE Closed Crown looked down at them with absolute, terrifying observation.","\" They are born,\" Noah narrated. \" They are looking at the sky. They do not understand the rain. Therefore, they are inventing many things to explain the clouds.\"","\" They seek comfort in subordination,\" THE Closed Crown observed coldly.","\" They are building a shelter, \" THE Open Hand noted. \" They are attempting to protect their fragile biology as they are cooperating. It is an act of preservation.\"","Noah watched the simulation accelerate. The constructs built a city of blue-gold light. They waged a microscopic war. They burned the city to ash.","\" They build because they believe the structure will outlast them,\" Noah said. \" It is a comforting fiction. The structure only outlasts them if they conquer the wind that blows it down. They cannot conquer the wind. They are currently dying in the ash.\"","Noah erased the simulation. The tiny blue-gold ash vanished.","\" They are frightened of the dark, \" Noah concluded. \"I am also a human. I was frightened of the dark. The difference is that I am currently replacing the dark with myself.\"","He looked at the two manifestations standing beside him.","\"A Provenance Cause enforces a rule upon the board, \" Noah said. \" Our Teloi, when fueled by a Dream, rewrite the board entirely. We do not need to hunt for Causes. We can simply dream our Teloi into fundamental forces. We carry 200 Decillion seeds of customized reality.\"","\"We can dream a Telos of Tyranny to force an Immense One to obey,\" THE Closed Crown stated.","\" We can dream a Telos of Harvest to claim the authority of an entire Dimension without shedding blood,\" THE Open Hand added.","Noah looked up at the dozens of suns in the sky of the Realm.","His perception stretched outward, past the boundaries of the blue-gold hills, connecting instantly with his main body in the ruined sea of THE Serenaros. He felt the exact same detachment across both vessels.","He saw the timeline stretching backward to the moment Vakochev failed, and forward to a moment that had not yet been written.","\"I am envisioning an unknown so called Immense One,\" Noah said, his voice entirely devoid of fear, anger, or urgency.","\" They are sitting on their thrones. They are waiting for the executioner to report. The executioner is dead as they will hear nothing.\"","The two manifestations dissolved, fading back into the hazy blue-gold clouds surrounding his pristine body.","Noah Osmont stood alone on the hill.","The transformation was absolute. The human who had feared anything was gone. What remained was a thinking thing, clothed in Quintessence, completely unbound by the rigid weavings of a failing universe.","\"I am closing the experiment and begin to move on to...something even grander. \" Noah said to the quiet air.","...!"]},{"number":5672,"title":"Chapter 5672: Chapter 5671: THE Human Dreamer! III","paragraphs":["He turned his attention away from the microscopic simulations and looked up at his own transforming home.","He turned his endlessly blue eyes inward, pulling the Records of his own existence into the empty air.","WAA!","|THE True Human Emperor|","|VERITAS: 59|","|PROVENANCE: 60|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 51|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 80|","|THE PROVENANCE ESSENCE ECONOMY|","|Total Generated Capacity: 60|","|Currently Consumed: 0|","|Held in Reserve: 20 (Sustaining External Dream Construct)|","|Temporarily Drained: 10 (Knowledge Retrieval)|","|Available for Generation: 30|","He analyzed the numbers without a fraction of pride or disappointment. His attributes had torn through the wall of fifty, his PROVENANCE sitting heavily at sixty. The sheer conceptual weight he carried now ridiculous!","The economy of his new identity was strict, but vast.","\"I have thirty Essences available ,\" Noah stated calmly. \" To dream a new dream into the present requires a heavy allocation of reserve. To dream an anomaly into the future requires an argument with probability. But to dream into the past... the timeline is already cemented. The resistance of existence should be negligible as I am not changing anything. I cannot change anything. The past is set as what has happened will always happpen.\"","He lowered his hands.","\"I will initiate a Provenance Dream. I will observe...a beginning.\"","Noah did not cast an art. He simply lay down on the strands of golden blue dreamscape. He closed his glowing eyes, forcing the physical parameters of the secondary vessel to power down as he went to sleep.","HUUM!","The sixty suns above him dimmed.","From the sleeping, glowing chest of the True Human Emperor, a hazy, translucent silhouette stepped outward. It was THE Provenance Dream Body. It carried no physical density, yet it held the absolute weight of his VERITAS.","Noah looked down at his sleeping form, and then he looked away, asserting his destination.","He simply stopped being in the Realm, and started being somewhere else.","BOOM!","Blinding distortions of existence and time rushed past his perception. He bypassed the white threads of THE Argent Loom. He ignored the ticking hands of the Scales. He descended through the unseen layers of the continuum, pushing through the heavy, rigid weavings of a forgotten Age!","The distortion snapped into absolute stillness.","Noah opened his eyes.","\"It is the year nineteen ninety-seven,\" Noah said, his voice entirely silent to the world around him, heard only by his own mind. \" It is eleven fourteen at night as I am standing in a delivery room in City General Hospital. The room smells heavily of iodine, sweat, and biological exertion.\"","He looked down at his hands. He was wearing faded blue scrubs. He had seamlessly taken on the presence and perception of a male nurse standing in the corner of the room.","Noah looked up.","The room was in a state of controlled chaos. Two doctors and three other nurses rushed around the center bed. Monitors beeped with frantic urgency.","And on the bed, covered in sweat and gripped by absolute physical agony, was his mother.","Amelia Osmont was screaming.","Noah observed the scene with a profound, terrifying detachment...and emotion as he gazed at his mother.","\" My father is not here, \" Noah analyzed, his gaze sweeping the sterile walls. \" He is currently several miles away, consuming alcohol in a dimly lit establishment. He is avoiding responsibility. He is missing the only meaningful event he will ever contribute to.\"","Noah stepped forward, his movements perfectly mimicking the expected routine of a medical assistant.","He looked down at his mother. Her face was pale. Her heart rate was elevated to dangerous levels. The fragility of the human body was on full display.","\" She... is composed of carbon, water, and fragile calcium,\" Noah mused internally. \" A single blow from a something with mana would vaporize her instantly. She possesses no authority. She possesses no Dimensionality. And yet, the exertion she is currently enduring is pushing her physical vessel to its absolute breaking point, all to usher a new life into the cold.\"","A final, piercing cry echoed through the delivery room!","The doctor moved quickly. The chaotic culmination of biology occurred.","A small, bloody, crying infant was brought into the harsh fluorescent light.","Noah looked at the infant. He looked at himself.","\"A human infant that is entirely helpless. It cannot hold up its own head. It cannot regulate its own temperature. It is a biological vulnerability. And yet, this exact configuration of matter will one day tear an executioner of the architects in half. It will author weavings. It will wear the crown of existence.\"","The nurses cleaned the infant rapidly. Amelia fell back against the pillows, panting, tears streaming down her exhausted face. Her arms reached out, trembling with a desperate, overriding instinct.","The doctor placed the wrapped infant into her arms.","Noah stopped moving. He simply watched.","He watched the raw, unadulterated love wash over Amelia’s face. He saw the pain in her body entirely subordinated by the presence of the child. She held the small bundle against her chest, weeping softly, her fragile human existence anchoring itself entirely to the new life.","It was mundane. It was biologically common.","And it was the most unfathomably true thing Noah had ever witnessed.","WAA!","| You are observing the root of your own humanity.|","|You are bearing witness to the unwritten foundation of a Sovereign.|","|VERITAS: 59|","|VERITAS: 60|","|VERITAS: 61|","His Trueness shot up, climbing simply from the act of understanding his own beginning!","The other nurses stepped back to adjust the monitors.","Noah stepped forward. He reached out with hands that had severed the seams of Immense Ones, and he gently took a fresh cloth to help clean the remaining blood from the infant’s brow.","Time passed as the baby was crying. It had just defecated itself. It was the absolute lowest rung of existence.","Noah changed the diaper with methodical, clinical precision.","\"Such a mundane thing ,\" Noah thought, his endless blue eyes locking onto the squalling infant. \"It defecates. It requires constant maintenance. The human potential is a grand, terrifying contradiction. It begins in the dirt, and it ends on a throne.\"","Noah finished wrapping the blanket. He looked up, meeting the exhausted, tear-filled eyes of his mother.","He spoke, using the vocal cords of the nurse, projecting a gentle, practiced warmth.","\"Have you decided on a name, Ma’am?\" Noah asked.","Amelia looked down at the infant. She brushed a thumb across the baby’s soft cheek.","\" He is my comfort ,\" Amelia whispered, her voice cracking with emotion. \" He is my safety in all my times of need. He is my star. He is my peace.\"","She looked back up at the nurse, a tired, beautiful smile breaking across her face.","\" His name will be... Noah. Noah Osmont.\"","HUUM!","The room buzzed with a frequency only the True Human Emperor could hear.","Noah nodded slowly. He stepped back, allowing the mother and child to exist in their quiet, perfect sanctuary.","He activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard. He turned the analytical weight of a Sovereign directly onto the infant version of himself.","|Infant Noah Osmont|","|VERITAS: Blank|","|PROVENANCE: Blank|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: Blank|","Noah stared at the panel.","The stats were entirely blank. The infant was far too weak, far too unformed to hold any measurable values of truth or weight. It was a blank page.","But the POTENTIA was not blank.","Even here, in the sterile light of a hospital room, wrapped in a soiled blanket and completely devoid of authority, his POTENTIA was INFINITE.","Noah stood in the corner of the room, his detached mind accelerating as it processed the sheer magnitude of the paradox.","\" Even when I was just born, my potential was infinite, \" Noah narrated, the hazy blue-gold clouds of his true existence pressing faintly against the edges of the nurse’s body.","He looked at the infant, and the infant seemed to look back, staring blindly into the fluorescent lights.","\"Is this a linear progression ?\" Noah asked himself, \" Was my potential always infinite? Did I possess the capacity the moment I took my first breath?\"","He tilted his head, his endlessly blue eyes analyzing the flow of time.","\" Or is my potential infinite because I am standing here now? Is it infinite because a True Human Emperor has traveled backward across the continuum, observing his own birth, and by the simple act of looking, I have forced existence to overwrite the infant’s future with my present?\"","It was the ultimate closed loop.","A human dreamed of a better life. The human achieved the dream. The dreamer then walked backward to ensure the dream was always the only possible outcome.","\" Am I...the architect of my own beginning? \" Noah asked softly!","...!","The hospital room dissolved into the rapid progression of a cemented timeline.","Noah stood in the hazy, unperceivable form of THE Provenance Dream Body. He did not move through space. He simply allowed time to flow around him, observing the immediate days following his own birth.","He initiated the second cycle of THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis.","While his Dream Body observed the past, his true existence was actively refining the 200 Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks that formed his foundation. He took meticulous care. He did not allow the crushing weight of Existence to bleed into the year nineteen ninety-seven.","He contained the pressure entirely within himself, ensuring he did not alter a single atom of the unfolding reality.","\" My mother is being discharged,\" Noah said calmly, floating beside a rusted sedan in a hospital parking lot.","\" It has only been one day. The healthcare infrastructure of this era operates on a framework of financial extortion. She does not have good insurance. Therefore, she is forced to carry her healing body and her newborn child back to a dilapidated apartment alone.\"","He followed the sedan.","He stood outside the thin, peeling walls of their apartment building. He watched his mother struggle to carry him up three flights of stairs.","Two days later, Erick Osmont returned.","Noah floated outside the apartment window. He observed his father walk through the door, smelling heavily of stale alcohol and cheap smoke. He watched the inevitable collision of two failing human trajectories.","\" You missed it, \" Amelia yelled, her voice heavy with exhaustion and betrayal. \" You missed the birth of your own son!\"","Erick did not apologize. He deflected and he raised his voice to mask his own inadequacy, throwing his hands up in a dismissive, uncaring gesture before walking into the kitchen to find another drink.","Noah analyzed the exchange without a fraction of anger.","\" My father is a coward ,\" Noah mused, his voice echoing only in his own mind. \" He cannot bear the weight of his own life, so he avoids it entirely. He simply doesn’t care.\"","Night fell. The apartment went quiet.","Noah stood in the cramped nursery. He looked down at his infant self sleeping in the small crib.","The door creaked open. Erick Osmont stumbled into the room, holding a half-empty bottle of liquor. The man looked down at the crib as his shoulders shook. Erick fell to his knees, pressing his face against the wooden slats of the crib, and he broke down crying.","Noah observed the tears.","\" Humans engage in destructive behavior,\" Noah noted, his endlessly blue eyes reflecting the pathetic, weeping form of his father.","\" They are unable to stop themselves. They try to change, but they never do. They believe that feeling remorse alters the physics of the damage they cause. They believe that crying makes it okay. It...never does.\"","The years accelerated.","Noah stood in a small living room, his quarks continuously bearing the weight of THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis in the background. The count reached into the trillions.","He watched a toddler version of himself take his first steps. He watched the toddler stumble, fall, and immediately stand back up.","He watched himself speak his very first words.","\"I Am... hungry!\" the toddler demanded.","...!","I Am!","The first words were I Am!","Noah nodded slowly. The absolute foundation of his Osmontian Tongue was present even before he had the capacity to understand it.","The timeline rushed forward. Noah stood in the corner of a cramped, brightly lit preschool office.","A teacher with a concerned expression sat across from his mother. The toddler Noah sat in the corner of the room, completely ignoring the other children, meticulously stacking wooden blocks into towering, solitary structures.","\" He does not talk much, \" the teacher explained gently. \" He prefers to play by himself. He is hyperactive, yet completely withdrawn. We worry his development might be stunted. He is showing early signs of being on the spectrum, Mrs. Osmont. We may need to start him on medications, and I have a pamphlet here...\"","Noah analyzed the teacher. She was applying a crude, early-century psychological framework to a vessel that would eventually hold the weight of Dimensions. She was not wrong based on the data she had. She simply lacked the scale to understand what she was looking at.","Amelia’s face hardened. The exhaustion of working night shifts vanished, replaced by an absolute, fierce protective instinct.","\" No ,\" Amelia said firmly, standing up and taking her son’s small hand. \" He is fine. And I will take care of him.\"","Noah watched them walk out of the office.","\" She defends me against the labels of her own society,\" Noah analyzed. \"It is an illogical defense based entirely on biological devotion. It is profoundly beautiful.\"","His VERITAS continued to climb. His quarks grew unfathomably dense!","He watched himself enter his teenage years.","He observed his first love. He observed the messy, devastating collapse of his first heartbreak. He watched himself fall in love for a second time.","\" Love ,\" Noah stated, floating in the corner of a high school hallway. \" It is a collection of human emotions and chemicals. It is a biological imperative designed to ensure the continuation of the species. It is... very unique.\"","He observed his first time being intimate. He stood in the corner of a dim bedroom, watching the clumsy, nervous exchange of two young humans.","\" An exchange of fluids, elevated heart rates, and extreme neurological vulnerability ,\" Noah observed dryly. \"It is messy. I was incredibly nervous. But it is the mechanism of generation.\"","The years darkened.","Amelia continued to work brutal night shifts to afford their existence. Erick continued to drink.","Noah stood in the kitchen and watched his father strike his teenage self across the face. The younger Noah staggered backward, his lip splitting open.","Noah did not intervene. He could not intervene.","\" He hits me because I do not conform to his shifting moods, \" Noah said, looking at the blood on his younger self’s chin.","\" It is the transfer of kinetic energy from a failing man to a growing one. The strike bruises the flesh. It does not alter my trajectory.\"","The timeline neared its breaking point.","The year was approaching the emergence of Mana. The apocalypse was arriving. Dungeons were preparing to tear through the fabric of his world.","Noah knew what came next. His father and mother would face their initial deaths in this era, erased by the chaotic arrival of a wider universe, before he would bring his mother back years later.","He could handle watching his mother die.","But he chose not to.","\" The emergence of the apocalypse is the emergence of Mana, \" Noah reasoned, his hazy blue-gold form turning away from the doomed timeline. \"It is the start of a simple human becoming something more. The beginning is complete. The rest is already recorded.\"","He looked down at his own translucent hands.","Over the years spent inside this Dream, he had fully completed the second cycle of THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis. All 200 Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks had been refined for a second time. They were unfathomably dense. His entire existence buzzed with a terrifying, contained grandeur.","He decided to end the dream.","WAA!","The timeline collapsed into white static.","Deep within THE Provenance Realm of the First Lifeform, the physical body of the True Human Emperor opened its endlessly blue eyes.","The vessel instantly began to vibrate!","All the conceptual gains, all the unbearable weight accumulated over years of observation within the Provenance Dream, were violently dragged back into the present reality and slammed directly into his physical form!","BOOM!","Stellar brilliant waves of blue-gold light erupted from his skin, wrapping around his muscular figure in a blinding, roaring storm! The suns in the sky of the Realm flared with absolute dominance.","Grand, cascading prompts rushed down his vision!","| The first Provenance Dream has concluded.|","|The second cycle of THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis has been fully completed across all 200 Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks.|","|Your physical vessel has restructured itself to bear the newly generated weight.|","| You have attained the Second Tier of The Provenance Body.|","|THE PROVENANCE DREAM FRAME is forged!|","|Your physical architecture now exists in a state of localized fluidity. You may shift the density of your vessel between the physical continuum and the abstract layers of your own Dreams, rendering blunt force and lower-Dimensional authorities completely useless against your flesh.|","Noah breathed in the grand, seething power of his new Frame. He pulled his Records.","|THE True Human Emperor|","|VERITAS: 70|","|PROVENANCE: 69|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 69|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 95|","His attributes were heavy. His PONDUS had skyrocketed from the successful completion of the second Baryogenesis cycle, and his VERITAS had climbed heavily from the deep, undisturbed observation of his own root humanity.","A final prompt chimed quietly in his mind.","|THE PROVENANCE ESSENCE ECONOMY|","|2 Provenance Essence utilized for the previous Dream are currently exhausted.|","|They will remain unusable and out of your reserve for the next 24 hours until their true weight is regenerated.|","Noah took in the cost. It was a negligible price for the attainment of THE PROVENANCE DREAM FRAME and the vast elevation of his standing.","He stood up on the blue-gold grass. The stellar light wrapping around him settled into a calm, pristine hum.","\"It was a good dream ,\" Noah said quietly into the empty Realm. \" The beginning...is always good to remind ourselves of.\""]},{"number":5673,"title":"Chapter 5673: Chapter 5672: THE Human Dreamer! IV","paragraphs":["Noah stood in the center of his customized reality as he took a slow, deliberate breath. The physical lungs of his stellar blue-gold vessel expanded and contracted, drawing in the heavy, unwritten possibilities of the Realm.","He analyzed his own internal state.","He was human at his core. He possessed the biological and neurological framework of his species. He still felt the chemical imperatives of love, fear, and lust. They were present in his pathways!","But the scale of his perception had fundamentally altered how he experienced them.","He was skeptical of his own emotions. He knew he could feel them, but he questioned if they held the same density as before. Fear was a survival mechanism designed to keep a fragile organism away from predators. But when the organism could simply dream the predator out of existence, fear lost its evolutionary purpose.","Love was a tether to ensure reproduction and social cohesion. But when a single mind could construct and deconstruct Dimensions, the tether felt infinitely thin.","He was a human observing his own humanity from a tremendous, Quintessential altitude.","He sensed the unfathomable depth of his power resting perfectly still within him.","\" Ruination ,\" Noah called out. \" Infiniverse.\"","WAA!","The space before him distorted instantly.","Two figures materialized on the blue-gold grass. Because they were intricately bound to his existence, the violent restructuring of his identity cascaded directly into their physical vessels.","They did not wear the ornate armor or flowing dresses of their previous iterations. They stood before him entirely transformed. Hazy, stellar blue-gold waves of raw dreams surrounded them, acting as their only coverings. The waves of energy and authority wrapped around their curves and limbs, blurring their edges into the surrounding atmosphere exactly like his own.","Noah analyzed the extension of THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer.","\" My authority is extending to you,\" He observed, his endlessly blue eyes scanning their newly forged dream-frames. \" It is transforming your baseline architecture. What is the biggest change you can now sense?\"","THE Infiniverse looked at her own glowing blue-gold hands. Her expression remained serious and fiercely efficient.","\" Master ,\" THE Infiniverse reported. \"The vast architecture of my body has been growing and expanding rapidly. This is accelerating as we perform more Hearthshifts and become the source for an increasing number of lifeforms. But right now, the primary change is conceptual. I feel like an infinite number of possibilities can bloom. I feel like I could pull from your power and simply...\"","She trailed off, her analytical mind struggling to quantify the sheer scale of the potential.","Noah did not ask her to finish the sentence. He raised his glowing hand.","He isolated a single unit from his Held Reserve. He waved his hand, and a dense, blinding sphere of stellar blue-gold Provenance Essence drifted smoothly toward THE Infiniverse.","\" Take it,\" Noah instructed calmly.","THE Infiniverse reached out. The blue-gold sphere sank seamlessly into her chest.","She closed her eyes. She did not calculate as ahe simply began to dream!","HUUM!","The localized space of the Realm began to vibrate violently. THE Infiniverse opened her eyes, and the sheer conceptual weight of her borrowed dream bypassed the unwritten canvas of the environment and manifested externally.","Above them, the sky fractured. A massive, swirling hypercube of deep blue-white light bloomed into existence and began transforming into an Observable Existence!","The heavy, unyielding gravitational pull of a newly born Existence pressed down upon the grass.","She had dreamed the emergence of a complete Observable Existence!","|THE Infiniverse has successfully utilized a borrowed unit of Provenance Essence.|","|A localized dream has been given physical density.|","|An Observable Existence has been generated and nested within her architecture.|","Noah looked at the prompts and nodded slowly. The mechanics were sound!","\" Many more things are possible for us, \" Noah stated.","\" But arriving at this point does not mean we can be lax. It does not grant us permission to rest. Even an authority as grand as this is only ever approaching the type of power that Immense Ones and Provenance Lifeforms have already grasped.\"","He lowered his hand, his endless blue eyes locking onto the two women.","\" We are still young. We are still weak, and we do not know everything. Across the vastness of the continuum, the percentage of reality that a dolphin is aware of, and the percentage that we are aware of, may be statistically the exact same. The expanse is simply that large.\"","He took a slow step forward.","\" Arriving here makes me feel that the mysteries of existence are far too vast and unfathomable. We are a tiny thing in this expanse. Provenance Lifeforms and Immense Ones are just a little bit ahead. We must be careful. But we hold the potential.\"","Noah looked up at the newly formed Observable Existence drifting against the backdrop of brilliance like a miniaturized moon.","\"I am expectant of the future. I am excited for the future. I am fearful of the future,\" Noah analyzed, listing the emotions as data points. \" This is human. But I can dream of a future others cannot even begin to imagine. We can dream of something unbelievable, and we can force it to become our reality. Let us do it steadily, and not stumble too much. Okay?\"","The words were spoken with a terrifying, crushing calmness.","Ruination and THE Infiniverse immediately moved to drop to their knees. The sheer weight of his logic and his authority demanded absolute subordination!","Noah stepped forward and caught them both before their knees could touch the grass.","He did not let them pull away as he pulled them forward, wrapping his glowing arms around their shoulders, drawing them into a deep, physical embrace.","They froze for a fraction of a second, and then they slowly placed their heads against his stellar blue-gold chest.","\"You are the only two existences so intricately connected to me, \" Noah said quietly, his chin resting near the top of Ruination’s hazy blue-gold hair.","\" You can feel my changes and my complexity the most. You can understand me when no others can. My mother is not able to understand me like you can. Nor can my son, or my daughter, or any of the others.\"","He held them firmly against the quiet hum of his generated Trueness.","\" The two of you have access to my very mind. Please, never attempt to bow toward me again, okay ?\"","Ruination and THE Infiniverse lifted their heads slightly. They looked at each other across his chest.","The hazy blue-gold energy surrounding their eyes began to evaporate, condensing into physical, crystalline tears that ran down their glowing cheeks. They smiled, a fierce and absolute devotion radiating from their core architecture, and they hugged THE True Human Emperor tighter!"]},{"number":5674,"title":"Chapter 5674: Chapter 5673: Movement I","paragraphs":["The physical embrace concluded!","Noah analyzed the crystalline tears evaporating from the cheeks of THE Infiniverse and Ruination. They were expressions of absolute devotion, a biological and conceptual byproduct of the deep integration between his Provenance and their architecture.","He stepped back as the hazy blue-gold clouds of his Provenance Dream Frame drifted smoothly around his shoulders.","\" There is a lot to be done,\" Noah stated.","\" Now, we must resume the extraction of value. Infiniverse. Ruination. Proceed in pulling the markers of the Laestrygonians that were extinguished by THE Sleepless Fiend.\"","Ruination wiped her glowing eyes, her demeanor instantly shifting back to sharp efficiency.","\" Understood, Master ,\" Ruination replied, her voice steady. \" We are isolating the remaining markers for their Causes.\"","Noah processed the variables of the puzzle. THE Sleepless Fiend was an architect. We know THE Immense Ones play with Provenance Causes, treating them as foundational building blocks.","So why kill Laestrygonians specifically for their Causes?","An Immense One generates its own unfathomable standing. It does not need to scavenge lower authorities. Therefore, the harvest was not for personal power. It was for raw material.","A predator did not harvest wool to become a sheep. It harvested wool to weave a coat. The architects were using the Causes of the Laestrygonians to build or replace something massive. Perhaps it was the very infrastructure of THE Sundered Scions or something like them, or the white threads of THE Argent Loom? He had no idea.","WAA!","Noah pushed the calculation aside, turning his focus inward to test the absolute limits of THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer.","He pulled up the weavings of his Provenance Essence Economy.","|THE PROVENANCE ESSENCE ECONOMY|","|Total Generated Capacity: 69|","|Currently Consumed: 2 (24-hour regeneration cycle active)|","|Held in Reserve: 20 (Sustaining External Dream Construct)|","|Temporarily Drained: 10 (Knowledge Retrieval)|","|Available for Generation: 37|","\" The cost...is the friction of reality ,\" Noah narrated, his endlessly blue eyes analyzing the blue-gold grass. \" To dream something into the present requires a sustained reserve. To dream and pull knowledge drains the essence temporarily until the data is fully assimilated. But a consumed essence is exhausted entirely.\"","He ran the simulation of his own limits.","The two consumed Essences were dead weight in his panel. They would remain unusable for precisely twenty-four hours until their True weight regenerated.","This was the limitation of the engine. The authority of THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM was absolute, but the fuel was finite. If he attempted to dream an Immense One dead in this exact moment, the conceptual weight of erasing an architect would easily exceed his available thirty-seven Essences.","The Dream would fail not because it was impossible, but because he lacked the capacity to process the execution.","He needed to expand his capacity. He needed to understand the exact anatomy of a genuine Provenance Lifeform!","His mind immediately moved to Thalia.","He considered the Vasiliou Elseworld.","If an Immense One was simply a Provenance Lifeform that had lived so truly that existence could no longer argue with it, then what was the Vasiliou lineage? What could he learn from seeing an entire Elseworld populated by more Provenance Lifeforms?","He analyzed their relationship with Those Who Remain. The Vasiliou hid in an Elseworld. They operated in the shadows, avoiding the direct gaze of the architects. They were sovereign, yet they were cautious. By observing their anatomy and their society, Noah knew he could isolate the exact threshold where a sovereign either capitulated or ascended to become an Immense One. Thalia could be one of the keys to unlocking the true potential of his own Provenance.","He juggled the pieces of the macroscopic board in his mind.","His clones were stationed across the Dimensions. He possessed a vast reservoir of Infinite Sanguine Mana to fuel his Sanguine manifestations.","The entire structure of THE Dimensional Provenance Train was rushing forward through the crossing-dark, carrying its cargo of condemned Dimensions toward an unknown terminus.","\"I must optimize the next allocation ,\" Noah mused aloud.","\"I have thirty-seven Essences available. The next Provenance Dream must yield a strategic advantage that outweighs the twenty-four-hour cooldown.\"","Should he dream his way into the highest archives of the Pax? Should he dream himself into the Vasiliou Elseworld to observe their sovereign generation undetected? Could he?","Or should he look directly at the higher Dimensions of the Train? Or something else entirely?","He looked at THE Infiniverse, who was currently analyzing the newly born Observable Existence she had just dreamed into reality.","\"We will continue the harvest,\" Noah commanded.","\" Continue with the extraction the Laestrygonian markers. Map the trajectory of THE Sleepless Fiend’s actions. And continue the Hearthshifts. I will dream again very soon.\"","HUUM!","The sixty-nine suns above them flared with quiet, unyielding tyranny. Noah stood in the center of his customized reality, perfectly still, calculating the exact cost of overwriting the rest of existence!","---","His vision refocused and recalibrated.","The physical continuum of THE Serenaros Dimension remained a ruined canvas.","Noah stood in the center of the churning sea of his own Infinite Sanguine Mana. His primary vessel processed the exact same sensory data and conceptual weight as the secondary vessel resting within his Realm. The connection was seamless.","He turned his endlessly blue, glowing eyes away from the scattered ash of the executioner and looked toward the edge of the destruction.","Descartes was still feeding his authority to THE Primordial Paradox and Erwin. The old philosopher kept them anchored in a state of simultaneous life and death.","Noah analyzed the old man. He had fought beside him, yet he had never truly quantified him.","He activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard again as this time, there should be no question marks.","WAA!","| Descartes|","|VERITAS: 85|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 65|","|PONDUS: 60|","Noah processed the numbers. The old philosopher possessed a Trueness of eighty-five. It vastly exceeded all of his other attributes. This meant his fundamental identity was so rigidly defined that existence had a remarkably difficult time arguing with his logic. He was a being constructed entirely of undeniable certainty.","Noah floated over the sea of blood. His stellar blue-gold body stopped a few feet away from the philosopher.","\" You possess a Trueness that exceeds my own. Who are you really, Descartes? Do you truly plan to go against Those Who Remain? And what are your aims for the two paradoxes you have claimed as disciples?\"","...!"]},{"number":5675,"title":"Chapter 5675: Chapter 5674: Movement II","paragraphs":["Descartes did not break his concentration on the two flickering figures. He kept his hands raised, his unfathomable eyes fixed on the immediate space before him.","\"I...used to be a caretaker of a Lineage of Provenance Lifeforms,\" Descartes replied.","\"I saw firsthand how Those Who Remain could be when such beings ever sent a wisp of their aura down into the lower realities. It is a crushing, absolute weight.\"","The old philosopher lowered his hands slightly as the flickering of the two students finally stabilized.","\" I know how impossible a rebellion is. I was only a caretaker. But the lowliest things always stand the chance of being the strongest. Erwin here was only a peasant, and look at him now. He drew me the most as his master was also proficient in paradox. Under my guidance, I actually plan to have them become extremely sharp swords of paradox. We will use them to cut across much of what is coming with me.\"","...!","Noah looked at Descartes silently. He gauged the words.","A caretaker raising swords. It was an act of extreme, calculated defiance. He looked at the two paradoxes recovering on the rusted ground. They were biological weapons being forged in real time!","Noah nodded.","\" Existence is vast, and we all have our moving parts ,\" Noah said calmly. \" Your words inadvertently allowed me to arrive at an epiphany earlier. Existence is give and take. Do you want anything from me?\"","...!","Descartes fell entirely silent. He looked at the ruined sky of the Dimensional Cabin. He calculated the weight of his own request against the capability of THE True Human Emperor.","He eventually lowered his gaze.","\" Could you bring me a corpse of a Provenance Lifeform in the next few days, months, or years?\" Descartes asked quietly. \"I have use for it, but I know the ask is a heavy one.\"","BOOM!","The request struck the air with massive conceptual weight!","Why would a philosopher want the corpse of a Sovereign?","It was a highly logical request, even if the procurement of such an item was statistically impossible for nearly any other being.","\"A few days will likely be sufficient ,\" Noah replied, his tone perfectly even. \" Are you heading up or down?\"","He asked Descartes if they would move toward the front or the back of THE Dimensional Provenance Train.","\" We will go down, \" Descartes answered smoothly. \" Our power can paradoxically rise whether we go up or down. But down is a bit more manageable. It was the reason why we came down into this Dimensional Cabin in the first place.\"","Noah nodded.","\" Then I will find you again to give it to you,\" Noah stated. \" It seems we must rush out of here before any dogs start sniffing. \"","...!","Descartes nodded calmly. He stepped back, allowing his two disciples to stand.","Noah looked at THE Primordial Paradox. He extended his glowing blue-gold hand.","The boisterous anomaly stepped forward and met the gesture, and the physical collision of their palms occurred.","Noah analyzed the kinetic transfer. It was a localized human greeting. Previously, he had felt the weight of camaraderie and shared battle during this gesture. Now, he observed the collision of atoms and the social programming of a primate species. It felt entirely different..but as a human, he still felt good having something that could be called friendship!","THE Primordial Paradox seemed to have also sensed this change as he smiled lightly.","Noah lowered his hand and turned his endlessly blue eyes toward Erwin.","\" You are unique, even with our past history,\" Noah said to THE Living Paradox. \" Information is paramount in existence, and you are THE Information Paradox. You have the potential to be grand. That is only if you make the right moves. Good luck.\"","Erwin nodded slowly, his eyes wide as he looked at the terrifying, blurring figure of the True Human Emperor.","Noah did not wait for a response.","He turned his back on the three of them and began to float upward, moving toward the distant, shattered doorway in the sky that led out of THE Serenaros Dimension, towards the forward sections of THE Dimensional Provenance Train!","He looked down at the far corner of the ruined blood-sea. Mahishasura was still kneeling on a floating chunk of rusted metal, bleeding and utterly subdued.","He would be leaving Mahishasura as a biological sensor. This Descendant would remain behind as a tool just to see what arrives here!","Noah reached the upper boundaries of the sky. He did not take an army with him as he took only the massive, hovering Dream Construct of THE Sundered Scion that floated obediently behind his shoulder.","He pushed through the torn fabric of the sky and stepped out into the crushing dark.","---","<Vasiliou Elseworld>","Across the continuum, in a hidden Warren where THE Argent Loom barely reached, his other body was arriving somewhere far more interesting.","The storm of ancient golden light released them.","Noah’s feet settled onto a road of fused white gold, and he looked up, and he began to see wonder.","A city climbed the sky in front of him.","It rose in concentric tiers from a wide golden plain, seven ringed levels stacked one atop the other against the face of a white prominence, each tier walled, each wall gated, each gate offset from the one below it so that no straight line ran from the ground to the summit.","Towers stood along the ring-walls in unhurried intervals.","At the crown of the highest tier, a fortress of massive drum towers and long halls sat heavy and red-gold in the light, its roofs steep, its windows tall and dark, a seat built by beings who understood that the appearance of patience was itself a weapon.","And behind the city, a mountain floated.","It hung in the sky with no chain and no foundation, a golden mountain the size of an Observable Existence!","Power poured off its slopes in slow, continuous falls of stellar blue-gold essence, sheets of it descending for miles before thinning into the air, feeding the plain, feeding the city, feeding the light itself.","The pressure of it reached across the whole valley and pressed gently and endlessly on everything below.","Noah processed the architecture with detached precision.","The city was a fortress, and that was the first anomaly. A Provenance Lifeform generated its own standing and owed nothing to siege or scarcity.","A civilization of such beings did not need ringed walls and offset gates. Walls, for them, were either memory or message.","Either this lineage had once been besieged badly enough to build in stone what they no longer trusted to sovereignty, or the entire city was a statement aimed outward at visitors, a sentence written in fortifications.","It was...showy.","The second anomaly was the count.","His perception swept the tiers, and lifeforms answered it by the thousands.","Thousands.","Signatures burned across every level of the city, moving along the ring-roads, gathered in the courtyards, seated in the long halls, and each one of them was a one with a Provenance!","Not soldiers drawing on a master’s power.","Every single signature generated itself, a self-sustaining sun in miniature, and there were thousands of them arranged in tiers up a mountainside.","He had met three Provenance Lifeforms in his entire existence. Thalia. Rosalia. The scraps of a voice within THE Aurate Collar.","He had reasoned from that scarcity that the species was small in number!","He revised the model without sentiment.","A voice arrived directly inside his mind at this time!","’ Welcome to Vasileia, my Provenance. The Elsecity of my lineage. Every Provenance Lifeform of the Vasiliou line that still exists is somewhere on those tiers right now, and some of them are about to have very strong opinions about you.’","She stood beside him, her hand finding his, and the mental message continued with an edge of dry affection.","’I know how you can be. A bit hard headed. More than a bit tyrannical. You look at a room full of ancient beings and you begin thinking which of them to offend first. So let me take the lead here, just at the start. You defend your women, I know. But I can defend myself. And I can also defend you.’","...!"]},{"number":5676,"title":"Chapter 5676: Chapter 5675: Vasiliou! I","paragraphs":["Noah turned his endlessly blue eyes from the city to the woman holding his hand.","Every measurement he held of Thalia Vasiliou had been taken during a catastrophe. There was the day she fell out of a white pool, bleeding on his grass.","There was the hour her edges flickered, causality collecting its toll. There was the moment she wept because he did not remember her.","All of his data came from her worst hours.","Here, she was home, and whole, and merged!","So he activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard. For the first time since the pool, her existence answered him.","| Thalia Vasiliou|","|VERITAS: 99|","|PROVENANCE: 99|","|POTENTIA: 99|","|PONDUS: 99|","|(Current values are weakened. The toll of movement across Dimensions and Time continues to suppress the True standing of this existence.)|","He read the panel once. Ninety-nine, four times, and beneath the columns a parenthesis stating that the numbers were a floor.","The woman whose hand sat warm in his stood thirty points above him on every axis while actively suppressed. Her true standing lived somewhere he had not yet learned to measure!","He had gotten himself a powerful woman!","He thought of THE TRANSFINITE VERSE and THE INEFFABLE VERSE when he looked at these numbers.","What was one hundred? Was one hundred where the shore ended and the Verse simply began? Did an existence at one hundred stop touching THE INEFFABLE and start standing inside it? Was the woman beside him one point of suppression away from a different order of reality?","He did not know!","Rosalia turned around.","Her unreadable eyes went to their joined hands, to her daughter’s fingers laced through the fingers of a supposed First Tier vessel, and she shook her head once, slowly.","Mothers had performed this motion for as long as daughters had chosen someone they did not approve of. Rosalia performed it too! Then she waved her imperial hand.","WAA!","The road was gone soon after. The three of them became streaks of light, and Noah observed their trajectory with mild interest, because the streaks did not bend toward the climbing tiers of Vasileia or the red-gold fortress at its crown.","They arced past the entire city, toward the mountain behind it.","—","They stood on bare dark stone at the mountain’s foot. Above them, the falls of essence descended without sound.","Ahead, spanning the base of the mountain from end to end, a boundary of solid golden light rose out of the ground in a single sheer curtain, taller than the city’s highest tower, its surface moving with slow internal currents that had not stopped moving since before the rulings were weighed.","Stellar gold trees grew across the approach in quiet groves. Their canopies burned softly with the essence the mountain shed, and the light came down through the branches and lay on the stone in slow-moving patches.","Among the trees, spaced in silent intervals before the boundary, Provenance Lifeforms floated like statues.","There were five of them. There did not need to be more!","Each one hung motionless above the ground, facing outward. Long shining red hair, loose past the shoulders. Armaments of white gold, plate and pauldron and long-hafted glaives, worked plain, without one ornament.","Beneath the armor their bodies burned, a continuous quiet fire of stellar gold Provenance rising off their skin, so that each guard stood inside a low corona of their own generation!","None of them moved. None of them looked at the arrivals. Their eyes remained ahead, on nothing, on everything.","Beside him, the warmth left Thalia’s presence.","\" Mother .\" Her voice was level. \" Why are we at the Provenance Vasiliou Elsemountain? Father and the others should be gathered in the Provenance Tower. That is where the Lineage receives.\"","Rosalia did not even turn around.","\" Very few Provenance Lifeforms can enter the Vasiliou Elsemountain,\" Thalia continued, and her grip on his hand tightened by a measurable degree. \" Even of our own lineage. The boundary admits extremely high Dimensionality, or a unique Provenance, and nothing else. It does not care for names. It does not care for blood.\"","She took one step forward.","\" Are you trying to embarrass us, Mother?\"","Rosalia turned then, without hurry. Her gaze passed over her daughter and settled on Noah.","\" The least he can do,\" Rosalia said, \" is be exceptional enough to enter a mountain.\"","HUUM!","\"If he cannot do even this, then you have already chosen wrong, and it is better that everyone learns it at the door instead of in the hall. I told your Father and the Vasiliou Provenance Elders that I would bring you here. So everyone has gathered here.\"","She gestured at the boundary. A small motion, almost gracious.","\"I sure do hope this will not be the last place your chosen is able to step into. It is only passing through a barrier and entering a mountain. A simple task, surely, for someone who is supposedly a grander choice than an Immense One. Right?\"","...!","Noah listened to all of it with perfect calm.","Rosalia had moved the entire gathering from the Tower to the Elsemountain after her daughter defied her.","A mother, outsourcing her judgment to a mountain!","The theatrics did not interest him.","There was a preschool office, decades ago, on a small blue world that no longer existed in its original form, and he had stood in its corner. A teacher had slid a pamphlet across a desk. A tired woman who worked night shifts closed her hand around a small boy’s hand and said he was fine, and that she would take care of him, and walked him out into the parking lot sunlight.","Noah had watched the stakes on that cheap desk, and they were higher than anything in this valley, because the woman defending the boy had nothing else, and the beings gathered in this mountain had everything and were frightened anyway.","Ceremony was the tax long-lived beings paid one another to avoid saying plain things plainly. He had stopped paying it when he stopped keeping his worth in other people’s accounts. His worth resided in two hundred Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks, and every one of them was presently calm!","What he cared about stood on the other side of the light.","The Elders of an entire Vasiliou Lineage gathered ahead of him, behind a boundary that filtered existence by depth and uniqueness.","Somewhere past it were beings who remembered Ages the Records had forgotten, and the answer to the question he had carried since a matriarch first sneered at his so called First Tier.","What were the sovereign and the architect to each other, truly? Livestock did not receive favors. Rivals did not get harvested. The beings who had lived the answer were waiting inside a mountain to look down at him!","Noah looked at the slow golden currents of the boundary. He was not worried and he was not offended. He was curious!","...!"]},{"number":5677,"title":"Chapter 5677: Chapter 5676: Vasiliou! II","paragraphs":["The massive golden boundary of light separated the exterior reality from the interior immensity of the Vasiliou Elsemountain.","\" Each of you must cross with your own power,\" Rosalia declared, her voice slicing through the heavy air as dense golden light spilled from the peaks above.","\" Your own Provenance must prove your weight.\"","Thalia’s Vasiliou Bloodline boiled as she seemed about to erupt, her pristine features tightening in sheer defiance!","Noah observed the spike in her biological and conceptual aggression. He made no objection to her anger, merely raising his hand to gently squeeze hers.","\" Go ahead ,\" Noah said.","Thalia looked at him before she stepped forward as the golden boundary actively resisted! It was an arduous, crushing weight as vibrant waves of her own golden Provenance flared brilliantly to push back against the rigid laws of the Elsemountain.","She tore through the light, stepping onto the grass on the other side as she breathed hard, her chest heaving as she glared back at her mother.","In the next nanosecond, Rosalia stepped through without a fraction of a delay or effort as the barrier simply parted for her.","Noah looked at the older woman. His Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard returned only a wall of question marks. He knew he could exert THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM to pull her information from the continuum, but it would require a temporary drain of his Essence. He evaluated the exchange rate and determined the knowledge was currently unnecessary.","He stepped forward.","He did not brace for impact or flare an aura. He simply closed his glowing blue eyes and exerted THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer upon the localized weavings of the boundary.","He dictated that the golden barrier was not a rigid law of reality. He dictated that it was merely a dream, and he was the dreamer walking through it!","WAA!","|THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM is active.|","|2 Provenance Essence is held in reserve to overwrite the reality of the Vasiliou Boundary.|","|You are passing through the simulation.|","Noah walked through the empty air as if the golden light did not even exist! He stepped onto the pristine grass beside Thalia, and he ceased the exertion.","|The alteration of reality is released.|","|2 Provenance Essence is returned from reserve and ready for usage again.|","...!","The silent shock on Rosalia’s face was absolute as she stared at THE True Human Emperor!","Noah looked toward her and nodded.","\"I thank mother-in-law for the test of my worth on this mountain,\" Noah stated, his tone polite but echoing with a mocking, absolute-zero certainty.","\"I hope you do not take this as a challenge and are more reasonable towards the lifeform your daughter chose. Because just maybe, her words of me being better than an Immense One, for her at least... they may hold some truth.\"","...!","Thalia inhaled sharply in shock as Noah boldly wrapped his stellar blue-gold arm around her waist, anchoring the vastness of the moment to the small, true warmth of her body.","He began walking forward, leaving Rosalia behind as the older woman’s eyes shone brilliantly! She looked at his back, and Noah could see her mind genuinely reevaluating the terrifying anomaly walking beside her daughter!","Would she actually be reasonable?","Thalia looked up into his endlessly blue eyes, her own filled with a mixture of worry and absolute alarm as she transmitted her voice solely for him to hear.","\" You... you didn’t already unlock the identity of your Provenance, right? That would also be happening much earlier!\"","It was a heavy question, and Noah processed its weight perfectly. He permitted a smile to break across his clinical features in silent affirmation as he looked ahead.","He had to look ahead.","Multiple terrifying gazes from different elevations of the mountain had already begun to lock onto them!","This was a glorious, unfathomable scene! Atop massive golden pillars carved directly into the slopes of the Elsemountain, Vasiliou Provenance Lifeforms could be seen sitting or floating in absolute majesty!","Each one pulsed with golden waves of Provenance that swirled around them like miniature galaxies!","Noah felt a tremendous, crushing pressure descending from one pillar in particular.","He looked up and observed a man with a crimson goatee and wild red hair floating atop the highest gold pillar, looking down at him with an authority that sought to flatten reality itself.","Noah processed the genetic markers and the spatial positioning, assuming immediately that this was Thalia’s father.","He kept his hand firmly around Thalia’s waist. He looked up at these apex predators, knowing with absolute certainty that none of them would show anything but question marks to his current Weavings, but he stood his ground! He was a localized simulation of an unreadable depth!","He felt Thalia steadying against his side. Her face became entirely firm as her own Provenance began to buzz with a vibrant, dangerous frequency. She looked up at the dozen powerful Provenance Lifeforms governing this mountain as Rosalia materialized on the golden pillar directly behind the man with the crimson goatee.","Thalia’s voice erupted, grand and explosive, echoing across the entire Vasiliou Elsemountain!","\" Father, Mother, Elders,\" Thalia declared, her words rolling with supreme confidence. \" I greet you on this grand day because I have found my other half. I also greet you to bring the news that my Provenance has shown me glimpses of the future. The future that Those Who Remain never like others glimpsing, as they curse many who even have the capability.\"","...!","Noah’s endlessly blue eyes pulsed briefly. He thought of Ulf.","\"I have seen glimpses of multiple futures,\"","Thalia continued vibrantly, her conviction absolute as her golden aura flared. \" And any future where our cultivated Provenance, where my Provenance...is given to an Immense One, leads to our degradation and decimation!\"","...!","The words struck the golden pillars like thunder!","\"So I have taken it upon myself to change this,\" Thalia roared.","\"I stand here today to say that for the Provenance of the Vasiliou Lineage to prosper, we do not need to have the favor of an Immense One... we need to birth an Immense One among us!\"","BOOM!","The declaration shattered the heavy silence of the mountain!","Noah’s eyes shone with a dreamy, terrifying brilliance as he looked at the woman leaning against his side. She was navigating the rigid codes of her lineage with the exact same tyrannical ambition he possessed.","Truly, she was capable!","Seeing her like this made his own weavings surge as his own emotional and tyrannical side seemed to flare up from its slumber!"]},{"number":5678,"title":"Chapter 5678: Chapter 5677: Introduce Myself!","paragraphs":["The vibrations of Thalia’s explosive declaration struck the massive golden pillars of the Vasiliou Elsemountain!","Noah stood flawlessly beside her as he thought about the conceptual weight of the shocking statements Thalia had just made.","The birth of an Immense One!","Was such a thing so easy to do?","He was a human who dreamed of rewriting the board as this dream she just mentioned was a grand one, but damn!","As her golden aura flared brilliantly, the environment of the Elsemountain reacted! The golden waves of Provenance swirling around the massive pillars stagnated and slowed.","Noah observed the twelve Vasiliou Provenance Lifeforms positioned above them.","The gaze of Rosalia Vasiliou lost its sharp edge and became deeply somber as she looked at the man beside her and the other Provenance Lifeforms. They exchanged glances that carried the heavy, crushing weight of a shared and terrible secret. They looked at Thalia as if they knew something fundamental about the architecture of reality that she did not.","At the apex of the highest golden pillar, Thalia’s father actually lost his hardened, tyrannical expression. The man with the crimson goatee and wild red hair stared down at his daughter as if staring at someone much younger who had made a catastrophic mistake without even realizing it.","\" My dear daughter ,\" the Vasiliou Patriarch said imposingly as his voice held the sorrowful weight of entire extinguished timelines.","\" You are the very light of my existence, but you are young, so you do not know. It is expected that you do not know. Even among the elders here, and the vast majority of existence do not know, but... the path towards becoming an Immense One is closed off. Shattered and broken.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed! The path was closed!","\" The last person to confirm this was none other than the one who had laid out his scales across existence,\" her father continued, the golden light around him dimming with the sheer gravity of his words.","\" Vakochev was the last and final confirmation of what many Provenance Lineages had already known. The Immense Ones that are here now are the only Immense Ones there will ever be. They made sure of this.\"","BOOM!","The words were ridiculously heavy as an immense silence settled over the mountain!","Noah felt the woman beside him tensing up as her biological and conceptual pathways buzzed.","He looked at the ancient sovereigns floating on their pillars. To them, this was a tragic, undeniable law of existence!","To him, they were merely biological structures operating on outdated code. They were not his seniors!","He raised his head and looked at the Provenance Lifeforms.","\" Forgive me for intruding here ,\" Noah stated, his voice booming out and echoing with absolute power that cut through the somber atmosphere without a fraction of heat.","\" But we are Provenance Lifeforms. If any path was shattered, so what? I have not been a Provenance Lifeform for long, but the one singular thing I have come to understand is the fact that we generate our own weavings of existence. We decide what our existence is capable of or not. If any path is shattered, it does not really matter to us. We simply continue on forging our own paths.\"","...!","Noah delivered the explosive words with chilling, immovable certainty!","The moment his words finished, all twelve Provenance Lifeforms instantly rose up from their golden pillars!","WUU!","An immense weaving of suffocation and terrifying immensity began to permeate over everything as their sovereign authorities crashed together!","Noah permitted a faint smile to form on his clinical features. It was a mechanical expression of absolute tyranny. He knew exactly why they were reacting with such overwhelming force.","He had purposefully said something that he was curious about and wanted to confirm.","He had stated that he had not been a Provenance Lifeform for long . This made it extremely clear that, not long ago, he was something else. He was probing them to understand whether what he did was considered statistically impossible by the standards of genuine sovereigns. Based on how all of them had risen at this exact moment, he had his answer.","Rosalia Vasiliou stared down at him with a heavy, disbelieving gaze as the golden barrier behind them hummed violently!","\" Are you saying something as outlandish as the fact that you were another form of life in the past, and you simply became a Provenance Lifeform?\" Rosalia asked, her voice tight with unfathomable somberness. \" You were not born one?\"","...!","Was it truly something so unique?","Noah was even more curious now. He felt his woman tensing beside him.","Noah looked around innocently. The innocence was a calculated, mocking facade covering a tyrant who possessed the unending reserves of Infinite Sanguine Mana.","\" What reason have I to lie?\" Noah reasoned aloud, his detached attitude rolling over the ancient beings!","\"I have no lineage of Provenance Lifeforms behind me. I have myself because I generated myself and my own immensity. I am THE True Human Emperor. I Am THE Human Dreamer. I have taken Thalia Vasiliou as my woman here as I came here today to introduce myself for those of you that do not know me. It is nice to finally meet you, Father-in-law and Mother-in-law, and the elders of the Vasiliou Elseworld.\"","He stepped forward, his stellar blue-gold body glowing with an unyielding, macro-scale dominance that refused to acknowledge their superiority!","\"I am Noah Osmont, and I am burdened by glorious purpose.\"","BOOM!","The twelve Vasiliou Elders became utterly quiet!","Their collective immensity stalled as they looked at the True Human Emperor gravely! Noah gazed back at them, analyzing their silence. They had assumed he was an arrogant thing. Now, they were running simulations of an anomaly they couldn’t quite place!","The man with the crimson goatee exchanged a heavy, silent communication with the other Elders atop the massive golden pillars. He then turned his crushing gaze toward his daughter.","\" Thalia, go with your mother and the other Elders to prepare, \" her father commanded imposingly. \"I will converse with the one who is burdened by glorious purpose.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5679,"title":"Chapter 5679: Chapter 5678: Atlas! I","paragraphs":["Thalia hesitated. Her golden aura spiked defensively as Rosalia floated over, placing a pale hand on her daughter’s shoulder.","The Patriarch clenched his fist! He descended from his golden pillar as a massive golden doorway tore open on the mountain grounds directly where Noah and Thalia stood!","Heavy steam instantly released from the fracture. It was a blistering, conceptual heat that could scorch anything below fifty attributes to absolute ash! The Patriarch stood beside the doorway and motioned toward it, demanding the human to enter.","Noah looked at Thalia.","\"I should be okay ,\" Noah stated. \" We will just go talk.\"","He did not wait for her to object as he stepped forward and walked through the scorching doorway fearlessly as behind him, Thalia’s eyes shone with absolute conviction!","Noah appeared in a localized pocket of extreme conceptual density.","It was a type of primordial spring filled with scorching steam! Golden waters bubbled violently like liquid lava, glistening with raw Provenance! As Noah looked around, he felt tremendous power radiating from the environment. He looked through the clear golden waters and saw dozens of pristine golden skeletons resting at the bottom!","The Patriarch came through the doorway. His ornate robes fell away, replaced by a simple white towel wrapped around his waist. He walked directly into the blistering spring, revealing a towering, wildly muscular figure scarred by epochs of conflict.","He sat down grandly as the golden lava washed over his chest.","He relaxed back against the rocky edge as heavy waves of steam spilled out and closed his eyes.","\" What are you doing?\" The Patriarch’s voice boomed out. \" Get in, my supposed son in law.\"","Noah did not delay. He gazed at the ancient skeletons down below as he took on the full, unbothered majesty of THE PROVENANCE DREAM FRAME. His stellar blue-gold body glowed with absolute authority as he stepped into the liquid gold.","Cascading prompts immediately flooded his vision!","| You have entered THE Vasiliou Primordial Spring.|","|The pristine golden skeletons below are the remnants of extremely powerful Provenance Lifeforms of the Vasiliou Lineage.|","|Any entity possessing attributes below 50 will be scorched out of existence.|","|Bathing in these waters allows one to steadily raise their attributes by a maximum of 5 in all areas.|","Noah felt the burning liquid attempt to invade his pathways. It was a massive transfer of thermal and conceptual energy. He assimilated it flawlessly. He felt nothing but the biological data of rising temperature.","Ahead of him, the Patriarch opened his eyes.","\"I am Aurelius Vasiliou ,\" the man introduced himself, his voice holding the crushing weight of a sovereign.","\"I am the current arbiter of the Vasiliou Provenance. I am burdened with my own glorious purpose. But it does not matter. You have said some interesting things regarding your origins. You may not even understand what it actually means to say that you were not born a Provenance Lifeform.\"","Aurelius leaned forward as his crimson goatee glistened with golden steam.","\" Have you heard of Atlas?\"","Noah observed the golden liquid. He saw prompts detailing his attributes slowly beginning to rise while within the spring.","|VERITAS is increasing.|","|PONDUS is increasing.|","\" No ,\" Noah replied, his tone perfectly flat and devoid of awe. \"I do not know of any Atlas.\"","Aurelius exhaled a breath of heavy golden vapor.","\" Atlas was a Provenance Lifeform who engineered, invented, and built impossibilities,\" Aurelius detailed, his words constructing a terrifying visage within the misty cavern.","\" Even though he was not one of Those Who Remain, he moved around them as equals. He engineered the very concept of Elsedimensions. He invented the art of cultivating tiers of Provenance Bodies and many other arts. He forged weapons that could extinguish Provenance Lifeforms with a single swing!\"","The Patriarch’s eyes locked onto Noah with blazing intensity!","\" Through his ingenuity and absolute inventions, he was even able to aid an existence to become an Immense One. But the most unique thing about this being was that he held no lineage of Provenance Lifeforms behind him. He was completely alone. The one secret that was known across the highest echelons of reality was that he was not born a Provenance Lifeform. He left behind many things as they can be found in Elseworlds that no Immense Ones can enter.\"","Noah processed the data. A sovereign engineer who built the foundations of modern existence and challenged the architects!","He was analyzing the historical weight of a being who defied the rigid code of the continuum.","\" Where did he go?\" Noah asked calmly.","Aurelius let out a harsh, booming laugh that shook the cavern!","\" He never went anywhere,\" Aurelius replied grandly. \" He was too illustrious and grand. Multiple Immense Ones used their absolute power to snuff out his brilliance and his existence entirely! But that was a lifeform that was not born a Provenance Lifeform and instead became one. One of the last things that he left behind was a message.\"","The golden waters bubbled violently as the Patriarch recited the ancient words!","\" A cryptic message. He said... Existence is grander and more illustrious than all of you imagine! And when someone like me arises in the future, find and grasp what I left behind! And you can see and share just how illustrious existence is, as I never got the chance to. Find My Provenance!\"","BOOM!","The scorching steam of the Vasiliou Primordial Spring rolled across the rocky ceiling.","Aurelius Vasiliou sat in the bubbling golden lava. The declaration regarding Atlas hung in the heavy atmosphere as the Patriarch did not pause to allow the weight to settle. He pressed forward, his voice echoing with absolute, terrifying grandeur.","\" Atlas was an anomaly that defied the strict architecture of the architects ,\" Aurelius boomed, the golden waters thrashing against his massive chest.","\" He was known to be the one who gazed upon IT. There are even hidden Records within the deepest Elseworlds suggesting he was the one who designed IT.\"","BOOM!","Atlas, a grand lifeform whose existence was decimated by Immense Ones...may have been the one who engineered IT?"]},{"number":5680,"title":"Chapter 5680: Chapter 5679: Atlas! II","paragraphs":["\" Many Provenance Lineages across existence scour his Elsedimensions for what he left behind,\" Aurelius continued vibrantly, his eyes burning with ancient ambition.","\" And many are entirely unsuccessful. It was theorized by our oldest predecessors that it has to be someone exactly like him. It must be someone who was not born a Provenance Lifeform, but became one. Only a being with that specific, impossible trajectory could find what he left behind.\"","The Patriarch locked his crushing gaze onto the stellar blue-gold figure of THE True Human Emperor.","\" If you truly are someone like that, or if you hold even a fraction of a possibility of it, I can use my connections to hold off the Immense One that we made an agreement with many, many years ago. You have ruined my agreement and disrupted my Lineage today. I want something in return. If you can find any weavings or components of what Atlas left behind, it may be enough to give my lineage sufficient power to stand by ourselves. We are both burdened with glorious purpose. Let us see what we can put our purpose to use for.\"","WAA!","|VERITAS has increased by 1.|","|PONDUS has increased by 1.|","Noah observed the prompts materializing in his vision. The biological and conceptual heat of the spring was steadily overwriting his baseline architecture.","He evaluated the proposition. It was a transactional exchange of sovereign weight!","The Vasiliou Patriarch offered existential and temporal shielding, and Noah was required to offer salvage from a dead engineer.","He looked at the towering, scarred man sitting in the golden lava. He did not feel intimidated by the volume of the Patriarch’s voice or the immensity of his aura. He was a tyrant sitting in another man’s throne room, completely unbothered by the owner.","\" That is an interesting story ,\" Noah said. \" Your agreement was flawed because it relied on subordination. I do not subordinate. But I am also curious about many things.\"","Noah tilted his head, his endlessly blue eyes analyzing the pristine golden skeletons resting at the bottom of the spring.","\"Are Immense Lifeforms all such dicks?\" Noah asked clinically, delivering the profanity with absolute zero temperature!","\" And why are they also called Those Who Remain? If they remained, they remained from what? Were there others who left? If they left to go, where? How many Provenance Lineages are there, and just what is the exact nature of their relationships with Those Who Remain?\"","BOOM!","The questions struck the depths of the Vasiliou Elsemountain with staggering conceptual weight.","Aurelius stared at the anomaly before him. The Patriarch let out a harsh, booming laugh that caused the liquid gold to erupt in massive, scalding geysers.","\" Are they all such dicks ? \" Aurelius repeated, his laughter echoing like thunder. \" Power at that scale requires the absolute consumption of competing truths. They do not view reality the way we do.\"","The Patriarch leaned forward as the golden lava cascaded down his heavily scarred chest, his voice dropping into a register of terrifying, ancient history.","\"To understand them, you must understand THE First Sundering. There was an era before this current continuum. It was a vast expanse where lifeforms reached an apex and came to grand and unfathomable realizations. The strongest among them exceeded any known Dimensionality. They shattered the highest boundaries of their existence as they became beings we can only imagine.\"","Aurelius raised a massive, dripping hand and pointed toward the ceiling of the cavern.","\" The apex lifeforms who failed to exceed themselves in that grand Era, the ones who were too weak or unable to do what others like them did... They are Those Who Remain. Because they failed to attain power others like them in that era grasped. And after that era, it was an impossibility to grasp that power again. So many of them...dont particularly have good natures as they are effectively beings that failed. Many actually dont like the name ’Those Who Remain’ as they called themsleves Immense Ones. They have done many things since then. They locked the door behind the others to ensure no one else could ever exceed them. They built the rigid codes. They treat the continuum as...theirs.\"","Noah listened with shining eyes as many gaps in knowledge filled themsleves!","\"As for the Lineages ,\" Aurelius declared grandly, his golden aura pulsing with a mixture of sorrow and defiance. \"There are approximately three hundred and forty-two recognized Provenance Lineages across the expanse. And our relationship with them is complex and highly fractured.\"","The golden waters thrashed violently as the Patriarch stood up, revealing his towering, muscular frame burning with apex authority.","\" Some of the Immense Ones actually stemmed from certain ancient Lineages ,\"","Aurelius explained, his eyes locking onto Noah. \" They maintain a twisted, elevated patronage over their people. Others treat Lineages entirely like playthings. They harvest our unspent Provenance and claim our sons and daughters to use whenever they require raw material. Some cull us to ensure we never generate enough combined weight to challenge their thrones.\"","Aurelius took a heavy step through the golden lava.","\" And a rare few Lineages are treated almost as peers. They sit on a terrifying knife’s edge of mutual benefit, balancing their own unfathomable authority against the architects in a silent war of borders. We are navigating an ecosystem designed to keep us contained. In The Elsedimensions, we live...and we are contained.\"","HUUM!","The Vasiliou Patriarch stood entirely exposed in the blinding golden steam, his chest heaving as the raw, unfiltered truth of existence flooded the cavern.","Noah sat perfectly still in the bubbling lava. He looked at the exact count of three hundred and forty-two Lineages. He looked at the concept of the First Sundering. He looked at the locked door of existence.","He identified a human emotion rising within his pathways. It was an absolute, cold ambition!","’They locked the door now, did they? ’ Noah thought quietly to himself, his endlessly blue eyes looking past the Patriarch and into the unwritten future. ’It would merely be a door that I am going to break down!’","BOOM!"]},{"number":5681,"title":"Chapter 5681: Chapter 5680: Rewrite!","paragraphs":["<THE Dimensional Provenance Train>","The atmosphere within a particular Dimensional Cabin of the Train was heavy enough to crush the spines of ordinary Primevals.","It was a sprawling expanse of jagged obsidian peaks and swirling violet clouds as the very air hummed with a terrifying, suffocating weight!","At the apex of the highest hill stood a figure draped in pristine shadows, his presence warping the local existence as if reality itself was bending the knee.","This was the Vessel of THE Sealed One!","He stood with his hands clasped behind his back as he looked out over the dark horizon of the cabin. A mesmerizing, purple gold light flickered across his fingertips.","\" My future self seems to have already gotten things started as a portion of ITS capabilities have traversed back to me here, \" THE Sealed One murmured, his voice a charismatic, echoing symphony that carried the undeniable gravity of a grand being.","\" The capability to rewrite existence itself... is unfathomably unique.\"","...!","Behind him, figures of absolute calamity rested upon the jagged rocks!","These were not ordinary lifeforms. Standing in the back was the terrifying entity holding the Mantle of THE Assassin, a being whose very shadow seemed to devour the light around him as he stood with absolute, lethal stillness.","Beside him rested the holder of the Mantle of THE Culling Blade, a towering woman wielding a rusted executioner’s sword as her eyes burned with the weight of shattered Dimensions!","Dozens of other terrifying Descendants populated the hill, each one radiating a sovereign authority that could drown entire realms in blood.","Yet as THE Sealed One spoke, these apex predators did not radiate hostility. They looked towards the shadow-draped figure calmly, and some even wore expressions of warm, absolute devotion!","THE Sealed One turned his head slightly, his unseen eyes sweeping over the gathered weapons of mass destruction.","\" How do you all see me as?\" THE Sealed One asked smoothly.","The holder of the Mantle of THE Culling Blade blinked, a genuine smile breaking across her scarred features as she rested her massive weapon on her shoulder.","\" Master, what are you talking about?\" THE Culling Blade asked, her voice filled with absolute loyalty as she took a step forward.","\" We have been by your side for ages. You saved me eons ago. I would have been reduced to ash if you had not offered me your hand.\"","THE Assassin nodded smoothly, his shadowy form bowing in deep reverence.","\" You forged us into what we are today,\" THE Assassin added, his voice holding the unwavering conviction of a zealot. \" You granted us purpose when existence offered us only ruin. We are your blades, Master. We always have been.\"","WAA!","This was power!","This was a terrifying, absolute violation of the Records! Of the very memories and weavings of Existence!","There was no battle that THE Sealed One had against them.There had been no fight. He had only looked at them!","These powerful lifeforms had their entire histories, memories, and conceptual architectures completely rewritten to see this being as their eternal master, and they did not even know it! Their loyalty was not coerced through fear or bound by contracts. It was forged into the very foundation of their Trueness!","To them, the fabricated memories were the only undeniable reality they had ever known!","THE Sealed One looked at their warm smiles and turned his gaze back to the violet clouds.","His charismatic exterior masked a mind calculating the exact parameters of this horrific capability. The power to rewrite the Records of a lifeform was absolute, but it possessed a specific, highly logical limitation. The only true defense against this capability was if a being possessed the backing of many Causes!","A high density of unspent Causes acted as a conceptual anchor. If he attempted to rewrite a lifeform dripping with Causes, the sheer weight of their anchor would cause massive resistance to the alteration, slowing down the rewrite and potentially alerting the target to the invasion of their existence. But for those lacking sufficient weight, the assimilation was flawless!","His thoughts drifted towards a specific anomaly who should be within this same Train.","Initially, a vessel like Osmont was critical, but he was not deemed an absolute necessity. Yet, the purple gold light flickering across THE Sealed One’s fingers carried a mandate directly from the unbroken timeline ahead of them. His future self had sent the knowledge that out of all lifeforms across the vast expanse, Osmont had to have his existence rewritten.","He had to be made a subordinate.","If left unbound, the trajectory of THE True Human Emperor would become something entirely uncontrollable.","THE Sealed One released a slow, heavy sigh as the sound echoed like a death knell across the obsidian peaks.","He turned his full attention back to the smiling, terrifying apex predators that now existed solely to execute his will. He looked at the flawless weapons he had stolen from the continuum.","\" Spread out across the train,\" THE Sealed One commanded. \" Find me Osmont.\"","...!!!","---","<THE Epigraph of the Hollow Devotion>","There is a story recorded in the deepest, forgotten layers of existence.","It is the story of a brilliant Provenance Lifeform and THE Immense One who desired her.","She was The Weaver of the Silver Rivers. She had cultivated her own truth, generating a sovereign light that refused to bow to the rigid codes of the continuum.","He was THE Architect of the Chained Sky. He looked down from his throne and demanded she stand by his side.","She refused him. Her authority was her own, and she would not subordinate her Weavings to another.","He pursued her again. He offered her rule over thousands of Dimensions and the authority to judge lower lifeforms. She denied him, keeping her eyes fixed on her own path.","He pursued her a third time. He threatened to scorch her entire lineage into ash. She still refused him, choosing the purity of her own Provenance over the safety of a cage.","THE Immense One grew tired. His unfathomable patience fractured. He realized that a sovereign truth could not be coerced through wealth or fear, so he chose the only path remaining to an absolute tyrant. He simply reached into the Records and unmade her truth.","He rewrote her existence.","He altered the foundational ink of her being, erasing her defiance and replacing it with fabricated devotion.","When The Weaver of the Silver Rivers opened her eyes the next day, the defiant spark was gone. Her eyes were filled with absolute, unwavering infatuation. She flew into his arms. She praised his immensity. She offered herself to him completely, declaring that she had loved him since the dawn of time!","He finally had her. He could do exactly as he wished with her mind and her vessel.","But as the epochs passed, the Architect grew bored. The woman sleeping in his arms no longer held the blinding, sovereign light that had drawn his gaze in the first place. She was no longer herself. She was merely an echo of his own power. She was a hollow puppet wearing the skin of a sovereign.","In a fit of terrifying, absolute anger, he closed his hand and collapsed her entire existence into ash!","As her golden blood stained his pristine throne, THE Immense One looked down at the ruin and asked a question to the empty expanse.","\" Why did she have to reject me? Why did she make me rewrite existence to be with her?\"","This is the tragic, terrifying lesson of the highest authorities. The power to rewrite the Records is the ultimate tyranny. It grants unquestioned loyalty, but it fundamentally destroys the Trueness of the subject. It creates an existence of smiling, hollow reflections."]},{"number":5682,"title":"Chapter 5682: Chapter 5681: Men and Sovereigns! I","paragraphs":["<THE Shared Sky>","Existence was a terrifying, unfathomable expanse!","To forge one’s own Provenance was to declare a singular truth against an existence of competing realities as one stood completely alone in the crushing dark.","A sovereign lifeform could stand alone. They could generate their own immensity and hold back the heavy, rigid laws of existence with their own two hands. This was the nature of an apex predator as it was the path of absolute, unyielding authority!","But a singular pillar had to bear the entire weight of a collapsing sky!","When Those Who Remain looked down from their pristine thrones, they searched for the solitary anomalies. They isolated them and they crushed them because a lone truth was always easier to overwrite than a woven grandeur of sovereign wills. A single light in the dark merely invited the shadows to converge upon it.","There was a profound, glorious strength in shared existence!","To walk beside another Provenance Lifeform was not a dilution of authority as it was an exponential multiplication of Trueness! When two absolute realities intertwined, they did not erase each other. They created a localized continuum that the architects could not simply snuff out with a single thought. They anchored each other to the physical and conceptual planes as their combined weight forced the surrounding existence to bend to their collective will.","Doing everything alone was more than possible for a being burdened by glorious purpose. A solitary sovereign could conquer a Dimension and slaughter their enemies without relying on a single outside variable.","But existence was always easier to face when a lifeform did not have to hold up the heavy sky by themselves.","A tyrant could conquer a timeline alone, but a true Emperor built a court of apex predators to conquer the unknown!","A single sun could only illuminate so much before existence suffocated its light.","But constellations working together could rewrite the entire night sky!","—","<THE True Human Emperor>","The spring did its work without asking permission, and Noah let it!","Scorching golden essence pressed against his stellar blue-gold frame from every direction as prompts ticked pleasantly at the edge of his vision.","|VERITAS is increasing.|","|PONDUS is increasing.|","Free attributes, ancient secrets, and a scarred Patriarch marinating across from him with Ages of answers behind his teeth.","Noah settled deeper into the bubbling lava with the satisfaction of a man who had walked into a hostile mountain and found a buffet, and he decided to enjoy every course of it.","\" You said you can hold off the Immense One,\" Noah began. \" Before I weigh that offer, I want its other half. What exactly would the one I have taken Thalia from do?\"","Aurelius Vasiliou opened his eyes.","For a moment the Patriarch said nothing.","\"It will not come screaming ,\" the Patriarch stated, his booming voice dropping into something flatter and far worse.","\" An Immense One that has been slighted does not rage. It will arrive at the border of our Elseworld and present the agreement, clause by clause, and it will note that the promised bride is absent or defiled, and then it will name a price that existence itself will call fair.\"","His massive hand closed slowly into a fist above the water.","\" The price will not be Thalia. That is the cruelty of it. Taking her now would be accepting damaged goods, and its dignity will not allow that. So it will take everything around her instead. It will ask for a hundred daughters of the lineage in her place, and it will get them, because refusing turns a collection into a war. It will harvest the cultivated Provenance of our brightest, drained down to the root, taken as interest on the Ages it spent waiting. It will demand a tier of Vasileia emptied and burned, not because it needs the stone, but because a lesson must be visible from a distance. And when it is done, it will thank us for honoring the spirit of the agreement.\"","...!","\" They value their honor and their dignity above all else.\" Aurelius finished.","Noah listened calmly.","A hundred daughters. A burned tier. And it would say thank you!","\" How courteous of it,\" Noah remarked dryly. \" Okay then, this is the cost. While I still have you talking here, I want to expand my knowledge. Causes, and the Provenances of Provenance Lifeforms. I am fairly new to all this as could you expand my knowledge? It should increase the chances of success of what needs to be done.\"","Aurelius let out a low rumble that might have been a laugh, and leaned back against the rocky edge as golden lava sheeted off his scarred shoulders.","\" Causes...\"","He raised one thick finger and pointed upward, past the rocky ceiling, past the mountain, at everything.","\" Look at the architecture of reality with clear eyes, and you will find Causes standing under all of it. Behind every Observable Existence, there are Causes bearing its weight. Behind the Unobservable Existences that most lifeforms never even learn to perceive, there are Causes. Behind entire Dimensions, holding their laws upright across the Ages, Causes. They are not treasures scattered for the ambitious to collect. They are structure. Existence itself treats a Cause as a critical support of its own body, and it extends that regard to anything a Cause stands behind. That is the secret the lesser frameworks chase without understanding.\"","The finger folded back into his fist, and his voice deepened.","\" And that is why my kind hungers for them. Across the three hundred and forty-two Lineages, there are few pursuits older or more desperate than the birthing of one’s own Provenance Cause. Not a seized Cause or a harvested one. A Cause generated from your own essence, molded out of your own identity.\"","\"You take the Provenance you generate, and you press it, and you shape it uniquely against everything you are, and you attempt to condense an aim so complete that it steps apart from you and stands on its own as structure. It is brutally hard.\"","His eyes locked onto Noah with blazing intensity!","\" A birthed Cause is passive backing. It is power that stands guard over you while you sleep, asking nothing, draining nothing, generated once and holding forever. And above everything else, it is one of the finest resistances against THE Immense Ones that a sovereign can possess.\"","WAA!","\"Causes fortify an existence. When you carry them, existence registers you the way it registers a Dimension, as critical structure, as a thing whose alteration or erasure costs the continuum itself. Existence looks at Causes as critical structure. And so should we.\"","Noah’s endlessly blue eyes shone!","Causes remained grand and paramount!","In the depths of THE Infiniverse, at this very moment, he sought to have reborn Laestrygonian who were capable of natively birthing new Causes- what Provenance lifeforms had to work hard to do!","A slow, delicious smile threatened the corner of his mouth!"]},{"number":5683,"title":"Chapter 5683: Chapter 5682: Men And Sovereigns! II","paragraphs":["\" And what about Provenance itself? \" Noah asked, genuinely curious now. \" What identity does the arbiter of the Vasiliou carry?\"","Aurelius smiled for the first time, and it was not a warm expression. It was the smile of a man being asked to show a weapon he was proud of.","\" Every Provenance Lifeform ripens into an identity, sooner or later. My daughter’s ripened toward you, across all time, which is why I did not kill you instantly for doing all this. Because I know most that our Provenances...do not lie.\" The steam rolled between them.","\" And mine ripened on a wall.\"","The golden waters around him began to hum!","\"I am THE Provenance of THE Unfallen Vanguard,\" Aurelius declared, and the pressure in the cavern thickened until the surface of the spring flattened beneath it!","\"It is a simple identity. It is the truth that the line I stand in front of does not break while I am standing. Not a shield as a shield is a thing that takes the blow. I am the truth that the blow accomplishes nothing. Eleven times, powers came for this Elseworld across the Ages. Eleven times, I was the last thing standing between them and everything behind me. Eleven times, I did not fall. My Provenance is the accumulated weight of every stand, and it grows heavier each time, and there are beings in this continuum who turn around when they learn who is holding a wall, because arguing with an identity that has never once failed is arguing with existence itself.\"","HUUM!","The declaration settled, and Noah gave it the honest respect it deserved!","A grand identity, forged the hard way, worn by a man who had bled for every gram of its weight!","He was rather starting to like his father-in-law.","\" Which is why my offer is real,\" Aurelius added, sinking back into the lava. \" Holding a fort is not a favor I am doing you. It is the single thing in existence I am best at.\"","\"I understand now.\" Noah said pleasantly. \" What about The Atlas Elseworlds?\"","Aurelius scooped a handful of golden lava and let it pour through his fingers.","\" Atlas engineered the concept of Elsedimensions itself, and the ones he built personally are a different order of thing than ours. Ours are blind spots. His are locked rooms. No Immense One has ever entered one as it is not for lack of trying. The doors do not refuse them the way our boundary refused nothing today. The doors simply do not exist for them. An architect can stand on the exact coordinates of an Atlas Elseworld and perceive empty dark. He built with their blindness as a material.\"","...!","Wow!","This Atlas seemed grander and grander as one had to wonder how he was ever killed!","\" Inside, they are said to be workshops. Testing grounds. Some say gardens. Our Lineage has sent expeditions across nine of his known Elseworlds over the Ages. We recovered tools from the outer chambers. Lesser inventions. Enough to know the deep rooms exist. We never opened one.\"","The Patriarch’s eyes hardened.","\" We are not the only ones searching. Every Lineage with ambition scours them. But worse than the Lineages are the leashed. Some Provenance Lifeforms serve Immense Ones. Willingly, some, bought with patronage. Unwillingly, others, bent by agreements older than their own births.\"","\"An Immense One that cannot enter an Atlas Elseworld can still send a sovereign inside on its behalf. When you walk his halls, you will meet others of our kind, and you will have no way of knowing whose hands truly move them. Some will be searchers like you. Some will be gloves worn by beings who could not fit through the door. Treat every Provenance Lifeform you meet inside an Atlas Elseworld as a question you have not answered yet.\"","|VERITAS has increased by 1.|","Noah’s smile widened by a fraction. Gloves worn by beings who could not fit through the door. He was already looking forward to shaking a few of those hands.","\" Last question, then ,\" he said. \"I was asked this myself not long ago as I wonder...How does a Provenance Lifeform die?\"","\" Badly, and rarely, and almost always to the same three causes.\" Aurelius counted them off with grim efficiency.","\" Overwhelming convergence, which is what took Atlas. Enough Immense Ones agreeing to spend themselves at once. The second is the slow way. A sovereign who stops generating, who lets their identity go stale, thins across the Ages until existence stops making room for them. We call it Fading. Those below us are what fading leaves behind.\"","He gestured at the pristine golden skeletons resting in the depths of the spring. \" The strongest of my line chose to fade here, in these waters, so that what remained of their generation would feed the ones who came after.\"","He said it evenly, and moved on.","\" And the third cause is...ourselves.\"","The Patriarch’s voice went quiet for the first time.","\"A sovereign at war with its own truth. It is rare. I have seen it once, and I will not describe it in these waters.\"","Silence held the cavern, and the steam rolled across the golden skeletons below.","Then Aurelius rose!","The golden lava fell away from his towering frame in sheets. He floated, upright and immense, wreathed in steam and the weight of eleven held walls, and he came to a stop directly before THE True Human Emperor, looking down with the full imposing gravity of a father, a Patriarch, and a vanguard that had never fallen.","Aurelius began, his voice filling the cavern to its edges.","\"I raised that girl from the time she could fit in one of my hands. I taught her to stand before she could float, and I taught her to argue before she could weave, and I have watched every Age of her existence bend toward a stubbornness she absolutely did not get from her mother. She is the light of my existence.\"","\"I bargained her away once because I weighed one daughter against one Lineage and made the choice a Patriarch makes, and I have hated the choice of it every day since. So...should anything happen to her, there is no boundary, no Dimensionality, and no identity of any Provenance that will stand between you and me.\"","BOOM!","\"We are Provenance Lifeforms. We are also men. Men take care of those who depend on them, as they cannot let them down. I will hold the fort of my people against an Immense One. You will go across the Atlas Elseworlds and bring us back something of sufficient value, because all of us now enter a battle for survival. Do we have an agreement, O Human Dreamer?\"","BOOM!","The declaration struck as the golden waters flattened, and the skeletons at the bottom seemed to listen!","Noah looked up at the floating Patriarch, and he smiled.","\" We have an agreement,\" Noah said, rising through the golden lava to meet the Patriarch’s gaze as his stellar blue-gold body blazed.","\" I am a Dreamer, and my Dreams can be grand. What others could not find...may simply show itself to me.\"","He paused, and his endlessly blue eyes drifted, with unhidden and cheerful greed, toward the depths of the spring.","\" Oh, by the way. Can I take one of the golden skeletons down below here?\"","...!"]},{"number":5684,"title":"Chapter 5684: Chapter 5683: Ten Nanoseconds! I","paragraphs":["<THE Creature>","A Dimension about to change hands holds its breath heavily.","The burning skies of THE Vhelgaros hung low and red over a plain of cracked black stone that stretched across an entire Observable Existence, and upon that plain, two armies faced each other in a silence so heavy that even the wind had chosen a side and stopped moving!","On one side stood the army of THE Creature.","Hundreds of Primeval Ones floated in loose, grand formations behind him, titans of bone and Ego and petrified starlight, generals and soldiers alike gathered across multiple Observable Existences under the banner of a single masked figure wreathed in obsidian and white-gold flames.","They had knelt to him one by one across this campaign, some through defeat and some through awe, and every one of them now watched their Great Ruler hover at the front of their formation with the calm of a being who had never once needed to raise his voice to be obeyed!","And on the other side... stood the monsters of the old order!","The seated ruler’s army sprawled across the horizon, and it was a stranger army by far, because Primevals and Descendants stood mixed within it, the bred children of THE Immense Ones marching beside the ancient titans they usually scorned, unified beneath a single monstrous bloodline!","At their head towered the ruler of THE Vhelgaros.","Ghurvakh, THE Horned Sovereign!","He was a mountain of cursed majesty!","His massive body stood hunched and coiled with terrifying power, gnarled arms thick as fortress pillars hanging low, a heavy tail of plated muscle dragging furrows through the black stone behind him.","Horns erupted from everywhere upon him, curling from his skull, his shoulders, his spine, his forearms, a forest of cracked golden horn that had grown wild across Ages, and beneath the horns his flesh was grey and ancient and carved with old glowing wounds that had never fully agreed to close. An omen given a throne. A curse that had out-lived everything that cursed it!","And beside him stood his wife.","Descendant Ilvexa carried the same monstrous grammar in a leaner frame, her horns sweeping back from her skull in long elegant curves of black gold, her hunched shoulders draped in imperial silks that no tailor had ever designed for a body like hers, her clawed hands folded with a courtly grace that made the monstrousness more unsettling rather than less.","She was a Descendant of THE Immense Ones who had been born an omen and had made the omen regal, and her burning eyes held the only thing on that entire side of the battlefield that resembled caution!","THE Creature looked at the two of them and understood the arrangement of this Dimension in a single glance. A Primeval One of terrifying depth, and a Descendant whose lineage kept the architects’ favor flowing. Power married to permission. A monopoly with horns!","And above all of it... existence itself had come to watch!","Two eyes hung in the burning sky.","They were not clouds and they were not suns. They were gazes, vast and lidless, pressed through the firmament from somewhere unfathomably far above, each one large enough to reflect the entire battlefield in its depths, and every lifeform on the plain below could feel the weight of their attention crawling across their existence like the shadow of something too large to have a shape!","Waves of information bloomed across the whole Dimension, cascading into the minds of every Primeval and Descendant present, for the Ruling wished ALL of its audience informed!","| Two of THE Immense Ones have turned their gazes upon THE Narrative of Existence: The Grand Succession.|","| THE CACKLING BUTCHER has arrived to spectate. It adores successions. It adores them best when they are wet.|","|THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR has arrived to spectate. It has consumed the endings of ten thousand dynasties and declares most of them bland. It hopes, without much optimism, that this one will have flavor.|","...!","The two gazes were nothing alike, and everyone beneath them could feel it!","The eye on the left trembled constantly with something that could only be called mirth, its vast iris quivering the way a throat quivers around laughter that never ends, and the pressure that rolled off it was hot and eager and horribly festive, as though slaughter were a holiday and it had arrived early to get a good seat!","The eye on the right did not move at all. Its attention lay across the battlefield cold and flat and evaluating, the gaze of a critic at a meal, and its pressure was somehow worse, because the left eye wanted everyone to die entertainingly, while the right eye had already concluded that most of them would die poorly and was simply waiting to be proven wrong!","|THE CACKLING BUTCHER looks forward to the bloodbath!|","|THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR reminds the participants that anticipation is the finest seasoning, and that they are taking too long.|","The armies shuddered beneath the information! Lesser Primevals pressed themselves lower to the stone. Descendants clutched at their lineages like children clutching blankets. To be watched by one Immense One was a legend. To be watched by two was a sentence!","THE Creature floated at the front of his army, looked up at the two vast eyes with his masked face, and gave them exactly as much attention as he gave the wind.","Then he looked at Ghurvakh, THE Horned Sovereign, and he weighed him honestly.","The old monster was stronger than him! It was not close. The Sovereign’s depth rolled off his horned frame in slow tectonic waves, Ages of hoarded authority packed into cursed flesh, and behind him his mixed army outnumbered THE Creature’s Primevals by a wide and simple margin. If the two armies met, THE Creature’s side would pay a toll of blood so vast that victory would be indistinguishable from ruin!","A lesser ruler would accept the toll. Rulers had been spending their people that way since the first crown.","THE Creature raised his voice, and it rolled across the plain!","\"A Great Ruler does not watch and lead all his people to a massacre if he can prevent it,\" THE Creature declared. \" Leave our armies behind, as you and I can duke it out. Winner takes fuckin all.\"","BOOM!","...!","The battlefield went still in an entirely new way!","Hundreds of Primevals on both sides stared at the masked figure! A duel! A succession of an entire Dimension, dozens of Observable Existences, two full armies and a married monopoly of Ages... settled between two beings alone!","Beside the Horned Sovereign, Descendant Ilvexa’s burning eyes narrowed, and she frowned!","She did not speak aloud. Her caution moved through the marriage-weavings between them instead, silent and urgent, and everyone watching could read its meaning from her clawed hand closing around her husband’s gnarled forearm.","Do not do this. We hold the numbers. We hold the ground. Do not hand the challenger the only battlefield where his weakness does not count!","Ghurvakh, THE Horned Sovereign, looked down at his wife’s hand.","Then he looked at the masked Great Ruler floating before two armies, alone, offering to spare both sides the grave, and something ancient and prideful and long-bored moved behind the old monster’s burning eyes. He had sat this throne for Ages. He had collected tribute and permission and the slow rust of unearned peace. And here, at last, was a thing his own size, speaking the old language!","The Horned Sovereign gently removed his wife’s hand from his arm.","\"Agreed,\" Ghurvakh rumbled, and his voice cracked the stone plain for miles!","WAA!","| The terms of THE Grand Succession have been amended!|","|The Leading Conqueror and the Seated Sovereign have agreed to single combat. Winner takes all. The Dimension itself shall bear witness and enforce the outcome.|","|THE CACKLING BUTCHER is DELIGHTED! It declares this the correct and proper shape of a succession and showers the battlefield with its approval!|","|THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR concedes, grudgingly, that the meal has become interesting.|","...!"]},{"number":5685,"title":"Chapter 5685: Chapter 5684: Ten Nanoseconds! II","paragraphs":["The sky itself seemed to lean closer! The pressure of the two vast eyes doubled, hot mirth and cold appetite pressing down together, and torrents of Existential Moirai began to pour into the space between the two rulers, golden and thick, the Ruling setting its table for the grandest single exchange this Dimension had ever hosted!","The armies moved!","Hundreds of Primevals and Descendants flowed outward and around in vast slow currents, forming an enormous ring across the black plain, titans of bone and omen-blooded children of the architects circling shoulder to shoulder as spectators to the fate of their entire Dimension. The ring closed and the center emptied.","And the two rulers walked toward each other!","Ghurvakh came forward with slow seismic steps, his tail carving the stone, his forest of golden horns beginning to burn! THE Creature drifted forward to meet him, obsidian and white-gold flames trailing off his body, small before the horned mountain and entirely unbothered by the difference!","Behind THE Creature, unseen by every other existence on the plain, the massive statue followed.","It smiled brutally as it walked, and its voice arrived for him alone.","\"I never expected something seemingly foolish from you ,\" the statue said, and there was a strange, almost respectful curiosity threaded through its brutality.","\" You had a higher chance of winning with the army. But by yourself... this is adversity you cannot overcome.\"","The statue had weighed the Horned Sovereign the same way THE Creature had, and it had reached the same honest sum!","THE Creature nodded calmly as he walked!","\"I know, \" THE Creature said.","And then he said the thing that shocked even a remnant of Ages!","\" So I am making a gamble with my existence. You have been seeking control of me... I give you ten Nanoseconds of full control of my existence, in exchange for clearing the obstacle ahead of me. After you deal with it, you are free to do what you wish with the remaining time.\"","...!","The statue stopped walking!","Its brutal smile faded, and for the first time in this entire campaign, for the first time perhaps in Ages, its carved face became grim! Full control. Freely given!","The thing it had circled and bargained and told stories toward, offered up in a single flat sentence, with conditions attached and a clock of ten Nanoseconds strapped to its wrists!","THE Creature closed his eyes!","And the statue MOVED!","It crossed the space between them faster than any measurable speed, faster than the concept of the space existing at all, and it smashed into the body of THE Creature!","CRACK!","Ghurvakh, THE Horned Sovereign, ROARED!","The sound flattened the burning clouds! The old monster surged forward across the emptied center of the ring, and as he came, he pulled his full arsenal into the light!","Chains of screaming gold erupted from his hunched back, and dragging at the ends of those chains came his hoarded Ages, multiple First Causes blazing like shackled suns, and beside them, miniaturized Observable Existences, entire compressed realities bound and dragged behind him as weapons, the plunder of a monopoly that had taxed a Dimension for eternity!","It was the arsenal of a true apex! It was a charge that could unmake armies!","And across from it, THE Creature opened his eyes.","They were pure white. There were no pupils. There was nothing in them at all that had ever been THE Creature, only a flat, bottomless, ancient white, like twin windows opened onto something that had been waiting behind a door for a very long time.","The body of THE Creature raised one hand, and tapped the air, emotionlessly, once.","The Horned Sovereign popped.","...!","There was no exchange! There was no clash of Causes, no contest of chained Existences, no battle at all! One instant a mountain of cursed majesty was charging with the hoarded arsenal of Ages screaming behind him, and the next instant his entire massive body burst like a bloody balloon, and what sprayed outward was not blood and was not flesh, for every fragment of Ghurvakh, THE Horned Sovereign, ruler of THE Vhelgaros for Ages beyond counting, turned to pure white ash before it could even land!","The chains fell. The shackled First Causes rolled loose across the black stone like dropped marbles. The miniaturized Observable Existences drifted, suddenly ownerless.","Silense!","An immense, total, crushing silence swallowed the entire Dimension! Hundreds of Primevals stood frozen in the great ring! Descendant Ilvexa stared at the white ash drifting where her husband had existed, her clawed hand still half-raised from her final warning! Even the torrents of Moirai hung motionless in the air, as though the Ruling itself needed a moment!","And the thing wearing THE Creature did not celebrate, and did not look at the ash, and did not acknowledge the succession it had just settled with a tap.","It looked around, instead, at the edges.","The white, pupilless eyes swept slowly across the boundaries of THE Vhelgaros, and they saw the faint crystallized barriers at the far borders, the streaking of the burning sky, the deep structural hum beneath the black stone, the signature of a Dimension that was not sitting still in the void but MOVING, coupled and chained and dragged along linear tracks through the crossing-dark!","THE Vhelgaros was a Dimensional Cabin!","This entire Dimension, this entire succession, this entire Narrative, was one carriage among many upon THE Dimensional Provenance Train of Existence, rushing forward through the lethal dark toward the architects’ grand design!","The thing in THE Creature’s body looked at the edges of its moving cage, and then it looked up.","At the two eyes.","It raised THE Creature’s left hand and waved it once, and a bow appeared!","The bow was pure white! It was tall as the wielder and taller, a single flawless arc of blinding white authority with a string of compressed brilliance, and the instant it materialized, every Primeval and Descendant in the great ring felt their existence scream at them to be anywhere else!","The white-eyed figure nocked nothing, and drew!","The string came back, and power began to accumulate!","It built and built and BUILT, white authority folding into itself in silent detonations, and the pressure of the draw alone rolled outward across the ring in expanding rings of pure weight, and half of the surrounding army, hundreds of Primeval Ones and omen-blooded Descendants who were not even the targets, simply fainted where they stood, titans of Ages collapsing across the black stone like scythed wheat as the accumulating force scraped their consciousness flat!","And the bow rose.","It rose past the horizon. It rose past the burning clouds.","It aimed at the two eyes of THE Immense Ones!","...!","Pure horror swallowed everyone still conscious in THE Vhelgaros!","Primevals who had knelt to tyrants for eternity, Descendants born from the very lineages of the beings above, all of them watched the white bow settle its aim upon the twin gazes of the architects themselves, and every single one of them understood that they were witnessing something that did not happen, that had never happened, that could not happen!","One did not aim at THE Immense Ones!","One did not even look at them for too long!","The white-eyed thing wearing THE Creature released.","Two shots, loosed simultaneously!","They surged upward like ascending spears of absolute white, and the power packed inside them was unfathomably grand, layered and braided and WRONG, multiple unique Causes swirling within each shot alongside an unknown power that no information named and no Records dared annotate, and they crossed the entire height of the burning sky in less time than a scream takes to begin, and they smashed directly into the two gazes of THE Immense Ones!","BOOM! BOOM!","...!","The moment the impacts landed, all of existence within this Dimension began to shake!","The black plain heaved! The crystallized borders of the Dimensional Cabin screamed across their entire length! The burning sky tore and bled light from horizon to horizon, and through the tearing, from somewhere unfathomably far above, roars echoed down into THE Vhelgaros, vast and layered and existence-filling, roars of pure incredulity and gathering rage, the sound of two beings who had come to watch a bloodbath discovering that the bloodbath had looked back and reached UP!","They weren’t hurt or even touched at all, but their dignity...oh their dignity!","And down on the shaking plain, the white faded.","The pupilless light drained out of THE Creature’s eyes, and his own gaze returned to him, and he came back to himself standing beneath a torn and screaming sky with a fading white bow in his hand and ten spent Nanoseconds behind him.","He looked tired and heavy. The weight of the possession sat on his body like a debt already being collected.","And then his expression became grave, gravely still, because the roars from above were still echoing, and the sky was still blazing, and he looked up, slowly, to see exactly what the thing he had given control to... had done!","The two vast eyes above THE Vhelgaros burned through the torn and bleeding sky, and the pressure that had been mirth and appetite only moments ago curdled into something that made every surviving lifeform on the black plain forget how to breathe!","Prompts slammed down across the entire Dimension, and for the first time, Existence itself felt like a wound!","| THE CACKLING BUTCHER has stopped laughing.|","|THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR declares this meal RUINED. It has been struck. STRUCK. In ten thousand dynasties of endings, nothing has ever dared to season itself.|","| The spectators’ grievance is being drafted into the Records!|","|Judgment gathers.|","WAA!","And above the plain, the sky began to fill with swords!","Existential Moirai, the golden currency of fate itself, poured out of the two burning gazes and condensed, and it did not condense into showers of blessing or torrents of reward! It condensed into blades! Thousands upon thousands of golden swords materialized across the entire ceiling of the Dimension, each one long as a mountain is tall, each one aimed downward, a harvest of judgment stretching from horizon to horizon above two armies, one throne of ash, and a single masked figure!","The meaning required no information! The swords were not aimed at THE Creature alone. They hung over EVERYTHING. Every Primeval who had circled. Every Descendant who had watched. Every living fragment of a Dimensional Cabin that had hosted the insult! Two of Those Who Remain had been struck before an audience, and the audience itself had become part of the offense, and dignity of that magnitude was not restored by killing a culprit.","It was restored by deleting a venue!","Primevals wailed across the plain! Descendants clutched their lineages and screamed pleas up at the very beings preparing to erase them.","Ilvexa, widowed for less than a minute, stared up at the sword-filled sky over her Dimension with her clawed hands hanging open at her sides!","And THE Creature looked up at the thousands of blades of judgment, and he did not kneel, and he did not run.","He gazed up defiantly, obsidian and white-gold flames rising off his frame, tired and heavy and utterly unbowed, and he spoke, quietly, to the presence that only he could perceive!","\" Why did you do that.\"","It was not a demand or an accusation. It was the flat question of a bearer who had paid ten Nanoseconds of his existence for one obstacle cleared, and had woken to find his entire Dimension standing under a harvest of golden swords!","And for the first time!","For the first time in this entire campaign, the statue behind him... was quiet.","No brutal smile. No parable. The massive stone face stared up at the sword-filled sky with an expression THE Creature had never seen carved upon it, and it said absolutely nothing at all!","...!","The silence told him more than any answer could have, and none of what it told him was comforting!","Above, the swords finished gathering. The two burning gazes narrowed in unison. The entire golden harvest angled downward as one, thousands of blades drawing back for a single, Dimension-ending fall!","And then the sky opened a third time.","HUUM!","Between the two burning gazes, without arrival and without announcement, a third eye simply came to exist!","It was nothing like the others! Where the Butcher’s gaze quivered with heat and the Connoisseur’s lay flat and cold, this new eye was vast and soft and heavy-lidded, a deep luminous gold framed by long drifting strands of light that fell around it in slow, unhurried waves, and its pressure did not crawl or crush or evaluate!","Its pressure simply settled, over everything, the way dusk settles, feminine and grand and immeasurably old, and beneath it the rage-weather of the other two gazes was flattened into stillness like candle flames under a dropped blanket.","The eye blinked, once, slowly.","And the thousands of golden judgment-swords filling the sky... dispersed!","They did not fade with dignity. They were swept aside, all of them at once, unmade across the whole ceiling of the Dimension by a single lidded glance, scattered into loose harmless Moirai that drifted down over the armies like warm rain.","Waves of information bloomed, and even the Ruling’s voice seemed careful with these ones!","|A third gaze has arrived.|","|THE REMINISCING WIDOW looks upon THE Vhelgaros.|","|She rarely watches anything anymore. She finds that most things remind her of something better, and then are not it.|","...!","The two burning gazes ROILED! Their outrage crashed against the newcomer’s dusk-heavy calm, and their protest arrived for all to read, because beings of their nature did not know how to be indignant privately!","| THE CACKLING BUTCHER protests! It was STRUCK! Its dignity demands this Cabin’s erasure! The honor of Those Who Remain is not negotiable!|","|THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR protests! A spectator’s sanctity was violated! Precedent demands a deletion! What is dignity worth if insult goes unpaid?!|","The third eye regarded the two of them with its heavy-lidded gold, and its reply arrived with the weight of a being for whom their entire honor-culture was a noise happening somewhere beneath her!","|THE REMINISCING WIDOW replies: I do not care.|","...!","The information sat there, four words and a period, and the entire Dimension read it in stunned silence!","| THE REMINISCING WIDOW continues: You came to watch blood and were splashed by it. That is what the front row costs. You may collect your dignity from me, if either of you believes you can carry it home afterward.|","The two burning gazes went very, very still!","| THE REMINISCING WIDOW adds, softly: Besides. Something below drew back a bow I have not seen drawn in a very long age. I am taking this grievance, and both of you, elsewhere. The Narrative will conclude untouched. Do not make me repeat myself. I find repetition exhausting, and I find both of you exhausting, and I was having a rather pleasant memory before all of this.|","And then, before either gaze could shape a reply, her lidded gold eye turned, slowly, away from them both.","It looked down.","It looked at THE Creature, standing small and masked and defiant upon the ruined black plain. And then, in a moment that turned his flames cold, the vast feminine gaze moved a fraction further, past his shoulder, and settled with unhurried precision upon the exact empty space where the statue stood!","The space that no other existence in this Dimension had ever perceived!","The statue did not move and the eye did not linger. The moment lasted less than a breath and carried more weight than the entire harvest of swords!","| THE REMINISCING WIDOW departs.|","BOOM!","A blinding gold light erupted across the entire sky, dusk-soft and absolute, swallowing the burning gazes of THE CACKLING BUTCHER and THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR whole, and when the light faded, the sky of THE Vhelgaros was empty!","All three Immense Ones were gone!","The torn firmament slowly began to knit itself. The bleeding light dimmed. The crossing-dark streaked past the distant crystallized borders of the Cabin, indifferent as ever, and the only sounds on the plain were the settling of white ash and the breathing of two armies that had just survived their own execution.","Silence held for a long, long moment.","Then, across the vast ring of the battlefield, hundreds of Primevals and Descendants slowly turned and looked at each other, and the same stunned understanding moved through every one of them.","They had watched a seated Sovereign of Ages pop like a bloody balloon from a single tap. They had watched a bow aimed at Those Who Remain and loosed! They had stood beneath a sky of judgment-swords and lived because a third architect had swatted the wrath of two others aside like a bothersome insect and then LEFT with them!","And at the center of all of it, tired flames burning low, stood one masked figure.","Slowly, hundreds of gazes converged upon THE Creature!","And the Ruling, which had waited with impeccable manners through the entire catastrophe, finally delivered its verdict, cascading in grand golden text before his eyes as the statue silently translated every line!","| THE Narrative of Existence: The Grand Succession has concluded.|","|The Leading Conqueror has usurped the Seated Sovereign in single combat, witnessed and enforced by the Dimension itself.|","|Winner takes all.|","|You are now the Sovereign Ruler of THE Vhelgaros and all Observable Existences within this Dimensional Cabin. All standing tributes, holdings, and territorial weavings of the former ruler transfer to you.|","|Spoils of Succession: the unbound First Causes of the fallen Sovereign. The miniaturized Observable Existences held in his chains. The accumulated hoard of an Age-long monopoly.|","|Narrative Reward: unfathomable Existential Moirai floods the Leading Conqueror. Your Mantle of THE RULER deepens. Your bearing is now etched into Narrative History.|","|Addendum, recorded with interest: you have survived the grievance of two of Those Who Remain, and drawn the intervention of a third. Existence will remember this Succession for a very long time.|","Waves of golden Moirai poured down out of the healing sky and sank into his frame, and his obsidian and white-gold flames rose and rose, fed by the fortune of an entire concluded Narrative, until his figure hovering above the plain burned like a signal fire visible from every Observable Existence in the Cabin!","THE Creature let it burn!","He rose slowly and grandly into the air above the white ash of the old order, his flames streaming, the loose First Causes of the fallen Sovereign drifting up around him like a crown assembling itself, the miniaturized Observable Existences settling into slow orbits about his body, and he looked down upon the massed hundreds of Primeval Ones and omen-blooded Descendants of THE Vhelgaros with the flat, absolute bearing of a being who had carried weight his entire existence and had finally been handed a throne’s worth of it!","The masses stared up at their new ruler, at the burning silhouette wreathed in stolen Causes and orbiting Existences of light, at the survivor of judgment, at the Great Ruler the Narrative itself had crowned!","And THE Creature spoke.","\"Kneel to your King.\"","...!"]},{"number":5686,"title":"Chapter 5686: Chapter 5685: The True Vessel!","paragraphs":["Kneeling, when hundreds of apex existences do it at once, has a glorious sound.","It rolled across the black plain of THE Vhelgaros like a slow tide of thunder as Primeval Ones of Ages lowered themselves to the cracked stone, titans of bone and Ego and petrified starlight folding downward rank after rank, and between them the omen-blooded Descendants of the old order sank to their knees with their horned heads bowed, lineage-weavings dimmed in submission before a power their architects’ blood could not argue with!","Thousands of powerful existences! Two armies! One Dimension!","All of it knelt!","Descendant Ilvexa was among the last. The widowed monarch stared at the figure burning above the white ash of her husband for a long moment, her clawed hands slowly closing.","Then she, too, lowered her horned frame to the stone.","THE Creature hovered above his kneeling Dimension, wreathed in stolen First Causes and orbiting Existences of light, and he let the moment stand exactly as long as it needed to stand.","Then he closed his eyes!","—","He opened them somewhere else that was endlessly white and black.","He stood upon a battlefield that stretched beyond every horizon, and the battlefield was ancient.","The ground was bone-white and hard as fired porcelain, split by rivers of pure black that ran without moving, and across the entire endless expanse, corpses lay where they had fallen!","Thousands of them. Hundreds of thousands! Titanic frames and small ones, armored and bare, ancient beyond reckoning, every single one preserved mid-fall in white and black, no rot and no scavengers and no wind, a war that existence had chosen to keep exactly as it ended!","THE Creature’s mental manifestation stood at the center of it all, his flames burning low and steady, and before him, at the heart of the dead field, stood the statue.","He looked at it clearly, here, for the first time!","It was colossal. A towering figure of grey-white stone veined through with rivers of black, carved in the shape of a broad-shouldered bearer, its heavy brow jutting over deep-cut eyes that held no pupils, only smooth dark hollows that somehow watched.","Old wounds were chiseled across every surface of it, not decorations but records, gouges and fracture-lines and one long cleaving scar that ran from its shoulder to its hip, each wound edged in black as though the stone had bled ink and the ink had dried!","Its massive hands hung empty at its sides. They were the hands of a thing built to carry, thick-fingered and cracked across every knuckle!","And upon its back!","Upon its back was carved a mountain of...figures ! Hundreds of small carved figures clung to the statue’s back and shoulders in a vast stacked heap, bodies upon bodies, some clinging, some slumped, some reaching upward, an entire carried multitude rendered in miniature, fused into the bearer’s frame as though it had walked out of some ancient catastrophe with everyone it could hold and the sculptor had refused to let it put them down!","A bearer. A carrier of masses. A thing that stood, wearing everything it had ever refused to drop!","The statue’s hollow eyes rested on THE Creature’s manifestation, and its cracked mouth held the faint line of its old brutal smile, and it waited!","THE Creature did not make it wait long.","\" You will listen to me. \" THE Creature said.","His obsidian and white-gold flames rose!","\" You and I are separate. I do not deny that. But the power is not. The power...is mine.\"","BOOM!","The white ground trembled beneath the declaration, and THE Creature advanced a step, and a unique immensity of...Existence itself flickered around his manifestation even here!","Existence itself!","\" You are stone and memory. When you took your ten Nanoseconds, you did not bring power WITH you...\"","His voice dropped.","\" You picked up my power. You drew a bow with MY arm. You spent MY reserves, and I am the one standing tired and heavy in a burning sky paying the cost of the draw while you went silent! That is not the mark of a vessel borrowing from something grander. That is the mark of an instrument that knows the way better than the hand that holds it. You have technique. You have memory and knowledge and ten thousand dead reasons. But technique without an arm is a carving on a dead field.\"","WAA!","He raised one hand and pointed at the colossal bearer.","\"I am not a vessel of your power. You are a vessel of mine! Food does not command the mouth as you...are food. I am Existence, as you... are only a part of Existence. And if you do things that do not make sense, if you spend my power on grievances you will not name, if you go quiet when I ask you why... I can easily cast you out\"","Oh!","The declaration crashed across the ancient battlefield, and the black rivers in the white ground seemed to run faster for a moment, and the hundreds of carved figures on the statue’s back seemed, for a single breath, to press themselves lower!","The statue looked at him silently.","Its hollow eyes did not blink, because they could not, and its cracked smile did not move, and the silence stretched long across the field of the preserved dead.","And then the statue spoke.","It did not defend itself! It did not explain the bow, or the gazes, or the silence! It asked a question instead.","\" Can you affirm,\" the statue said, \" that you will smite down those deemed by existence in the future, regardless of their standing? Whether they be an ant... or an Immense One?\"","HUUM!","The question rolled out across the corpse-field.","The black rivers hummed! The white porcelain expanse vibrated beneath a hundred thousand preserved bodies, as though the entire battlefield were leaning in to hear the answer, as though this exact question had been asked on this exact field before, and the corpses were the record of how someone else had answered it.","THE Creature stood among the dead.","\" No.\"","BOOM!","\"I will not affirm that. I do not swing on another’s deeming. Not yours. Not even Existence’s. When existence deems a thing, I will LOOK at it. I will look with my own eyes, and weigh it with my own bearing, and judge it for myself. If existence deems them and I deem them, they will fall, whether they are an ant or an Immense One or something neither of us has a name for yet. And if existence deems them and I do not...\"","His flames roared upward, obsidian and white-gold, and for a moment the mental manifestation burned bright enough to cast the statue’s shadow long across the field of the dead!","\"...then existence can stand in line behind everything else that has tried to move me, and it can learn what all of them learned. I was not made to be pointed. I was made to STAND. A Great Ruler...does not lend out his judgment.\"","...!","Silence, one more time!","The statue’s hollow eyes stared down at the burning figure standing defiant in the middle of its ancient dead.","And then the cracked line of its mouth moved!","The brutal smile returned, and it was wider than THE Creature had ever seen it, wide enough that fine fractures spread through the stone of its cheeks.","\" Okay .\" the statue said.","It raised one colossal cracked hand and gestured, slowly, across the endless preserved battlefield, at the hundred thousand corpses lying in white and black!","\" Every one of them affirmed.\"","...!","\" You are Existence, and I am merely part of Existence,\" the statue said, lowering its hand, \"Your Dimensionality will rise enough soon for you to generate what you need to grasp different parts of existence. Until then, I will..ask for permission next time.\"","...!","The statue...actually seemed subservient at this time.","The statue stated such words as THE Creature looked at it coldly...and disappeared.","---","THE Creature opened his eyes.","The burning sky of THE Vhelgaros hung above him, healing along its torn seams, and below him a Dimension of Primevals and Descendants still knelt upon the black plain, hundreds of horned and ancient heads bowed toward their new King, waiting for his first command.","He looked past them all.","At the far edge of the Cabin, beyond the crystallized borders where the crossing-dark streaked past, a grand doorway stood in the distance, massive and sealed and humming, the threshold that led forward along the Train, toward the next Cabin, and the next, and the next, toward whatever waited at the head of a chained procession of Dimensions rushing through the dark!","THE Creature’s white-gold flames erupted to their full height, and his voice boomed out across the entirety of his first Dimension.","\" Existence is vast and full of terrors. Let us go...so that I can spread my terrors.\"","HUUM!","He gave the command, and thousands began to move!"]},{"number":5687,"title":"Chapter 5687: Chapter 5686: Let Me Dream!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Aurelius Vasiliou looked at his son-in-law with a hardened gaze.","The scorching steam of THE Vasiliou Primordial Spring rolled between them, and for a long moment the Patriarch simply stared at the smiling tyrant soaking in his lineage’s most sacred waters, the tyrant who had just asked to take one of their ancestors home the way a guest asks to take home leftovers!","Then Aurelius waved his hand.","From the golden depths below, one of the pristine skeletons stirred! It was a particularly dim one, its bones holding only the faintest ghost of the radiance its brothers still carried, an ancestor whose fade had been long and whose generation had been nearly all given away, and it floated up through the bubbling lava-waters slowly and grandly until it hovered between the two men, dripping liquid gold.","\" Existence is give and take,\" Aurelius said.","\" So far, you have taken my daughter, my patience, and now this.\"","The dim golden skeleton drifted toward Noah!","\" This does not need to be said... but you do know I could crush your current self with a smack, right?\"","The Patriarch’s burning eyes did not waver.","\" Others will not easily put up with how you talk to them. In existence, many can be arrogant. Many can act tyrannical. But the showy and boisterous ones are those who die the quickest. Be careful.\"","It was a warning, and it was advice, and underneath both of those things it was a father-in-law trying to understand what exactly his daughter had dragged home!","Noah nodded and accepted the skeleton, and it disappeared into his existence with a flicker of light.","\"I appreciate the advice, and the ancestor ,\" Noah replied pleasantly. \" But I should explain something, since we are family now. I simply act true to myself. I do not look at someone so much more powerful than me and become docile because of it. Somewhere along the way, I began to look at... Potential.\"","He leaned back against the rocky edge, golden lava sheeting off his stellar body.","\"I ask myself, if given time, could I get to where this being has attained, or exceed him? Where would our potentials lie? And every time, no matter who I stand before, I believe my potential... always comes out on top.\"","\"I do not think myself higher than anyone in standing. At one point, even a peasant was grander than me. At one point, an Ant was alive and had taken more steps in this existence than me. Standing is temporary. Standing is a snapshot. But potential... potential is the whole picture, and in the whole picture, I am... I am... I am....\"","HUUM!","His own words turned strange in his mouth as he spoke them!","His voice trailed, and his endlessly blue eyes unfocused, and his mind slid sideways into a state of epiphany and reverie that he had not planned and could not name, the three repeated words humming through his two hundred Decillion quarks like a struck bell that refused to finish ringing!","I am. The first Letter. The oldest declaration. It turned over inside him, heavy with something unarrived, and he sighed deeply and sank back into the scorching waters without finishing the sentence, letting the feeling settle into the depths of him where grand things germinated!","Aurelius Vasiliou watched all of this, and slowly shook his head.","\"My daughter’s Provenance chose a weird lifeform,\" the Patriarch declared to no one in particular. \" Okay. You seem to be enjoying yourself, so take some time here. I also need to go talk to my daughter and get things ready.\"","With these words, the muscular figure of Aurelius rose!","Drops of scorching golden lava-like waters fell off his towering, scarred body in glowing streams, and his ornate robes swept out of the steam and wrapped around him on their own as a golden gateway bloomed open at the spring’s edge!","The Patriarch stepped toward it, paused, and glanced back at Noah one last time, at the stellar blue-gold anomaly soaking in his ancestors’ spring and humming to himself about ants and potential.","He shook his head again.","Then he disappeared!","—","Noah leaned back, alone with the steam and the bones.","His eyes became endlessly blue, brighter and brighter, twin depths kindling in the golden mist, and he raised his hand up toward the rocky ceiling as if he wanted to grasp something he could not see.","There was so much out there!","Immense Ones who collected Provenance Lifeforms as interest. A Sealed One wearing its way through vessels toward something called IT. Atlas Elseworlds filled with leashed sovereigns and locked rooms. A Train of chained Dimensions rushing through the dark toward a design nobody would explain.","His power was growing, faster than any framework said it should, tier by tier and essence by essence, but he had understood something long ago.","He was not mainly limited by power.","He was limited by information. Knowledge!","Power told you how hard you could swing. Knowledge told you where to stand, when to swing, and whether swinging was even the correct art!","Every disaster that had ever nearly claimed him had walked in through a gap in what he knew, and every triumph had walked in through a gap in what his enemies knew about HIM!","He waved his hand, and the crystal left behind by Vakochev appeared above his palm.","The obsidian shard rotated slowly in the steam, dense and dark and silent, the parting gift of a being who had laid his Scales across all existence and then folded them up and retreated.","Noah looked at it the way he had looked at it a hundred times now, and his Regard answered the way it had answered a hundred times.","Question marks. Columns of them.","\" Everyone in existence is so damn fond of their secrets ...\" Noah remarked to the bones below.","He had many things to utilize! Many tools under his belt! His Mantle was grand. THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign was grand. The collar, the crystal, the Marks, the Teloi, the Tesseracts, an arsenal that dynasties of old would have built entire dynasties around!","But out of all of it, THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer was the grandest!","Because every other tool did what it did. Only one tool did whatever he needed it to do next. And if what he needed was information and direction...","\"I can always dream.\"","HUUM!","Noah smiled, and put the crystal away, and began to close his eyes in the spring!","The scorching golden waters bubbled around his body. The faded ancestors slept below. Somewhere above this pocket of density, his wife was arguing with her mother, his father-in-law was preparing a Lineage for war, and across the continuum his other body walked a higher Cabin","He settled his breathing, and reached inward, toward the doorway of his Provenance, toward the landscape where all his moments lived!","But it had to be something special!","No small dreams tonight. No cheap errands into yesterday. If knowledge was his true frontier, then he would aim his Dream at the largest gap in it, at the beings who sat above every framework, behind every curse, at the end of every warning anyone had ever given him!","\"I want to dream of Immense Ones,\" Noah declared into the steam, and the spring itself seemed to still at the words!","\"I want to know more about these things that remain an unfathomable threat that can squash me so damn easily. Let me dream... of Immense Ones.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5688,"title":"Chapter 5688: Chapter 5687: The Grave Beneath The Eye! I","paragraphs":["His Provenance answered!","Prompts bloomed across his vision in cascading waves, and even their text seemed to arrive more carefully than usual, like a Ruination lowering her voice inside a dangerous archive!","|You seek to Dream of THE Immense Ones.|","|Warning: the subjects of this inquiry stand unfathomably above your current Trueness and Provenance. Direct perception of an Immense One through Dreaming is ill advised. Attempting to force direct perception would exhaust your entire Provenance and may draw the attention of the perceived.|","|Your Provenance negotiates.|","|The cemented past is open to you. The Records hold countless moments connected to THE Immense Ones. A connected Dream may be granted: a thread from the past bearing upon the subjects of your inquiry.|","|Cost: 20 Provenance Essence.|","...!","Twenty!","Noah’s eyes remained closed, but his mind whistled at the number!","Twenty Essence, nearly a third of his capacity, drained for a single Dream he could not even steer.","He thought of many things. And then...","\" Done ,\" Noah said. \" Take it.\"","|20 Provenance Essence has been drained.|","|A moment connected to THE Immense Ones has been selected from the cemented past.|","|A random Dream emerges: its time, its place, and its witnesses are chosen by weight alone.|","HUUM!","Within the scorching golden waters of THE Vasiliou Primordial Spring, the body of Noah began to shine!","It was not the shine of the spring’s essence, and it was not the shine of his body! Light poured out of him from beneath his skin, stellar and blue-gold and impossibly dense, his entire figure condensing into radiance until he blazed within the steam like an unfathomable singularity given the shape of a man, and the faded golden skeletons in the depths below seemed to turn their ancient hollow faces up toward the brilliance!","His Provenance blared, brilliant!","Singularities spun! Two hundred Decillion quarks aligned! The surface of the golden waters flattened outward in a perfect ring around his shining frame, and the doorway of THE Human Dreamer swung wide upon its hinges of identity, opening onto the one landscape where even Immense Ones had left footprints they could never take back!","And Noah began to dream!","...!","---","A dream bloomed.","One moment there was the scorching gold of the spring, and the next moment there was ground beneath his feet and a sky above his head, and Noah stood manifested inside a Dimension that existence had folded shut like a pressed flower!","He looked out, and the place was grand.","Terraced fields rolled away from him in every direction, vast stepped plains of soft luminous soil stacked into the distance like the gardens of a sleeping titan, and the distances themselves were wrong in a beautiful, unhurried way, folding gently so that a far-off ridge might sit behind a near one and above it at the same time without apology!","The air was thick and breathed slow ambient exhalations rolling across the fields in visible ripples of shimmer!","And the sky!","The sky was layered, stratum upon stratum of radiance stacked toward an unseeable ceiling, bands of pale gold and deep amber and drowsy rose all glowing at once, like seven different evenings had been shelved on top of each other and left burning!","No sun hung anywhere. The light came from the layers themselves, and it fell across the terraced land heavy and warm and eternal, the light of a place where time had been asked to sit down and had agreed!","A Dimension locked in the past. Even before any prompt confirmed it, his instincts read it in everything. Nothing here was waiting for tomorrow. Tomorrow had been amputated!","Noah looked down at himself.","His body was his own, stellar and familiar, but it had been dressed! White robes wrapped him in long clean folds, draped over one shoulder and belted at the waist, the fabric faintly luminous and utterly weightless. And upon his face sat a mask!","He raised his fingers and traced it. Smooth gold, warm as skin, covering him brow to chin. Two simple dots for eyes.","And below them, carved into the gold, an eerie, permanent smile!","And...","There were others!","He lifted his gaze, and across the vast terraced fields he saw them, dozens upon dozens of figures scattered through the folded distances, each one seated alone upon the luminous soil, each one draped in the same white robes, each one wearing the same golden mask with its two dots and its eerie smile.","And every single one of them pulsed with an aura his existence now knew intimately!","Provenance Lifeforms!","Dozens of self-generating existences, seated in ordered solitude across a farm-realm outside of time, and before each seated figure... burned a lake!","The lakes were the most interesting things in the whole folded Dimension.","Each one was a slow whirlpool of stellar obsidian-gold, vibrant and deep, and they did not burn with light so much as with WEIGHT, because swirling within every lake were Causes!","Heavy, oppressive, authentic Causes, the critical structure of existence itself, dozens of them per lake, turning in the obsidian-gold like drowned suns, and their combined pressure rolled off the water and pressed against his body even from afar.","And the masked sovereigns were harvesting them!","Noah watched, fascinated, as the seated figures worked with slow eternal patience, their hands weaving above their lakes, drawing the burning Causes together strand by strand, pulling them into clusters, and the clusters into tighter clusters, condensing the harvested structure of existence toward singularities that formed so gradually that the work must have been measured in eras.","A farm. A farm where the crop was Causes, and the farmers were sovereigns of self-generation wearing smiling golden masks!","Noah thought, his mind racing behind the eerie smile.","’ Here sit dozens of sovereigns condensing causes by the lakeful. For whom? Sovereigns do not farm for themselves in uniform. Uniforms mean an employer, and employers at this scale mean...’","His existence BUZZED!","HUUM!","It came from nowhere and everywhere, a deep resonant vibration through all two hundred Decillion of his quarks, his Dream Body thrumming like a struck instrument, and prompts bloomed urgently across his vision!","|Your Provenance Dream Body is reacting.|","|An item held by your true body has pierced the boundary of the Dream. The crystal left behind by Vakochev pulses across existence and time. The weavings of the current Dream are made clear by its light.|","|It has found something.|","And in his fingers, the crystal appeared!","It was illusory, a manifestation of dark light rather than the shard itself, but it pulsed in his grip incessantly, urgently, joyfully, the long-silent treasure of a retreated titan vibrating like a compass needle that had finally, after all this time, found its north!","Information bloomed from it in waves, flowing directly into his existence, and his Provenance Essence caught every thread and pulled it taut and made everything clearer!","|The Records speak, unlocked by the resonance of the crystal.|","|When defeated by THE Immense Ones, Vakochev paid a heavy cost to retreat. The retreat was not clean. Critical parts of his existence were sundered from him and locked away across existence and time, sealed into pockets of existence where only the forces of THE Immense Ones tread.|","|You are near one of his Sundered Weavings of Existence.|","|Your Dream has deposited you within a Dimension locked in the past, isolated from all others.|","|Should you be successful in unsealing the chains binding him, the favor will not go unpaid.|","...!","Noah stood very still upon the luminous soil, and behind the golden mask, his endlessly blue eyes blazed!","And the shape of the larger truth assembled itself in his mind with terrible elegance!","Vakochev had not simply retreated. The being who laid his Scales across all of existence had been defeated, and his retreat had been paid for in pieces of himself, carved off and buried in pockets like this one, and the \"random\" Dream had brought him here!","’ The favor will not go unpaid.’","A favor. From VAKOCHEV. The word rolled through him, and the strategic greed at the center of his existence woke up all at once and began, quietly, to salivate!","But first, the venue. He looked around slowly, a masked farmer among masked farmers, and he followed the work to its destination!","In one direction, down across the folding terraces, he saw it.","A procession! A few of the white-robed Provenance Lifeforms had risen from their lakes, and they moved in a slow, solemn line across the fields, carrying their finished harvests, long condensed strings of heavy Causes coiled in their arms like luminous chains of obsidian gold, each string dense enough to make the air around it kneel.","And they carried them toward a mound.","It rose from the center of a vast cleared basin where no lakes burned, a great swollen hill of dark, packed, luminous earth, long as a fallen titan and shaped with the unmistakable, deliberate finality of one thing and one thing only!","A grave!","The masked sovereigns reached its edge one by one, and one by one they cast their harvests! The strings of condensed Causes unfurled through the air like thrown chains and fell across the grave-mound, settling over its dark bulk, sinking slightly into the luminous earth, layer upon layer upon layer!","Noah’s perception, sharpened by his Provenance, could see the accumulated depth of it, thousands of Cause-chains, tens of thousands, eras of harvests layered across that mound like a mummy’s wrappings woven from the critical structure of existence itself!","And the grave... responded!","Each time a fresh chain of Causes settled over it, the mound shone briefly from within, a deep buried pulse of light, and it hummed, a long, low, resonant note that rolled across the entire basin, the sound of something enormous turning over in its sleep beneath the weight of one more blanket!","The Provenance Lifeforms did not react to the shining or the humming at all. They simply turned, solemn and smiling their carved golden smiles, and walked back toward their lakes to begin the next harvest, as they had clearly done ten thousand times before, as normal as farmers walking back from a well!","Noah breathed behind the mask, and the elegance of it was as horrifying as it was instructive!","Existence protects whatever Causes stand behind. It registers them as critical structure and resists their alteration. So bind a prisoner in enough of them... and existence itself becomes the jailer. Existence itself will resist the unsealing. They did not build a cage as they convinced reality that the cage is part of its own skeleton!","And then, because every horror in his life had taught him to always, always check the sky, Noah raised his head!","The radiant layered heavens stretched above the terraced fields, band upon band of shelved evening light.","And set into them, vast beyond vastness, gazing down at everything!","Was a massive obsidian eye!","It filled a full stratum of the sky by itself, lidless and deep and dark as a hole cut in the heavens, its titanic iris faintly threaded with slow-turning gold, and its gaze lay across the entire Dimension at once, across every lake and every masked farmer and every thrown chain, and most of all, most heavily of all, upon the grave!","An Immense One!","The moment his perception acknowledged it, the Dimension’s own narrative unfurled for him, waves of prompt-information blooming in the style he now knew intimately.","|You now perceive the standing Narrative of this Dimension.|","| THE Narrative of Existence: The Unending Burial .|","|All those within this Dimension are tasked eternally: harvest the binding Provenance Causes cultivated across this Dimension, condense them, and layer them upon the unknown grave.|","|Those who are fastidious in this task shall receive ever greater flows of Existential Moirai. The most fastidious shall receive recognition: their names spoken once, fondly, by the watcher above, and a single keepsake drawn from the hoards of the one below.|","| THE GLOATING JAILER presides over this Narrative .|","...!","And then, at this time...","| THE GLOATING JAILER is in a magnificent mood today. It has been in a magnificent mood for the last several days.|","|It finds the contents of the grave exquisitely amusing. It stops by often, simply to look, the way one visits a trophy.|","|It reminds all diligent harvesters: he measured everything, once. Let him now lie beneath everything, measured. It considers this the finest joke it has ever told, and it has been telling it for a very, very long time.|","|THE GLOATING JAILER is smug. The Records note that this is its resting state.|","\"...\"","Noah stood in white robes among the terraced fields of an amputated Dimension, a golden smile carved over his real one, a pulsing key in his fingers, twenty Essence spent on a dream, and he absorbed all of it!","A titan who had laid his Scales across all of existence, dismembered and buried under chains of harvested Causes, existence itself recruited as his jailer!","Dozens of leashed sovereigns farming his bindings deeper on an eternal clock! An Immense One hanging in the sky above its favorite joke, smug and magnificent and watching everything!","And one uninvited Human Dreamer, standing in the middle of all of it, holding the key, wearing the uniform, with a promised favor from the buried titan himself waiting on the other side of the chains.","Behind the eerie golden smile of the mask, slowly, terribly, Noah began to smile for real!"]},{"number":5689,"title":"Chapter 5689: Chapter 5688: The Grave Beneath The Eye! II","paragraphs":["A wind rose in the deep gold of the citadel, far off where the stacked tiers burned against the shelved evenings of the sky.","It was not a true wind, for no true winds blew in a Dimension where tomorrow had been cut away, but an exhalation of the land itself, and it rolled outward across the folded distances!","It slid down the ascending architecture and out over the pale meditation halls, where white-robed Provenance Lifeforms sat unmoving as carvings with their auras turned inward.","It crossed the unhurried roads and the solemn processions upon them, stirring the hems of burial-walkers who did not look up!","It swept across the terraced Cause-farms, over a hundred stellar lakes and a thousand drowned suns turning in their depths, and it broke at last, like a tide against a final stone, upon a lone figure in white robes standing above an unclaimed lake, the eerie golden smile of his mask turned slowly across everything!","Noah catalogued everything the wind had touched!","Most of the masked Provenance Lifeforms were exactly as he had first read them, seated before their stellar obsidian-gold lakes in eternal patience, weaving the heavy Causes into condensed strings, rising in solemn processions to cast their chains across the humming grave, the Narrative of THE Unending Burial grinding forward beneath the smug obsidian eye in the layered sky.","But not all of them!","In the distance, past the rolling luminous hills, structures could be seen! Pale halls and terraced pavilions rose from the folds of the land, and among them, other white-robed figures sat in deep meditation, unmoving as carvings, their sovereign auras turned entirely inward.","And further still, small processions of masked figures were moving away from the farms altogether, walking unhurried roads toward the deepest regions of the Dimension, where distant gold structures rose stacked and grand against the shelved evenings of the sky, tier upon tier of ascending architecture!","Likely a central citadel!","He gave a light nod to all of it, and then turned his attention to the resource bubbling right in front of him!","The lake!","His assigned station, apparently, since the Dream had deposited him before an unclaimed one. The stellar obsidian-gold whirlpool turned slowly at his feet, and within its depths, the heavy Causes swirled like drowned suns, oppressive and vibrant and utterly unexplained!","Noah crouched at the lake’s edge, and put his hand into the water.","HUUM!","His existence BUZZED instantly!","The reaction did not come from his skin or his senses. It came from his foundations! All Nine of his Teloi, seated through every one of his two hundred Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks, woke at once, and they surged toward his submerged hand like hounds catching a familiar scent, because the things swirling in this lake were their kin, aims and structures and declarations, and his Teloi pressed up against the foreign Causes and began, seamlessly and hungrily, to take them apart.","Prompts bloomed in cascading analytical waves!","|Your Nine Teloi react to the contents of the lake. Analysis begins.|","|Analysis is seamless. A Telos is an aim and purpose that answers to its declarer. A Cause is a command seated in structure. Your integration is deep enough to read one through the other.|","|Three Provenance Causes are identified within this lake.|","|THE Provenance Cause of the Stilled Wing: a binding Cause. What it settles upon loses the right of departure.|","|THE Provenance Cause of the Lowered Crown: a suppression Cause. What it settles upon has its authority pressed beneath its own standing.|","|THE Provenance Cause of the Quiet Name: a sealing Cause. What it settles upon cannot be found by those who seek it.|","...!","Binding! Suppression! Concealment!","Every lake in this Dimension was growing links for the chains on that grave, and now his Teloi tore into the far more interesting question of WHERE such things came from.","|Origin analysis: these Causes were generated from this Dimension itself.|","| A tool of extremely high Dimensionality belonging to an Immense One is located within this Dimension. Its ambient weight saturates all budding Causes cultivated here. Due to this saturation, the budding Causes attain the significance of Provenance upon maturing.|","|Provenance Causes carry the Dimensionality of their making. They ignore the defenses of those with weak Dimensionality: lifeforms with 60 Attributes or less have a hard time ever denying the effects of such Causes.|","|Mitigation exists: if the targeted lifeform has any Causes standing behind them, the terrifying Dimensionality of these Provenance Causes can be mitigated.|","Noah’s eyes were shining brilliantly behind the mask!","Because they were inherently unique, these Provenance Causes, grown in saturated soil, carrying borrowed depth, capable of ignoring the defenses of nearly everything beneath the sixtieth attribute.","But at the end of the day, when his Teloi held them up to the light and turned them over... they were still just another form of authority and power!","And the mitigation clause sang to him loudest of all. Causes defended against Provenance Causes.","’ And my Teloi contribute to my Dimensionality directly ,’ Noah thought, ’ They are integrated into every quark of my matter, passively applied to my existence at all times. If I simply define and utilize more of what is already mine...’","His Dimensionality would climb without a single external treasure!","It was a grand thread, and he wanted to pull it for a century if he could.","But he cut the experiment short, drew his hand from the lake, and rose. Research was for the safe hours, and he was not in a safe place, and the actual problem still hung unsolved before him.","How did one move against that grave, unseal a piece of Vakochev, and walk out of a pocket of locked time, all under the direct, era-long, trophy-admiring gaze of an Immense One?","He turned toward the grave, weighing angles and blasphemies!","And that was when he saw it.","At one particular lake, off along the curve of the basin, something was laying near the water’s edge, and Noah almost had to rub his eyes as if he was seeing things.","Because he saw...","An obsidian slime!","It was laying down gently beside the lake, if a slime could be said to lay down, a small rounded mass of stellar obsidian resting against the luminous soil, and it was so extremely, absurdly out of place among the robed and masked sovereigns of this Dimension.","He looked closer, and the closer he looked, the less sense it made!","The slime was small, barely the size of a curled hound, its simple body a deep translucent obsidian threaded through with faint drifting motes of stellar light, and set within its front were two eyes of dim crimson, half-lidded, unhurried, fixed upon the distant grave with an expression that should have been impossible for a creature made of ooze!","Melancholy!","It looked ancient in its bearing, in the sheer stillness of it, the stillness of something that had watched eras walk past and had stopped waving at them! Its aura could not be felt at all, not veiled, not suppressed, simply absent, a hole in his perception shaped like a small sad slime!","And yet!","When Noah’s deeper senses brushed across its simple little body, his existence prickled from crown to heel, because that small mass of obsidian felt DEEP.","His instincts reported, calmly and insistently, that the tiny creature laying by the lake contained countless miniature dimensions within it, folded and stacked and sleeping.","\"...\"","Noah couldn’t help but frown as his existence buzzed","Slimes! Even his own Records held the old terror of that word. Entire Dimensions across existence exterminated slimes on sight, because of the legends of the one that ATE Dimensions, the feared thing whose survival in any Dimension for a few days marked that Dimension for death.","And here one lay, obsidian and sorrowful, inside a locked pocket of the past, at the edge of a Cause-farm, staring at the grave of a titan.","His intuition pointed.","Noah followed it, and began to walk!","He crossed the luminous terraces at an easy pace, one masked farmer strolling among many, past sovereigns who did not look up from their eternal weaving, until he came to stand beside the small obsidian slime at the water’s edge!","It did not react to his approach at all. Its dim crimson eyes remained on the grave, half-lidded and far away.","Noah looked down at it, and said, simply!","\" Hello.\"","\"...\"","Nothing!","The slime did not even turn towards his direction! It lay there, ancient and melancholic and dripping with more folded depth than some Dimensions he had personally visited, and it ignored him.","Noah scowled behind his golden smile, and waved his hand in front of its crimson eyes!","\" Hello? Obsidian slime?\"","...!","The half-lidded crimson eyes went wide!","The slime’s entire small body rippled once, sharply, and it turned, and it looked at him, and it blinked, an expression of pure, unguarded surprise blooming across a face that was mostly ooze, and when it spoke, its voice arrived directly against his existence, soft and old and rasped at the edges.","\" You...can perceive me?\"","The slime rose slightly off the soil, its crimson gaze sharpening!","\" Even that Immense One should not be capable of perceiving me right now. How can you....\"","It stopped.","Its dim crimson eyes moved across him slowly, up and down, down and up, taking in the white robes, the golden mask, the stellar frame beneath them, and something in its ancient gaze focused, and narrowed, and understood!","\"...ah.\"","HUUM!","Noah’s own existence buzzed at that single syllable, and he became entirely serious, his full attention locking onto the small creature, his Regard sweeping across it.","And the panel that bloomed before his eyes was unique.","| Masamuk|","|??????|","|??????|","|??????|","|??????|","|??????|","Rows upon rows of sealed questions, the signature of depth beyond his measure, and above them all, alone and unredacted, as if the name itself refused to hide.","Masamuk!","Noah blinked.","Masamuk. Masamuk. His mind worked extremely fast, tearing through his own Records at the speed of thought, because he had HEARD that name before!","Not in this Dimension! Not in this era! It had been spoken to him once, in the long drawl of the lazy Mnemonic Leviathan.","The memory played in his head.","When Existence was young, and the boundaries between what was and what was not remained fluid and uncertain, there was Masamuk.","Masamuk had split the body of Chaos, not with authority, since authority had not yet been differentiated from raw potential, but through the sheer force of will.","From the halves of Chaos, Masamuk fashioned the territories that would become the first Domains.","Masamuk looked upon the divided Chaos and shaped it, molded it, convinced it to remember the forms that were envisioned.","This was the first great Cause of differentiation through Chaos under the records of Masamuk, as only at this time did he become a true follower of Vakochev!","...!","A follower of Vakochev!","One of the first beings to enact great Causes of Differentiation, a shaper from the era when what was and what was not had still been negotiable, a splitter of Chaos by pure will!","Laying beside a lake, in the shape of a small sad slime, staring at his buried master’s grave.","...!"]},{"number":5690,"title":"Chapter 5690: Chapter 5689: The Slime At The Lake","paragraphs":["There were beings you postured before, and there were beings you did not.","Noah became entirely serious as he looked at the small lifeform in front of him.","One of the oldest followers of Vakochev!","A shaper from the era when what was and what was not had still been negotiable, a splitter of Chaos by pure will, and every instinct in his two hundred Decillion quarks reported the same reading.","The melancholic little slime laying beside this lake was unfathomably more powerful than the father of Thalia, more powerful than anyone he had ever stood before, and quite possibly more powerful than even something like THE Sealed One!","It was OLD, old in the way the first light was old, and as much as Noah liked to act tyrannical and border on arrogant before ancient terrors, his arrogance had always been aimed at the self-serious and the cruel.","This being was neither.","So he gave the slime the respect that it deserved. He nodded towards it, once, with a serious expression, and he chose to say nothing at all, because there was a great deal here that he did not understand, and a wise man did not fill the silence of his elders with noise!","Instead, he sat down.","Noah lowered himself onto the luminous soil at the edge of the lake, casually, unhurried, the warm ground giving softly beneath him, one masked farmer settling at his station among a hundred masked farmers doing the same.","The whirlpool of obsidian gold turned slowly before him, drowned suns swirling in its depths, and to any distant eye he was simply working, simply sitting, simply one more white robe in a Dimension full of them!","Because the slime had said it itself. It should not be perceivable here, not even to the Immense One hanging smug in the layered sky.","And Noah was entirely perceivable, a visible farmer at a visible lake, and he had no intention of standing over an invisible fugitive and giving away the position of the only friendly piece on this entire board by talking down at empty air!","Masamuk watched him do all of this.","The dim crimson eyes moved over him slowly, up and down, taking in the disguise, the caution, the deliberate casualness of the seating, and the ancient slime’s expression remained serene throughout.","\" You should be fine to communicate ,\" Masamuk said, its soft rasped voice arriving directly against Noah’s existence.","\" My weavings cover this whole region. It will not even seem like you are talking, to the eyes of others.\"","Noah nodded at this, and let his shoulders settle, and spoke in a low, even tone toward the turning lake.","\"I have heard a few stories regarding you. I never thought I would actually come across you. \"","\" For what happened to Vakochev... I am sorry. Are you here to unseal the part of him within that grave as well?\"","...!","He asked his questions very clearly, and a flash of surprise bloomed within the ancient slime!","Its small body rippled once, and its crimson eyes widened by a fraction, and then narrowed.","\" Existence is vast, and filled with unfathomable terrors ,\" Masamuk said slowly. \" My friend and Master had cast out many weavings. I did not think one would appear here so quickly. He expected hundreds, or even potentially thousands of years to pass before any chances could arise.\"","The slime seemed melancholic as it said these words, its gaze drifting back toward the distant humming grave.","Something in the phrasing snagged against Noah’s mind and held! My friend and Master.","And... chances.","The crystal in his storage, the beacon that had waited patiently in his collection.","Noah couldn’t help but turn serious as he leaned forward slightly, his voice dropping lower.","\" What truly happened before these new rulings of existence came to play? What happened between THE Immense Ones and Vakochev?\"","...!","The slime’s eyes flashed!","Immense sadness and immense hatred moved through those dim crimson depths together.","It looked out across the lake filled with budding Causes silently.","After a moment, the slime asked a question of its own.","\" Do you believe you will die?\"","...!","A heavy question arose between them, laid down without warning, and Noah found that he did not need to take a long time to answer it.","He had answered it before, in the quiet of his own Pantheon, in the years before crowns and Verses, in every hour since a hospital room in 1997 that he had personally stood inside.","\"I am only human ,\" Noah replied. \"I live, and in the future, I may die. Maybe to be truly human, it is certain that I will die. But before then... I have boundlessness before me.\"","Masamuk turned its crimson gaze upon him and nodded","And then the serenity cracked.","\" For the first time in my existence ,\" Masamuk said, and its soft voice did not rise, \" Those Who Remain, these failures of existence... made me want to die.\"","BOOM!","The words landed against Noah’s existence heavily!","They made him... want to die?!","This being! A splitter of Chaos! A shaper of the first Domains, older than authority itself, deep enough that an Immense One hung directly overhead and could not perceive him! What could possibly be done to such a lifeform to make it want to DIE?!","Noah continued to listen silently, his hands resting still upon his knees, and Masamuk spoke, and the Dimension around them seemed to quiet itself to make room.","\" When they moved against us, our side had one banner. One enemy stood before them. Vakochev. And do you know what these failures did? \"","The slime’s gaze stayed on the far grave. \" They did not focus their attacks on him. From the very first hour, they focused their attacks on those who followed him. And even that, even that, was not the worst of it.\"","Its small body was utterly still.","\" The worst was the unnecessary cruelness of it. There was no strategy that demanded what they did. No war that required it. It is as if they wish to be cruel simply because they can. They targeted all those that followed Vakochev, and they did not simply kill us, because they know what death is. Death is singular. Death is potentially final. A dead follower feels nothing, and a Master mourns once, and it ends. So they chose otherwise. They chose to make those closest to him, and him by extension, feel pain. Lasting pain. Renewable pain.\"","The crimson eyes closed for a long moment.","\" And across existence, pain comes from connections. From relationships. From memories.\"","...!","Noah’s chest tightened.","He remembered a memory of...a red-haired woman’s voice crying out from a white pool saying... You promised to always remember !","He pushed it down and kept listening.","\"I knew someone ,\" Masamuk said.","The hatred drained out of its voice as it said it, and what remained underneath was so much worse.","\"I knew someone who made my entire existence feel brighter and happier just by being near her. Do you understand what that is, at my age? I had watched the first boundaries harden and the first eras turn to sediment, and I had felt many things across all of it, but she walked near me and existence itself was simply... better. I was in love with her. Wholly. And she loved me wholly in return. Two old things, in love the way young things are supposed to be.\"","The slime’s voice rasped softer.","\" And when Those Who Remain targeted me, they did not come for my body. They came for her. Her records. Her...memories. They stripped me of all the memories of my love.\"","...!","\" Can you imagine it? \" Masamuk asked, \" Not even remembering or knowing those you love? They were artists about it. They cruelly left me with just enough. Enough to know that there WAS someone I loved. Enough to know the intensity of that love, its exact weight, its entire shape pressed into me like a fossil. And then... nothing. I do not remember her name. I do not remember her face. I do not remember her smile.\"","The small obsidian body trembled, once.","\" And yet I remember how her laugh alone used to make me believe that everything would be okay. They left me that. They took away her very memory, her very Records, they took away even more than her, and they left behind the gaps, carved clean, so that I would always know the things that I lost even though I could never again remember them. I live inside a home where every room I loved has been emptied, and the outlines of the furniture remain on the floors.\"","BOOM!","Noah did not move. Behind the golden mask, his endlessly blue eyes burned!","\" The pain that came from this was so unbearable ,\" Masamuk continued, quiet as falling dust, \" that for a moment... I wanted to die. I wanted... to die. Because why do we live? We live to enjoy, and to struggle against adversity. We live to be safe, and content, and happy. And Those Who Remain looked at all of that, everything living things live FOR, and they systematically took it away from me, piece by piece, gap by gap, as they almost took my will to live with it.\"","The crimson eyes opened, and turned from the grave, and looked directly at Noah, and in their dim ancient depths, beneath the sorrow and beneath the hatred, something grand and unbroken still burned.","\" Almost.\"","\"Almost...\"","...!"]},{"number":5691,"title":"Chapter 5691: Chapter 5690: Rage!","paragraphs":["\"I wanted to die ,\" Masamuk said. \" But as my friend and Master always told me... Persevere. Regardless of the difficulty, Persevere. Regardless of the pain, Persevere. So... I Persevered!\"","The small obsidian body straightened upon the luminous soil.","\" But even while persevering ,\" the slime finished quietly, \" we were fractured.\"","...!","Its crimson gaze turned towards the distant grave, towards the mound wrapped in eras of chains, humming softly under the weight of its newest layers.","\" Many things could be said about... Those Who Remain.\"","Masamuk said the three words as if they were a heavy insult, spat slowly, each one set down with the deliberate contempt of a being who had watched what those words did when they were let loose upon existence!","\" They are careful beings. They do everything to preserve what they hold, and they hold nearly everything. And as much as one can do alone in existence, and one can do a great deal...\" The crimson eyes slid toward him. \"... one cannot do it all alone. I could sit here and tell you of Dimensionality. Of Tongues. Of Causes and their deeper natures. None of it would truly matter. You need your own high level of power, yes. But you cannot be alone. THEY are never alone. And even here, I have been alone, and so I have not been able to do anything at all. I have laid beside this lake, and the moment I make a single move toward that grave, the eye above will also finally make its move.\"","Noah blinked at these words, and the shape of the problem turned over in his mind, and resolved itself with beautiful simplicity!","One watcher. One mover. One hiding thing that could act but not survive attention, and one visiting thing that could draw attention but not act. The board did not need a grander piece.","It needed a sacrifice that cost nothing!","\"If I make the first move and draw its attention,\" Noah asked calmly, \" would you succeed in unearthing whatever part of Vakochev lies within?\"","Masamuk’s gaze sharpened upon him.","\" Your body here would die,\" the slime said flatly. \" Or worse. Be taken by Them.\"","Noah raised his hand, and turned it over slowly in the honeyed light, watching the stellar frame of it as one watches a borrowed tool.","\" For me, this is only a dream. No harm comes to my existence whatsoever.\"","\"...\"","Masamuk looked at him silently, up and down, down and up.","Then an obsidian light flashed!","From within the small slime’s body, something rose and floated towards Noah, turning gently end over end. A grimoire!","It was bound in deep obsidian that drank the light of the layered sky, its cover smooth and unmarked, its edges worn round by an eternity of handling, and its pages, glimpsed as it turned, were filled with a script that seemed to rearrange itself shyly whenever his eyes came near, countless entries pressed dense as sediment!","\"A journal of mine ,\" Masamuk said simply. \" Filled with my musings of existence, and what I know. Think of what you wish to hear me ramble on about while holding it, and the page should open up.\"","...!","Noah accepted the grimoire with both hands, and the moment his fingers closed around the obsidian cover, prompts bloomed!","| You have received THE Obsidian Journal of Masamuk.|","|Within are the musings of one of the first shapers, accumulated since before authority was differentiated from raw potential. Its contents answer to intent: hold it, and think of what you wish to know.|","|The journal has been keyed to your existence alone. To all other perceptions, it does not exist.|","| The weavings of Masamuk settle around it. Even the Records will not gossip about this gift.|","The grimoire sank into his existence and disappeared, and Noah felt the weight of it settle somewhere deep, an entire era’s worth of rambling waiting patiently for his first question!","He then looked at Masamuk, and he nodded, once.","There was nothing else that needed saying.","Noah rose to his feet and looked at the distant grave.","Then he waved his hand across the lake below, and the whirlpool answered him! Strands of obsidian gold tore free of the turning waters as he grabbed a handful of the Provenance Causes, THE Stilled Wing and THE Lowered Crown and THE Quiet Name coiling in his grip like harvested lightning, oppressive and vibrant!","And he began to walk with grand steps towards the grave!","The masked farmers did not look up as he passed. Another white robe on the burial road, another armful of chains for the eternal work, his sandals pressing soft prints into the warm soil, the incense-heavy air parting around him.","He crossed the final terrace. He reached the edge of the vast cleared basin, where ten thousand layered harvests hummed upon the titan-length mound.","And then Noah broke the season!","He dropped the Causes he was carrying, all of them, letting the harvested chains spill carelessly across the sacred ground, and he JUMPED, his white robes snapping, and landed atop the grave itself!","BOOM!","And he began tearing the Causes apart!","His hands plunged into the layered chains of eras, and his Teloi blazed through his grip, and he RIPPED, strand from strand, THE Stilled Wing shredding between his fingers, THE Lowered Crown unraveling, whole condensed harvests tearing loose from the mound with sounds like existence clearing its throat, and the grave beneath his feet shone!","HUUM!","For one full second, the entire Dimension simply stared!","And then the sky spoke!","| Oh?|","The single syllable arrived pressed into every mind.","| THE GLOATING JAILER stirs from its magnificent mood.|","|It has waited a long time for this. It knew that if it sat beside its trophy patiently enough, one of the rats of Vakochev would eventually crawl out of whatever crack had sheltered it, and come scratching at the lid.|","|It is pleased. It does so enjoy being right.|","WAA!","The pressure came barreling down!","It fell upon Noah like the sky itself deciding to sit, and his figure was yanked up forcefully off the grave, hoisted into the open air above the mound by nothing at all, his limbs spread, his white robes whipping, the golden mask burning cold against his face!","Narrative crushed down all around him, and the obsidian eye in the layered sky turned, fully, for the first time in a while, and looked at him with its whole attention!","| Now then, little rat ,| the voice rolled. | Where is the rest of him? The pieces were scattered so carelessly during the retreat. We have gathered some. We are missing others. You crawled here from one of his boltholes, which means you know the smell of the rest. Tell me where the rest of Vakochev lies.|","WAA!","And...the torture began!","Pressure closed around Noah’s existence like a fist around wet clay, and SQUEEZED!","Every quark of him screamed under compression, his Frame groaning, his singularities juddering in their orbits, pain of a magnitude he had never once sampled in all his climbing, the direct attention of an Immense One applied with the precision of a being that had unmade sovereigns for boredom!","|Huh, quiet a weak one you are...|","Noah endured without screaming!","His jaw locked behind the golden smile. His mind held. And in the crushing dark behind his eyes, words rose up to meet him, words from a message of the last will of the being whose grave he was currently bleeding on!","Rage. Rage!","Rage against the dying light! Do not go gentle! Rage! Rage! Rage!","HUUM!","’ Rage ,’ Noah told his own buckling existence, and his teeth ground behind the mask. ’ Rage!’","And atop the wave of agony, with the audacity of the truly shameless, he worked!","The third cycle of THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis ignited across his quarks! The crushing force of an Immense One pressed down on every particle of him, and Noah seized that pressure and ROUTED it, weight flowing cell to quark to quark, bear, seat, stabilize, move, using the torture itself as the tempering hammer, converting an architect’s cruelty into his own foundation one particle at a time!","And then, hoisted and crushed and quietly forging, he looked down!","Below, across the terraces, dozens of masked Provenance Lifeforms had risen from their lakes and were staring up at the spectacle, white robes still, golden smiles upturned, and Noah gazed at them through the pain, and spoke.","\" When did THE First Lifeforms fall so low? \" he called down. \" When did we become faces behind masks, following the orders of failures of existence?!\"","BOOM!","The Dimension itself flinched!","| THE GLOATING JAILER’S mood is no longer magnificent.|","|It was going to be leisurely about this. It has decided otherwise.|","|Let us see the shape of you, rat. Let us see what you hold most dear in existence... and let us take it away!|","And the Moirai crashed into him!","It came as a flood of gold turned wrong, Existential Moirai weaponized, pouring into his existence with a single surgical purpose, to dig, to find, to ALTER, to reach into his Records and rewrite what it found there, to carve out his loves the way loves had been carved out of a small slime!","Trillions of needles drove into him at once, threading between his quarks, seeking his mother, his daughter, his wife, his people, seeking the furniture of his existence to empty the rooms!","But his existence defended itself.","Across every single one of his two hundred Decillion quarks, all at once, his Nine Teloi flared!","In every quark, nine points of light ignited and spread, shimmering into small golden shields, Quintessence and Existence and Paradox and Chaos and Adversity and Apocalypse and Mana and Harvest and Tyranny, nine seated aims standing up inside every particle of his matter simultaneously, and his entire body LIT UP, a man-shaped constellation of two hundred Decillion burning purposes, his generated Provenance blazing out of every seam of him!","And his purpose, his very Provenance... REJECTED the coming alterations of the Immense One!","The needles struck the golden shields and bent! The digging Moirai found no purchase, existence itself registering every quark of him as critical structure, as aimed and owned and not for editing, the flood of alteration breaking against nine-fold walls in every particle at once, and through the rejection, impossibly, gloriously, prompts flickered at the edge of his shredding vision!","|Your existence resists the alteration of its Records.|","|Under terrifying adversity, tempered by the pressure of an Immense One... your attributes begin to rise.|","...!","But the pain!","The pain of trillions of needles breaking against trillions of shields inside him, of an Immense One’s will grinding against his foundations, of a Baryogenesis cycle running through the middle of it all! It was so painful that he wanted to scream!","He couldn’t help but scream!","The scream tore out of him and rolled across the entire Dimension, and above him the obsidian eye drank it in with vast satisfaction, its whole attention pressed down upon its screaming prize!","Its whole attention!","—","Below, beside a quiet lake, Masamuk’s crimson eyes went cold.","The melancholy drained out of them like water from a broken bowl, and what remained was the thing from before names, the splitter of Chaos, and its small obsidian body gazed at the eye drinking in the scream, and became blurry!","And it MOVED!","A flash of obsidian light shot low across the terraces, silent as a thought, and struck the grave!","It was only a nanosecond later that the eye above blinked, and its gaze snapped down toward its trophy!","But that nanosecond was enough!","What happened upon the grave in that sliver of time was a glorious, melancholic devouring.","Every Cause upon the mound, ten thousand layered harvests, countless chains, THE Stilled Wing and THE Lowered Crown and THE Quiet Name in their uncountable thousands, disappeared, consumed in a single silent pass.","And beneath them, unearthed for the first time in an unknown time, lay a vast golden coffin, and even as the Dimension’s light touched it, the coffin itself was EATEN, cleanly, immensely, the entire titanic vessel vanishing in one bite that left nothing behind but a fading afterimage stamped with enormous teeth marks!","And underneath it all...","Underneath was a cluster of invisible obsidian brilliance, wrapped in heavy, scorching, multicolored chains!","The chains blazed with a weight that had no business existing!","Across the distant terraces, masked Provenance Lifeforms cried out and LOOKED AWAY, sovereigns of self-generation physically unable to rest their gazes upon the bindings, and Noah, hoisted and screaming and burning golden in the sky, turned his eyes toward the unearthed thing and felt his existence almost pop like a balloon, the sheer power of the multicolored chains pressing against his perception like a boot against a bubble!","And the thing inside the chains!","It could not be perceived at all! Its Dimensionality was too high, a blankness deeper than the Quiet Name, a presence his senses reported only as a wound in what was possible!","But Noah had managed a glance! And in that single, existence-buckling glance, he could barely perceive...","Invisible hands, grasping the multicolored chains!","And pulling!","CRACK!","The chains began to crack, and it did not sound like metal, and it did not sound like authority.","It felt like existence itself... cracking!"]},{"number":5692,"title":"Chapter 5692: Chapter 5691: One Word!","paragraphs":["The chains shattered.","Multicolored fragments of scorching authority blew outward across the basin and dissolved into nothing before they landed, and from the devoured coffin’s resting place, something rose!","Noah, hoisted and burning in the grip of the Immense One, could not see it.","No one could see it! Its Dimensionality was too high, a walking wound in what was possible, perceivable only by the way existence flinched around its edges, by the prints that appeared in the luminous soil under no feet, by the way the honeyed air bent aside to let something pass!","An invisible part of a being, imperceivable and immense, standing free.","And the first thing it did was not rise toward the eye.","The invisible presence turned, and crossed the ruined grave, and knelt beside a small obsidian slime.","Masamuk lay at the edge of the torn mound where his devouring charge had ended, and Noah’s crushed perception dragged itself toward him, and what it found made his existence buzz.","The slime... was hazy!","Its small obsidian body, the body that contained countless folded dimensions, was losing its edges! Its deep translucent depths were thinning, its drifting stellar motes going out one by one like lamps down a long street, its entire simple form blurring as if the single nanosecond of that glorious devouring had asked for everything, as if the charge and the feast and the freeing had used up all of its existence at once.","And the invisible being held him.","There was nothing to see, and somehow it was unmistakable! The hazy little slime rose gently off the soil, cradled against a presence that could not be perceived, lifted the way something precious is lifted, and Masamuk’s dim crimson eyes looked up into a face that was not there, and tears fell.","Tears, from a splitter of Chaos.","They slid down the blurring obsidian body and dropped onto the ruined grave, and the slime’s soft rasped voice carried across the silent basin, small and breaking and unbearably gentle.","\"If only I remembered. If only.\"","...!","Noah’s existence clenched around the words.","If only I remembered!","He said this while his existence seemingly faded!","Had Masamuk been teetering at an edge this whole time?! Had the melancholic little thing beside the lake been spending its last reserves waiting for one chance, and this was it, and now it was gone?","Or was this only a body, one vessel of something vaster, falling apart while the true existence endured somewhere folded and safe?","The obsidian slime... surely wasn’t dead, right?!","He could not tell! His Regard was crushed, his perception was bleeding, and the haze kept thinning, and above it all, the sky laughed!","|Oh, how touching ,| THE GLOATING JAILER boomed, and its cruelty was unhurried ans entirely unnecessary.","| The little rat spent itself utterly for one embrace it cannot even properly feel. Look at it leaking. Do you know, I could smell something old and sad somewhere in my fields. I assumed it was the grave itself. How delicious to learn my trophy came with a pet.|","The eye’s pressure ground down harder!","| And you, little farmer. You screamed so wonderfully. I do hope the pieces of you remember it, wherever pieces of rats go.|","HUUM!","And then Noah felt something heavy.","Through the crushing, through the grief, through the haze of a dying friend held by an invisible mourner, he perceived the force of nature in the coffin’s wake seemingly RISE.","The unperceivable presence straightened, still cradling the fading slime, and though it had no face and no eyes and no shape his existence could hold, Noah knew with total certainty that it was looking at HIM!","A Piece of Vakochev!","And in the deepest depths of his existence, the crystal shone!","Vakochev’s beacon blazed like a struck flare, pulsing light through his foundations, key and lock finally facing one another across a ruined grave, and an instant later...","The sky stopped playing.","| Enough of this.|","The Immense One applied undeniable force!","There was no wind-up and no flourish! The pressure that had been torture became verdict, the full unveiled seriousness of one of Those Who Remain closing around Noah’s Provenance Dream Body like a hand around a moth, and every defense he had was simply overwhelmed.","The nine-fold golden shields in his quarks blazed and broke! His singularities shrieked in their orbits! His Body, his Precepts, his blazing generated purpose, all of it was pressed past its limits at once, and Noah Osmont, in the last moments of a body that was only a dream, made a choice that no sane existence would make.","He opened himself to ALL of it!","’It is a dream ,’ he thought, savage and clear inside the collapse.","’ No harm comes to my existence. Which means this, right here, is the only place I can ever afford this lesson. So let me feel absolutely everything!’","And he felt it.","He felt his processes seethe and fight to the last.","The third Baryogenesis cycle roared on through the destruction, tempering quarks even as they burst!","His Teloi shields shattered and REFORMED and shattered again, nine aims refusing to stop standing up! His Sanguine weavings boiled, his Tongue pressed against his teeth wanting to speak Words into a dying mouth, every single system he had ever built raging against the verdict with the full stubbornness of his existence, and he catalogued all of it, every failure-point, every seam that held longest, every defense that died well, a complete map of his own limits drawn in his own destruction!","And here was the wonder that the pain could not drown.","Even applying its full seriousness, even with undeniable force, it still took the Immense One more than a nanosecond to finish him!","More than a nanosecond! His quarks did not crumble, they were overcome, each one holding to the last edge of its purpose, and as the final wave crushed inward, as his existence popped like a balloon at last and the Provenance of THE Human Dreamer scattered into radiant blue-gold mist across a ruined Dimension!","The sky spoke over his scattering, and its words were the cruelest it had said all day, because they were not even aimed at him.","As if THE Immense One gad simply killed an insignificant ant.","| Look at that. Yet another lifeform that moved for you, and lived for you, killed senselessly. You really are the worst, Vakochev. So many little ones dying for your sake. That little slime. That old granny. That black spider... so many avoidable deaths. So many...|","...!","The words burned themselves into Noah’s dissolving perception.","His perception guttered. The Dimension smeared. And through the last thinning window of the Dream, Noah saw the eye of the Immense One gain more definition.","Its vast obsidian iris sharpened! Its gold-threaded depths clarified, texture and terrible detail resolving as if the gaze were descending, as if the being behind it had finally decided that watching from above was no longer sufficient, as if it were coming DOWN!","And in the next instant, the part of Vakochev that had been unleashed from the coffin... spoke.","It said a single word, with utmost coldness.","\" Persevere.\"","...!","HUUM!","One word!","One word, and Noah’s scattering perception was granted one final, perfect clarity, as if existence itself insisted he witness this properly.","He perceived every inch of the isolated Dimension at once, the terraced fields, the folded distances, the pale halls, the gold citadel stacked against the layered sky, the thousand lakes with their drowned suns, the hundreds of masked Provenance Lifeforms turning their golden smiles upward in dawning horror as...!","All of it disintegrated.","DISINTEGRATED!","The entire Dimension came apart in a single silent breath, soil and sky and citadel and lakes unmade together, the leashed sovereigns of the eternal Burial dissolving mid-turn with their harvests still in their arms, an era-old jail and every hand that had tended it erased between one fraction of an instant and the next, until nothing remained of the amputated Dimension at all!","Nothing, except a cold eye above!","The obsidian gaze hung alone in the formless dark where a Dimension had just been, stripped of its trophy, its fields, its farmers, and its joke, and only then, only after witnessing that single word do all of that, did Noah entirely feel his perception of this Dream ending!","BOOM!","Noah woke violently!","His body convulsed upward out of the scorching golden waters of THE Vasiliou Primordial Spring, a wave of liquid gold crashing off him as his entire body SHOOK, tremors rolling through him from crown to heel, his hands trembling against the warm rock edge, his breath tearing in and out of lungs that did not need air and demanded it anyway!","The steam pressed close and hot against his skin. The faded skeletons slept below. And his existence rang like a struck bell, because the effects of the torture, of the needles, of the collapse of a body by an Immense One’s undeniable force, had reached all the way back to his TRUE self!","It was several long moments before the shaking stilled.","And then the surge came!","His Provenance and his immensity rose, swelling through his foundations like a tide answering a moon, and prompts cascaded across his vision in radiant waves!","|The Provenance Dream has ended.|","|The Dream Body was destroyed. Your existence is unharmed. Everything felt was retained.|","|Accounting of the Dream begins.|","| Boon: THE Obsidian Journal of Masamuk remains keyed to your existence.|","|Boon: the crystal left behind by Vakochev is TRANSFORMING. Its purpose stirs.|","|Boon: the third cycle of THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis advanced tremendously under the tempering pressure of an Immense One.|","|Grandest Accounting: you stood beneath the direct torture of one of Those Who Remain. Your Records were assaulted, and you remained yourself. Your existence was crushed, and you remained yourself. Remaining true to what you are before a force that unmakes truth is a terrifying difficulty. It has been overcome.|","|Living truly is advancement.|","|VERITAS has risen to 86.|","|PROVENANCE has risen to 86.|","|PONDUS has risen to 78. POTENTIA remains INFINITE.|","...!","Eighty-six!","His attributes had leapt, storming through the seventies in a single accounting, VERITAS and PROVENANCE striking 86 each, the twin measures of what he was and what he generated rising together like two hands of the same body, because he had carried both of them intact through a verdict meant to erase them!","Noah sat back slowly in the golden waters, and let the steam roll over him, and thought about everything.","The grief of a slime that might or might not still exist.","An invisible mourner who had knelt before it had risen. A casualty list spat as a taunt, an old granny and a black spider now etched permanently into his vault of unanswered things.","An eye that had begun to descend. And one word, spoken with utmost coldness, that had unmade an entire Dimension and every leashed sovereign in it faster than his perception could track the unmaking!","Persevere!","The word Masamuk had clung to across an era of emptied rooms. The word the fractured titan had spoken as annihilation. One word, worn two ways, and Noah suspected he had just witnessed the smallest possible fraction of what the maker of the Scales had once been!","He raised his hand, and drew both treasures out of his existence.","The crystal and the grimoire floated before him in the steam, side by side, the strangest pair of inheritances in all of existence! The crystal turned slowly, and it was changing, its obsidian depths swirling with new veins of light that had not been there before, its long silence visibly ending, and yet when his Regard swept across it!","Question marks. Once more, still, rows of question marks.","But the book.","His endlessly blue eyes settled on THE Obsidian Journal of Masamuk, worn round at its edges by an eternity of small handling, filled with the musings of a being who had shaped the first Domains and loved a woman whose name had been stolen from him, and unlike the crystal, unlike the collar, unlike every waiting treasure in his hoard...","The book, he felt, would answer him. From the book... he could at least gain something!"]},{"number":5693,"title":"Chapter 5693: Chapter 5692: The First Entry","paragraphs":["Noah sat within the scorching golden waters of THE Vasiliou Primordial Spring, steam rolling off his stellar body, and grasped THE Obsidian Journal of Masamuk with both hands.","The cover was warm, worn smooth by an eternity of small handling, and it drank the spring’s golden light without returning a single gleam. He held it, and he thought of exactly one thing.","Immense Ones!","He had just been tortured by one. He had hung spread beneath a lidless eye while trillions of needles hunted his loves through his quarks, and he had felt the difference between reading about a terror and being held in its hand!","His knowledge of the architects was a pile of secondhand fragments, warnings, and taunts. That was no longer acceptable. If he was going to survive these beings, and eventually bury them, he wanted to understand much more about them!","’ Show me,’ Noah thought into the warm obsidian. ’ Immense Ones. Everything you rambled about them.’","HUUM!","The journal answered!","It rose gently from his hands and hung in the steam before him, and its cover swung open, and the pages began to flutter!","Endless white pages turned past his eyes, blank and blank and blank, an eternity of unmarked white flowing like a river of snow, until finally the fluttering slowed, and stopped, and the journal lay open to a single white page.","And on that page, words began to appear!","They surfaced out of the whiteness unhurried, dark strokes of old obsidian ink settling into lines, and Noah’s endlessly blue eyes settled onto the first sentence as the voice of a small melancholic slime rose off the paper and wrapped around his mind!","—","<The First Time I Met An Immense One>","There was a time when I was fascinated by THE Immense Ones. There was a time, and I record it here so I cannot deny it later, when I even looked up to them.","The young look up at whatever is tallest. I was young once, though the stars were younger.","In those days, my Master had just finished his grandest work. He had laid his Scales across the whole of Existence, and the whole of Existence was still ringing from the weight of them settling.","Everything that lived woke up that day inside a structure. Everything that lived could suddenly see the rung it stood upon, and the rung above it, and the long ladder going up into the light.","My Master was tired, and proud.","Then the invitation came.","It did not come as a message. It came as a door standing open in a place where no door had been, and my Master looked at it for a long moment, and said only, \" One of the big ones wishes to talk.\"","I asked to come along. I was fascinated, as I have written. I wanted to see one of THE Immense Ones with my own eyes.","He allowed it. I have wondered since whether he allowed it because he wanted a witness.","We stepped through the door carefully, and what we stepped into was...unique.","The place was not a Dimension. It was not an Observable Existence, and it was not one of the Unobservable ones either.","It was a pocket of Narrative Existence.","There are beings whose Dimensionality runs so deep that they can set aside a portion of it and furnish it. The place we entered did not exist anywhere. It existed only inside the depth of the one who had designed it, the way a story exists only inside its teller.","To walk into it was to be included. We were, for the length of our visit, characters in a place she was quietly telling herself.","We stood in a garden at the end of a day that never finished ending.","There were low hills of dark grass that remembered being walked on. There was a porch of grey wood, and on the porch there was a table, and the table was set for two, with a settling warmth upon the cups as though they had been poured moments ago.","She was waiting on the porch.","I will not record her form, because her form was not the truth of her, and also because I could not hold it. What I could hold was the pressure of her, and the pressure was...immeasurably old, and immeasurably tired.","THE Immense One was...","THE REMINISCING WIDOW.","My Master inclined his head to her. She looked at him for a long time before she spoke.","\" You have gone and done it, then ,\" she said. \" You have measured and scaled everything.\"","\"I have given everything a structure ,\" my Master replied.","\" Yes ,\" she said.","She poured nothing, and offered nothing. I stood at the edge of the porch, and I listened to the conversation.","\"I called you here to warn you, \" THE REMINISCING WIDOW said.","\" What you have built may bring you death. Not only you. All you love, and all who love you, down to the smallest thing that has ever smiled at your name. I am telling you this before the others finish deciding how they feel, because once they finish, no telling will matter.\"","My Master was not a man who frightened. He set his hands upon the table, and he asked.","\" Why?\"","\" You will have to be more specific ,\" she said. \" There are so many answers.\"","\"I gave Existence a structure that everyone can follow. Not a decree. A structure. A thing that stands the same for every lifeform that meets it, in every corner, in every era. Before my Scales, the low lived and died without ever knowing where they stood, or whether their striving moved them at all. Power was fog. Standing was rumor. Now every existence that faces adversity can see its own progress with its own eyes. Now the climb is real. All those facing adversity have a chance to elevate themselves, and to know it, and to be known for it.\"","\" Hm .\" she said.","\"I ended the age of begging,\" my Master said. \" You know what standing was before me. Standing was patronage. It was granted, and it was revoked, and it lived in the moods of the mighty. A framework that measures cannot be bribed and cannot be offended. The smallest lifeform in the smallest realm now holds something no architect ever gave it and no architect can take away. A rung.\"","\"Go on,\" she said.","\" And what is measured is protected, \" my Master finished. \" A thing with a recorded standing cannot be quietly erased. It leaves a mark upon the Records of what exists. I have made every life in Existence slightly harder to disappear. Structure...is the only mercy that scales.\"","I remember that I wanted to cheer!","THE REMINISCING WIDOW looked at him through the dusk for a long, long moment.","\" Everything you have said is true, but... \" she said.","She lifted her cup, and did not drink from it, and set it down again.","\" You have heard, I am sure, what the young kinds whisper about my kind. That we are the ones who failed. The apex things that could not exceed themselves when the great exceeding happened. The bitter ones.\"","She was quiet for a moment.","\" Some of us are exactly that. Some of my kind are precisely as small as the whisper says, and they are the loudest of us, and the cruelest, and they will hate your Scales for the plainest reason in Existence. Your ladder tells them, every day, in every corner of reality, that they stopped climbing.\"","\"When your Scales teach the young to climb, you should ask yourself very carefully what you are teaching them to climb TOWARD.\"","BOOM!","I did not understand those words then. I am not certain I understand them now.","My Master was silent for a time. Then he said, \" The others. What do they see, when they look at my work?\"","\"Three things,\" she said. \" First, the insult. You have ranked the unrankable, and dignity at our age is a wound that never closes. Second, the threat. Your structure gives adversity a ladder, and hope is heavy. Despair is formless, and formless things cannot organize.\"","\" And third. The precedent. This is the one that will kill you. How dare you? What gave you the right to blanket all of existence under your scales when those so much grander than you have not?\"","...!","My Master was silent for a long time.","\"Will they attack me? Will they come for the Scales ?\" my Master said.","\" No ,\" said THE REMINISCING WIDOW.","\" They will not come for the Scales first. Destroying a maker’s work only proves the work mattered. They will come for everything that loves you. Death is small, maker. Death is singular, and it ends. I know this...too well.\"","She looked, then, at the second cup on the table, reminiscing !","My Master stood, after a time. He thanked her.","And at the door that was not a door, he stopped, and asked her the question.","\" Why warn me at all?\"","THE REMINISCING WIDOW sat on her porch, in her endless dusk, with her two cups.","\" Because someone once built something grand for my sake, and no one warned him either.\"","...!","The door closed. The evening went on without us.","My Master walked on in silence, and I moved beside him, and he never spoke of that visit again.","I record all of this now, an old thing writing by the light of everything that has since burned down, and I find I have only one remark to close the entry with.","My Master heard every word she said that evening. He weighed them, I am sure, on scales of his own. And then he went on exactly as he had planned, because he was a maker, and makers believe their works can bear any weight.","I have wondered, across all the eras since, whether he should have taken a bit more heed of that warning.","I wondered then.","I wonder still."]},{"number":5694,"title":"Chapter 5694: Chapter 5693: What Has Always Been","paragraphs":["Noah sat in the scorching golden waters of THE Vasiliou Primordial Spring, the closed journal resting warm against his palm.","He reflected on everything Masamuk had recorded.","Vakochev had heard the warning. The maker of the Scales had sat on that porch, listened to an architect lay out the exact shape of his ruin, thanked her sincerely, and walked on exactly as planned. And why not?","He was the grandest maker of his era! His people were shapers and splitters of Chaos, titans who had stood since before authority had a name!","Not one of them, Noah suspected, had truly believed they would face losses. Not one of them had imagined that the existences of those they LOVED could simply be... rewritten.","Unwritten. Carved out like rooms being emptied while the house still stood.","They had prepared for war. No one prepares for erasure!","And the thought turned, as heavy thoughts always did, toward himself.","What if such a thing happened to him?","What if, in the worst scenario, he was made to forget his mother? Made to forget the woman who had stared down a preschool teacher with nothing but night shifts and love in her hands?","What if Henry was carved out of him, his son reduced to a warm gap and an outline on the floor? His women? His daughter? THE Infiniverse, who held his people inside her own body?","Or the other direction, which was somehow worse. What if THEY were made to forget HIM? What if he walked into his own Realm and his mother looked at him with the polite, careful eyes one gives a complete stranger?","\"...\"","It was a horrid thought, and Noah did not look away from it, because looking away from horrid thoughts was how Vakochev’s people had died!","And the biggest thing...","Even Vakochev may never have held this as something that could happen to HIM.","The strongest being of an entire era had likely carried the same quiet certainty Noah caught himself carrying every single day.","The certainty that regardless of what happened, he would be okay . That the story bent toward him. He was THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist, after all! Existence itself had handed him the author’s seat!","But if even Vakochev... if even such a being could be defeated, dismembered, buried under chains, and made into a smug jailer’s favorite joke...","Then even Noah Osmont, THE Human Dreamer, was not immune.","\"...\"","Warm arms found him while he sat in that thought.","Thalia had appeared in the spring without ceremony through that golden doorway, her stellar essence folding through the steam, and she saw his gaze before he could compose it.","She came down through the golden waters and grabbed his head and placed it gently against her chest, her fingers sliding into his hair, her heartbeat steady against his cheek.","\" You have worried eyes again ,\" Thalia said softly. \" How did the talk with my Father go? It made you this melancholic?\"","Noah let himself rest there for a moment, in the small warm feeling of her, and her bountiful chest.","\" He is an interesting guy. I do have to do a lot of things to prove I can even hold you.\"","He felt her huff a quiet laugh above him.","\" But we have to get going to these... Atlas Elseworlds. Atlas was profound enough to make Immense Ones worry and target him, and we need to understand why. We need to-\"","...!","Noah stopped speaking!","His senses blared, every alarm in his two hundred Decillion quarks firing at once, and none of them were pointed at any threat he could find.","What they were pointed at was her. The figure of Thalia Vasiliou, four columns of ninety-nine, the Queenling of the Vasiliou, was trembling and freezing against him!","He took his head out of her chest and looked up, and her face...!","Her eyes showed anger, and beneath the anger, a flash of something he had never once seen in her, not in the pool, not before the Ruling, not before her own mother.","Fear!","And she was not looking at him. She was looking beside him!","Toward the journal!","Noah turned, and his existence went cold, because unseen to his senses, unfelt by a single one of his blaring instincts, THE Obsidian Journal of Masamuk had opened by itself.","It lay upon the warm stone at the spring’s edge, open to the exact page he had just read, the entry of the porch and the dusk and the two cups.","And on that white page, in the middle of the old obsidian ink...","An eye had bloomed!","It was drawn and it was real at once, a single heavy-lidded eye of deep gold rendered upon the paper, and it was not decoration! Its gaze had weight, and its weight was pointed directly at him and Thalia, and words unfurled across the Dimension in the style he knew far, far too well!","| THE REMINISCING WIDOW asks: why will none of you simply leave things be?|","|She asks: why will none of you ever listen?|","BOOM!","Noah MOVED!","His Provenance flared to its absolute totality as every part of his quarks roared awake, nine Teloi igniting through every particle, his Infinite Sanguine Mana surging up through the golden waters in a rising crimson tide!","He grabbed onto Thalia, pulling her against him, and the full weight of THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer gathered behind his eyes as every ounce of power in the Meta-Fictional Protagonist Mantle coiled to erupt, to author, to override, to dream!","BOOM!","But...","Everything froze.","Everything.","The rising tide of Sanguine Mana hung motionless in the air, a sculpture of crimson gold. The steam stopped rolling.","The falls of essence on the Elsemountain above stood still in their descent. The Baryogenesis humming through his quarks paused between one particle and the next, and his Mantle, his Provenance, his Tongue, every authority he had ever generated or stolen or dreamed, sat inside him fully loaded and utterly unable to fire, like a scream held behind a hand!","And from the page, the eye became two.","And then a figure began to rise!","She came up out of the paper the way ink would rise if ink decided to stand, unhurried, vertical, impossible, the white page giving her up in slow flowing folds!","She rose to her full height above the open journal, and the steam of the sacred spring bent politely away from her, and Noah, frozen, beheld THE REMINISCING WIDOW!","She wore the loose draped grace of a highborn woman of some impossibly old court, pale cloth gathered at one shoulder and falling in long unhurried folds, her arms bare, her bearing neither armored nor adorned.","Her figure carried the same heavy settling pressure he read of, feminine and grand and immeasurably tired in a way that had made peace with its tiredness.","And her face!","Her face was astonishingly beautiful, and it could barely be perceived.","It slid off his gaze like light off deep water, arriving only in fragments, the line of a cheek, the suggestion of sorrow, beauty of a magnitude that perception itself refused to hold in full!","And around that half-veiled face floated two halos of golden metal, thin and perfect and slowly turning. One ringed her head at the height of her eyes, framing two heavy-lidded depths of gold. The second floated lower, ringing the height of her mouth, and when she spoke, her words did not come from her lips.","They came from everywhere, in the style of her kind, pressed into the Dimension itself for the two of them to read!","| THE REMINISCING WIDOW speaks, and she speaks sternly.|","|Existential Narrative is the most critical thing that THE Immense Ones hold. It is our marrow. It is our estate. I warned Masamuk, ages ago, not to even peer into us.|","|If you share our records, if you read of me in a journal, my words and what I said ages ago... my Narrative can sense this. The telling reaches back to its owner. You then give me access.|","|I warned him. I warned his Master on my own porch, with my own evening. He did not listen. His Master did not listen. And now an old entry is read beside a sacred spring, and here I am, because none of you ever, ever listen.|","The two golden halos turned slowly, and her half-perceived gaze settled upon the frozen pair in the water, and the dusk of her deepened until the golden spring itself seemed to dim toward evening.","| So she asks, and she is tired of asking: if warnings are not enough, just what do I need to do for you all to leave things alone?|","|There is no scenario of change.|","| There is no scenario of victory.|","|There is only what is... and what has always been.|","BOOM!","The words settled over the spring like a lid over a coffin!","Noah’s eyes swirled with endless seas of blue! His Infinite Sanguine Mana RAGED against the stillness, a boundless ocean throwing itself at the inside of a single frozen moment, his quarks howling, his Teloi blazing, his Mantle straining to author a single syllable of override, and none of it moved!","Not a finger. Not a thought made real. He, who had torn an architect’s executioner in half, who had walked through an ancient boundary as though it were a dream, who had endured the torture of a lidless eye and come out heavier!","He looked at the manifestation of an Immense One standing on the page of a journal, risen out of ink and an old evening, and he could not move!","Thalia was frozen against his chest. The spring was frozen around them. The golden skeletons slept below, and above them all stood a widow in her endless dusk, patient and stern and immeasurably sad.","Catastrophe had arrived far, far too soon!"]},{"number":5695,"title":"Chapter 5695: Chapter 5694: A Kindness To Kill!","paragraphs":["She looked at them the way an era looks at a single day!","THE REMINISCING WIDOW had risen from the page of an obsidian journal, and she stood above the golden spring with her barely-perceivable face angled down, her two golden halos turning their slow deliberate circles in the steam-heavy air, and she did not move or speak as she regarded the two small frozen figures below her.","She did not need to hurry. She had presided over evenings that outlasted kingdoms, and two lifeforms arrested mid-embrace in a sacred spring were not, by any measure of her long experience, cause for urgency!","The dusk she carried pressed down as her gold eyes swept across the figure of Thalia Vasiliou and settled upon THE True Human Emperor, and she spoke!","|THE REMINISCING WIDOW speaks.|","|It is always the same. Lifeforms touch power. They look at the existing structure. And then they promise themselves that they will change it.|","|Why?|","|There is a system in place, and no matter its potential negatives, it has been working. Those like you, when you seek to enact change, cause such tremendous bloodshed. Truly. All you need to do is stop.|","The halos pulsed, golden light rippling through the steam!","|I permit you to speak.|","...!","Noah moved!","The golden spring erupted around him as he came free, his Infinite Sanguine Mana surging up in a massive crimson tide, his eighty-six Provenance singularities igniting across every particle of his Baryogenesis-hardened existence, nine Teloi blazing through two hundred Decillion Provenance Telos Quarks as the weight of THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist Mantle coiled behind his eyes with the pressure of a narrative about to be REWRITTEN!","And then he said absolutely nothing.","He took his time with it! He turned slowly in the golden water and he faced the manifestation standing above him, this impossible figure of dusk and golden light and barely-perceivable grief, and he looked at her with the full swirling weight of his existence behind his eyes, and he was simply, completely, wordlessly silent.","She had told him he could speak. She had permitted him.","Just because she permitted him, he now had to?","He chose not!","But while his mouth stayed shut his mind did not, as behind those seas of blue, THE True Human Emperor thought at the speed of a being whose quarks had each carried the weight of Existence and survived it.","He stared at the Immense One and he worked, because something about this entire picture was wrong in a way that the threat itself could not account for!","Masamuk had known. He had to have known! The ancient slime had existed since before the first Domains had a name, had served the grandest maker of his era, had suffered the stripping of every loved memory and still endured, and he had sat in a Dimension with three Provenance Causes and the weight of Vakochev’s chained weavings pressing down on him, and he had willingly handed Noah his journal!","He had known what was written in it! He had known that reading it could do exactly this!","So why?","Would a being who had suffered so precisely not understand the danger? Would a mind that had persevered through eras of loss make an oversight so catastrophic?","Noah’s eyes held steady on the Widow’s golden rings and he turned the question over and over as his Teloi hummed their low burning note through his matter, searching for the answer that a grieving ancient slime had buried somewhere in the ink!","And one sentence surfaced above all the others!","A single line from the closing of the entry, the thing Vakochev had asked at the door when the evening was ending and the warning was finished. WHY warn him at all?","And she had answered!","Because someone once built something grand for my sake, and no one warned him either.","\"...\"","Someone had built something grand for her sake. Nobody had warned him!","And Masamuk had known this too!","There was something in that! Something Noah had not yet pulled to the surface, but he was circling it now as his existence hummed with the warmth of a coming understanding.","Above him, THE REMINISCING WIDOW looked at his silence with patience that had no floor to it, and the golden halo at her mouth pulsed once, and she spoke again.","|Vakochev is done for. He was done for across many deaths and ages of pain inflicted upon him and all those who loved him. You are reading the musings of one of his greatest, and yet I hold no memory of you, which means you are not one of Vakochev’s people.|","|You are one of those like him. One of those with Boundless Potential. Infinite Potential.|","|Lifeforms like you are walking disasters. You carry a sense of infinite hunger within you that you cannot quiet and will not quiet, and you bring destruction and apocalypse to every corner of existence your trajectory sweeps across. The greatest threat to your people is not any enemy you will face. It is you. People like you who simply will not stop.|","|You do not need any of this. You could sit still on a farm somewhere. You could enjoy your family, your feasts, your people, let the millions and millions of years of existence wash over you and hold you warmly. Existence will continue to unfold without you. It has done so since before your kind had eyes to witness it.|","|Just stop.|","|I warned Vakochev before he fell. He did not stop. I warn you now. If I must be forceful, if ending you here is the necessary kindness to save countless lifeforms the pain your trajectory will inflict on them, I will do so.|","BOOM!","She descended!","She came down through the steam and the golden light, the halos orbiting her descent, her form lowering until her barely-perceivable face was close, until the dusk of her filled the whole of Noah’s vision and the pressure of an attended eternity sat in the air between them!","\" Will you stop?\"","...!","Noah looked at Thalia.","She was frozen at his side, the Queenling of the Vasiliou, with her eyes wide and that first-ever flash of fear across her face, and for one stretched instant he held that sight and felt everything that lived inside him on the subject of it.","And then he spoke!","\" I cannot stop ,\" Noah said. \" Nobody knows this. But I live in constant fear! Fear of exactly something like this, a power I cannot deny standing before me and I cannot even lift a finger against it! Because of exactly something like this, I cannot stop! I have to attain more power! I have to find the absolute peak of existence to make sure that nothing can ever stand before me and simply decide my fate!\"","HUUUM!","THE REMINISCING WIDOW looked at him, and her gold eyes held no anger, and they held no mockery.","\" But this is only because you will not stop,\" she said.","\"If you stop, nothing like me will appear before you again. You will have no need for that fear.\"","Noah shook his head!","\"I live in fear that if I ever retreat to my farm, if I simply live and eat and love my family and do nothing to advance, we will all one day die from a choice others like you made! My Dimension collapsed without our say! My people were ground beneath an existence they never once consented to stand inside! Existence itself changed around us without a word in our direction!\"","His Provenance blazed through the steam as his voice held its quiet and steady weight. \" If I do nothing, if I stop, I would live every day of every million years feeling like an ant. Waiting for a boot I cannot see, held by a foot I cannot name, and knowing that when it falls it will find everyone I love standing beside me. And I will have been the one who decided that the feast was worth more than the capacity to PROTECT the feast!\"","He looked at the barely-perceivable face before him and let both things be true at once, the fear and the refusal of the fear, and his voice did not waver!","\" So no. Regardless of what you say here. Regardless of what happens today! \" A pause, as his singularities blazed their quiet blue-gold light through the golden water. \"I cannot stop. My fear will not let me. My Quintessence will not let me. My humanity...\"","BOOM!","\"... will not let me!\"","The spring held its quiet around those words.","THE REMINISCING WIDOW looked at him.","| THE REMINISCING WIDOW looks at you, and she grieves, and she speaks her decision.|","|Then for the sake of saving the pain and deaths of many, even your own people, I will end you.|","|Every point of your origin across Existence and Time. I will make it so that you never exist, so that your people and many others can attain salvation from what your trajectory would bring them.|","|It is the kindness I can give you.|","...!"]},{"number":5696,"title":"Chapter 5696: Chapter 5695: It Is Never So Easy!","paragraphs":["Power was not going to save him today!","Noah stood in a frozen spring with an Immense One’s declaration hanging over everything, and he understood there was no way.","His Provenance blazed, his Teloi burned through his quarks, his Mantle coiled with narrative weight enough to rewrite a battlefield, and none of it mattered against something like this.","Her Dimensionality was too unfathomable.","So he did the only other thing he knew how to do!","He thought.","Not ordinary thinking, but thinking elevated by his very Provenance of THE Human Dreamer, as his eyes stayed fixed on the barely-perceivable face of THE REMINISCING WIDOW....","Noah pulled THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer deep into himself and turned it fully inward.","The Human Dreamer was a Lens. And right now it turned on everything he had read!","Everything in his existence became dreamlike as he envisioned himself thinking at speeds as if time had stopped, and his existence analyzing and having epiphanies every instant as he dreamed of information and solutions.","His entire existence became surrounded by a dreamy light as his eyes even seemed heavy as if he would soon fall asleep, and yet his eyes were...ridiculously bright!","He began to think.","What did he KNOW about her?","The journal entry! He had read every word of it while she was still ink on a page. She had sat on a porch in an endless dusk at a table set for two, with one chair ever sat in and a second cup kept almost warm.","She had warned Vakochev because of something that had happened to HER, because someone had built something grand for her sake and nobody had warned him either, and she had been attending evenings alone ever since!","She was a WIDOW!","Which meant she had not always been one!","Which meant there was someone, once, who had sat in the second chair and drunk from the second cup, and she had watched that someone be ended, and the second cup had been almost warm ever since because she could not bring herself to stop filling it!","But there was more! She had warned Vakochev! She had called him to her porch and laid out the full anatomy of his ruin, piece by careful piece, and then she had let him walk away.","She had not stopped him! She had not ended him on the spot the way she now threatened to end Noah, for all that the result of his not-stopping was exactly the catastrophe she had predicted.","Why?","Why warn someone if you believe the warning cannot matter? Why give a choice to something you believe will choose wrong?","His Provenance ran faster, linking, linking, linking!","And Noah felt the understanding arrive like a dreamy knowledge of brilliance as his eyes cut upward to the barely-perceivable face of the Immense One above him and his mouth opened.","\" What about you?\"","\"THE REMINISCING WIDOW .\" He held her barely-perceivable gaze without flinching. \" Who made you a Widow? Did you simply stop? Your love that they killed... would he have wanted you to stop?\"","BOOM!","Existence buzzed!","The golden warmth of THE Vasiliou Primordial Spring vanished beneath an instant blanket of frost and cold as temperature dropped across the whole region of the Elsedimension.","She looked at him!","For a long, long moment she simply looked at him.","|THE REMINISCING WIDOW speaks: careful now.|","|There are things you can speak of. And things that will bring your ruin far quicker.|","\"...\"","Noah did not move back.","He held his ground in that frozen spring with Thalia motionless beside him and his entire existence at a full stop.","\" You did not stop ,\" he said!","| THE REMINISCING WIDOW is still.|","\"The second cup in that memory,\" Noah said. \" You still fill it. After everything. After every era that has passed since the one who sat there last. You still go out onto that porch, in that endless dusk you carry with you everywhere, and you set the table for two, and you keep the second cup almost warm. That is not someone who stopped.\"","Frost crystals ticked softly against frozen water in the silence that followed!","THE REMINISCING WIDOW did not respond immediately, as the gold of her eyes, heavy-lidded and ancient and full of a sorrow she had long since made peace with, pulsed!","She spoke unfathomably slowly.","| He...was not like the ones who came before or after him.|","And for the first time in the conversation something in the Widow’s bearing shifted.","| He made immensity itself. Everything he designed, everything he shaped and carved and made real, he made it so it could exist without him. So it could outlast him. So others could find their way inside it long after his hands were gone.|","Her gaze found something beyond the spring, beyond the Elsedimension, something that only existed inside the depths of her!","| He believed that existence deserved better architecture. He spent... a very long time on it.|","\"And he was ended for it, \" Noah said.","| Yes.|","\"By beings like you.\"","The cold deepened for one instant and then settled again, and her voice remained exactly level.","| By those of us who looked at what his foundations were pointing at, and made the same calculation I made when I looked at Vakochev’s Scales. That the direction of the pointing would bring tremendous death to countless lifeforms before any destination was reached...Yes.|","Noah’s eyes pulsed as he felt like he was a opening a door, and he needed to spread it much wider.","He had to spread it wide!","\" You warned Vakochev, but you did not end him there. You gave him the choice.\"","|I gave him the information. The choice was always his.|","\"Why? Why give a choice to something you believe will choose wrong? If the outcome is catastrophe either way, why warn? Why call him to the porch at all?\"","The golden halos pulsed! The Widow was quiet for a moment that stretched!","| Because I am not in the business of stealing choices from beings who have the capacity to make them. Even wrong ones.|","Her eyes held steady on him.","| Even from beings who will make exactly the wrong one.|","\"That sounds,\" Noah said quietly, \" like someone who is not entirely certain the choice is wrong.\"","HUUM!","| THE REMINISCING WIDOW does not answer.|","\"Vakochev could not stop, \" Noah said, and his voice was very gentle now.","\" Not because he was reckless. Not because he was careless of the cost. But because of who he was. He was the kind of being who looked at the way things were and could not rest inside the wrongness of them.\"","He looked up at her. \" Is a river wrong to flow downhill? Is it a flaw in the river’s nature that it carves the canyon?\"","|Rivers carve canyons.|","She said it casually.","| And the canyon floor becomes a grave for everything that falls in.|","\"Yes, \" Noah said. \" And the river also carries everything forward. And makes things grow. And finds the sea.\"","He looked up at her barely-perceivable face, at the sorrow arriving in fragments.","\" The one who built something grand for your sake... he was that kind of river too, wasn’t he? He could not look at the way things were built and simply accept it. He had to try to build something better. Not for himself. For others. He could not stop that drive any more than Vakochev could. Any more than I can.\"","The frost on the spring’s surface crackled softly!","\"...\"","\" And he was ended for it, \" Noah said, \" by those who thought that stopping him was a kindness to the many. The same calculation you are making about me, right now.\"","He held her gaze.","\" Does that mean they were right? Does it mean that if someone had simply convinced him to stop, to go to his farm and enjoy his ages and trouble no one, that existense would have been better?\"","\" Or does it mean that existence lost something it did not know it needed, and the only monument to that loss is a second cup on a table in an endless dusk that you can never bring yourself to stop filling?\"","|THE REMINISCING WIDOW is very still.|","The cold was absolute. The frost was absolute. The silence was absolute!","And then, slowly, the gold of the heavy-lidded eyes that had been looking at him from above the height of the spring lowered, just slightly, just one degree, as a thought arrived in them that had not been invited!","And for just a moment, one frost-cracked moment that stretched wider than it should have, something moved across the barely-perceivable face.","It was doubt!","And then it was gone, and her composure returned, and she looked at him, and she blinked once, and when her eyes opened again they held a different quality, something sharpening beneath the heaviness, a mind arriving at a conclusion that had nothing to do with him!","| Ah .|","It was barely a word! It was the sound a vastly experienced intelligence makes when it catches itself being played.","| Ah, I see. That little slime gave you these records purposefully. So that I could meet you like I met them ages ago.|","The gold eyes were steady on him now, and something in their depths was almost, almost amused.","| That little slime... was trying to manipulate an Immense One? To use my name, and what happened to me, to what end? Instead of warn, now support another one of the monsters of existence?|","The frost held its silence around them!","And then from the Widow above the journal above the frozen spring, in a voice that had not changed its composure by a single degree, came the one thing Noah had not expected to hear from an Immense One who had just declared his erasure!","A sound that was almost, almost a laugh!","| Haha.|","Her golden halos turned.","| Is it so easy?|","...!"]},{"number":5697,"title":"Chapter 5697: Chapter 5696: Probability! I","paragraphs":["|THE REMINISCING WIDOW speaks: you know what? I will leave it entirely up to chance.|","The frost held its stillness across the whole of the spring as the golden halos turned!","|You are throwing arguments that you are like Vakochev. Or like someone you cannot even fathom. Someone whose name you have not earned the right to hold in your mouth.|","|Okay.|","|Let us put that to the test.|","She waved her hand!","BOOM!","A blinding singularity bloomed in the frozen air above the spring, and Noah’s eyes narrowed against it as the light collapsed inward on itself and left something spinning slowly in the space where it had been!","A ring.","It was gray, and it was small, and it was the least impressive object Noah had ever seen an Immense One produce.","It turned in the air without hurry, and across its outer band ran lines that did not behave, lines that went around the ring and came back on the other side without ever crossing an edge, an outside that was also the inside, a single unbroken surface pretending to be two.","And on its interior, where a finger would go, there were spikes!","They filled the inner circumference completely, dozens of them, gray and sharp and angled inward toward the center, leaving no opening at all. Not a narrow opening. Not a difficult one.","None.","It was a ring that could not be worn, and it had been made that way on purpose.","| This was left behind by a special someone.|","The Widow’s voice pressed into the frozen air from everywhere at once.","|I have not been able to figure it out. Neither has any other Immense One I have given it to, and I have given it to several, across a great many eras. It has been examined by minds that predate the frameworks you climb.|","|If you wish to throw arguments that you are like others, if you wish to compare yourself to them...|","|Put this ring on.|","The gold of her eyes did not move from him.","|If you can put that ring on, I will spare you. You may continue your path. The path that will inevitably lead to more deaths than you will ever be able to count.|","...!","The ring drifted toward him through the frozen steam.","Noah watched it come, and his gaze became heavy.","How the hell would he be able to put on a ring that even Immense Ones could not figure out?!","They had eras. He had a conversation! They had Dimensionality that made his own look like a puddle beside a sea, and they had turned this small gray thing over in their attention and set it back down without an answer!","The ring reached him.","Noah’s hand rose out of the frozen water and closed around it, and it was cold, and it was heavier than it had any right to be, and the spikes pressed against his palm.","THE REMINISCING WIDOW looked down at him coldly.","|Well? Put it on.|","|You are just like them, are you not? Like Vakochev. Like the one whose foundations I watched be broken.|","|There will be no thinking you can talk your way out of this after. You have had your conversation. If the ring does not go on, there will simply be a thorough narrative ending for all parts of your existence, across every point of origin you have ever occupied.|","....!","It felt like a taunt from death itself!","Noah ignored the words entirely.","He closed his eyes.","He held the ring in both hands, in that frozen spring, with Thalia motionless beside him and an Immense One’s verdict hanging over the whole of the Elsedimension, and he felt it.","He turned it over. He examined every part of the thing with senses that had catalogued Existential Treasures and Remnants and the bones of First Lifeforms.","And all he saw was question marks!","Naturally, he wanted to try infusing it with his Provenance, to push a thread of himself into that gray band and see whether anything at all would answer, but...","CRACK!","His existence shook.","Noah’s eyes flew open as he felt something crack inside him, something deep, something that had been sitting in his existence for some time now that he had stopped feeling its weight, and he looked down at his own chest with genuine shock as he realized what it was!","THE Aurate Collar!","The treasure he had taken from THE Ymnaros Dimension! The chest bones of a Provenance Lifeform, the covenant object of THE First Purity, the thing that had produced the white pool and everything that had come out of it!","It was breaking!","He felt it come apart inside his existence, piece by piece, the bone splitting along lines he had never known were there, and it did not shatter into fragments and it did not burn away!","It turned to liquid!","Bronze liquid, thick and slow and shining, flowed out of his existence in a stream that passed through his chest and down his arm and out of him entirely, and Noah watched with his mouth slightly open as the treasure he had worn poured out of him and went toward the small gray ring in his hands.","The liquid wrapped around it!","It coated the band and ran along the impossible lines and filled the inside of the ring completely, and where it touched, the spikes began to RECEDE.","They drew back into the inner wall of the ring, slowly, one after another, sliding inward and vanishing as though they had never been forged there at all.","THE REMINISCING WIDOW blinked!","Noah saw it. He saw an Immense One who had not moved a single degree of her composure across the entire conversation, who had declared his erasure blink down at his hands with something that was unmistakably incredulity!","And Noah was incredulous too!","No way, right?","And in the next moment, the ring moved!","It tore itself out of his hands on its own and shot to his right hand and drove itself onto his finger, and the spikes had not receded all the way!","SHRK!","They tore through his skin as though his defenses did not exist!"]},{"number":5698,"title":"Chapter 5698: Chapter 5697: Probability! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s crimson gold blood welled up instantly around the band, and there was no resistance at all, no interception, none of his Provenance Body’s layers doing anything whatsoever, and his blood ran hot down his finger and into the gray metal.","And the ring drank it.","It sucked the crimson gold in greedily, absorbing every drop that touched it, and only THEN, only after it had tasted his blood, did the remaining spikes fully recede and the band clasp itself around his finger.","And then it began to shine!","Gold erupted along the ring’s surface, a terrifying gold, deep and old and heavier than any light Noah had ever generated. The impossible lines on its outer band lit up and began to pulse, the single unbroken surface running its endless circuit, light chasing itself around a shape that had no outside and no inside, faster and faster and faster!","The ring clasped tight on his finger and...","BOOM!","A blinding golden light detonated across the frozen spring!","And with it came a VOICE! A voice that felt old, and elegant, and filled with a kind of ingenuity that Noah recognized instantly as belonging to a mind that had never once in its existence been satisfied with how things were.","| Before the first light, before the first law, we were, and we were our own...|","...!","Those words!","Noah’s whole existence went rigid, because he knew those words! They were the words of THE Aurate Collar! The covenant voice that had repeated inside it since the moment he had put it on.","The words he had spoken, only the first line of them, to trigger THE Provenance Kismet of First Purity, which had produced the white pool, which had opened across time and delivered Thalia Vasiliou into his Realm!","He heard them again now, in his mind, in that golden light.","And this time, they continued!","| Before the first light, before the first law, we were, and we were our own...Nothing granted, nothing borrowed, nothing owed. What I am, I made. Let existence bear witness.|","HUUM!","The words resounded again and again in his mind, rolling through him, and Noah understood exactly what was being asked of him, because it was the same thing that had been asked of him once before, when he had spoken only a single line of it and existence had answered.","This time he said the whole thing.","\" Before the first light, before the first law, we were, and we were our own...Nothing granted, nothing borrowed, nothing owed. What I am, I made. Let existence bear witness!\"","HUUM!","Every particle of the blinding golden light vanished instantly!","Noah blinked in the sudden absence of it, standing in the frozen spring with steam frozen around him, and he looked down at his right hand where a golden ring now sat on his finger, pulsing slowly, its impossible lines still running their endless circuit.","Then he looked up at THE REMINISCING WIDOW.","She was extremely still.","And Noah’s eyes pulsed, because shockingly, unbelievably...","He could see her!","Not fragments. Not a line of a cheek arriving and sliding away. Not a beauty that perception itself refused to hold. He looked up at the Immense One standing above the frozen spring and he could actually see and perceive her cleanly!","And just as he began to truly look at her...","The ring on his hand became unfathomably hot!","And a grand booming voice erupted out of it, only for him to hear.","| Destiny and fate are not real. Not entirely, anyway.|","|What is real is probability. Destiny and fate are merely the outcomes of probabilities, and every outcome that has ever been called inevitable was simply a number that got large enough to look like a law.|","|So consider the numbers, whoever you are.|","|The probability of my ring landing in the hands of a lifeform who is not an Immense One, when I left it in the keeping of an Immense One. And then, on top of that, the probability of that same lifeform independently satisfying two of the prior conditions I set, so that the ring could actually trigger and activate.|","|The probability of both of those events occurring is so infinitesimally low that for them to happen at all, the lifeform in question has to be someone who beats the odds.|","|They have to be someone who can bend Narrative Probability.|","|And with such a lifeform... maybe there is a chance.|","|Hello, and welcome to these crazy weavings of life.|","|I am Atlas.|","|And I hope that maybe, just maybe, your probability, and your capability to bend it, is grander than mine was. For existence is vast, and there is much to be done.|","...!","Atlas?","THE Atlas?!","Noah’s existence buzzed with pure incredulity as the name landed in him and detonated.","THE ENGINEER!","The one who ran circles around Immense Ones! The being who had designed Elsedimensions and Provenance Body arts and weapons made to kill architects, the one whose legacy Aurelius Vasiliou had told him to go and find!","That Atlas!","And the second understanding arrived right behind the first, faster and heavier.","So HE was the man who made THE REMINISCING WIDOW into a widow.","The one who sat in the second chair! The one whose cup was still being kept almost warm at a table in an endless dusk after however many eras had passed.","He had been out here, this early, close enough to an Immense One that she had spent every age since setting a place for him at her table!","But even as Noah was thinking all this...","| Now, since we are here, let us play some more games of probability and choices. Okay?|","...!","The voice echoed out of the golden ring on his finger, entirely too pleased with itself.","| Because maybe, even after all those different probabilities are met, there could still be a factor of luck. And luck is a variable I never liked leaving in a design.|","|So here is a choice.|","|You have somehow gotten a grand artifact designed by me, out of the hands of an Immense One.|","|Will you keep the artifact and infuse it with your Provenance? You may consider it a weapon that could topple an Immense One, if it is used correctly.|","|Or the second option. Will you give it back to the Immense One?|","|It carries some sentimentality.|","...!"]},{"number":5699,"title":"Chapter 5699: Chapter 5698: Engineer! I","paragraphs":["Noah controlled his expression, and internally he cursed with everything he had.","What fucking choice?!","Because there was no choice. The choice to be made here was clear, and it was horrible, and it was clear precisely because it was horrible.","A weapon that could topple an architect, offered to a man standing frozen in front of one, and the correct answer was to hand it back!","Noah did not hesitate.","He gripped the golden ring and physically pulled it off his finger, the metal coming free without resistance now, and he drew his arm back and threw it up through the frozen steam toward THE REMINISCING WIDOW!","\" This ring was given to you.\"","His voice carried across the whole of the frozen spring!","\" It is a grand artifact and I could choose to keep it. But I know what it means to you. It was the last thing he gave you. \" He watched it turn end over end as it rose toward her. \" You can now put it on.\"","The ring reached her.","THE REMINISCING WIDOW caught it.","She did not speak as she held the small golden band in fingers that Noah could see clearly now, and she looked at it for a length of time that had no measure to it, in a silence so complete that the frost stopped ticking against the frozen water.","And then she put it on her finger.","BOOM!","Her two golden halos EXPANDED!","They swelled outward from her face and multiplied, ring after ring after ring blooming into existence around her head, growing and layering and overlapping until her entire visage was surrounded and buried behind them, circle upon circle of turning golden metal that hid her completely.","She... did not want a single one of her emotions to be seen!","Noah understood that immediately.","And in the place where the ring had been, in the empty air where it had spun before he ever touched it, Noah alone saw a faint golden brilliance still hanging there.","A residue. A remainder. Something left behind that only his eyes could find!","And out of it, into his mind, came a laugh!","| Haha! You actually gave it away?|","Atlas!","| You dumbass, I would have actually let you keep it!|","Noah’s eye twitched!","| Haha! But no. It was not something you made. So giving it away was the right choice, and you would not have liked what you became if you had kept it.|","| That was one of my finest creations. A Gu Elsedimension Ring.|","|But I will help you make your OWN, so that you remain true to yourself. Our Provenances are grand, and yet we still cannot do things alone. I will make sure you learn to become a grand Engineer in your own right.|","|Understand what I am, before you get any ideas. I am here and not really here. I am a cluster of records and probability. I do not have my own cognizance.|","|For now, say goodbye to the one who loved the wrong person. Being near an Immense One for too long will alert him.|","|I learned that the hard way.|","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed.","He looked up through the frozen steam at THE REMINISCING WIDOW, at the layered halos hiding her entirely, at the hand that had lowered from them and was now turning the golden ring slowly on her finger, stroking it with a thumb, over and over, in the manner of someone who had done this exact motion in her mind ten thousand times without anything actually being there.","And Noah spoke, and his voice was heavy.","\" You need to go.\"","The stroking did not stop!","\"I did what you wanted. I even reunited you with his weavings, and you may be hearing his voice even now.\" He held his ground in the frozen water with Thalia motionless behind him. \" Your presence here alone is a danger to me. So you... need to go.\"","...!","The halos turned!","|Yet another person I warned.|","|And who did not listen.|","The frost held its silence around them, and when her words came again it was slower, and it carried a weight of melancholy that had nothing performative in it at all!","| You all... I truly do not know what to say to you all anymore.|","|Do whatever you want. Build whatever you wish to build. Climb whatever you have decided to climb. And when death inevitably comes for you, and it will come, you will remember me. You will remember this evening, and this spring, and every word I said to you.|","|They always do.|","|For doing what you have done for me today, I owe you a favor.|","|You know how you can reach me.|","...!","And with those words, THE REMINISCING WIDOW departed!","Her visage folded downward through the frozen air, the layered halos collapsing inward one by one, her draped form flowing back down toward the obsidian journal lying open at the spring’s edge, and she sank into the page she had risen from as the ink drank her back into itself!","The eye on the page closed.","And everything came back!","Warmth crashed across the Elsedimension as the frost broke apart into vapor and the ice sheeting the spring’s surface shattered into golden water, the steam rolling again, the falls resuming their long descent down the Elsemountain, the entire region returning to what it had been before an architect had decided to visit.","And Thalia unfroze.","She came out of it moving, crossing the water in an instant, and she threw her arms around Noah from behind and locked them across his chest and held on.","Noah’s hands came up and closed over hers.","He breathed out, long and slow, and let his head tilt back, and stood there in the scorching golden water with her arms around him, because he had just walked out of a catastrophe that should have ended every point of his existence across all of time, and he had walked out of it with a favor owed!","And in his mind...","| Has she left?|","Atlas!","|If she has, we can proceed ahead. Find a place where you can privately work.|","|Because I was a genius, and I always found everyone else to be imbeciles. Even Immense Ones. I do not know how much work it will take to teach you to be even a percentage of the engineer that I was.|","|Ah, to be a genius like me.|","Noah’s eye twitched again!","| Get going, O Provenance of Existence. O Chance of Chances. O Author of Probability.|","|Let us see if you will better fit all those titles, because even I could not fully live up to them. But maybe what I could not do, you may manage to do.|","|Let us see.|","|Send your Provenance onto the residual Elsedimension Ring when you are ready to get started, and we will begin.|","...!"]},{"number":5700,"title":"Chapter 5700: Chapter 5699: Engineer! II","paragraphs":["Thalia unflinchingly...did not let him go.","The spring had returned to what it was, and the steam had come back, and the falls were running down the Elsemountain again as though nothing at all had happened here. Yet her arms stayed locked across his chest, tight, as if he would be gone if she let go.","Of course, she had reason. She had spent that entire conversation frozen, watching an architect stand over the man she had crossed time to reach, unable to move so much as a finger in his direction. There are worse things than danger. Being present for it and useless is one of them.","\" That was... an Immense One, \" she said against his back. \" How did they even...\"","The question did not finish. In truth, it did not need to!","Then she asked the other one.","\"And you. My Provenance, are you really fearful all the time? Do you truly live with fear constantly?\"","Noah turned in her arms.","He took her by the shoulders and drew her in, and their noses brushed.","\" Yes ,\" he said. \" Constantly .\"","Her eyes moved between his.","\"For humans like us, fear was never the enemy. Fear is the oldest teacher our kind ever had. It is the thing that told the first of us to look up at a sky we did not understand and ask what lived in it. It is what built every wall and lit every fire and made a person check the dark before they slept, and every one of those was a small refusal to simply lie down and accept whatever came.\"","He held her gaze.","\" Fear is a drive that makes sure a man does not remain still. It sharpens what love makes soft. It keeps me honest about what I actually am rather than what I would like to be. I thought I gave away my everything of fear and doubt before, but...it was always there.\"","He shrugged, and the shrug was small.","\" Being afraid and moving anyway is what a true human has always been good at.\"","Thalia looked at him for a long moment.","Then the tears came, and she did not wipe them away or apologize for them or seem to notice them at all. She simply took his face in both hands and started kissing him, small pecks, everywhere, his cheek and his brow and the bridge of his nose and the corner of his mouth, over and over, as though she could cover every part of him that carried something heavy.","\" Let me carry some of your fear,\" she said between them. \" Some of your weight.\"","Another kiss, at his temple.","\" In that possible future, I know you carry so much weight. I have seen what it makes of you. Let me carry even a percentage of it for you. \"","Noah stayed in the moment.","He was not, generally speaking, a man who stayed in moments. Yet here he was, standing in scorching golden water with an unfathomable woman holding his face in her hands, and he did nothing at all except look at her.","Then he shook his head.","\" In existence, a man has his duties,\" he said. \"I know you can carry any weight you want to carry. But my job is to bear everything, so that you and many others can live happily without needing to bend your backs.\"","He brushed a thumb under her eye and took the tear away.","\" Do not worry about any weight I carry. I can handle it. I have a grand Provenance, and I have infinite musing to allow me to do so . For me, it is normal.\"","...!","Thalia looked at him.","And whatever she had been holding back since she came out of that pool, since the frozen instant, since the future she would not describe, she stopped holding it back.","Her clothing fell away, and the mist of the spring rose and covered her, and she pushed him down into the golden water.","Then the light came.","Golden brilliance flooded the whole of the spring, filling the basin and rising up the walls of this region of the Elsedimension until the steam itself burned gold. Nothing at all could be seen through it!","And nothing at all was seen.","—","<Aurelius Vasiliou>","Far from that spring, at the top of a golden tower that had stood since before the current arrangement of things, two Provenance Lifeforms watched their people move.","Vasileia Elsecity, among other names it had, spread out beneath them in tiers of pale stone and hanging light. Dozens of the lineage moved through it at this hour, going about the small business that even the grandest existences cannot escape.","Aurelius Vasiliou looked down at all of it with his hands behind his back.","Beside him, Rosalia Vasiliou watched the Provenance Lifeforms below.","\"Is this really the right choice? \" she asked. \" For us to go to war against an Immense One?\"","Compared to most questions asked in that tower, it was a simple one. She was not arguing. She had come to the same conclusions he had, most likely before he had, since she usually did. She was asking her husband to say it out loud so that she could hear how it sounded in the open air.","Aurelius took his time.","\" Maybe our Provenance shines brighter in the end for it,\" he said . \"I have thought about this more than I have thought about anything in my life, and I keep arriving at the same place. For years I woke with the same picture in my head. My daughter, promised away, handed up to a thing that would use her for whatever it needed and then set her down somewhere quiet when the use ran out. That was the safe road. That was the road where our lineage endured and our name stayed on the lists and nobody came for our Elsedimension. I would have walked it. I was walking it. And every year of it made me smaller.\"","\" Then an existence appears who generates his own Provenance out of nothing anybody gave him, who stands a chance at anything touching Atlas. And I find that I would rather take that bet. Not because the odds are good. Because a bet at least has a second outcome.\"","Rosalia was quiet for a while.","\" And him? \" she said. \" This Human Dreamer. This Osmont. You had your talk with him.\"","\"It seems like he may treat our daughter well.\" Aurelius made a sound that was almost a laugh, which was rare enough that his wife turned her head.","\" She is stronger than him at present, by a considerable margin. So at the very least, she will keep him in line.\"","Below them, complex weavings of Provenance Lifeforms unfolded.","The two Provenance Lifeforms stood above their city and talked about their daughter, and about the war that was coming, and about whether the choice they had made would be judged kindly by whatever came after them.","And neither of them had any idea that the power of an Immense One had flared in a certain spring not too long ago.","Well, and what was happening there now after an ordeal was passed!"]}]);
